1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MATILDA===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The surname of this lady has not been identified. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06paul/page/214 The Scots Peerage VI: 214]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Patrick Graham of Kincardine and Dundaff and Matilda had the following children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir William Graham of Kincardine d. 1424
2 CONT # Matilda Graham
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/214/mode/2up The Scots peerage] founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of 
2 CONC that kingdom. Published 1904 by D. Douglas in Edinburgh .  Vol Vl.  Page 214
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir Patrick Graham of Kincardine and of Dundaff and Matilda (?); Sir William Graham of Kincardine d. 1424 Matilda Graham
2 CONT
2 CONT The above was cited from; [http://thepeerage.com/p10806.htm#i108058 thepeerage] website
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Patrick Graham, Lord Dundaff, Knight-Banneret was born at of Kincardine, Forfarshire, Scotland. He married Matilda. Sir Patrick Graham, Lord Dundaff, Knight-Banneret married Euphemia (Egidia) Stewart, daughter of Sir John Stew
2 CONC art and Alicia More (Mure), circa 1384; 2nd marriage for him. They had 4 sons (Sir Patrick, Earl Palatine of Strathearn; Sir Robert of Kinpunt; David; & Alexander).2,3,4 Sir Patrick Graham, Lord Dundaff, Knight-Banneret died in 14
2 CONC 00.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: There is no mention of a Sir William Graham being the result of Sir Patrick Grahams' marriage with Euphemia Stewart. Therefore, it is my conclusion that Matilda is the mother of Sir William Graham. Credit to HRH Prince Kiere
2 CONC n de Muire Von Drakenberg
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations: [S370] Unknown author, The Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles, by Gerald Paget, Vol. 1, p. 213; Burke's Peerage, 1938, p. 1775. [S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 558. [S16
2 CONC ] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. III, p. 533-534. [S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 611.
