1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Patrick Graham, 1st Lord Graham1===
2 CONT * M, #108234, d. 24 June 1466
2 CONT * son of: Alexander Graham,  d. from 14 March 1415/16 to 8 January 1421/22; son of Sir William Graham of Kincardine and Gille Stewart
2 CONT * Married: Hon. Christian Erskine, daughter of Sir Robert Erskine of that Ilk, 1st Lord Erskine and Lady Elizabeth Lindsay.1,2 She married, secondly, William Charteris of Kinfauns in 1476.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick Graham, 1st Lord Graham was the son of Alexander Graham.1 He married Hon. Christian Erskine, daughter of Sir Robert Erskine of that Ilk, 1st Lord Erskine and Lady Elizabeth Lindsay.2 He died between 24 June 1466 and 1478.1
2 CONC ,2
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Lord in Regency in the minority of King James II.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Patrick Graham, 1st Lord Graham and Hon. Christian Erskine
2 CONT * William Graham, 2nd Lord Graham+2 d. 1472
2 CONT * Elizabeth Graham+4 d. 1506
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p10824.htm#i108234
2 CONT **1. Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 228. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT **2. BP2003 volume 2, page 2752. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT **3. Matthew H.C.G., editor, Dictionary of National Biography on CD-ROM (Oxford, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1995). Hereinafter cited as Dictionary of National Biography.
2 CONT **4. Hans Harmsen, "re: Chester Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 21 August 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Chester Family."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Baron Graham; m. Christian Erskine; father of Elizabeth Graham. [Royal Descents, p. 92]
2 CONT
2 CONT A hostage in England 1427-32 for the ransom of King James I; cr. 28 June 1445, Lord Graham; m. Christian Erskine; father of William Graham, 2nd Lord Graham. [Magna Charta Sureties, Line 43E, p. 54]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Clan Graham  fought at the Battle of Dunbar in 1296 where Sir Patrick Graham of Kincardine was the only man of all the Scots not to retreat and instead fought to the death.
