1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===JOHN WALLACE OF THURISTOUN===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Wallace of Thuristoun is the son of George Wallace of Elderslie and the younger brother of Patrick Wallace of Elderslie. He had a precept of sasine from the crown estates for the lands of Thuristoun in 1480 [https://archiv
2 CONC e.org/stream/exchequerrollsof09scot#page/680/mode/1up The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland, IX, p. 680] and on 19 November 1499 he and his brother Patrick are noticed in the witness list of a charter made in favour of Hugh Wallace, bro
2 CONC ther of John Wallace of Craigie. [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/24/mode/1up Liber Protocollorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, etc. A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 34 on pp.24-5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Exchequer Rolls of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1480: Renfrew. Sa. Johannis Wallace t. Thuristoun, Ellersly.[https://archive.org/stream/exchequerrollsof09scot#page/680/mode/1up The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland, IX, p. 680]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Protocol Book of Master Cuthberti Simonis===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 November 1499: "Patricio Walles, filio et apparenti herede Georgii Walles de Ellirsly" and "Johanne Walles, fratre germano eiusdem Patricio" are noticed in the witness list of a charter in favour of "Hugonis Walles, [fratre]
2 CONC  germani Johannis Walles de Cragy." [https://archive.org/stream/liberprotocollor02bain#page/24/mode/1up Liber Protocollorum M. Cuthberti Simonis, etc. A.D. 1499-1513, protocol number 34 on pp.24-5]'''
