1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===HAWES VALLANCE (aka HAWES WALLACE)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hawes Wallace is the wife of John Ralston of that Ilk and the mother of Thomas Ralston of that Ilk. By a charter dated 11 February 1505 her son Thomas confirmed that he had exchanged the lands of Ralston in Paisley parish, in t
2 CONC he sheriffdom of Renfrew, for the lands of the Hill of Dunlop and Rossholm, in the Cunningham division of the sheriffdom of Ayr. He reserved the liferent of his father and mother: "Reservatis libero tenemento Joh. Railstoun patri 
2 CONC suo, et rationabili tertia Hawes Wallace matri sue cum contingeret".  [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/622/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, charter number 2929]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 February 1505: [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi02scot#page/622/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, charter number 2929]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 February 1506:  Instrument of Sasine in favour of Thomas Railstoune [Ralston], son and apparent heir of John Railstoune [Ralston] of that Ilk, of lands of Railstoune [Ralston] in barony and sheriffdom of Renfrew, reserving o
2 CONC ne third thereof to Hawes Vallace [Wallace], spouse of said John, following on precept, dated 4 January 1505/6, by said John. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f3%2f1115&st=1&tc=y&
2 CONC tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+ralston+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/3/1115]'''
