1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===HUGH RALSTON OF THAT ILK===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hugh Ralston of that Ilk served on an Assize on 21 August 1531 [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi03scot#page/268/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546, charter number 1229 on pp. 268-69 but s
2 CONC ee note 2 on p.269]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hugh Ralston of that Ilk is reported to have been killed at the Battle of Pinkie Cleugh, which took place on 10 September 1547 [https://archive.org/stream/topographicaldes00robe#page/277/mode/1up Robertson's Ayrshire, p. 277]''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/topographicaldes00robe#page/n6/mode/1up Topographical description of Ayrshire, more particularly of Cunninghame, together with a genealogical account of the principal families in that bailiwick. By Ge
2 CONC orge Robertson (Cunningham Press, Irvine, 1820), 442 pp. For Ralston of Ralston see pp. 276-9]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyo01pateuoft/page/n6/mode/1up History of the County of Ayr : with a genealogical account of the families of Ayrshire. By James Paterson. Vol. I (John Dick, Ayr, MDCCCXLVII), 463 pp. For
2 CONC  Ralston of that Ilk see pp. 265-70]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_0NEKAAAAYAAJ/page/n2/mode/1up Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Landed Gentry of Great Britain and Ireland. By John Burke, Esq., and John Bernard Burke, Esq. Vol II. M - Z (Henr
2 CONC y Colburn, London, MDCCCXLVII), 1673 pp. For Ralston of Ralston see p. 1096]
