1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN WALLACE OF ELDERSLIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''THE ANCESTRY OF JOHN WALLACE OF ELDERSLIE HERE TREATED IS UNCERTAIN'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''George Crawfurd identified him as the son of William Wallace of Elderslie and the grandson of Patrick Wallace of Elderslie. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015080378733;view=1up;seq=105 George Crawfurd, A General 
2 CONC Description of the Shire of Renfrew, etc., p. 87] James Paterson followed Crawfurd, also identifying him as the son of William Wallace of Elderslie and the grandson of Patrick Wallace of Elderslie. He says this of him: "John Walla
2 CONC ce of Ellerslie, who married a daughter of Cunninghame of Craigends, and had a charter for Ellenton 1530." [https://archive.org/stream/historycountyay00pategoog#page/n231/mode/1up Ayrshire, p. 220]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Charles Rogers disagreed: "In the lands of Elderslie, Patrick Wallace was succeeded by his son John, who to his inheritance added the lands of Elienton (Helington), of which he and his wife had a charter in 1530. He cites page 
2 CONC 87 of Crawfurd's History of Renfrewshire as the source of this information. [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n76/mode/1up The Book of Wallace, p. 24] Crawfurd himself cites a charter in the collection of the Ea
2 CONC rl of Dundonald: "Carta penes J. Com. de Dundonald." [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.39015080378733;view=1up;seq=105 George Crawfurd, A General Description of the Shire of Renfrew, etc., p. 87]'''
