1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ANDREW LUNDY OF BENHOLM===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Spurious Pedigree'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Andrew Lundy of Benholm is identified as the grandson of Robert Lundy of Benholm  in Dr. Robert Lundie's account of the family (another Robert Lundy of Benholm intervening), but this is wrong.  [https://www.electric
2 CONC scotland.com/webclans/htol/lundin8.html Lundie of Benholm] Andrew Lundy of Benholm is in fact the son of Robert Lundy of Benholm, rather than his grandson. [http://www.lundie.org/newsite/book/pdf/Lundy_lundie_lundin_book_benholm.p
2 CONC df The House of Benholm]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===EVIDENCE FROM THE NATIONAL RECORDS OF SCOTLAND===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 June 1523: Sasine to Andrew Lundy [Lundie], as heir of the deceased Robert Lundy [Lundie] of Benhome [Benholm] his father, of the lands of Inchmedane [Inchmeddan], Tulloch of Benhome [Tully of Benholm] and Kyrktone of Benholm
2 CONC e [Kirkton of Benholm], with the mill thereof; which had been in nonentry for four years, and to which Andrew had the King's Dispensation to enter notwithstanding his minority. On Chancery Precept of Clare Constat, dated 25 June a
2 CONC n.reg. 10 (A.D.1523). Sasine dated 2 June 1523. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f24&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Andrew+Lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland,
2 CONC  Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/24]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: The Sasine bears to be dated earlier than the Precept, which shows that there must be some clerical error.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 May 1524: Sasine to Andrew Lundy [Lundie], as heir foresaid, of the Manis of Benholme [Benholm]; which had been in the King's hands for five years by reason of ward. On Chancery Precept of Clare Constat dnted 16 May an.reg.1
2 CONC 1 (A.D.1524). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f25&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Andrew+Lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Ben
2 CONC holm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/25]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 February 1525-26: Precent by Andrew Lundy [Lundie] baron of Benhom [Benholm], for giving sasine to John Lundy [Lundie] his brother german, of the shadow half of the lands of Tollow in the barony of Benhom [Tully of Benholm];
2 CONC  conform to lfrerent charter thereof granted to said John. Dated at Benhom [Benholm], 26 February 1525/6. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f26&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Andrew+Lun
2 CONC dy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/26]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 July 1548: Sasine to William Lundy [Lundie], as heir of Andrew Lundy [Lundie] of Benholme [Benholm] his father (who was killed in the battle of Pinkie), of the Manis of Benholme [Benholm], the lands of Inchmedden [Inchmeddan]
2 CONC , Tullo of Benholme [Tully of Benholm], and Kirktoun of Benholme [Kirkton of Benholm], with mill thereof. On Chancery Precept of Clare Constat dated 4 June an. reg. 6 (A.D.1548). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalo
2 CONC gue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f27&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Andrew+Lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/27]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===GENEALOGY===
2 CONT
