1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/William-Graham-of-Netherby/6000000016669767621
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Sir William "4th Laird of Fintry" Graham
2 CONT *Birth: about 1496 in Fintry, Forfarshire, Scotland
2 CONT *Death: about 1546
2 CONT *Parents:  Sir David "3rd Laird of Fintry" Graham and Jean Graham
2 CONT * Spouse: Catherine Bethune (also known as Beaton) — married [date unknown] [location unknown]. She was the sister of Cardinal David Beaton.   Katherine Beaton died about 1544.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Katherine Bethune and Sir William Graham are recorded as:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT #     David Graham (born 1525) (heir), married Margaret Ogilvy
2 CONT #     Walter Graham (born 1526), 
2 CONT #     James Graham (born 1527), 
2 CONT # daughter mar., Crichton of Innernitie 
2 CONT #     Gorthe Catherine Graham (born 1530-1575), married Christopher Armstrong.
2 CONT # Margaret Graham (3rd daughter)  (born about 1530), married Alexander Ogilvy
2 CONT # daughter who mar. Dr Thomson in Dundee.  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Graham-9024
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth and death dates are rough estimates based upon the generation of 25-30 years, and not accurate.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Graham, fourth of Fintry, who obtained, in 1529 and 1541, charters from James V constituting his extensive lands in Forfarshire, Stirlingshire, and Perthshire, into " two free baronries, to be held blench of the crown, to 
2 CONC be called the baronries of Strathdichty, Comitis, in Forfarshire, and Buchlivy Graham, in Monteith.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Fintry married Catharine, daughter of John Beaton, of Balfour, and sister of Cardinal Beaton, Archbishop of St. Andrews and Chancellor of Scotland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William Graham 4th Fintry (1505-1600) married Lady Catherine or Katherine Bethune who may be also Beaton of Balfour born abt 1509. Born Fintray Forfarshire Scotland whose mother was Lady Jean / Janet GRAHAM Of Montrose. Willia
2 CONC m Graham married Lady Catherine Beaton abt 1529 and they had a child called David. They married at Fintray Forfarshire Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Beaton's (born Balfour Fifeshire) father was Laird John BEATON / BETHUNE 6th Of Balfour, (1465-1524) and her mother was Lady Elizabeth MONEYPENNY Of Kinkell, (1475-1514).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William possibly had several wives:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Katherine Beaton/Bethune
2 CONT *Katherine Murray, the widow of James Scrymgeour of Glasswell. There was no issue by this marriage  This marriage was brief as William died about 1546. 
2 CONT *Dauphine Armstrong
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of his children may have been by wives other than Jean. Any additional sources are welcome. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Sources
2 CONT # Burke, J., A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great Britain. 
2 CONT #     Burke, J. (1838). A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great Britain and Ireland Enjoying Territorial Possessions Or High Official Rank: But Uninvested with Heritable Honours 3. London: Henry Colburn. p. 1
2 CONC 21.  
2 CONT #     http://inchbrakie.tripod.com/abookofthegraemes/id61.html  
2 CONT #     Clan MacFarlane, https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I19987&tree=CC  
2 CONT #     https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/2:2:3KKN-P76 : accessed 20 February 2019), entry for Walter Graham of Meiklewood; "Dogs of Menteith" file (2:2:2:MM6V-RWF), submitted 26 November 2018 by Ken Doig [identity withheld for pr
2 CONC ivacy  
2 CONT #    A Book of the Graemes, http://inchbrakie.tripod.com/abookofthegraemes/id61.html  
2 CONT #     The Peerage, Person page 66921, http://www.thepeerage.com/p66921.htm#i669207  
2 CONT #     Webcards Person Sheet, Laird William 4th Fintry, http://venitap.com/Genealogy/WebCards/ps44/ps44_122.html  
2 CONT #     Sir Francis Mudie, David M. Walker, (1964), Mains Castle & the Grahams of Fintry, Issue 9 of Publication (Abertay Historical Society) [Abertay Historical Society Publication. no. 9.], Abertay Historical Society,, University 
2 CONC of Virginia. 36 pages 
2 CONT #     Family Search, William Graham (1505-1600), https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LHX5-H4R/william-graham-1505-1600  
2 CONT # https://www.patrickspeople.scot/ourfamily/7494.htm cites
