1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===HUGH RALSTON OF THAT ILK (aka HEW RALSTOUN OF THAT ILK)===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Hugh Ralston of that Ilk (Otherwise Hew Ralstoun of that Ilk) made his last will and testament, at Woodside in Beith, on 23 May 1613, and died there in August in the same year. He appointed his wife, Janet Hamilton, his only ex
2 CONC ecutor. His sons Hugh and John witnessed this deed. [https://archive.org/stream/descriptionsofsh00hami#page/79/mode/1up William Hamilton of Wishaw, Descriptions of the Sheriffdoms of Lanark and Renfrew (Maitland Club, Glasgow, MDC
2 CONC CCXXXI), page 79]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from Collections Towards a History of the Monastery of Kilwinning===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 March 1551: Charter granting the lands of Woodside to Hugh Ralston of that Ilk . . . . . [https://archive.org/details/cu31924092901564/page/n276/mode/1up Collections: Kilwinning charter number 32 on193-6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 October 1570: Bond by Hugh Ralston of that ilk to the earl of Eglinton for £20. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f2%2f7%2f19&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hugh+ralston&ko=p&r=&ro
2 CONC =s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/2/7/19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 April 1572: Charter witnessed by Hugone Ralstoun de eodem, and others. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/539/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1546-80, charter number 2065]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 January 1580: Two charters witnessed by Hugone Ralstoun de eodem, and others. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi05scot#page/29/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1580-93, charters numbered 95 and
2 CONC  96]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 December 1609: Copy Tack by Alexander, commendator of Kilwynninge with consent of the convent thereof setting to James Hammiltoun of Ardoch and Elizabeth Hammiltoune, his spouse and the longest liver of them in liferent and a
2 CONC fter their deceases to Andro Hammiltoun, their eldest son and apparent heir, whom failing, said James' heirs and assignees whomsoever, for 19 years from Lammas 1583, the teind sheaves of the lands following. viz the 5 merk land of
2 CONC  old extent of Over and Nether Ardochis adn 12 shilling land of same extent called Caslandi lying contiguous, within the parish of Kilwinning, also the 18 shilling land of old extent of Rouchband (Rouchbank), 16 shilling land of C
2 CONC rummoke, 12 shilling of Ruddisyeard in Bogesyde, and 6 shilling and 8 penny land of Fullwodeheid alias Bogesyde, within the parish of Beith, also the lands of Dastway extending to 10 shilling land of new extent, the half merk land
2 CONC  of new extent called Guyddeiscroft, half merk land of new extent called Carlingemyrebrige, and 2 acres of land in the Utter Byreflat, occupied by Jesper Speir, Johne Speir, his son, Petir Browne and Jesper Browne, his son, and th
2 CONC e rig of land occupied by William Park, lying in the village of Kilwinning, bailliary of Cunningham and sheriffdom of Air. Tack duty 4lib Scots. At Kilwinning, 18th October 1583. Witnesses John Hamilton of Auchentiber, Robert Blai
2 CONC r, brother german to Johne Blair of that ilk, Thomas Eset, messenger, Gavin Nasmith, notary. Copy signed by witnesses also by James Hamilton of Ardo, Elizabeth Hamilton signs with hand at pen lead by J Boill, notary public; attest
2 CONC ed also by Master John Heriot, joint notary. Original subscribed by commendator and by Deynes James Michell, Robert Currie and John Deyne. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2692&s
2 CONC t=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Ralstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/2692]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Copy made by Master Claud Hamilton at Kilwinning, 8th December 1609. Witnesses HUH RALSTOUN OF THAT ILK, HUGH RALSTOUN, HIS SON. Cuthbert Hamilton of Auchintiber, Robert Kyll, burgess of Irwene, John Michell in Irwene. [https:/
2 CONC /catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%2f2692&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Ralstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register House charters, 1st series, reference RH6/2692]
2 CONC '''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 October 1617: Charter by the deceased Hugh Ralston of that ilk, to deceased William Mure, lawful son of deceased Archibald Mure at the kirk of Beith of the lands of Kirkhoushill or Rodger's Mailling, [http://catalogue.nrscot
2 CONC land.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f3%2f31%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hugh+ralston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Archives of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, refer
2 CONC ence GD3/1/3/31/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
