1 NAME William /Wallace of Elderslie/
2 GIVN William
2 SURN Wallace of Elderslie
2 _MARNM Wallace of Elderslie
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 19 MAR 1549 AND 31 MAR 1549
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == WILLIAM WALLACE OF ELDERSLIE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie here treated is the son of John Wallace of Elderslie. [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n76/mode/1up The Book of Wallace, Volume I, pp. 24-5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Charles Rogers says this of William Wallace of Elderslie: "In his will dated 19th March 1549, and confirmed 8th April 1551, William Wallace of Elderslie names as his executors his wife 'Janet Schaw' and William Wallace, whom th
2 CONC e testator describes as 'my heir.' and William Wallace whom he names as 'my son'. Rogers goes on to say that 'my son' is probably a clerical error for 'my grandson', although this seems unlikely. [https://archive.org/stream/bookof
2 CONC wallace01roge#page/n76/mode/1up The Book of Wallace, Volume I, pp. 24-5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie here treated died in March 1549. He was alive on 19 March 1549 but he died before 31 March 1549. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, reference CC9/7/1 pp. 120-21]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie made his last will and testament on 19 March 1549. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, reference CC9/7/1 pp. 120-21]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076639896857& Image of Testament 1]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076638965976& Image of Testament 2]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace is said to have married married Catherine Crawfurd. '[http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ww/wallace02.php Stirnet: Wallace 02]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie married Janet Schaw. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, reference CC9/7/1 pp. 120-21] The marriage is noticed by the Reverend Charles Rogers [https://archive.org/stream/bo
2 CONC okofwallace01roge#page/n76/mode/1up Ayrshire, II, pp. 24-5] but James Paterson completely missed William and his second wife. [https://archive.org/stream/historycountyay00pategoog#page/n231/mode/1up Ayrshire, II, p. 220]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie had at least four children. The name of their respective mothers is not known.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Wallace-of-Elderslie/386438004180004903?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1519979164394&through=6000000076500993851
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Wallace/6000000076735067660?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1539011760826&through=6000000076500993851
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Wallace-of-Monktonhill/6000000076681607941?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1539011905117&through=6000000076500993851
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/David-Wallace/6000000076683382027?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1539012130062&through=6000000076500993851
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 November 1536: Renfrew. Vicecomes de Renfrew respondebit pro vjcxx li. de firmis terrarum de Thornlie jacentium in baronium suam .......... et pro vijclxxv li. de firmis terrarum de Ellerslie jacentium infra dictam ballium [h
2 CONC ttps://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=umn.31951d004665231;view=1up;seq=692 George Powell McNeill, MA., LL.B. (editor), Rotuli Scaccarii Regum Scotorum. The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland, Vol. XVI. A.D. 1529-1536 (H.M. General Regist
2 CONC er House, Edinburgh, 1897), p. 616]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 November 1536: Renfrew. Vicecomes de Renfrew iijmiijcvj li. de firmis terrarum de Thurstoun jacentium in baronium de Renfrew [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=umn.31951d004665231;view=1up;seq=692 George Powell McNeill, 
2 CONC MA., LL.B. (editor), Rotuli Scaccarii Regum Scotorum. The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland, Vol. XVI. A.D. 1529-1536 (H.M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1897), p. 616]'''
