2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 9 SEP 1513
2 PLAC Killed at Flodden
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He died on 9 September 1513 at Flodden Field, Northumberland, England, killed in action.3
2 CONT
2 CONT On 1 July 1505 he was retoured heir to his father.1 In January 1508/9 obtained a charter erecting his lands in the Lennox and others in Perthshire, not already forming part of the barony of Gleneagles, into the barony of Haldane, 
2 CONC the house of Rusky being appointed the principal messuage.1 He fought in the Battle of Flodden on 9 September 1513.3
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 3, page 3744.
2 CONT
