1 NAME Walter /Ross/
2 GIVN Walter
2 SURN Ross
2 _MARNM Ross
1 NAME Walter Ross, 8th Lord of Balnagowan
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1490
2 ADDR
3 CITY Cromarty
3 CTRY Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 MAY 1528
2 ADDR
3 CITY Tain
3 CTRY Scotland
1 OCCU Laird of Balnagowan
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT Not the son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Ross-2nd-Lord-of-Halkhead/6000000002188078971
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1528 - On February 29, Patrick Hamilton, a Protestant martyr, was burned at the stake in St Andrews. Walter, eighth Laird of Balnagowan, was slain at Tain in 1528, possibly during a clan feud. He was succeeded by his son Alexander
2 CONC  Ross, the ninth Balnagowan Chief of Clan Ross. The relics of St. Duthus/Duthac were stored at the Castle, when the Presbyterian Church of Scotland became established in the area. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.greatclanross.org/htext6.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir David Ross, seventh Laird of Balnagowan, built the original wing and towers of the castle from fieldstone on the lands. David's first wife, Helen Keith of Inverguie, gave birth to four sons: (1) Walter, who became the eighth L
2 CONC aird; (2) William, who became the first Laird of Invercharron; (3) Hugh, who became the first of the Rosses of Achnacloich; and Angus, who married the daughter of William MacCulloch of Plaids. David's second marriage was to the da
2 CONC ughter of the Duke of Albany. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The '''eighth Laird, Walter of Balnagowan''', married Marion, the daughter of Sir John James Grant of Grant, and produced the following offspring: (1) Alexander; (2) Katherine, who married a magistrate of Tain; and (3) Janet, who 
2 CONC married the fifth Lord Lovat. He was supposedly killed in a clan feud at Tain in 1528. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.balnagown.com/about-balnagown/our-history/
2 CONT
2 CONT Timeline of the Lairds of Balnagown & Balnagown Castle
2 CONT
2 CONT The lands of Ross existed long before there was a Clan Ross. It was from this highly fertile and desirable area that this clan, rather unusually, took its name. The Clan name first appears around the 11th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1368
2 CONT
2 CONT It all started with Clan Ross
2 CONT
2 CONT The first Laird of Balnagown was Hugh Ross. He was given the land by his half-brother William, the Earl of Ross in 1368. William had no direct male heir, and it would have been quite usual to pass on both his title and his lands t
2 CONC o a male sibling. William, however, had fallen foul of the King, David II, who bestowed the Earldom instead on William’s daughter Euphemia.
2 CONT
2 CONT The allegiance of the Clan was a different matter and it stayed firmly with Hugh, the 1st Laird of Balnagown, who was regarded as Clan Chief from then on. Hugh of Rarichies changed his name to Hugh Ross to further establish his li
2 CONC nks with the land and clan, and Balnagown came to be regarded as the seat of the Clan Ross. It would become the home of the Ross Clan chiefs for several hundreds of years.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1398
2 CONT
2 CONT Then came Walter
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter, the 3rd Laird, made an astute marriage to Catherine, daughter of Paul Mactyre, an infamous freebooter. He had made a vast fortune through shady dealings and Catherine’s dowry included the lands of Strathoykel, Stathcarron 
2 CONC and Freevater. This marriage greatly extended the Balnagown estates to the north and west.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *The Scottish Antiquary: Or, Northern Notes & Queries, Volumes 3-4.   “Line of Balnogown.”  Page 10.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=jX4DAAAAMAAJ&pg=RA1-PA10&lpg=RA1-PA10&dq=Catherine+married+Alexander+Ross+of+Balnagown+and+di
2 CONC ed+on+12+April+1592.&source=bl&ots=J9ADARm_4L&sig=ACfU3U1fm3N2Ox0hyOyLUyP5M_-ud6rYrg&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjjgoHelZvqAhVECs0KHTmOBo0Q6AEwAnoECAoQAQ#v=onepage&q=Catherine%20married%20Alexander%20Ross%20of%20Balnagown%20and%20died%2
2 CONC 0on%2012%20April%201592.&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I21049&tree=CC
