1 NOTE {geni:about_me} When Catherine Graham of Gorthe was born about 1527, in Dumfries, Dumfriesshire, Scotland, United Kingdom, her father, Sir William Graham 4th of Fintry, was 47 and her mother, Catherine Bethune, was 38.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Christopher John Christie of Barngleish about 1544, in Dunfermline, Fife, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT When Sir John Christopher Armstrong was born in 1526, in Dumfriesshire, Scotland, United Kingdom, his father, Sir John Armstrong, was 46 and his mother, Lady Elizabeth Graham of Montrose, was 29. He married Lady Catherine Graham o
2 CONC f Gorte about 1545, in Dumfriesshire, Scotland. They were the parents of at least 14 sons. He died on 22 September 1606, in his hometown, at the age of 80, and was buried in Langholm, Dumfriesshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Graham-675
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Gorthe Catherine Graham was born about 1530 in Falde, Scotland. She was the daughter of Sir William Graham 4th of Fintry. She married Christopher Armstrong in 1545 in Barngleish, Dumfriesshire, Scotland. They were the parents of a
2 CONC t least 4 sons, among them:
2 CONT
2 CONT #     John Armstrong (1545 - 1628), 
2 CONT #     Robert Armstrong (1563 - 1564), 
2 CONT #     William Armstrong (1565 - 1649).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine died in 1575 in Dumfriesshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Note
2 CONT
2 CONT '''There is some uncertainty about who her mother was. Other names mentioned are:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Katherine Bethune/Beaton (born about 1489), cf. Biography text of WikiTree profile David Graham and https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L1W3-PF6
2 CONT *    Margaret Armstrong (born about 1520), cf. https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p6296.htm''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Any additional sources are welcome.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
