2 CONT '''14 June 1584: Precept of clare constat granted by Hew, Earl of Eglinton, Lord Montgomery for infefting Robert Montgomery, son of Robert Montgomery then deceased as heir of his father in the lands of Skelmurlie (Skelmorlie), Loc
2 CONC hlebosyid, Lochrynsay (Lochranza) and Synnokis (Sannox); reserving nonetheless the free tenement and liferent of the lands of Lochlebosyd to Dorothy Sempill, spouse to deceased Robert Montgomery for the whole time of her life Date
2 CONC d at the burgh of Irvine Witnesses: Hew, Master of Eglinton, Robert Mur of Caldwell, Neill Montgomery of Langschaw, Hew Montgomery of Hessilheid, John Montgomery of Scottistoun, Gavin Ralstoun, younger of that ilk and others [http
2 CONC ://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f7%2f1%2f12&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ralstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of E
