1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 14 MAY 1599 AND 31 MAY 1599
2 PLAC Scotland
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM WALLACE OF ELDERSLIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie here treated is the son of William Wallace of Elderslie. He is called "my heir" in his father's last will and testament dated 19 March 1549. [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n78/
2 CONC mode/1up The Book of Wallace, p. 25] '''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The identity of his mother is less certain. At the time of his death, his father was married to Joneta Schaw, but she is not specifically said to be the mother of William here treated [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id
2 CONC =6000000076638965976& The Last Will and Testament of William Wallace of Elderslie] It is possible, therefore, that he is the son of Catherine Crawford, although, presently, it is difficult or impossible to be certain of the identi
2 CONC ty of her husband. James Paterson says that Catherine Crawford had a son named William who was his father's heir in 1556 [https://archive.org/stream/historycountyay00pategoog#page/n231/mode/1up Ayrshire, p. 220] but Charles Rogers
2 CONC  ignores the work of his predecessors and makes no mention of her. [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n76/mode/1up The Book of Wallace, pp. 24-5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Father's Testament Testamentar===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie made his last will and testament on 19 March 1549. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, reference CC9/7/1 pp. 120-21]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076639896857& Image of Testament 1]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076638965976& Image of Testament 2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie died in May 1599. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, The Testament Testamentar of umqle William Wallace of Ellerslie, reference CC8/8/34 pp. 158-165]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Testament Testamentar===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie made his last will and testament on 19 March 1599. He nominated his sons John Wallace, Gabriel Wallace, and James Wallace, to be his executors. He also nominated the following people to be oversmen:
2 CONC  John Wallace elder of Craigie, John Wallace, younger of Craigie, together with William Wallace of Johnston, and John Wallace in Monktonhill "my brothers germane" and Allan Hamilton of Ferguslie "my sone in law." Among the legacie
2 CONC s he left was two hundred merks to "Jonet Wallace my dochter lawll spous to Alla[n] Hamiltoun of Ferguslie" together with four hundred pounds which was owed to him by Allan. He also left forty pounds to Elizabeth Wallace "dochter 
2 CONC naturall to Wm Wallace my son and appeirand air." He also left one hundred merks to his son William, money which William owed to his father. He also forgave his brother David Wallace of "all soumes of money & debts awin be him to 
2 CONC me."
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076681984218& Image of Testament 1] 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076682328893& Image of Testament 2]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076682173019& Image of Testament 3]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076682304828& Image of Testament 4]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076680355542& Image of Testament 5]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076680485439& Image of Testament 6]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076679910290& Image of Testament 7]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076680358224& Image of Testament 8]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie married Janet Hamilton. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Edinburgh, The Testament Dative of umqle Jonet Hamiltoune auld ladie Elirslie spous to Wm Wallace of Elirslie, reference 
2 CONC CC8/8/22 pp. 117-19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Wife's Testament Dative===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''When his wife died William Wallace of Elderslie, together with their sons, John Wallace, Gabriel Wallace, and James Wallace, gave up her testament dative and inventory. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasg
2 CONC ow, The Testament Dative of umqle Jonet Hammiltoun auld Ladie Elirslie spous to Wm Wallace of Elirslie, reference CC/8/22 pp. 117-19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076677091347& Image of Testament 1]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076679034884& Image of Testament 2]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076678490910& Image of Testament 3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Wallace-of-Elderslie/6000000024527057505?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1539007240175&through=386438004180004903
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Hamilton-of-Ferguslie/6000000013444994894?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1539007910788&through=386965409640004995
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Gabriel-Wallace/386965713410004982?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1539007468192&through=386438004180004903
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Wallace-of-Murehead/386965409640004995?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1539007389825&through=386438004180004903
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Hugh-Wallace/6000000076665560956?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1539008080046&through=386438004180004903
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Wallace/6000000076650665863?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1539008162673&through=386438004180004903
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28-29 May 1583: Procuratory of Resignation by Gilbert Watt, litster in Kilmarnok appointing [ ] his procurators to resign into the hands of Sit Mathowe Campbell of Lowdoun, knight, sheriff of Air, his superior, his tenement of 
2 CONC land with yard thereof in the burgh of Mauchling (between the tenements of William Patersoune, Androw Fischear and John Fischear on the east, the tenement of Alexander Sim on the south, the tenements of Alexander Adam, Thomas Fisc
2 CONC hear, Nicoll Mirrie and Andro Allan on the west and William Paterson's new yard on the north) lying in the lordship of Kylismuir and sheriffdom of Air and that in favour of John Gemmill, notary in Cumnok. At Kilmarnock, 28th May 1
2 CONC 583 Witnesses Alexander Boyd, servant to Lord Boyd, John Ramsay, litster, John Boyd in Kirkdyke of Kilmarnock, David Bordland, servant to said John Gemmill  Also at Richardtoun, 29th May 1583 Witnesses William Wallace of Ellirslie
2 CONC , Hugh Wallace, his son, John Turbat, messenger Signed by the granter with hand at the pen led by Archibald Lrymar and Adam Turbat, notaries public [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH6%
2 CONC 2f2666&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Ellirslie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Recprds of Scotland, Register House Charters, reference RH6/2666]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 July 1585: Tack by Alexander Conynghame of Craganis to William Knok, younger of Selveland, of the 20s. lands of Ryvras (except what belongs to the Laird of Elrislie) for his lifetime [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrson
2 CONC linecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD148%2f221&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elrislie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cuninghame Family of Craigends, Renfrewshire, reference GD148/221]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 November 1585: Renunciation by Steven Symsoun in Rywrayis in favour of Alexander Cwninghame of Craganis of his possession of the lands of Rywrayis, at the desire of William Wallace of Elrislie, who has granted Steven a tack 
2 CONC of Muirheid and other lands [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD148%2f222&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elrislie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cuning
2 CONC hame Family of Craigends, Renfrewshire, reference GD148/222]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 December 1585: Contract of Excambion between Alexander Cwnynghame of Cragennis (with consent of Gabriel C., his tenant of the lands of Windihill alias Buittismaling and Muirheid) on the one part, and William Wallace of Elris
2 CONC lie (with consent of Steven Symsoun, his tenant in Rywrais) on the other part, whereby after adjustment of marches in reference to former disputes between them, the said William exchanges the 20s. lands of Rywrayis for the 20s. la
2 CONC nds of Windihill, which Alexander dispones to him [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD148%2f223&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elrislie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland
2 CONC , Papers of the Cuninghame Family of Craigends, Renfrewshire, reference GD148/223]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 December 1586: Decreet Arbitral (registered 12 September 1587) pronounced by Mr. David Conynghame, Bishop of Aberdeen, William Wallace of Ellirslie, William Porterfeild of that Ilk, James Conynghame of Eschinyaird, John Quhi
2 CONC tfurd, apparent of that Ilk, and Mr. Adam Wallace, one of the bailies of Glasgow, friends and arbiters chosen for the part of Elizabeth Conynghame, widow of James Craufurd of Auchinnames and Alexander Conynghame, now her spouse, o
2 CONC n the one part; and Mr. Archibald Crawfurd, parson of Englishame, John Boill of Kelburne, John Shaw of Bargarrane, William Crawfurd of Knightswood, George Campbell of Stenestoun, and Frisall of Knok, friends and arbiters for the p
2 CONC art of Patrick Crawfurd furd of Auchinnames, on the other part; regarding Elizabeth's claim to the third of Auchinnames and Auldmuir, alleged intromitted with by Patrick Crawfurd, and regarding the heritable right of the lands of 
2 CONC Quhytsyd, and other matters. [Deed in complete] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD148%2f228&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Ellirslie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland,
2 CONC  Papers of the Cuninghame Family of Craigends, Renfrewshire, reference GD148/228]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 April 1598: Procuratory of Resignation by William Wallace of Elrislie of his 20/- lands of Rywrayis (except a part called the Clippingis), in favour of Alexander Cunynghame of Cragens, in terms of Contract. [Dated at Paisley
2 CONC : no Cunningham witnesses] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD148%2f322&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elrislie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cuningh
2 CONC ame Family of Craigends, Renfrewshire, reference GD148/322]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 April 1598: Feu Charter by Claud, Lord Paisley, in favour of said Alex. C. of C. of above subjects. Witnesses (at Paisley), John Whitefurd of that Ilk, William Wallace younger of Johnestoune, William Wallace younger of Elris
2 CONC lie, etc. Seal. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD148%2f323&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elrislie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cuninghame Family 
2 CONC of Craigends, Renfrewshire, reference GD148/3223]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 June 1605: Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands of Lempetstane in the barony of Renfrew to James Wallace of Mureheid, son of the late William Wallace of Elderslie, and James's wife E
2 CONC lizabeth Wallace. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi06scot#page/589/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1593-1608, charter number 1623 on p. 589]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1612:Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands of Lempetstane in the barony of Renfrew to James Wallace of Mureheid, son of the late William Wallace of Elderslie, and James's wife El
2 CONC izabeth Wallace. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi07scot#page/271/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1609-1620, charter number 727 on p. 271]'''
