2 CONT ===Commentary by https://www.geni.com/people/Marshall/6000000052015070826?through=386438004180004903
2 CONT
2 CONT Quote from "The Book of Wallace": "William Wallace, son of William Wallace and Janet Schaw, had, in 1554, from his superior, William Wallace of Caigie, a charter of the lands of Elderslie ; while in 1583 he was confirmed in the la
2 CONC nds of Helington, and in 1507 in the lands of Kysewaeth and Windymill. He died in May 1590. In his "latter will," which is dated at Elderslie on the 14th May 1590,  he names as executors his sons James, Gabriel, and John ; and as 
2 CONC "oversmen" John Wallace, elder, and John Wallace, younger, of Caigie ; also William Wallace of Johnstoun, John Wallace of Mnnktoimhill, his brothers, and Allan Hamilton of Ferguslie, his son-in-law. His "free gear" is estimated at
2 CONC  £1478, 5s. 4d. He married, first, Janet Hamilton of Ferguslie, who died in December 1580. In her testament-dative she is described as " auld Lady Ellerslie." Of the marriage were born four sons, William (of whom subsequently), Ja
2 CONC mes, Gabriel, and John. "
2 CONT
2 CONT The Book of Wallace (https://archive.org/details/bookofwallace01roge) seems to indicate that there was another generation between this William and the William that currently is stated his son. The potential missing William is marr
2 CONC ied to Elizabeth, daughter of Hugh Stewart of Neilstoneside (see pages 27 & 28 of the Book). The writing in this part of the Book is particularly contorted, so I would appreciate any help in its interpretation.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Book (p. 25) also states that this William wrote a will dated 14 May 1599 that named three of his sons, James, Gabriel, and John, as its executors. The "free gear" was estimated to be worth £1478, 5s, 4d in the inventory of hi
2 CONC s estate.
