2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT When Sir Alexander Bruce, 5th Lord of Livingstone was born in 1530 in Airth, Stirlingshire, Scotland, his father, Sir, was 25 and his mother, Janet, was 20. He married Janet LIVINGSTON in 1547 in Burgh, Lanarkshire, Scotland. They
2 CONC  had 15 children in 21 years. He died as a young father in 1551 in his hometown.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Alexander Bruce, 5th Lord of Livingstone (Source: Family Tree on Geneanet)
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Bruce IIIrd of Airth
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendant of Robert the Bruce, King of the Scots (1274- 1329)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ==[https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n52/mode/1up?view=theater The Bruces of Airth and their cadets by Armstrong, William Bruce p 16-17etc]
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander succeeded his father ante 8 March 1552, as at that date he was enfefted ^ as " son of the deceased Robert Brus of Erth," in the lands of Erth held of Holyrood. On 1 July 1547, Sir Alexander had a charter ^^ from Queen Ma
2 CONC ry, with consent of the Regent Arran, on his father's resignation of part of Erth, reserving his liferent and a reasonable tierce to Marion Bruce of Clackmanan, should she survive liim : on 14 May 1548, Sir Alexander had another c
2 CONC harter in the same terms of the Mill of Airth, he is mentioned in a great number of transactions," and in October 1577, Alexander Brus of Airth is licensed'" to remain at home and absent himself from the army summoned to meet the 
2 CONC Regent at Dumfries. In 1595 " a dreadful feud fell out with the Earl of Marr on one side and the Lords Livingston, Elphinstone, and Bruce ofalliance- offensive and defensive with Alexander, lord Livingston, and others. Sir Alexand
2 CONC er Bruce died^ 16 March 1600, having been in possession of Airth forty-eight years ; he appears to have been unwisely liberal to his relations, brothers, nephews, sons, and grandsons, from which may be traced the decline in the fo
2 CONC rtunes of the House of Airth, he having during his long life alienated so much property from the principal estate of the family. Sir Alexander married^ Janet, second daughter of Alexander, fifth lord Livingston [by Lady Agnes Doug
2 CONC las, daughter of John, second earl of Morton, whose mother was the Princess Johanna, daughter of James l. of Scotland by Lady Jean Beaufort his Queen]. J Sir Alexander's will, confirmed 14 August 1600,^ will be found in the Append
2 CONC ix," also that of his wife who died 4 October 1599. By Janet Livingston, Sir Alexander Bruce had issue five sons and two daughters, viz. : 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1. William, died during his father's lifetime, of whom presently.
2 CONT >2. Robert of Kinnaird, of whom presently. 
2 CONT >3. Sir John of Kincavel was captain^ of Stirling Castle 1585, had a charter from his father of West Bordland in Denny, and is mentioned in several transactions f her died lSQ7i.having married Jean," eldest daughter of Sir Robert 
2 CONC Drummond, third of Medhope ; she is mentioned '"as " Dame Jeane Drummond, lady Kincavel " in her daughter's marriage settlement, 1638 ; by her Sir John had issue five sons and two daughters, viz. : —
2 CONT
2 CONT >>(1) Sir Alexander of Kincavel, auoooodod IGQF^. nf,^p
2 CONT >>(2) William," succeeded to Kincavel and had a daughter Grizzel,'^ who married Gavin, second son of Gavin Hamilton of Raploch, 1666.
2 CONT >>(3) Robert, Minister of Aberdour, he was a great traveller in Palestine, etc., he is mentioned in many transactions and had succeeded to Kincavel in 1652,' for he is then styled " of Kincavel." He is guardian to his niece Grizze
2 CONC l in IGGG, and is again styled^ " of Kincavel " on that occasion. He is also mentioned in his sister Margaret's marriage contract. Robert married Janet Watson,^ relict of Mr. Andrew Aytoun ; they liad children,^ but there is no fu
2 CONC rther record of them.
2 CONT >>(4) Walter, minister of Inverkeithing,^ was guardian to his niece Grizzel, 1G52, is mentioned in his sister's mariage contract and in many other '^ transactions ; he married Jean,' daughter of Alexander Menzies of Rotenell, and 
2 CONC was dead* in 1674, when Jean is called his relict.
2 CONT >>(5) John of Wrae," procurator to his sister Anna, 1643, he had two daughters,^" heir-portioners of their father, Jean and Marion.
2 CONT >>(6) Margaret married/^ October 1638, Sir John Stirling of Garden, Knight.
2 CONT >>(7) Anna married James Bruce of Powfoullis.
2 CONT >>[Note. — Nothing more is known of tlie Braces of Kincavel.]
2 CONT
2 CONT >4.Sir Alexander of Bangour,'- mentioned as " fourth son of Sir Alexander Bruce of Airth," 1588. He is mentioned," 5 September 1597, as having been " son lawful of Sir Alexander Bruce of Airth," and being then deceased. He married
2 CONC  Helen Hamilton,^* [who re-married William Congleton of that Ilk as his second wife], and had issue one son and oin daughter, viz. ; —
2 CONT
2 CONT >>(1) Alexander of Bangour, is enfefted^* as heir of Alexander Bruce of Baugour in 6 oxgates of land of Hill of Airth, 10 July 1609. He resigns^ his land of Hill of Airth in favour of Sir John Bruce of Airth, 21 June 1617.
2 CONT ander Bruce of Baugour in 6 oxgates of land of Hill of Airth, 10 July 1609. He resigns^ his land of Hill of Airth in favour of Sir John Bruce of Airth, 21 June 1617. (2) Margaret/ married William Congleton, son of William Congleto
2 CONC n above mentioned, by his first wife, Mary, daughter of John, lord Yester.
2 CONT >>[Note. — Mrs. Gumming Bruce states ^ that the first Alexander of Bangour was succeeded by his son Patrick, whose grandson, Robert Bruce, married Janet, daughter of Sir Jolin Lauder of Fountainhall, Bart., but from reference to A
2 CONC ppendix, p. xlvii., it is clear that the the first Alexander was succeeded by his son Alexander. No more is known of this branch.]
2 CONT
2 CONT >5. Robert had from his father " the eliaplanrie of our Ladie aisle founded and situated on the south side of the Kirk of Airth," 30 October 1572 ;* he is executor* to both his father and mother's wills and mentioned therein as th
2 CONC eir youngest son, he is also stated to have had from his father " the lands of Garwell ; this ia au instance, not uncommon in those days, of two sous of the same parents bearing the same christian name. In 1638 au Alexander Bruce 
2 CONC of Garwald is retoured heir^ to Robert Bruce of Garwald, his fatherj
2 CONT >6.Marion, married^ William Menteith of Kerse. Marriage contract dated 13th May 1557.
2 CONT >7.The other ^ daughter died young.
2 CONT
