2 CONT '''7 September 1597: Charter by Sir Patrick Bellenden of Evie, knight, in favour of William Carmichael, merchant in Kirkwall, of tenement and lodging called of old the "Subdeineis Ludgeing" in the New Wark in Kirkwall. Witnesses: 
2 CONC Lucas Mure, servitor to the said Sir Patrick, Simon Huttoun, skinner, Allester Murray, servitor to the said William Andrew Scott, skipper, David Taitt, mariner, William Ahanay, William Gudaill, and David Arthour, notary public. [h
2 CONC ttp://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Patrick+Bellenden&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Or
2 CONC kney, reference GD31/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 May 1601: Instrument of Sasine in favour of William Bannatyne of Gairsay and Issobell Selkrig, his spouse, of the 3d. lands of Newbigging, in island of Hoy, half of the 1d. lands called the Kirkhous in Osmoundwall, three half
2 CONC  penny lands in Fizea and Wardis, all lying in parishes of Hoy and Walls, and the house called the "subdeineis Mans" and the houses called New Wark or "chaiplaines chalmeris" lying in burgh of Kirkwall; following on charter, dated
2 CONC  20 November 1599, by Sir Patrick Bellenden of Evie, knight. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f10&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Patrick+Bellenden&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National R
2 CONC ecords of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/10]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
