1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===KATHERINE BELLENDEN (aka CATHERINE BELLENDEN)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to J. Finlay, Katherine Bellenden was the sister of Sir John Bellenden of Auchnoul, the Justice Clerk. [http://eprints.gla.ac.uk/37849/1/37849.pdf The Early Career of Thomas Craig, advocate] David Irving identified he
2 CONC r as Catherine Bellenden. According to Irving, Sir John Bellenden bequeathed an annual pension of twenty pounds to his cousin Thomas Craig. [https://books.google.com.au/books?id=2YwEAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA147&source=gbs_toc_r&cad=3#v=onepa
2 CONC ge&q&f=false Lives of Scottish Writers]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Protocol Book of Nicol Thounis===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 August 1560: Instrument of sasine in favour of Robert Craig, burgess of Edinburgh, and Katherine Bellenden, his wife, in four oxgangs of the lands of Kincavill . . . . .  [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso44scotuo
2 CONC ft/page/5 Protocol Books of John Foulis, 1546-1553, and Nicol Thounis, 1559-1564. Edited by James Beveridge, MA., and James Russell (Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh, 1927), protocol number 18 on p. 5]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 may 1560: Reversion by Robert Craig, burgess of Edinburgh, and Katherine Ballendein, his spouse, to said Sir James, for redemption of 4 oxgangs of land in town and lands of Kincavill which Thomas Robesoun occupies, in sherif
2 CONC fdom of Linlithgow, [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD237%2f16%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+craig&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Sivright of Plewl
2 CONC ands and Southhouse, reference GD237/16/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 February 1568-69: Procuratory by Robert Craig, burgess of Edinburgh, and Katherine Bellenden [Ballantyne], his spouse, following on (GD124/1/610). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference
2 CONC =GD124%2f1%2f612&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=katherine+bellenden&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1610&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Erskine Family, Earls of Mar and Kellie, reference GD124/1/612]'''
2 CONT
