1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jean Stirling (Chisholm) is my 14th great grandmother.
2 CONT Janet Milburn 6/1/22
2 CONT __________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Chisholm illegitimate dau. of William Chisholm 'The Robber Bishop of Dunblane.' Sir James acquired much more land from William Chisholm when the old Cathedral lands were sold or given away at the Reformation. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.thepeerage.com/p63833.htm#i638328
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Chisholm1 F, #165089, b. circa 1525, d. 1603 Father	William Chisholm, "Robber" Bishop of Dunblane1 b. c 1498, d. 14 Dec 1564 or 15 Dec 1564 Mother	Jean Graham1 b. c 1491 Charts	Pedigree of Rayburn Lamson Lewis
2 CONT      Jean Chisholm was born circa 1525 at Scotland.1 She married Sir James Stirling, 4th Lord of Keir, 1st Lord of Cawder, son of Sir John Stirling, 3rd Lord of Keir, Sheriff of Perth and Margaret Forrester, in 1542; His 2nd wife.
2 CONC  His 1st wife was Janet Stirling, daughter of Andrew Stirling and Marjory Cunningham.1,2 Jean Chisholm died in 1603 at Scotland.1 Family 	Sir James Stirling, 4th Lord of Keir, 1st Lord of Cawder b. c 1514, d. 3 Feb 1588 Child	
2 CONT
2 CONT     Margaret Stirling+1 b. c 1562, d. 15 Apr 1629
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT     [S11597] Ancestry.com, Information submitted by FrSmith550.
2 CONT     [S11585] The Scots Peerage, Vol. VI, edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, p. 226.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p5498.htm#i165088
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean was born about 1525, the illegitimate daughter of William Chisholm, Bishop of Dunblane, and Jean Graham. She married Sir James Stirling, 4th Lord of Keir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
