1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JOHN COLQUHOUN OF LUSS===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Colquhoun of Luss is the son of Humphrey Colquhoun of Luss and his wife Lady Catherine Graham. [https://archive.org/stream/chiefsofcolquhou01fras#page/109/mode/1up The Chiefs of Colquhoun, i, pp. 109]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Colquhoun of Luss died on 15 January 1574-75, that is 15 January 1575 when the date is adjusted to take account of the change to the Gregorian Calendar. [https://archive.org/stream/chiefsofcolquhou01fras#page/134/mode/
2 CONC 1up [The Chiefs of Colquhoun, i, p. 134]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Colquhoun of Luss married Christian Erskine. They were contracted on 25 January 1535 and married soon after. [https://archive.org/stream/chiefsofcolquhou01fras#page/109/mode/1up The Chiefs of Colquhoun, i, pp. 109] Chr
2 CONC istian Erskine died soon after 20 May 1564. [https://archive.org/stream/chiefsofcolquhou01fras#page/122/mode/1up Ibidem, p. 122]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of the First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Colquhoun/6000000003714021324
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Colquhoun of Luss married, as his second wife, Agnes Boyd.They were married soon after 3 November 1564. [https://archive.org/stream/chiefsofcolquhou01fras#page/123/mode/1up The Chiefs of Colquhoun, i, p. 123] Agnes Boy
2 CONC d died on 18 July 1584. [https://archive.org/stream/chiefsofcolquhou01fras#page/136/mode/1up Ibidem, p. 136]'''
2 CONT
