1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == THOMAS GRAHAM OF MEIGLE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Graham of Meigle, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/George-Graham-5th-of-Claverhouse/6000000024016631200?through=6000000034368105673 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Mariota-Fothringham/6000
2 CONC 000024013047365?through=6000000034368105673 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/323/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 323]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Graham of Meigle, here treated, is noticed as the brother german of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Graham-of-Claverhouse/6000000018446812102?through=6000000034368105673 on 11 October 1656, [https://catalogue.nrscotl
2 CONC and.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f5%2f4%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD220/1/B/5/4/5] and again on 20 October 1656. [https://catalogue.nrsco
2 CONC tland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f6%2f1%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n Ibidem: GD220/1/B/6/1/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Graham, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Blair/6000000206998880835?through=6000000034368712883 daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Blair-of-Balthayock/6000000206998549837 and received 
2 CONC with her, by a charter confirmed under the Great Seal, 26 January 1663, the lands of Potento, in the barony of Meigle, and sheriffdom of Perth. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/pag
2 CONC e/323/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 323]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 August 1656: Disposition by Sir Robert Graham of Morphie with consent of John Graham, now of Claverhouse, son and heir of the deceased William Graham of Claverhouse, his father and of David, Lord Lour, Walter Graham of Duntr
2 CONC oon, Thomas Graham, brother german to the deceased William Graham of Claverhouse and John Fotheringham, lawful son to the deceased Thomas Fotheringham of Denoon, now tutors testamentars to John Graham of Claverhouse since the dece
2 CONC ase of Dame Magdalen Carnegie, Lady Cleverhouse, his mother, in favour of James, Marquess of Montrose, his male heirs and assignees of all the teinds and others contained in GD220/1/B/5/4/4, together with the barony of Dundaff and
2 CONC  patronage of the kirk of Dundaffmuir, containing procuratory of resignation, precept of sasine and assignation to the writs and rents, crop 1653. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD22
2 CONC 0%2f1%2fB%2f5%2f4%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/B/5/4/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 and 20 October 1656: Disposition by David Lord Lour, Walter Graham of Duntroon, Thomas Graham, brother german to the deceased William Graham of Claverhouse and John Fotheringham, son to the deceased Thomas Fotheringham of Den
2 CONC oon, tutors to John Graham of Claverhouse, son and heir to the deceased William Graham of Claverhouse with consent of James, Master of Rollo and the remaining creditors of the deceased Earl of Montrose, in favour of John Graham of
2 CONC  Orchill, of the lands following, part of the lands belonging to the late Earl and disponed by the estates of parliament to the said William Graham for the benefit of the said Earl's creditors, as the just and equal division and p
2 CONC roportion of the said Earl of Montrose's estate, set apart for John Graham of Orchill in complete payment of all debts due to him, containing an assignation to the whole clauses contained in the said disposition granted by the est
2 CONC ates of parliament to the deceased William Graham of Claverhouse. Specifically the lands and tenements lying about the town of Auchterarder and teinds thereof (including the lands now possessed by Walter Graham), the town and land
2 CONC s of Damakellis, Over and Nether Berdralls, Peterhead, half of the town and lands of Aberuthven, the town and lands of Coulshill, Balzieman, Woodside, the croft of land in Auchterarder presently possessed by Thomas Mailler, the la
2 CONC nds of Drumfad, the manor place and precinct of Kincardine and wood thereof, all lying within the burgh of Auchterarder, baronies of Kincardine, Fosswalls and Aberuthven and sheriffdom of Perth, and the town and lands of Duchally 
2 CONC lying within the sheriffdom of Perth foresaid. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f6%2f1%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n Nat
