2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p2049.htm#i20489
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir David Lindsay, Lord Edzell [1]
2 CONT *M, #20489, 
2 CONT *d. December 1610
2 CONT *Last Edited=29 Sep 2008
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.01%
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir David Lindsay, Lord Edzell married, firstly, Lady Helen Lindsay, daughter of David Lindsay, 10th Earl of Crawford and Margaret Bethune.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Isobel Forbes, daughter of Arthur Forbes of Logie and Balfour, on 1 December 1585.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in December 1610.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of David Lindsay, 9th Earl of Crawford and Katherine Campbell.[1] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Lord of Session [Scotland].[2] 
2 CONT *He was styled as Lord Edzell [Scottish Law Lord].[2] 
2 CONT *He lived at Edzell, Brechin, Angus, Scotland.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir David Lindsay, Lord Edzell and Isobel Forbes
2 CONT *1. Margaret Lindsay+[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir David Lindsay, Lord Edzell and Lady Helen Lindsay
2 CONT *1. David Lindsay of Edzell+[2]
2 CONT *2. Alexander Lindsay+[2]
2 CONT  4.. Helen Lindsay 
2 CONT *3. Margaret Lindsay+[3] d. 9 Jul 1614
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. This is the order of the sons, and the order of the daughters, but some daughters could have been born before the sons . Thus Helen Lindsay is the elder daughter of Sir David Lindsay of Edzell and his wife Lady Helen Lindsay. S
2 CONC he is missing on many family trees. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Helen is recorded as the first daughter of Sir David Lindsay of Edzell in:
