1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Erskine of Balhaggardy must have succeeded before 1615, when Thomas Erskine appears as fiar (p. 418). He was married, in 1604, to Marjory Gordon, daughter of Sir Thomas Gordon of Cluny, and was succeeded by hi
2 CONC s son, Thomas, in 1625. He had other two sons, Alexander and William, the latter of whom was killed at Aberdeen, in 1639 (p. 271). A daughter, Margaret, or Magdalon, married James, fourth son of William Leslie, the fourth of Warde
2 CONC s — ancestor of the Leslies of Tarbet, in Ireland. – (John Davidson 1878, Inverurie and the Earldom of the Garioch)
2 CONT
