1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ELIZABETH LUNDY===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Heiress of Benholm===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''SPURIOS PEDIGREE'''<blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Dr, Robert Lundy Smith identified Elizabeth Lundy, here treated, as the daughter of Robert Lundy of Benholm. [https://www.electricscotland.com/webclans/htol/lundin8.html Lundie of Benholm] This is quite wrong, howev
2 CONC er. She is in fact the daughter and heiress of William Lundy of Benholm. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f30&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n N
2 CONC RS: GD4/30]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Lundy, here treated is the daughter and heiress of William Lundy of Benholm. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f30&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro
2 CONC =s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD4/30] She had a precept of clare constat for her father lands from Chancery on 11 April 1565 and took sasine of the same on 10 May 1565.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?r
2 CONC eference=GD4%2f31&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD4/31]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Lundy married Robert Keith, son of William Keith, the Earl Marshall. On 13 June 1566 she resigned her father's land to the crown in order to obtain a new grant in favour of herself and her husband. [http://catalogue.n
2 CONC rscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f61&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD4/61]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Keith/6000000003221155624?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1578072694098&through=6000000014322088464
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Keith/6000000003221155618?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1578072872239&through=6000000014322088464
2 CONT
2 CONT ===EVIDENCE FROM THE NATIONAL RECORDS OF SCOTLAND===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 February 1559-60: Assignation of the ward and nonentry of the lands of the deceased William Lundy [Lundie] of Benholme [Benholm], and of the marriage of Isabel (or Elizabeth) Lundy [Lundie] his daughter and apparent heir, by 
2 CONC Robert Carnegye [Carnegie] of Kynnarde [Kinnaird] knight to Robert Keycht [Keith] second son of William earl Merschel [Earl Marischal], whom failing, to William Keycht [Keith] second son of William master Marscheall, whom failing,
2 CONC  to George Keycht [Keith] the master's eldest son, whom failing, to any other person whom the earl or his heirs should name. At Benholm. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f30&st=1&t
2 CONC c=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/30]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 May 1565: Sasine to Elizabeth Lundy [Lundie], as heir of William Lundy [Lundie] of Benhom [Benholm] her father, of the Manis of Benhom [Benholm] and others, as in GD4/27. On Chancery Precept of Clare Constat dated 11 April a
2 CONC n.reg.23 (A.D.1565). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f31&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott fam
2 CONC ily of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/31]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 June 1566: Procuratory by Elizabeth Lundy [Lundie] heretrix of Benholme [Benholm], with consent of her spouse Robert Keyth [Keith] son lawful of William earl Merschell [Earl Marischal], and of her curators, for resigning the
2 CONC  lands and Manis of Benholme [Benholm], with the tower and fortalice thereof, Uver and Nether Knox, Inchmadan [Inchmeddan], Tulloch of Benholme [Tully of Benholm], Kyrktoun of Benholme [Kirkton of Benholm], with the mill, and the 
2 CONC lands and barony of Benholme [Benholm], into the hands of Queen Mary in favour of her spouse and herself in conjunct fee. Dated at Aberdeen. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f61&st
2 CONC =1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/61]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 June 1587: Procuratory by Robert Keyth [Keith] of Benholme [Benholm] and Elizabeth Lundy [Lundie] his spouse, for resigning the lands and barony of Benholme, the Mains of Benholme, with tower, fortalice and mills thereof, th
2 CONC e lands of Over and Nether Knokkis [Knox], Kirktoun of Benholme [Kirkton of Benholm], Inschemaden [Inchmeddan] and Tulloch of Benholme [Tully of Benholm], all united into the barony of Benholme [Benholm], into the King's hands for
2 CONC  new infeftment to be given them thereof, together with the patronage of the kirk of Benholme, parsonage and vicarge thereof, then in the King's hands. At Benholme [Benholm]. Signed "R. Keytht [Keith] of Deir [Deer]", And "Isobell
2 CONC  Lundy [Lundie] lady Benholm". [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f69&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the
2 CONC  Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/69]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 Jully 1587: Charter by King James VI granting the barony of Benholme [Benholm], as in GD4/69, to Robert Keyth [Keith] of Benholme [Benholm] and Elizabeth Lundy [Lundie] his spouse; on their own resignation. With a clause of 
2 CONC Novodamus, and annexation of the patronage of the kirk of Benholme [Benholm], parsonage and vicarage thereof, to the barony. Dated 30 July 1587, an.reg.21. (Reg.Mag.Sig. v. 1324). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatal
2 CONC ogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f71&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+lundy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/71
2 CONC ]'''
2 CONT
