1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM WALLACE OF ELDERSLIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie here treated is the son of William Wallace of Elderslie. His father made his last will and testament on 19 March 1599 and, among other legacies, he left to his son William one hundred merks, money w
2 CONC hich the younger William appears to have owed to his father. He also left forty pounds to: "Elizabeth Wallace dochter naturall to Wm Wallace my son and appeirand air." [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=600000007668035554
2 CONC 2& Image of Testament 5] He is not mentioned in the testament dative of  his father's wife,Janet Hamilton, who died in December 1589, but she is certainly known to be the mother of his younger brothers, John Wallace, Gabriel Walla
2 CONC ce, and James Walace, and it is quite likely, probable even, that he is her son. For mention Janet Hamilton's sons see [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076677091347& Image of Testament 1] and [https://www.geni.co
2 CONC m/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076678490910& Image of Testament 3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Testament Dative of Janet Hamilton===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie, together with his sons, John Wallace, Gabriel Wallace, and James Wallace, gave up the testament dative of his deceased wife on 2 May 1590. She died in December 1589.[National Records of Scotland, C
2 CONC ommissary Records of Glasgow, The Testament Dative of umqle Jonet Hammiltoun auld Ladie Elirslie spous to Wm Wallace of Elirslie, reference CC/8/22 pp. 117-19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076677091347& Image of Testament 1]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076679034884& Image of Testament 2]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076678490910& Image of Testament 3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Father's Testament Testamentar===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076681984218& Image of Testament 1] 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076682328893& Image of Testament 2]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076682173019& Image of Testament 3]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076682304828& Image of Testament 4]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076680355542& Image of Testament 5]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076680485439& Image of Testament 6]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076679910290& Image of Testament 7]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076680358224& Image of Testament 8]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie died in July 1623. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, The Testament Dative of umqle Wm Wallace elder of Elderslie, reference CC9/7/20 pp. 585-87]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Testament Dative===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, The Testament Dative of umqle Wm Wallace elder of Elderslie, reference CC9/7/20 pp. 585-87]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076681984218& Image of Testament 1]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076693079076& Image of Testament 2]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076692978867& Image of Testament 3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie was married. The name of his wife is not known but the probability of his marriage is implied by the fact that he had lawfull issue. Moreover, his putative mother is refrerred to as "auld ladie Elir
2 CONC slie" in her testament dative dated 2 May 1590, and this suggests that there was a younger lady Elirslie on this date.  [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, The Testament Dative of umqle Jonet  Hammiltoun 
2 CONC auld Ladie Elirslie spous to Wm Wallace of Elirslie, reference CC/8/22 pp. 117-19]  [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076677091347& Image of Testament 1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Wallace-of-Elderslie-younger/6000000076664610076?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520168558900&through=6000000024527057505
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Wallace/6000000076693522044
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Bastard Child===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Wallace/6000000076663124145?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520168732536&through=6000000024527057505
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 Dece,ber 1589: Letters of charge under the Signet at the instance of Robert, Master of Eglinton charging John Maxwell of Potterhill, William Wallace, younger of Ellerslie and [ ] relict of unquhile Patrick Maxwell of Stanelie
2 CONC  to deliver to Robert , Master of Eglinton the charter of taillie of the lands of Giffen [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f31%2f17&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ellerslie&ko=p
2 CONC &r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/31/17]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 April 1598: Feu Charter by Claud, Lord Paisley, in favour of said Alex. C[unningham]. of C[raigends]. of above subjects. Witnesses (at Paisley), John Whitefurd of that Ilk, William Wallace younger of Johnestoune, William Wal
2 CONC lace younger of Elrislie, etc. Seal. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD148%2f323&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elrislie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of t
2 CONC he Cuninghame Family of Craigends, Renfrewshire, reference GD148/3223]'''
2 CONT
