3 DATE 30 APR 2020
3 TEXT First Name
3 TEXT From The Crawfurd Peerage: With Other Original Genealogical, Historical, and Biographical Particulars Relating to the Illustrious Houses of Crawfurd and Kilbirnie (Google eBook) Andrew Jack & Company, 1829 - 484 pages.  Page 39:
4 CONT
4 CONT "Again to return to Laurence Crawfurd of Kilbirnie, succeeded Hugh his son and heir, who, adhering to the interest of Queen Mary, at the battle of Langside, after her escape from Dumbarton castle, joined her majesty’s troops with 
4 CONC a number of his vassals, for which offence he took remission from the regent, the Earl of Lennox, in the year 1571.
4 CONT
4 CONT "He was twice married, first with Margaret, daughter of Sir John Colquhoun of Luss ;
4 CONT
4 CONT and afterwards he espoused Elizabeth, daughter of David Barclay of'Ladyland ; by the first he had Malcolm, his son and heir;
4 CONT
4 CONT and of the last he had William, ancestor of that branch of the Crawfurds of Knightswood.
4 CONT
4 CONT He had, moreover, four daughters, viz.
4 CONT
4 CONT Marion, married to John Boyle of Kelburn, of whom the Earl of Glasgow is lineally descended;
4 CONT Margaret, to James Galbraith of Kilcroick, an ancient family in Stirlingshire; [Margaret married 2nd to Sir Aulay MacAulay of Ardencaple]
4 CONT Catherine, to William Wallace of Elderslee;
4 CONT Elizabeth, to David Brady of Castleton in Clackmannanshire.
4 CONT He deceased in the year 1576, and had for his successor Malcolm, his son and heir, who wedded Margaret, daughter of John Cunningham of Glengarnock, ...."
4 CONT
4 CONT Citations
4 CONT
4 CONT The Crawfords of Donegal and How They Came There, by Robert Crawford MA Publication: University Press, Dublin. 1897
4 CONT www.stirnet.com
