2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 June 1605: Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands of Lempetstane in the barony of Renfrew to James Wallace of Mureheid and his wife Elizabeth Wallace. James is identified as the lawful
2 CONC  son of the deceased William Wallace of Elderslie. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi06scot#page/589/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1593-1608, charter number 1623 on p. 589]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1612: Charter by which the King's Administrator confirms that he has granted possession of the lands of Lepetstane alias Ovir Leichland toJames Wallace and his wife Elizabeth Wallace. James is identified as the lawful s
2 CONC on of the deceased William Wallace of Elderslie. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/271 Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1609-1620, charter number 727 o
2 CONC n p. 271]'''
