2 CONT
2 CONT ===Her Father's Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie made his last will and testament on 19 March 1599. He nominated his sons John Wallace, Gabriel Wallace, and James Wallace, to be his executors. He also nominated the following people to be oversmen:
2 CONC  John Wallace elder of Craigie, John Wallace, younger of Craigie, together with William Wallace of Johnston, and John Wallace in Monktonhill "my brothers germane" and Allan Hamilton of Ferguslie "my sone in law." Among the legacie
2 CONC s he left was two hundred merks to "Jonet Wallace my dochter lawll spous to Alla[n] Hamiltoun of Ferguslie" together with four hundred pounds which was owed to him by Allan. He also left forty pounds to Elizabeth Wallace "dochter 
2 CONC naturall to Wm Wallace my son and appeirand air." He also left one hundred merks to his son William, money which William owed to his father. He also forgave his brother David Wallace of "all soumes of money & debts awin be him to 
2 CONC me."
2 CONT
