1 NAME Robert /Graham of Gartmore/
2 GIVN Robert
2 SURN Graham of Gartmore
2 _MARNM Graham of Gartmore
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 20 FEB 1573 AND 27 SEP 1574
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ROBERT GRAHAM OF GARTMORE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Graham,, here treated: "who, in 1547, was infeft in the lands of Wester Boquhapple by his brother, Earl John, but he sold these lands in 1553 to his brother-in-law, Archibald, Earl of Argyll, and his wife and son. In May
2 CONC  1547 he acquired part of Gartmore, and in 1554 he had a charter from Walter M'Awlay of Gartmore, granting the twelve-merk land of Gartmore to Robert Graham, brother-german of John, Earl of Menteith, whom failing, to Gilbert Graha
2 CONC m, his brother, a grant which was repeated in 1563 and 1568 to Robert and his wife and to Gilbert, his brother. Robert, being 'sumquhat evill disposit' made his will at Stirling 20 February 1572-73, and died not long afterwards, w
2 CONC ithout male issue by his wife, Elizabeth Erskine, a natural daughter of Thomas, Master of Erskine, to whom he was married in terms of a contract dated 29 January 1562-63. She survived him, and was still alive in 1577-78. Robert Gr
2 CONC aham had at least one lawful daughter, Margaret, named in his will. She died in August 1573. He had also a natural son John and a natural daughter Christian, both referred to in his will. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragef
2 CONC oun06pauluoft/page/157/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: pp. 157-8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 27 September 1574. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Robert Grahame of Gartmoir, reference CC8/8/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 January 1552: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/187/mode/1up RMS 1546-1580: charter number 834]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 August 1553: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/187/mode/1up RMS 1546-1580: charter number 834]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 May 1554: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/220/mode/1up RMS 1546-1580: charter number 978]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 January 1554-55:  [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/220/mode/1up RMS 1546-1580: charter number 978]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 April 1568: Precept of Sasine in favour of Robert Grahame [Graham] of Gartmoir [Gartmore] and Elizabeth Erskin [Erskine], his spouse, of the lands of Gartmoir and the pendicle called Bad, to be held in conjunct fee, 2 April 1
2 CONC 568. [Fragment of seal attached]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD22%2f1%2f458&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Robert+Graham+of+Gartmoir&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of 
2 CONC Scotland, Papers of the Cunninghame Graham Family of Ardoch, Dunbartonshire, reference GD22/1/458]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 April 1568: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/459/mode/1up RMS 1546-1580: charter number 1815]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 June 1568: Instrument of Sasine following upon the above mentioned precept, dated 2 June 1568. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD22%2f1%2f458&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Robert+Gra
2 CONC ham+of+Gartmoir&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cunninghame Graham Family of Ardoch, Dunbartonshire, reference GD22/1/458]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 June 1577: Extract special retour in sheriff court of Perth before John Peibles [Peebles], burgess of Perth, sheriff depute of Sir William, Lord Ruthven, sheriff principal, of William Graham of Gartaverten [Gartartan] as hei
2 CONC r to deceased Robert Graham of Gartmoir [Gartmore], HIS FATHER [Note], who died in May 1572, in 12 merkland of Gartmoir, with a pendicle called the Baid [Baad], in stewartry of Menteith, reserving liferent to Elizabeth Erskin [Ers
2 CONC kine], relict of said Robert. Notary: James Drummond, sheriff clerk. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD22%2f3%2f501&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Robert+Graham+of+Gartmoir&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df
2 CONC =&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cunninghame Graham Family of Ardoch, Dunbartonshire, reference GD22/3/501]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: Robert Graham of Gartmore was actually the uncle of William Graham of Gartaverten.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 August 1588: Instrument of Sasine following on a Precept by James, Earl of Gowrie, Lord Ruythvene [Ruthven], in favour of William Grahame as heir to his uncle, Robert Grahame of Gartmoir, in the 12 merkland of Gartmoir, 5 Aug
2 CONC ust 1588. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD22%2f1%2f458&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Robert+Graham+of+Gartmoir&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the 
2 CONC Cunninghame Graham Family of Ardoch, Dunbartonshire, reference GD22/1/458]'''
