1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===DAME ELIZABETH MAKGILL (aka ELIZABETH M'GILL) Lady Culzean===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Her Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Elizabeth Makgill made her last will and testament at the Coiff on 26 December 1621. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar of Dame Elizabeth McGill, lady Culzeane, parish of Kirkosu
2 CONC all, reference CC9/7/18 pp. 499-504]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Elizabeth Makgill, lady Culzean, died in January 1622. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar of Dame Elizabeth McGill, lady Culzeane, parish of Kirkosuall, reference CC9/7/18 pp. 49
2 CONC 9-504]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Elizabeth Makgill married Robert Logan of Restalrig. They were married before November 1576 but they must have divorced before 16 March 1579, when she was living in her father's household.  [https://archive.org/stream/scot
2 CONC speeragefoun02paul#page/486/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 486]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Child of the First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Logan/6000000000405410636?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1532090490235&through=6000000001213824348
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Elizabeth Makgill married Sir Thomas Kennedy of Culzean. They were married between 16 March and 28 April 1579. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/486/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 486]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of the Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Kennedy-of-Culzean/6000000080409714057?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1532098880052&through=6000000001213824348
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Kennedy-of-Culzean-and-Blairquhan/6000000001213920385?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1532099004265&through=6000000001213824348
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Alexander-Kennedy-of-Craignoch/6000000000884577324?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1532099296171&through=6000000001213824348
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/David-Kennedy/6000000001213868414?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1532099507004&through=6000000001213824348
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Helen-Kennedy/6000000008049489737?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1532099549499&through=6000000001213824348
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Kennedy/6000000015208847415
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Kennedy/6000000015208847415?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1532099940074&through=6000000001213824348
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Third Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Elizabeth Makgill married Sir William Mure of Rowallan. They were married before 7 September 1605. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f9%2f73&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Eliz
2 CONC abeth+Makgill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1600&di=y NRS: GD25/9/73]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 February 1580: Contract between Thomas Kennedy of Culean Tutor of Cassillis and Elizabeth Makgill his wife on the one part, and George Lockhart burgess of Ayr on the other part bearing that the said George Lockhart shall inf
2 CONC eft the said Thomas Kennedy and his wife their heirs and assignees in the 40 shilling land of Glenalloway and 40 shilling land of Auchaltan lying contiguous, within the Earldom of Carrick but redeemable upon the said George Lockha
2 CONC rt making payment to them within the Church of Mayboll of the sum of 2000 merks money of this Realm, and they on the other hand to grant a Letter of Reversion declaring the same redeemable upon payment of the said sum. As also to 
2 CONC grant a Letter of Assedation of the said lands of Glenalloway and Auchaltan to the said Geo. Lockhart during the not redemption for payment yearly of 200 merks at the terms of Whitsunday and Martinmas by equal portions. Witnesses 
2 CONC Mr David Makgill of Nisbet Advocate, Robert Cathcart his servant and Gilbert Kennedy servant to the Tutor of Cassillis. Dated at Edinburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f8
2 CONC 76&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+makgill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/876]'''
2 CONT
