2 CONT
2 CONT '''c. 1652: Discharge at the desire of Sir Alexander Kennedy of Culzeane, Kt, by James Craufurd goldsmith in Edinburgh as assignay named on the advice of deceased Dame Elizabeth Makgill, Lady Culzean, to decreets of 4 February 159
2 CONC 7-8 and 21 July 1598 against umquhile Thomas Kennedy, brother to Hew Kennedy of Bennan, for spoliation committed against umquhile Richard Makgill, sometime in Ferdinrioche and umquhile Uthrid Makgill, his brother, to [blank] Kenne
2 CONC dy, son to said umquhile Hew Kennedy of Bennan. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD60%2f57&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+makgill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Sco
2 CONC tland, Papers of the Family of Bennan and Finnarts, reference GD60/57]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/486/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, etc., Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms, Volume II (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1905), pp. 486-88 for the family of Eli
2 CONC zabeth Makgill and Thomas Kennedy of Culzean] 
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/historieanddesc00muirgoog#page/n7/mode/1up The Historie and Descent of the House of Rowallane by Sir William Mure, Knight, of Rowallane.Written in or prior to 1657 (Chalmers and Collins, Glasgow, 1825
2 CONC ), 141 pp.]
2 CONT # [http://www.electricscotland.com/history/nation/mure.htm Electric Scotland: Mure]
2 CONT # [http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I2038&tree=CC Clan MacFarlane and associated clans genealogy]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes and Comments===
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I2038&tree=CC
2 CONT
2 CONT We know the father married first in 1576 to''' Elizabeth McGill, they divorced in 1577/78.''' Then we have a blank period of 8 or 9 years until Logan marries (Jonet Ker) in 1586. Logan Home places the births of George and John as 
2 CONC 1587 and 1588, respectively. This wife, Jonet, is apparently mother also to Alexander (1590) and Jonet (bef 1596). Jonet Ker dies in 1596, and it is her tombstone that still exists in the St. Triduana Chapel in Edinburgh (a pictur
2 CONC e of her stone is on my web page: http://www.cyberramp.net/'rscmf/Triduana.htm>)
2 CONT
2 CONT Logan is said to have then married Marion Ker (relation to wife Jonet, unknown) who lived to be his widow and was mother to Anna (her birth would be between 1597-1606). I think Logan Home is missing a wife in there. If George and 
2 CONC John were not minors in 1600, this would place their births before 1587 and 1588; probably more like 1580 and 1581.
2 CONT
2 CONT As John married before 1606, I think my hypothesis is the correct one. If Logan Home is correct, John would have been 16 or 17 at the time of his marriage. This is unheard of back then. The average age for a man of wealth to first
2 CONC  marry was about 26, the girls first married around 20 or 21 years of age. If John were born about 1581, he would have been 25 at the birth of his first child; this is more likely the case.
2 CONT
2 CONT Since John's first child was born in May 1606, this is prior to the death of his father and the forfeiture, therefore eliminating the need for John to marry as a teenager.
2 CONT
2 CONT I discuss this in depth because this is the critical information needed if you are to trace your tree back to the last Laird. I hope you are all still with me at this point . The crux of it is that these kids need sorted out if an
2 CONC y of us are going to be able to connect to the Last Laird.
2 CONT
2 CONT That said, I'll repeat my family history for you: my line supposedly ...descends from the eldest son of the last laird...- this should be Robert (B. 1577) unless there was an illegitimate son and my family historian conveniently f
2 CONC orgot to mention that part. I have proof of my Logan line back to a marriage that took place in Aberdeen, SCT in 1635 between John Logan and Margaret Wat.
2 CONT
2 CONT  So obviously I have a gap and have been unable to prove John's parentage. Since I am stuck in trying to move backwards, I have spent years trying to move the last Laird's children forward, hoping my gamble would pay off. Since th
2 CONC e eldest two wandered off from Edinburgh it has been very difficult. But I think this is a very important part of the puzzle. One son quite possibly could have wandered off to Ireland......... Regards, Stephanie Plano, TX USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/mm4ae/makgill01.php#linklo Notes from www.stirnet: Makgill 01]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Makgill (d 05.1622) m1. (before 1576, div by 03.1578) Robert Logan of Restalrig (b 1555, d 07.1606) m2. (1578-9) SIr Thomas Kennedy, 1st of Culzean (d 11.05.1602) m3. (mcrt 04.04.1605) William Mure of Rowallan
2 CONT
