1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ALEXANDER FORRESTER OF GARDEN, who was under age at his father’s death  and had Sasine for the lands of Torwood as his heir on 9 May 1549,4 with Sir  John Bellenden of Auchenoule and James Sandilands of Cruvy being
2 CONC  appointed  his Tutors during his minority. He was served heir to his father in the barony of  Garden on 31 May 1575 and
2 CONT
2 CONT  m. Jean, daughter of John Erskine of Dun. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He d. by April of 1602 and was father of :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. James Forrester of Garden 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. John Forrester
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Alexander Forrester, was appointed Tutor to his nephew David Forrester of  Little Denovan, on 15 February 1609.4
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Duncan Forrester, was a substitute heir to Robert Forrester of Boquhan in the  lands of Easter Row on 26 December 1599 and, as heir of whom, he had Sasine  for lands in and around the Burgh of Stirling on 5 April 1602
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Archibald Forrester, who is named with his brother John Forrester of Little  Denovan in their resignation of their 8 acres of the lands of Auld Muir in  favour of their brother Mr. Duncan, on 9 May 1608.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Thomas Forrester, renounced a yard in the burgh of Stirling to his brother Mr  Duncan Forrester for which he took instruments on 11 October 1609, and is  then styled brother german to Sir James Forrester of Garden.2 He was  app
2 CONC ointed Commendator of Holyrood on 11 June 1617.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Barbara Forrester, m. David Livingstone, younger of Dunipace.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Elizabeth Forrester, m. Alexander Menzies of Weem, (c/m 23 March 1598. He  was widow of Margaret, daughter of Sir Duncan Campbell, 7th of Glenorchy,  whom he had m. by c/m 10 December 1588, and after Elizabeth Forrester’s  deat
2 CONC h, he m. thirdly, to Marjory, daughter of Alexander Campbell, Bishop of  Brechin, by c/m 20 March 1604).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.highlandtitles.com/blog/torwood-castle/
