2 CONT >>(2) Margaret married William Congleton, son of William Congleton above mentioned, by his first wife, Mary, daughter of John, lord Yester.
2 CONT >>[Note. — Mrs. Gumming Bruce states that the first Alexander of Bangour was succeeded by his son Patrick, whose grandson, Robert Bruce, married Janet, daughter of Sir Jolin Lauder of Fountainhall, Bart., but from reference to App
2 CONC endix, p. xlvii., it is clear that the the first Alexander was succeeded by his son Alexander. No more is known of this branch.]
2 CONT
2 CONT >5. '''Robert had from his father " the chaplanrie of our Ladie aisle founded and situated on the south side of the Kirk of Airth," 30 October 1572 ;he is executor to both his father and mother's wills and mentioned therein as the
2 CONC ir youngest son, he is also stated to have had from his father " the lands of Garwell ; this is an instance, not uncommon in those days, of two sons of the same parents bearing the same christian name. In 1638 an Alexander Bruce o
2 CONC f Garwald is retoured heir to Robert Bruce of Garwald, his fatherj'''
2 CONT >6.Marion, married William Menteith of Kerse. Marriage contract dated 13th May 1557.
2 CONT >7.The other  daughter died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT
