1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==[https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n52/mode/1up?view=theater The Bruces of Airth and their cadets by Armstrong, William Bruce p 16-17etc]
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander succeeded his father ante 8 March 1552, as at that date he was enfefted ^ as " son of the deceased Robert Brus of Erth," in the lands of Erth held of Holyrood.  By Janet Livingston, Sir Alexander Bruce had issue five son
2 CONC s and two daughters, viz. : 
2 CONT
2 CONT >1. William, died during his father's lifetime, of whom presently.
2 CONT >2. Robert of Kinnaird, of whom presently. 
2 CONT >3. Sir John of Kincavel was captain of Stirling Castle 1585, had a charter from his father of West Bordland in Denny, and is mentioned in several transactions f her died lSQ7i.having married Jean," eldest daughter of Sir Robert D
2 CONC rummond, third of Medhope ; she is mentioned '"as " Dame Jeane Drummond, lady Kincavel " in her daughter's marriage settlement, 1638 ; by her Sir John had issue five sons and two daughters, viz. : —
2 CONT
2 CONT >>(1) Sir Alexander of Kincavel
2 CONT >>(2) William," succeeded to Kincavel and had a daughter Grizzel,'^ who married Gavin, second son of Gavin Hamilton of Raploch, 1666.
2 CONT >>(3) Robert, Minister of Aberdour, he was a great traveller in Palestine, etc., he is mentioned in many transactions and had succeeded to Kincavel in 1652,' for he is then styled " of Kincavel." He is guardian to his niece Grizze
2 CONC l in IGGG, and is again styled^ " of Kincavel " on that occasion. He is also mentioned in his sister Margaret's marriage contract. Robert married Janet Watson,^ relict of Mr. Andrew Aytoun ; they liad children,^ but there is no fu
2 CONC rther record of them.
2 CONT >>(4) Walter, minister of Inverkeithing,^ was guardian to his niece Grizzel, 1G52, is mentioned in his sister's mariage contract and in many other '^ transactions ; he married Jean,' daughter of Alexander Menzies of Rotenell, and 
2 CONC was dead* in 1674, when Jean is called his relict.
2 CONT >>(5) John of Wrae," procurator to his sister Anna, 1643, he had two daughters,^" heir-portioners of their father, Jean and Marion.
2 CONT >>(6) Margaret married/^ October 1638, Sir John Stirling of Garden, Knight.
2 CONT >>(7) Anna married James Bruce of Powfoullis.
2 CONT >>[Note. — Nothing more is known of tlie Braces of Kincavel.]
2 CONT
2 CONT >4.Sir Alexander of Bangour,- mentioned as " fourth son of Sir Alexander Bruce of Airth," 1588. He is mentioned," 5 September 1597, as having been " son lawful of Sir Alexander Bruce of Airth," and being then deceased. He married 
2 CONC Helen Hamilton,^* [who re-married William Congleton of that Ilk as his second wife], and had issue one son and oin daughter, viz. ; —
2 CONT
2 CONT >>(1) Alexander of Bangour, is enfefted* as heir of Alexander Bruce of Baugour in 6 oxgates of land of Hill of Airth, 10 July 1609. He resigns^ his land of Hill of Airth in favour of Sir John Bruce of Airth, 21 June 1617.
2 CONT ander Bruce of Baugour in 6 oxgates of land of Hill of Airth, 10 July 1609. He resigns his land of Hill of Airth in favour of Sir John Bruce of Airth, 21 June 1617. (2) Margaret/ married William Congleton, son of William Congleton
2 CONC  above mentioned, by his first wife, Mary, daughter of John, lord Yester.
2 CONT >>[Note. — Mrs. Gumming Bruce states that the first Alexander of Bangour was succeeded by his son Patrick, whose grandson, Robert Bruce, married Janet, daughter of Sir Jolin Lauder of Fountainhall, Bart., but from reference to App
2 CONC endix, p. xlvii., it is clear that the the first Alexander was succeeded by his son Alexander. No more is known of this branch.]
2 CONT
2 CONT >5. Robert had from his father " the eliaplanrie of our Ladie aisle founded and situated on the south side of the Kirk of Airth," 30 October 1572 ;he is executor to both his father and mother's wills and mentioned therein as their
2 CONC  youngest son, he is also stated to have had from his father " the lands of Garwell ; this ia au instance, not uncommon in those days, of two sons of the same parents bearing the same christian name. In 1638 au Alexander Bruce of 
2 CONC Garwald is retoured heir to Robert Bruce of Garwald, his fatherj
2 CONT >6.'''Marion, married William Menteith of Kerse. Marriage contract dated 13th May 1557.'''
2 CONT >7.The other  daughter died young.
