2 CONT
2 CONT III. Sir JOHN BALLENDEN of Auchinoule, who had his father's office of lord-justice-clerk conferred upon him,* which he enjoyed above 20 years, in the reigns of queen Mary and king James VI. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, 2dly, Janet daughter of— Seton of Touch,* and got two charters, un∣der the great seal, to him, and Janet Seton his spouse, dated anno 1574.
2 CONT
2 CONT By her he had issue three daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Elizabeth, married,* 1st, to sir James Lawson of Humbie; 2dly, to sir John Cock∣burn of Ormistoun, lord-justice-clerk.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. '''Margaret,* married to William Stewart writer in Edinburgh''', and was mother of sir Lewis Stewart of Kirkhill.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Marion, married to John Ramsay of Dalhousie.
2 CONT
