1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===THOMAS BELLENDEN OF STENNESS===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Bellenden of Stenness is the eldest son and apparent heir of Sir Patrick Bellenden of Stenness and his wife Katherine Kennedy. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/64/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 264
2 CONC ] The date of his birth is not known, although he was not one of the heirs who are named in the charter which confirmed his father's possession of certain lands in Orkney. Presumably, therefore, he was born after this charter was 
2 CONC issued on 30 June 1564.  [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi04scot#page/418/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1546-1580, charter number 1710 on pp. 418-19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Bellenden of Stenness was alive on 12 October 1591  [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi05scot#page/752/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1580-1593, charter number 2191 on p. 752] but he is no
2 CONC t mentioned in his father's last will and testament dated 18 January 1607 and may have predeceased him. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Edinburgh, reference CC8/8/43 pp. 662-66] He certainly died before 5 July
2 CONC  1610, the date upon which his younger brother Adam was served heir to his deceased father. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM
2 CONC 1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=snippet&q=bellenden&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc., ii, p. 70]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 October 1591: Instrument of Sasine in favour of James Feaw in Clastrane, of the 6d. land of Clastrane and St. Margarets Quoy, in island of Stronsay; on (1) quitclaim and renunciation, dated 16 October 1591, subscribed by Tho
2 CONC mas Auchinlek, servant to Robert Earl of Orkney, as principal, and by Hew Gordoun of Bellinlone, '''Thomas Bellenden, apparent heir of Evie,''' and Patrick Gordoun as witnesses; and (2) precept of sasine, dated 12 October 1591, by
2 CONC  said Robert, Earl of Orkney; and upon infeftment said James Feaw gave sasine to Margaret Grott, his spouse, of the liferent of said lands. Witnesses to the Sasine: Malcolm Grott of Tankerness, Mr. James Maxvell, vicar of Stronsay
2 CONC , James Scolaw, eldest son to David Scolaw of Tofts, Olaw Scott, James Maxvell, son to said Mr. James Maxvell, William Maxvell, Alexander Dunbar, Magnus Feaw and Thomas Garioch. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalog
2 CONC ue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+Bellenden&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/4]'''
2 CONT
