1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ADAM BELLENDEN OF STENNESS elder===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Adam Bellenden of Stenness is the son of Sir Patrick Bellenden of Stenness and his wife Catherine Kennedy (aka Katherine Kennedy). [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/64/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 264] T
2 CONC he date and place of his birth is not known. However, his father and mother were married before 23 March 1567-68, and there is good reason for supposing that he was born after this date. [https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofs
2 CONC c27scot#page/287/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, pp. 287-88] He was served heir to his deceased father on 5 July 1610. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=q
2 CONC kxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=snippet&q=bellenden&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc., ii, p. 70]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Suit of Court===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Adam Bellenden of Stenness was one of the suitors of court for Stenness and Evie in 1617 [https://archive.org/stream/publicationsofsc27scot#page/401/mode/1up Records of the Earldom of Orkney, p. 401]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Father's Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' Sir Patrik Bellenden of Evie made his last will and testament on 18 June 1607, at his house in the Canongate near Edinburgh. The witnesses present were James Bannatyne, Patrick Wilsoun, minister, Matthew Locke, burgess of Edin
2 CONC burgh, and his son Adam Bellenden. He left his soul to God and his body to be buried in: "the Abbay kirk of Halyruidhous" and nominated and constituted his wife Kathrein Wilsoun to be his only executor and intomitter with his good
2 CONC s and gear. He left a number of small legacies, including twenty merks for the poor at his burial, one hundred merks to his daughter Margaret Bellenden, one hundred merks to Margaret Bannatyne, daughter to Robert Bannatyne, one hu
2 CONC ndred merks to his daughter Margaret Bellenden: "procreat betwix him and the said Kathrein Wilsoun. He also left an annuity to his mother-in-law Eupham Johnnestoun. Confirmation was granted to Kathrein Wilsoun on 21 July 1607. [Na
2 CONC tional Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Sir Patrik Bellenden of Evie, knight, in the Canongate, reference CC8/8/43]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000145333202908 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000145333334838 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000145333348821 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000145333022835 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000145332246901 Image of Testament]
2 CONT
