2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 April 1611: Supplication by John Maxwell, servitor to the Earl of Orkney, as follows: - On .......... March last Adam Bellindane of Stanehouse assaulted him on the lands of .......... in Orkney and pursued him with a "drawin
2 CONC  quhinger or dagger" and wounded him in the arm. He craves a summons against him. [on the back] "Apud Edinburgh, ultimo Aprillis, 1611. Fiate ut petitur. (Signed) S. R. Cockburne." [https://archive.org/stream/registerprivyco04coun
2 CONC goog#page/n345/mode/1up The Register of the Privy Council of Scotland, Second Series. Vol. VIII. A.D. 1544-1560, p. 323]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 June 1636: Fragment of a summons at the instance of his Majesty's Advocate and William Sinclair of Saba against Harry Stuart of Grinsay and others, to compear before the Council on 28th July next; and also against the follow
2 CONC ing as witnesses, Thomas Bawhanane, sheriff depute of Orkney, William Stewart of Maynes, Patrick McDowgall, his servitor, George Smyth, servitor to the said sheriff depute, Patrick Smyth of Braco, Robert Ballendene, servitor to Ad
2 CONC am Ballendene, elder of Stamhous, John Cromertie of Ske, Patrick Kincaid, and Henry Aitkine; dated at Edinburgh, 11th June, 1636, and signed Ja. Prymrois. [https://archive.org/stream/registerprivyco02coungoog#page/n639/mode/1up Th
2 CONC e Register of the Privy Council of Scotland, Second Series. Vol. VI. A.D. 1635-1637, p. 585]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 August 1637:  Supplication by William Sinclair of Saba, as follows: - Their Lordships have appointed William Stewart of Maynes and Patrick Smith of Brako to shear, lead and sequestrate the corns growing upon his lands of Over
2 CONC  Sandie for this present crop, but these gentlemen, for some special considerations, refuse to undertake the charge. He therefore craves that their Lordships would add to the commissioners for this purpose Adam Bannatyne, elder an
2 CONC d younger of Stennes, and Thomas Buchanan, sheriff depute of Orkney. The Lords, after advising, adjoin the said Thomas Buchanan to the said commission, and ordain him and the first two appointed commissioners, jointly and severall
2 CONC y, to shear, lead and sequestrate the said corns and stack them in some neutral place; prohibiting all person from hindering them herein, and commanding the lieges to assist the commissioners with their work. [https://archive.org/
2 CONC stream/registerprivyco02coungoog#page/n560/mode/1up The Register of the Privy Council of Scotland, Second Series. Vol. VI. A.D. 1635-1637, p. 506]'''
2 CONT
