2 CONT
2 CONT ===Monumental Inscription===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In loving memory of JAMES JOHNSTON of Coubister born 26 March 1798 died 10 Feb 1887 aged 89 and his 4th son WILLIAM PETRIE COUPER JOHNSTON born 28 May 1851 died and buried at Rangoon 3 June 1889 aged 38 and of his second son JO
2 CONC HN NUGENT JOHNSTON born 5th May 1884 died 10th Nov 1901 at Liscard, Cheshire and buried there aged 53 years and of his widow MARGARET OMAND ROBERTSON born 18th Feb 1819 died 4th March 1903 aged 84 years. Also in memory of his ance
2 CONC stors mostly buried here WILLIAM HALCRO of Aikers and Cava, Dean of Orkney and Provost of the cathedral, married MARGARET BRUCE died 1597. Their son ROBERT HALCRO of Cava and Houton, married 1st MARGARET IRELAND 2nd JEAN SCOLLAY a
2 CONC nd 3rd  ISOBEL BALLENDEN died about 1640, his son, by JEAN SCOLLAY, EDWARD HALCRO of Houton, married MARGARET HACRO died about 1657. Their son ROBERT HALCRO of Houton married ELIZABETH BEATTON died about 1696. Their son WILLIAM HA
2 CONC LCRO of Coubister and Cava, Gyre and Swanbister married 1726 MARGARET HONEYMAN died 1768. Their son HUGH HALCRO of Coubister and C Surgeon born 1732 married JEAN WARNING of Jamica and died there 1770. Their only son WILLIAM HALCRO
2 CONC  of Coubister and C born 1758 drowned at sea 1784. MARGARET HALCRO of Coubister, Cava and Gyre eldest, sister of HUGH HALCRO, born 1728 died 1811 married 1749 JOSHUA JOHNSTON, Writer, Stromness born 1720 died 1794 and buried here 
2 CONC and their son JOHN JOHNSTON of Coubister and C born 1760 died 1820 married 1788 JANE HARRIS TAYLOR of Quebec born 1773 died 1857 [Orkney Family History Society: Monumental Inscriptions at St. Nicholas's Kirkyard in Orphir, inscrip
2 CONC tion number 1/12/26]'''
