1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ISOBEL HAMILTON (aka ISSOBELLE HAMMILTOUN) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Isobel Hamilton is the daughter of Robert Hamilton of Inchmachan and his wife Margaret Bellenden. [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/432/mode/1up Hamilton Memoirs, p. 432]  [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/da
2 CONC ta/british/hh4aa/hamilton35.php Stirnet: Hamilton 35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Isobel Hamilton married Robert Stewart of Culbeg. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi07scot#page/217/mode/1up RMS: 1609-20, charter 582 on p. 217]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Stewart-of-Culbeg/6000000077015408050?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521817023988&through=6000000077015360278 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It cannot be regarded as certain but it seems quite likely, probable even, that Isobel Hamilton is also the mother of Captain James Stewart, and the Reverend Walter Stewar of Masatter:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/James-Stewart/6000000077102592324?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521817262413&through=6000000077015360278 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Walter-Stewart-of-Massater/6000000034605530863?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521908475505&through=6000000077015408050 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 November 1611: Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that Issobelle Hammiltoun, the wife of Robert Steuart of Culbeg, has quitclaimed her liferent interest in the lands of Nether Culbeg. Likewise, the King confi
2 CONC rms that Robert Steuart of Culbeg has given the five merk lands of Culbeg in the sheriffdom of Stirling to his eldest son Robert Steuart, procreated between him and Isobelle. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi07scot#page
2 CONC /217/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1609-1620, charter number 582 on page 217]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 February 1623: A charter by which Robert Steuart of Culbeg confirms that he has given the lands of Culbeg and others in the sheriffdom of Stirling to his future wife, Annabellam Erskene, for her lifetime. The charter was iss
2 CONC ued in fufillment of a marriage contract between Robert Steuart of Culbeg, who had the consent of his mother Isobelle Hammiltoun, and John, Lord Erskene and his natural daughter Annabellam Erskene. Because his mother held the land
2 CONC s of Nether Culbeg for her lifetime he also gave the lands of Dalbrene to his future wife in compensation. For greater security Annabellam Erskene obtained a charter of confirmation under the great seal of Scotland on 23 April 162
2 CONC 3. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi08scot#page/157/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1620-1623, charter number 452 on page 157]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 June 1626: Complaint by Sir Thomas Hoip of Craighall, knight, baronet, King's Advocate, and Captain James Stewart, son to the late Robert Stewart of Culbeg [https://archive.org/stream/registerprivyco03coungoog#page/n399/mode
2 CONC /1up Register of the Privy Council of Scotland, Second Series, VOL. II., A.D. 1627-1628, page 339]'''
2 CONT
