2 CONT '''10 July 1621: Extract registered bond by David Barclay of Ladyland and his cautioners to Robert Hamilton, son to James Hamilton of Kirktounholme being in life and failing of him by decease to John Hamilton [Note], his father fo
2 CONC r 2000 merks and during the non-payment to infeft them in the above order in an annualrent of 200 merks to be uplifted furth yearly of his 20 merk land of Ladyland lying in the sheriffdom of Ayr within the bailliary of Cunningham,
2 CONC  redeemable always on payment of the said principal sum. Dated at Glasgow and Ladyland and Recorded in the Books of Council and Session, 21st June 1623. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?referenc
2 CONC e=GD3%2f1%2f3%2f25%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=kirktounholme&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/3/25/1]'''
