2 CONT ===Writer in Edinburgh===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Craig, here treated, is the brother of Thomas Craig of Riccartoun, formerly Mr. Thomas Craig, advocate. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD172%2f1415&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&
2 CONC k=robert+craig&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1610&di=y NRS: GD172/1415]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Craig, writer in Edinburgh, died on 13 August 1607. [NRS: CC8/8/44]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Last Will and Testament ===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Craig made his last will and testament at Edinburgh on 30 July 1607. 
2 CONT
2 CONT . . . . . ffollowes the provisioun of my bairinis being thrie in number on lyffe . . . . . ffirst as to the provision of my dochtir Margaret gottin of the first marriage . . . . . I leif hir . . . . . sevin thousand mks . . . . . 
2 CONC ffolwes the provisioun of George and Rot Craiges my twa sonnes gottin of the second marriage wt umqle Margaret
2 CONT
2 CONT Confirmation was granted on 5 December 1608. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Robert Craig, writer, lawful brother to Mr. Thomas C., advocate before the Lords of
2 CONC  Session, reference CC8/8/44]'''
2 CONT
