2 DATE AFT 1566
1 TITL Lady
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY HELEN OGILVY ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05paul/page/6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage V: 6]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT James Stewart, 5th Lord of Innermeath (son of John Stewart 1517-1570 &  Elizabeth Bethune 1518-1567)  married Helen Ogilvy, daughter of James Ogilvy, 4th Lord Ogilvy, Lord Airlie and Elinor Sinclair, before 7 July 1554.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT * 1. JOHN, who succeeded.  
2 CONT * 2. Robert.
2 CONT * 3. James, 'at the horn' 1591.1. Married Margaret Maule.
2 CONT *4. William, of Logierait.2
2 CONT * 5. Mr. Patrick. As brother to John, Lord Innermeath  he is witness of a bond 26 August 1594.3 He was afterwards parson of Muckersy, and was, before 14November 1599, excommunicated by the Presbytery for papistry.4. One of these b
2 CONC rothers was father of Bernard Stewart, styled * brother's son of umquhil John, Lord Innermeith,' who is mentioned in 1617 along with Archibald his son.5
2 CONT * 6. Margaret, with her sisters, was executrix to her father. She was married, contract 11, 12, and 25 January 1595-96,6 to Sir Robert Orichton of Oluny.
2 CONT * 7. Beatrix, executrix to her father.
2 CONT * 8. Grizel, executrix to her father.
2 CONT * 9. Helen, married, contract 22 September 1578,7 to Walter Ogilvy of Oarnowseis.
2 CONT * 10. Elisabeth, married, contract 4 October 1580, to David Gardin of that Ilk.8
2 CONT * 11. Jean, married, contract 10 October 1591, to Walter  of Pitmadie, tutor of Duncrub, styled later Sir Walter Rollok of Gardin;9 secondly, to Sir Alexander Jardine of Applegarth.10
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *< [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage, Page 6] >
2 CONT * < [http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2226.htm#i66882 Our Royal Ancestors] > cites 
