1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From the Peerage page on Agnes Bethune:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p17478.htm#i174771
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Bethune [1]
2 CONT *F, #174771, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1540, 
2 CONT *d. after 1600
2 CONT *Last Edited=30 Mar 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Bethune was born illegitimately circa 1540.[2],[1] She was the daughter of Cardinal David Bethune and Marion Ogilvy.[2],[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, firstly, James Auchterlonie of Auchterlonie.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Sir Alexander Gordon, 3rd of Gight circa 1562.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, thirdly, Sir Patrick Gordon of Auchindoun after 1580.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died after 1600.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her married name became Auchterlonie.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was also known as Agnes Betoun.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From circa 1562, her married name became Gordon.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Agnes Bethune and Sir Alexander Gordon, 3rd of Gight
2 CONT *1. Elizabeth Gordon+[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S2226] Lawless Bethune, "re: Bethune Family," e-mail message to www.thepeerage.com, 27 March 2007. Hereinafter cited as "re: Bethune Family."
2 CONT *2. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume IV, page 511. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also  The house of Gordon by Bulloch, John Malcolm, 1867-1938  https://archive.org/details/houseofgordon01bulluoft/page/n275/mode/2up
