1 NOTE {geni:about_me} GEORGE SINCLAIR (3rd son of George 4th Earl of Caithness), the SECOND OF MEY, succeeded his brother, William (the second son) and, in 1573, got a precept of clare constat from Robert, Bishop of Caithness. In 1585 a
2 CONC nd 1592 he obtained Crown charters. In 1572 the Bishop appointed him Chancellor of the diocese of Caithness. He was a man of ability, who lost no opportunity of promoting his family interests, and considerable additions to the fam
2 CONC ily estates were made by him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Before 1583 he married Margaret, daughter of William, seventh Lord Forbes, and he died in 1616. He had four sons and five daughters: -
2 CONT
2 CONT William, his heir;    Sir John, of Geanies and Dunbeath;    James, who died young;    Alexander of Latheron, ancestor of the Sinclairs of Barrock and Brabster;    Janet, eldest daughter, who married Walter Innes of Inverbrakie;   
2 CONC  Margaret, who married, in 1608, Alexander Sinclair of Forss;    Barbara, who married Alexander Keith of Pittendrum, in 1610;    Elizabeth, who married William Dunbar, first of Hempriggs in Morayshire, and grandfather of Sir Willi
2 CONC am Dunbar of Hempriggs, etc., in Caithness;    Anne.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.fionamsinclair.co.uk/genealogy/Caithness/Mey.htm#Fourth
2 CONT
