2 CONT About George Sinclair, 2nd of Mey GEORGE SINCLAIR (3rd son of George 4th Earl of Caithness), the SECOND OF MEY, succeeded his brother, William (the second son) and, in 1573, got a precept of clare constat from Robert, Bishop of Ca
2 CONC ithness. In 1585 and 1592 he obtained Crown charters. In 1572 the Bishop appointed him Chancellor of the diocese of Caithness. He was a man of ability, who lost no opportunity of promoting his family interests, and considerable ad
2 CONC ditions to the family estates were made by him. Before 1583 he married Margaret, daughter of William, seventh Lord Forbes, and he died in 1616. He had four sons and five daughters: - William, his heir; Sir John, of Geanies and Dun
2 CONC beath; James, who died young; Alexander of Latheron, ancestor of the Sinclairs of Barrock and Brabster; Janet, eldest daughter, who married Walter Innes of Inverbrakie; Margaret, who married, in 1608, Alexander Sinclair of Forss; 
2 CONC Barbara, who married Alexander Keith of Pittendrum, in 1610; Elizabeth, who married William Dunbar, first of Hempriggs in Morayshire, and grandfather of Sir William Dunbar of Hempriggs, etc., in Caithness; Anne. http://www.fionams
2 CONC inclair.co.uk/genealogy/Caithness/Mey.htm#Fourth www.geni.com
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
