1 NOTE {geni:about_me} {{icn_check.gif}} Burke's Peerage Extract (full document attached)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir WILLIAM MURRAY OF TULLIBARDINE;  Jt Govr to JAMES VI (later also I of England) and Keeper Stirling Castle 1572; Comptroller Scotland; married 15 April 1547 Lady Agnes Graham, 3rd daughter of 2nd Earl of Montrose (see MONTROSE,
2 CONC  D), and died 16 March 1583, having had, with other issue (including William and Mungo (Sir)):
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''JOHN MURRAY (Sir), 1st EARL OF TULLIBARDINE,'''  so created 10 July 1606, as also LORD MURRAY, GASK AND BALQUHIDDER and earlier 25 April 1604 LORD MURRAY OF TULLIBARDINE (all S), PC (S 1592); born c 1550; Master Household c 15
2 CONC 78–92, knighted c 1584; married by 15 Nov 1576 Catherine, daughter of 2nd Lord Drummond (see PERTH, E), and died 29 July x 3 Aug 1613, having had, with other issue (see MANSFIELD and MANSFIELD, E):
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Murray, the twelfth feudal baron of Tullibardine, was brought up with King James, who in 1592 constituted him his master of the household. On 10th July 1606 he was created Earl of Tullibardine. His lordship married Cather
2 CONC ine, fourth daughter of David, second Lord Drummond, and died in 1609. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www26.us.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/20/mode/2up Page 20 - No 98
2 CONT
2 CONT (98) '''Sir John Murray of Tullibardine'''  , died 1613. He was served heir to his father 15th May, and to his grandfather 27th June, 1583. In 1590-92 he was M.P. for Perthshire. On 25th April 1604 he was created Lord Murray of Tu
2 CONC llibardine, and on 10th July 1606 Earl of Tullibardine, Lord Murray, Gask, and Balquhidder. He married, before 20th December 1576, Catherine, daughter of David, second Lord Drummond, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 98(a) William (No. 99 below).
2 CONT * 97(b) Captain John Murray, died before 13th February 1607.
2 CONT * 97(c) Sir Patrick, Earl of Tullibardine (No. 124 below).
2 CONT * 97(d) Sir Mungo, second Viscount Stormont (No. 126 below).
2 CONT * 97(e) Robert Murray, living 1618.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
