1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Sir Humphrey Colquhoun of Luss===
2 CONT * M, #22090, b. 1565, d. 1592
2 CONT * Last Edited=27 Dec 2008
2 CONT * Consanguinity Index=0.56%
2 CONT * born in 1565.2 
2 CONT * died in 1592 at Castle of Bannachra, Scotland, killed.2
2 CONT * son of Sir John Colquhoun of Luss and Agnes Boyd.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married,
2 CONT #  firstly, Lady Janet Cunningham, daughter of Alexander Cuninghame, 5th Earl of Glencairn and Janet Cuninghame, in 1583.1 
2 CONT # secondly, Lady Jean Hamilton, daughter of John Hamilton, 1st Marquess of Hamilton in 1585/86.2
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived at Luss, Argyllshire, Scotland.1 He feuded with the Macfarlanes and MacGregors.2 He had two other daughters by his second wife.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir Humphrey Colquhoun of Luss and Lady Jean Hamilton
2 CONT # Anna Colquhoun2
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://thepeerage.com/p2209.htm#i22090
2 CONT ** [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 201. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT ** [S37] BP2003 volume 1, page 860. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT ** [S37] BP2003. [S37]
