1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JAMES SOMERVILLE OF CAMBUSNETHAN  "Velvet Eye" ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Somerville of Cambusnethan, here treated, who was nicknamed Velvet Eye: "was eldest sone and heir to John with the Plaides and Katherine Carmichaell, the captain of Crawfuird's daughter". [https://archive.org/details/memo
2 CONC rieofsomervi1815some/page/88/mode/1up Memorie II: 88]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Somerville, elder of Cambusnethan, here treated, died in September 1613. He made his last will and testament at the place of Cambusnethan on 6 September 1623. The witnesses present were Claud Cleland, brother of James Cle
2 CONC land of that Ilk, Arthur Hamilton son of Robert Hamilton, and James Somerville in Chapellhall. The inventory of his moveable estate, including the money owed to him and the money owed by him, was given up by his grandson, Sir Jame
2 CONC s Somerville of Cambusnethan, knight, who had been nominated and appointed as his executor testamentar. At the time of his death James Somerville, elder of Cambusnethan, owed one thousand pounds to his bastard sone James: "James S
2 CONC omeruell his sone natural".'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Somerville, elder of Cambusnethan, nominated and constituted his grandson, Sir James Somerville of Cambusnethan, knight, to be his only executor and universal intromitter with his goods, gear and debts. He left his soul t
2 CONC o God and ordered that his corpse was to be honourably buried. He also left one half of his free goods and gear to two granddaughters, Jean Cleland and Marion Cleland, daughters of James Cleland of that Ilk. Sir Robert Hamilton of
2 CONC  Goslington, knight, acted himself as cautioner for Sir James Somerville of Cambusnethan, and confirmation was granted to him on 2 January 1624. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The  Testament Testamentar a
2 CONC nd Inventory; Protestations, of James Someruell, elder, of Cambusnethame, parish thereof, reference CC9/7/19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000181284656099 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000181301935845 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000181284476007 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000181301920842 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000181284142978 Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stirnet reports that James Somervell of Cambusnethan, here treated, died in September 1613. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4as/somerville02.php Stirnet: Somerville 02] This conflicts with the Memorie, where he is
2 CONC  reported to have died in September 1623. [https://archive.org/details/memorieofsomervi1815some/page/91/mode/1up Memorie II: 91] He was alive on 6 September 1623, the date upon which he made his last will and testament, but he pro
2 CONC bably died on that date, or very soon thereafter. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The  Testament Testamentar and Inventory; Protestations, of James Someruell, elder, of Cambusnethame, parish thereof, refer
2 CONC ence CC9/7/19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 April 1571: Extract contract by which Mr Alexander Sym, advocate, and Katherine Boithuell, his spouse, assign to James Somervell, apparent of Cambusnethane, a tack of the lands of Gutheris in the lordship of Gilmertoun occup
2 CONC ied by George Hill and formerly redeemed by the said James from the said Mr Alexander and Katherine, the said James make payment on his side and grant a heritable security therefor over the lands of Drummis in the said lordship. [
2 CONC https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f4%2f144&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquis
2 CONC es of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), Somerville Writs, reference GD40/4/144]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 March 1593: Licence under the Privy Seal to James Someruile of Cambusnetham to absent himself from hosts etc. for life because of ill health. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4
2 CONC 0%2f4%2f153&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cambusnetham&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), Somerville Writs, reference GD40/4/153]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 April 1595: LIBRI RESPONSIONUM. ..... Vicecomes respondebit pro £333 6s. 8d. de firmis omnium et singularum terrarum et baronie de Cambusnethaine, cum turre, fortalicio, molendinis, multuris, piscariis, lie outsettis, partib
2 CONC us, pendiculis, toftis, croftis, cottagiis, annexis, connexis, tenentibus, tenandriis, liberetenentium servitiis, advocatione et donatione ecclesiarum, capellarum, et capellaniarum earundem, jacentium infra balliam suam, existenti
2 CONC um in manibus supremi domini nostri regis per spatium duorum annorum et unius termini aut eocirca ultime elapsorum sasina non recuperata, que firme extendunt annuatim ad £133 6s. 8d. ; et pro duobus paribus calcarium deauratorum p
2 CONC er duplicationem albefirme earundem ; regi debitis per sasinam datam Jacobo Somervell [Edinburgh, 18 April.] [https://archive.org/details/rotuliscaccarii03mcnegoog/page/363/mode/1up The Exchequer Rolls of Scotland XXIII::  p. 363]
2 CONC '''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 March 1598: Extract Contract between James Hamiltoun of Libertoun on the one part, and James Somervell of Cambusnethan, with consent of John Somervell his son and apparent heir, on the other part; whereby the said James and 
2 CONC John Somervells, for the price of 9,000 merks, dispone to the said James Hamiltoun, his heirs and assignees whatsomever. The lands of the Overtoun of Quodquen, and a cotland of the Nethertoun of Quodquen, and 44 acres of land lyin
2 CONC g on the north side of the Common of Quodquen, called the Newmanis, lying within the Barony of Carnwath and Sheriffdom of Lanark: To be holden of the said James Somervell and his heirs in free blench, for payment of a penny on the
2 CONC  ground of the said lands yearly, at the feast of Whitsunday, if it be asked allenarly. Registered in the Books of Council and Session the 13 Feb 1598. Witnesses, Mr James Lokhart Younger of Lie, Hew Hamilton, brother to the said 
2 CONC James Hamiltoun of Libbertoun and others. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD118%2f67&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotl
2 CONC and, Papers of the Chancellor family of Shieldhill, Lanarkshire, reference GD118/67]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''(43) 4 October 1603 JACOBUS SOMERVILLE de Cambusnethan, haeres Joannis Somervell de Cambusnethan, patris, - in annuo reddito 20 m. de terries dominicalibus lie Maynes de Crawfurde et Midlo, in baronie de Crawfurde-Douglas. Iii.
2 CONC  41. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=%20somervell&f
2 CONC =false Inquisitionem Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum etc. II]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 February 1604: Charter issued by William Wardlaw, elder of Rickartoun. Witnessed by James Somerville of Cambusnethan and others. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/550/mode/1up RMS 1593-1608: number 1508
2 CONC ]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 February 1619: Charter by James Sommervell of Cambusnetham in fulfillment of bond, [blank] January, to Sir John Sommervell of Kerswell Hamiltoun, his grandson, disponing lands and barony of Cambusnetham, in sherrifdom of Lane
2 CONC rk, reserving liferent. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1206&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cambusnetham&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the fami
2 CONC ly of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/1206]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 December 1620: Charter by JAMES SOMERVELL OF CAMBUSNETHEM, with consent of John Somervell, his son and apparent heir, and James Somervell, son of said John, in favour of Jean Somervell daughter of deceased Sir John Somervell
2 CONC  of Kerswell, kt., of annualrent of £50 scots from lands and barony of Cambusnethem, in sheriffdom of Lanerk. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1207&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=J
2 CONC ean+Somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/1207]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 December 1620 x 15 February 1642: Extract bond (dated 23 December 1620) by JAMES SOMERVELL, ELDER OF CAMBUSNETHAN, John Somervell, his son, and James Somervell, his eldest son now living, to infeft Jean Somervell, said JAMES
2 CONC , ELDER'S pronevoy, daughter of deceased Sir John Somervell of Kerswell, kt., eldest son of said John, in annualrent of £500 from lands and barony of Cambusnethan, reg. B. of C. and S., 24 January, 1624; with bond of relief (dated
2 CONC  15 February 1642) by said Sir James Somervell [Note] to Sir John Hamiltoune, elder, of Bargany, kt., Sir John Hamiltoune, younger, of Carridden, kt., his eldest son, Sir James Hamiltoune of Broomhill, kt., and Gavin Hamiltoune of
2 CONC  Raploch, his cautioners, over £4 land of Nethertoun of Cambusnethan, premonition, renunciation, and ratification thereof, with consent of James Kincaid of that ilk, her spouse. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalo
2 CONC gue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1208&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+kincaid&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/1208]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note 1: Two quite separate documents are mentioned here. The first is an extract or copy of a document that was dated 23 December 1620, and registered on 24 January 1624. The second document is a bond of relief dated 15 Februar
2 CONC y 1642. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note 2: Sir James Somervell, mentioned here, ls the grandson of James Somervell "eldest son now living" of James Somervell, elder of Cambusnethan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 March 1621: Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that he has given certain lands in the barony of Cambusnethan to John Somerville, junior of Cambusnethan, the son and apparent heir of James Somerville, senior o
2 CONC f Cambusnethan, his father, to be held by him in liferent following the death of his father: “in vitali redditu post decessum dicti Jac”. The charter reserved the  liferent interest in these lands that was held by James Somerville
2 CONC  junior, also the son of John Somerville, junior of Cambusnethen: “reservando JACOBO  SOMERVELL, juniori, filio dicti Jo.,heredibus ejus”, who also had a grant of the lands and barony of Cambusnethan, which land and barony had bee
2 CONC n resigned in his favour by his grandfather, James Somerville, senior of Cambusnethan. His grandfather also reserved his own liferent interest in the barony, as well as that of his son and apparent heir, John Somerville, junior of
2 CONC  Cambusnethan, and John junior’s wife Marie Hamilton. The King also subscribed anew to incorporate these lands in the free barony of Cambusnethan, which lands and barony was to be held by James Somerville, junior, and his lawful m
2 CONC ale heirs, whom failing by his brother Thomas Somerville and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by his brother Patrick Somerville and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by the nearest male heirs whomever of James Somerville, jun
2 CONC ior, who bear the name and arms of Somerville. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/48/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, 1620-33, charter number 148]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    11
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 April 1629: Precept of Clare Constat granted by John, Earl of Mar Lord Erskine and Gareoche etc, liferenter of the barony of Carnewathe, and by James, Earl of Buchen, Lord of Ouchterhous, his son, fiar thereof, for infefting
2 CONC  JOHN SOMERVELL OF CAMBUSNETHANE, SON OF THE DECEASED JAMES SOMERVELL OF CAMBUSNETHANE, as heir of his said father, in the lands of Carswell, lying within the barony of Carnewathe and sheriffdom of Lanark, the Over Lands of the to
2 CONC wn of Quodquen, and one cottage land of the lower town of Quodquen, those 44 acres of land lying in the north part of the common pasture and ground of the lands of Quodquen commonly called Newmaynes, and also in those 2 oxgates of
2 CONC  land commonly called Haisties Land, in the town of Newbiging, all lying within the said barony and sheriffdom. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD118%2f147&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=
2 CONC &ko=p&r=GD118%2f147&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Chancellor family of Shieldhill, Lanarkshire, reference GD118/147]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
