1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAME NICOLA SOMERVILLE Lady Blantyre ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Nicolas Somerville, here treated, married Walter, Lord Blantyre. [https://archive.org/details/abstractsofproto10glas/page/124/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols X: 3303]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Books of the Town Clerks of Glasgow ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 February 1587-88: Walter, commendator of Blantyre, gave sasine to Patrick Somervell of the King's bedchamber, as attorney and in name of Nicola Somervill, spouse of the said Walter, of the liferent of the lands and property 
2 CONC mentioned in No. 3299 [Note] ; and that was done by the commendator, with his own hands, delivering to Patrick Somervill earth and stone of the ground and clap and hopper of the mill. Same witnesses as in No. 3299, with exception 
2 CONC of Patrick Somervell, but with the addition of Robert Sinclair, writer and co-notary. [https://archive.org/details/abstractsofproto10glas/page/124/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols X: 3303]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: The demesne lands (terris dominicalihus) commonly called the Maynes of Calderhall, with the mills, mill lands, multures, woods, annexes, connexes, tenants, tenandries and services of free tenants, and all the pertinents I
2 CONC ying in the shire of Edinburgh. [https://archive.org/details/abstractsofproto10glas/page/123/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols X: 2999]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==================================
2 CONT When Nichola Somerville was born about 1553, in Cambusnethan, Lanarkshire, Scotland, United Kingdom, her father, Sir James Somerville 6th Lord Somerville, was 34 and her mother, Lady Katherine Murray of Falahall Somerville, was 22
2 CONC . She married Walter Stewart on 31 December 1581, in Lanarkshire, Scotland, United Kingdom. They were the parents of at least 4 sons and 3 daughters. She died on 30 August 1614, in Blantyre, Lanarkshire, Scotland, at the age of 62
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/L6LR-QPB/nichola-somerville-1553-1614
