1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN SOMERVILLE OF CAMBUSNETHAN==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Memorie of the Somervilles, John Somerville of Cambusnethan, here treated, is the eldest son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Somerville-of-Cambusnethan/6000000002116167230?through=6000000181364612826 by his sec
2 CONC ond wife https://www.geni.com/people/Katherine-Murray/6000000017078979823?through=6000000181364612826 who is said to have been infeft in all the lands of Lothian. [https://archive.org/details/memorieofsomerv11815some/page/445/mode
2 CONC /1up Memorie of the Somervilles I: 445]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Somerville of Cambusnethan, here treated, died before 22 May 1594. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f4%2f158&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Katherine+Murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&
2 CONC dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD40/4/158]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 June 1560: Charter by which John Somerville of Cambusnethan confirms that he has given the barony of Cambusnethan to John Somerville, his son, procreated between him and his wife KATHERINAM MURRAY. John junior's charter, whi
2 CONC ch was witnessed by Patrick Murray, son of Patrick Murray of Fallahill, and others, was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on 19 January 1580-81. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/27/mode/1up RMS 158
2 CONC 0-1593: charter number 87]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1560: Charter by John Somervell of Cambusnethan to John Somervell, his son, procreate, between him and KATHERINE MURRAY, his spouse, of the lands of Quiodquen. Dated at Cambesnethan, 31 Jul 1560.  [https://catalogue.nrs
2 CONC cotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f168&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Cambusnethan&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, reference GD8/168]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 July 1560: Charter by John Somyrvaile of Cambusneithtane to John Somyrvaile, son of said John and Katherine Mwrray, his spouse, of the lands of Overton, Netherton and New Mains of Quodquen and the lands of Kerswell in the ba
2 CONC rony of Carnewetht. Witnesses: William Sewir in Pader, Thomas Franche in Neddirtownne, John Nicholl younger, John Robertownne, William Hegatt. [Signature.] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refer
2 CONC ence=GD40%2f4%2f139&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Somyrvaile&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), reference GD40/4/139]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 May 1578: Precept of sasine under the Quarter Seal in favour of Hugh, Lord Somervell, in respect of the lands of Gilmertoun, Drum and Gutteris, following on decree of declarator of redemption against John Somervell of Cambus
2 CONC nethem, KATHERINE MURRAY, his spouse, James Somervell younger of Cambusnethem and Margaret Hammiltoun, his spouse, and John Somervell, son of said John and Katherine. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details
2 CONC .aspx?reference=GD40%2f4%2f146&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Katherine+Murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), reference GD40/4/146]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 May 1580: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland in favour of John Lummisdane of Blanerne which mentions John Somerville, son of John Somerville of Cambusnethan, and KATHERINE MURRAY his mother: "Jo  Somerwel filius Joanni
2 CONC s S. de Cambusnethane, Katherina Murray ejus mater". [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/827/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 3015]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 May 1581: Contract between John Somerville of Cambusnethan, and KATHERINE MURRAY, his spouse, on the one part and John Somerville, their son, on the other part, whereby the said John Somerville younger, binds himself that he 
2 CONC shall not appoint, transact nor agree with James Somerville, eldest son to the said John Somerville, of Cambusnethan towards the disposition of the lands and barony of Cambusnethan, in favour of the said James, without the special
2 CONC  consent of his father. Charter at Cambusnethan, 4 May 1581. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f310&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Somerville+of+Cambusnethan&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n 
2 CONC National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, reference GD8/310]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 May 1594: Copy of letters of horning at the instance of Hugh, Lord Somervell, against KATHERINE MURRAY, relict of John Somervell of Cambusnethane, John Somervell, their eldest son, and James Somervell now of Cambusnethane in
2 CONC  terms of a decree of redemption of part of the lands of Gilmertoun dated 18 Dec. 1577. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD40%2f4%2f158&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Katherine+Murray&ko=p
2 CONC &r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kerr Family, Marquises of Lothian (Lothian Muniments), Somerville Writs, reference GD40/4/158]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Books of the Tow Clerks of Glasgow ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 August 1560: John Somyrvaile of Cambusneithan gave sasine to John Kello, junior, attorney, and in name of John Somyrvaile (son of the said John Somyrvaile and Katherine Murray, his spouse), of (1) a cottage land (terram eota
2 CONC giam) of the lower town of Quodquen; (2) his lands of the upper town of Quodquen, extending to a £7 10 s. farm (firme) ; (3) 44 acres of land, commonly called the New Maynes, lying on the north side of the common pasturage and of 
2 CONC the lands of Quodquen ; and (4) the lands of Kerswell, extending to a ten merk land of old extent, lying in the barony of Carnwetht and shire of Lanark. Witnesses: William Selkirk, in Pedder; Symone Feichear in Libertoune, and Tho
2 CONC mas Franche in Neddirtowne. [https://archive.org/details/abstractsprotoc04robegoog/page/n104/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols II: 578]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
