1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MICHAEL FRASER OF STONEYWOOD ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Michael Fraser: "styled of Stoney wood" is the eldest surviving son of https://www.geni.com/people/Andrew-Fraser-of-Stoneywood/6000000014573250842 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Irvine/6000000002116155068?thr
2 CONC ough=6000000035609361218, He  appears to have been born in 1544. He was under age at his father's death, his precept of clare constat as his father's heir, dated is 10 October 1565, stating that the lands had been in the Queen's h
2 CONC ands for two years by reason of ward. He had exemptions from hostings, assizes, etc., on 7 February 1583-84, "being vexed with the gravel." [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/11
2 CONC 1/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 111]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT He died after Martinmas 1588, and before 18 January 1588-89. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/111/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 111]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT  He married Isobel (or Elizabeth), daughter of Duncan Forbes of Monymusk, and by her (who survived him, and married, secondly, Walter Wood of Balbegno). [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun04pau
2 CONC luoft/page/111/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 111]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 March 1588-89: Confirmed inventory and testament testamentar of Michael Fraser of Stannewod [Stoneywood], naming Isobel Forbes, his spouse, William Fraser in (?of) Bogheids and Mr. James Forbes in Estireycht as executors test
2 CONC amentars with powers of intromission with his lands and baronies of Stannewod, Mukkall, Carnebrogies and Kynmondies, within the sheriffdom of Aberdeen, for the support of his children, and naming the said Isobel and William and Gi
2 CONC lbert Fraser of Waltertoun, brother of the said Michael, as tutors to his daughters. (Commissary of Aberdeen.) [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f38%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=
2 CONC Isobel+Forbes&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1530&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Lord Fraser and Fraser of Inverallochy, reference GD1/38/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
