1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MARGARET OGILVY ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Ogilvy, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stewart-Master-of-Buchan/6000000002354417377?through=6000000141850657986. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun02pauluof
2 CONC t/page/269/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 269]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Only Child ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Christiana-Stewart-4th-Countess-of-Buchan/6000000003650044824?through=6000000141850657986 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/n6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility
2 CONC  of that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume II. (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1905), 602 pp.]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stewart18.php Stirnet: Stewart 18]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Ogilvy was born by 1530 in Boyne, Banffshire, Scotland; the daughter of Sir Walter Ogilvy, 3rd of Boyne. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married twice, first to John Stewart, Master of Buchan, son of Sir John Stewart and Margaret Scrygemour.[2] After his death at the Battle of Pinkie on September 19, 1547, she married Sir George Barclay before October 14th,
2 CONC  1556.
2 CONT
2 CONT Facts
2 CONT
2 CONT Boyne, Banffshire, Scotland is no longer considered a locality. As of 1975 what was once named Banffshire is now part of the larger Aberdeenshire, Scotland; although Banffshire has been " retained as an historic county". [3]
2 CONT Boyne Castle has been preserved but is separate from this family branch and is located "...about 1.5 miles (2.4 km) east of Portsoy, Aberdeenshire, Scotland, 0.5 miles (0.80 km) south of Boyne Bay." [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikidata says Walter Ogilvy, 1st of Boyne and Margaret are her parents, however date mismatch says there must be a generation or more in between.
2 CONT The above note was in place when I adopted the profile. I believe it correct and think the mistake is due to these families inter-marrying over time.
2 CONT It appears this Margaret may be the daughter of Sir Walter, "3rd of Buchan" and Christian Keith.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Fact: Also Known As Lady Margaret Stewart
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ [Mosley, Charles, editor. Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes. Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003.]
2 CONT ↑ Paul, James Balfour, Sir, 1846-1931: The Scots Peerage : Founded On Wood's Ed. Of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage Of Scotland; Containing An Historical And Genealogical Account Of The Nobility Of That Kingdom: Free Download, Borrow
2 CONC , And Streaming : Internet Archive". 2020. Internet Archive.>Stewart, Master of Buchan, Vol II, pps 269
2 CONT ↑ [1]
