1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John Ross of Little Tarrel</strong>, son of Alexander R. of Little Tarrel and Sarah, daugh. of Thomas Ross of Greenhill ; was min. of Kilmuir-Wester in 1573; trans, to Tain in 1580; pres. by James VI. 25th April 1581. He 
2 CONC was appointed by the General Assembly in that month as one "who best knew the bounds of the country" for selecting the number of Presbyteries, with the kirks of each, for Ross ; was trans, to Kilmuir-Wester before 1585, but return
2 CONC ed here about 1589, and was appointed by the Assembly in 1606 constant Moderator of the Presbytery, who were charged by the Privy Council, 17th Jan. 1607, to receive him as such within twenty-four hours after notice under pain of 
2 CONC rebellion ; died 22nd Oct. 1616. He  marr. Christian, daugh. of Hugh Monro of Assynt in Easter Ross, and had issue — 
2 CONT * Hugh, fourth of Little Tarrel, served heir 21st Jan. 1617
2 CONT * Marion (marr. David Munro of Allan)
2 CONT * David
2 CONT * Alexander, first of Pitkerrie, died 1st Feb. 1649
2 CONT * George of Nether Pitkerrie
2 CONT * Nicolas, burgess of Tain
2 CONT * William."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc00scot#page/62/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. VII, page 62
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT .
2 CONT The Ross Family. Line of Little Tarrell
2 CONT Northern Notes & Queries, Vol. 4, No. 15 (1890), pp. 102-111
2 CONT
2 CONT  iii. Mr. John became third of Little
2 CONT  Tarrell. He was presented to the vicarage of Kilmuir and Suddy 10th
2 CONT  December 1573 (Reg. Sec. Sig. xii. f. 126); translated from Tain, 25th
2 CONT  April 1581, to the vicarage of Logie Easter, in succession to Mr. Thomas
2 CONT  Hay, abbot of Glenluce (lb. xlvii. f. 115). In 1587-8, Mr. John and his
2 CONT  brother David ' in Drummeddeth,' with about 400 armed men, went to the
2 CONT  place where the members of the Baillie Court of the earldom of Ross were
2 CONT  sitting in judgment, and declaring they would be revenged for a wrong
2 CONT done to Andrew Munro of Newmore, compelled the court to rise (Reg.
2 CONT  Priv. Coun. vol. iv.). In vol. v. of the same register there is a complaint
2 CONT  made by a certain John Ross that he was carried off from the Chanonry
2 CONT  of Ross a prisoner to Balnagown by Mr. John and many others. It does
2 CONT  not appear what became of Mr. John's nieces, portioners of Little Tarrell.
2 CONT  He obtained a charter, dated at Leith 16th March 1608, from David,
2 CONT  bishop of Ross, to him, his heirs and assignees, of the lands of Little
2 CONT  Tarrell, with tower, fortalice, manor, mill, etc., in feu ferme and heritage,
2 CONT  for the yearly rent of 42s., with 14s. of grassum, and certain payments in
2 CONT  kind. Confirmed 14th July 1610 (Great Seal, 46, 233). He died 22d
2 CONT  October 1616 (Fasti Ecc. Scot*), having married Christian, daughter of
2 CONT  Hugh Munro of Assynt (Sasine 25th March 1611), 'goodwife of Little
2 CONT  Tarrell' (Sasine ist February 1652), and had,
2 CONT  iv. Hugh. (See below.)
2 CONT  xi. David, son of Mr. John (witness, Sasine 14th September
2 CONT  1607).
2 CONT  xii. Alexander. (Seepost.)
2 CONT  xxii. George, * lawful son' (Sasine 25th March 1611). (See
2 CONT  post.)
2 CONT  xxx. Nicholas. (Seepost.)
2 CONT  - William, ' son of Mr. John, some
