1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Cavendish, 3rd Earl of Devonshire (c. 10 October 1617 – 23 November 1684) was the son of William Cavendish, 2nd Earl of Devonshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lady Elizabeth Cecil, daughter of William Cecil, 2nd Earl of Salisbury, on 4 March 1639. They had two children:
2 CONT *William Cavendish, 1st Duke of Devonshire (1641–1707)
2 CONT *Lady Anne Cavendish (c. 1660–?), married John Cecil, 5th Earl of Exeter and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT *Kidd, Charles, Williamson, David (editors). Debrett's Peerage and Baronetage (1990 edition). New York: St Martin's Press, 1990.
2 CONT *Leigh Rayment's Peerage Pages [self-published source?][better source needed]
2 CONT *www.thepeerage.com
2 CONT *From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Cavendish,_3rd_Earl_of_Devonshire
2 CONT *___________________
2 CONT *''''''William Cavendish, 3rd Earl of Devonshire1
2 CONT *''''''M, #10989, b. 10 October 1617, d. 23 November 1684
2 CONT *Last Edited=9 Mar 2011
2 CONT *''''''     William Cavendish, 3rd Earl of Devonshire was born on 10 October 1617.1 He was the son of William Cavendish, 2nd Earl of Devonshire and Hon. Christian Bruce.1 He married Lady Elizabeth Cecil, daughter of William Cecil,
2 CONC  2nd Earl of Salisbury and Lady Catherine Howard, circa 4 March 1638/39.1 He died on 23 November 1684 at age 67.1
2 CONT *''''''     He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Bath (K.B.) in February 1625/26.1 He succeeded to the title of 3rd Earl of Devonshire [E., 1618] on 20 June 1628.1 He succeeded to the title of 3rd Baron Cavendish of Hardwick,
2 CONC  co. Derby [E., 1605] on 20 June 1628.1 He has an extensive biographical entry in the Dictionary of National Biography.3
2 CONT *''''''Children of William Cavendish, 3rd Earl of Devonshire and Lady Elizabeth Cecil
2 CONT **1.Lady Anne Cavendish+1
2 CONT **2.William Cavendish, 1st Duke of Devonshire+1 b. 25 Jan 1640/41, d. 18 Aug 1707
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT *1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1127. Hereinafter cited as Burke's P
2 CONC eerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p1099.htm#i10989
2 CONT *________
2 CONT *William CAVENDISH (2° E. Devonshire)
2 CONT *Born: 1590
2 CONT *Died: 20 Jun 1628, London, Bishopsgate Str.
2 CONT *Buried: Derby, All Saints'
2 CONT *Father: William CAVENDISH (1° E. Devonshire)
2 CONT *Mother: Anne KEIGHLEY
2 CONT *Married: Christian BRUCE (b. 28 Dec 1595 - d. 16 Jan 1675, Southampton Buildings) (dau. of Sir Edward Bruce, 1° B. Kinloss, and Magdalene Clerk) 10 Apr 1608, London              
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Anne CAVENDISH
2 CONT **''''''2. William CAVENDISH (3° E. Devonshire)
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/CAVENDISH.htm#William CAVENDISH (2° E. Devonshire)
