2 CONT '''1 July 1673: Extract Registered Disposition by Robert Grahame of Morpeth (sic) [Graham of Morphie], eldest son and heir of deceased Sir Robert Grahame of Morphie and heir of deceased Sir Robert Grahame of Morphie, his grandfath
2 CONC er, with consent of Dame Marie Irving [Irvine], his mother, and of Magdalene Grahame, his spouse, in favour of John Scott, merchant, burgess of Montrose, of the lands of Cummiestoun [Commieston], with the pendicle thereof called W
2 CONC antounwalls, the barony of Canterland, and the lands of Wardroppertoun, etc; reserving to the said Robert Grahame the fishings of the water of Northesk within the bounds of said lands. Registered B. of C. and S. 9 February 1676. [
2 CONC https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD70%2f372&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+grahame+of+morphie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Scott of Brotherton, ref
2 CONC erence GD70/372]'''
