1 NAME David /Graham/ Viscount Dundee
2 GIVN David
2 SURN Graham
2 NSFX Viscount Dundee
2 _MARNM Graham
1 NAME David Graham, 3rd Viscount Dundee
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1700
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAVID GRAHAM Viscount Dundee, Lord Graham of Claverhouse ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''<blockquote>'''Fake Genealogy'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''According to at least one pedigree published by FamilySearch, David Graham, here treated, who was the Viscount of Dundee, and Lord Graham of Claverhouse, married a lady named Marion Bell, with whom he had five child
2 CONC ren. The baptism of one child, a daughter named Anna was registered at Montrose in Angus on 21 November 1670, and the baptisms of the other four at Hawick in Roxburghshire, William and Bessie, twins, on  1 October 1671, Robert on 
2 CONC 7 March 1675, and Archbald on 6 March 1678. [https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/K8FX-13T/david-graham-9th-laird-of-claverhouse-and-3rd-vicount-1649-1700 FamilySearch: David Graham 9th Laird of Claverhouse and 3rd Viscount] The 
2 CONC claimed marriage to Marion Bell is followed by at least one pedigree published by Ancestry. [https://www.ancestry.co.uk/genealogy/records/marion-bell-24-11h0?geo_a=r&o_iid=41013&o_lid=41013&o_sch=Web+Property Ancestry: Marion Bell
2 CONC ]'''</blockquote> 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''The marriage proposed  by FamilySearch and Ancestry, between David Graham, here treated, and Marion Bell, is not supported by the biographical summary printed in volume three of The Scots Peerage, which does not ide
2 CONC ntify a wife and children for him, suggesting instead that he died unmarried and without a legitimate heir. Moreover, one child awarded to him by FamilySearch, a daughter named Anna Grahame, whose baptism was registered at Montros
2 CONC e in Angus on 21 November 1670, is in fact the daughter of David Grahame, one of the bailies or magistrates of the Burgh of Montrose.'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''David Graham, third Viscount of Dundee and Lord Graham of Claverhouse, is the second of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Graham-of-Claverhouse/6000000018446812102 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Madeline-Carnegie/60
2 CONC 00000018446899049?through=6000000183434327834 and the younger brother of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Graham-of-Claverhouse-Viscount-Dundee/6000000018446246040?through=6000000183434327834. [https://archive.org/details/scotspee
2 CONC ragefoun03pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/331/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 331]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not peen identified for David Graham, third Viscount Dundee. However, he is reported to have died unmarried and without issue in 1700. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/gg/graham03.php St
2 CONC irnet: Graham 03]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 April 1675: Extract Registered Bond by Mr David Grahame brother german to the Laird of Claverhous, as principal, and John Scott of Canterland, and Mr Patrick Sandilands of Cottoun as cautioners, binding themselves to warrand
2 CONC  the magistrates of Aberdeen from all risk, in their liberating Robert Grahame of Morphie from the tolbooth of their town, where he was imprisoned for debts due to many persons therein named.- a protection from the King having als
2 CONC o been granted in his favour. Dated at Aberdeen. Registered in Books of Council and Session 2 June same year, 1675. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD137%2f1627&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp
2 CONC =n&k=david+grahame&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scrymgeour Wedderburn of Wedderburn Family, Earls of Dundee, reference GD137/1627]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 January 1691: Petition of Wm Welsh of Skarr against Erskine of Cambo, son and heir to Sir Charles Erskine of Cambo, Lyon King at Arms, deceased, and the officers of State as representing Lord Dundee and David Graham, his brot
2 CONC her, John Douglas of Stenhouse and the heir of James Wilson of Stramulligan. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=PA7%2f14&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=viscount+of+dundee&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=165
2 CONC 0&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Supplementary Warrants and Parliamentary Papers, reference PA7/14]'''
2 CONT
