1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.patrickspeople.scot/ourfamily/2056.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married Isabel BURNETT, daughter of Alexander BURNETT 9th of Leys and Janet HAMILTON, in 1555.1 2 (Isabel BURNETT was born about 1530.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Isabel, married in 1555 Robert Arbuthnot of Pitcarlies and Little Futhes, grandson to Sir Robert Arbuthnot of that Ilk, and elder brother of the famous and learned Principal of King's College, Alexander Arbuthnot. Alexander Burne
2 CONC t of Leys and his sons, John and Thomas, were bound by the contract to pay 500 merks for her tocher (Register of Bonds, Vol. I.)."
2 CONT
2 CONT >from ''The Family of Burnett of Leys''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "Robert, who succeeded his father. He married in 1555 Isabel Burnett, daughter of Alexander Burnett of Leys. In 1587 he was Sheriff-Depute of Kincardine, under George, Earl Marischal. He obtained a tack of the teinds of Little Fid
2 CONC des in 1589, and died prior to 30 July 1606. He had issue.."
2 CONT
2 CONT >from'' Scots Peerage (vol 1)'' 1 2
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert next married Jean BURNETT 'of Craigmill', daughter of William BURNETT of Camphill and Heiress OF CARMYLE.3 (Jean BURNETT 'of Craigmill' was born about 1570.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT " .... Margery Arbuthnott, daughter of Robert Arbuthnott of Little Fiddes and his second wife, Jean Burnett of Craigmill. They had issue an only son, James ... "
2 CONT
2 CONT >from ''Barons of Allardice'' 3
