1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Erskine-1198
2 CONT
2 CONT Magdelen was born in abt. 1585. She is the daughter of the daughter of John Erskine "of Pittodrie and Marjorie Gordon Erskine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Magdelen Erskine “of Pittodrie” married Alexander Jaffray, Provost of Aberdeen on 23 Nov 1611 in Aberdeenshire, Scotland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children baptised at St Nicholas, in Aberdeen, Aberdeenshire, Scotland -
2 CONT
2 CONT # Alexander 1614
2 CONT # John 1615
2 CONT # Patrick 1616
2 CONT # Christane 1618
2 CONT # Marjorie 1620
2 CONT # Thomas 1622
2 CONT # Jean 1624
2 CONT # William 1628
2 CONT # Maria 1629
2 CONT # Anna 1630
2 CONT # Barbara 1632
2 CONT # Magdalen 1633
2 CONT # Marie 1635
2 CONT # James 1637
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 28 September 1640 after 29 years of marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Provost Jaffray was baptised on 11th October, 1584, and married, in 1611, Magdalen Erskine, a daughter of the laird of Pittodrie, by whom he had fifteen of a family, prominent among whom were his eldest sons Alexander and John, bo
2 CONC th afterwards occupants of the civic chair. The other members of the family, many of whom died in infancy, were Patrick, born 1616; Cristane, 1618; a son, 1619; Marjorie, 1620; Thomas, 1622; Jean, 1624 ; William, 1628 ; Maria, 162
2 CONC 9 ; Annas, 1630 ; Barbara,1632; Magdalen, 1633; Marjorie, 1635; and James, 1637. The Provost died in January, 1645, and was interred on the 12th of that month in S. Nicholas Churchyard beside his wife who had predeceased him in Se
2 CONC ptember, 1640. - (Alexander Macdonald Munro 1897, Memorials of the aldermen, provosts, and Lord provosts of Aberdeen, 1272-1895)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900/Jaffray, Alexander < [https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Dictionary_of_National_Biography,_1885-1900/Jaffray,_Alexander link] >  “JAFFRAY, ALEXANDER (1614–1673), director of the chancellar
2 CONC y of Scotland and a quaker, son of Alexander Jaffray (d. 10 Jan. 1645), provost of Aberdeen, by his wife '''Magdalen Erskine of Pittodrie''', was born at Aberdeen in July 1614. … “
