1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.zoominfo.com/p/John-Crichton/1052636819 Sir John Crichton, 4th of Innernytie and Airliewright, had a charter for the lands of Airliewright following the death of his father on 1 July, 1620, and was retou
2 CONC red his heir in the lands of Airliewright and Kinclaven on 16 August, 1620.He m. by 9 July, 1616, to Isabella, daughter of Thomas Wintoun, of Strickmarten, when they had a charter for the lands of Airliewight with the fortalice an
2 CONC d manor thereof, Little Preston, Blackforkle, Burnhead, Blackfaulds and Muirland, in the barony of Auchtergaven, the lands of Kinclaven and others which had previously pertained to Sir John Crichton of Innernyie and had been appri
2 CONC sed by Thomas Winton of Strickmartin.He had issue,
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.zoominfo.com/CachedPage/?archive_id=0&page_id=-1815942503&page_url=//www.perthshireheritage.co.uk/Crichton_of_Innernyte.html&page_last_updated=2008-07-06T15:54:40&firstName=John&lastName=Crichton
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Crichton, 4th of Innernytie and Airliewright, had a charter for the lands of Airliewright following the death of his father on 1 July, 1620, and was retoured his heir in the lands of Airliewright and Kinclaven on 16 Augus
2 CONC t, 1620. He m. by 9 July, 1616, to Isabella, daughter of Thomas Wintoun, of Strickmarten, when they had a charter for the lands of Airliewight with the fortalice and manor thereof, Little Preston, Blackforkle, Burnhead, Blackfauld
2 CONC s and Muirland, in the barony of Auchtergaven, the lands of Kinclaven and others which had previously pertained to Sir John Crichton of Innernyie and had been apprised by Thomas Winton of Strickmartin. He had issue,
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Mary Crichton, of Innernytie, m. to Sir William Stewart, second son of Sir William Stewart, 11th of Grantully, (he d. in 1672) and had issue which succeeded to these lands following upon a resignation in his favour by his broth
2 CONC er-in-law David Drummond.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Alison Crichton, m. at Perth on 6 February, 1638, to David Drummond, 3rd Lord Madderty, (he m. secondly by c/m 10 December, 1641, to Beatrix, daughter of John Graham, 4th Earl of Montrose, and d. on 20 January, 1692. He d. on 2
2 CONC 0 January, 1692,) and d. in March of 1639. They had issue.
