2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 November 1592: Discharge and renunciation by Mr John Graham of Knokdoliane, lawful tutor to Robert Grahame, son liberal begotten between unquhile Robert Grahame of Knokdolian, his unquhile father and Elizabeth Sempill, his s
2 CONC pouse and as his lawful administrator in favour of Robert, Master of Eglinton (in consideration of 3200 merks Scots) of a yearly annualrent of 160lib Scots furth of the 5lib land Peacockbankis, corn milne thereof, the 4 merk land 
2 CONC of Overbordland, the lands of Quhitleyis, Galbrochhill, Auchentibbers, Littil Fulwode and Struthers all of old extent extending in whole to a 25 merk land lying in the parishes of Stewarton and Dunlop, Bailliary of Cunningham and 
2 CONC sheriffdom of Ayr and of another yearly annualrent of 36 bolls of oatmeal furth of the lands called Haning alea Lytillward, the lands called Stanyflatt and Benezaird and others and furth of the 10s land of Meirsyde, all of old ext
2 CONC ent lying in the parish and regality of Kilwinning, Bailliary of Cunningham and sheriffdom of Ayr. Dated at Irvine. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f49%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n
2 CONC &tn=n&tp=n&k=Elizabeth+Sempill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/49/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 April 1606: Disposition by Robert Grahme of Grougar, with consent of Margaret Montgomerie, his spouse, and William McKerrell of Hilhous, to Thomas Kennedy of Kirkhill and Agnes Kennedy, his spouse, of 50s. land of Pinbraid a
2 CONC nd Blakfardeine, part of £10 land of Craig in parish of Commonell. In dorso: note of resignation by said Robert, 31 December, 1607. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f672&st=1&tc=
2 CONC y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=grougar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/672]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 April 1606: Extract disposition by Robert Grahame of Growgar, with consent of Margaret Montgomerie, his spouse and William McKerrell of Hilhous, to David Kennedy of Corss and Janet Kennedy, his spouse, of 40s. lands of Polga
2 CONC rnokis, 20s. land of Over Preistoun, 10s. land of Quhytfardein, all part of £10 land of Craig, parish of Cammonell, and 20s. land of Mekleschallochtmuck, in parish of Girven. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/
2 CONC details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f673&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+montgomerie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/673]''
2 CONC '
