2 CONT == The Testament Dative and Inventory of her Father and Mother ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Ralston of that Ilk died intestate in July 1623, probably at Woodside in the parish of Beith, in the Cunningham division of Ayrshire. His wife Barbara Hamilton died intestate in October 1623. Their testamet dative and i
2 CONC nventory was given up by William Mure of Glanderston, tutor testamentar to Jonet Ralton, Barbara Ralston, Issobell Ralston Jeane Ralston, Margaret Ralston, and Kathrein Ralston, their children.  John Hamilton of Udston acted himse
2 CONC lf as cautioner for William Mure of Glanderston and confirmation was granted to him on 19 November 1625. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Williame Ralstoune of that Ilk
2 CONC , parish of Beith, and Barbara Hammiltoune, his spous, reference CC9/7/20]'''
2 CONT
