1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  William Ralston  was born in Paisley and died about 1753 in Seedhills, Paisley.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: OPR 559/4.1 Abbey, Paisley
2 CONT
2 CONT 1719 July 17
2 CONT
2 CONT William Ralston, maltman & Jean Ralston were booked for proclamation in order to marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT Renfrewshire Minute Books of Sasines
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Ralston of her liferent in the lands in Seedhill 10 May 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT Renfrewshire Particular Register of Sasines
2 CONT
2 CONT Glasgow 24 May 1722
2 CONT
2 CONT ...upon the 10 May 1722 compeared personallie Jean Ralstown spouse of William Ralston, maltman in Seedhill of Paslay having and holding in her hands ane contract of mariag past betwixt the sd Wm and her on the ane an other pairts 
2 CONC dated the eleiventh day of July 1719 years thereby; in contemplation of the mariag yrin contracted and yrafter solemnised the sd Wm Ralstoun obliged him his aires to infed and sease the sd Jean Ralstoun in liferent during her life
2 CONC  tym of all and haill an yearlie annuity of one hyndred punds Scottis money to be uplifted att twa tearmes in the year Whit Sunday and Martimas to equall portions furth of all and haill these his fyftein roods of land... being pai
2 CONC rt of the lands of Whytfoord in Probanlaw and sicklike these his six aikers and ane half aiker of the sds lands of Whytfoord lyand nxt adjacent and contigue with the said fyftain roods... also these his dwelling houses in Seedhill
2 CONC  1st the barn and stable yarding and crofting els belonging and haill other houses yearding and pertinents yr to belonging and all possessit bey the sd Wm Ralstown... all lying in the regalitie of Paslay and Shirefdom of Renfrew p
2 CONC roviding always that in case yr be childrein ane or mae procreat of the sd marriage the sd annuity is restricted to ane yearlie annuitie of ane hundred marks...
2 CONT
2 CONT Renfrewshire Minute Books of Sasines
2 CONT
2 CONT 21 Sept 1753
2 CONT
2 CONT Seasine Robert Ralstoun, Hamilton, son of the deceased William Ralston in Seedhill of Paisley on a Disp. dated 3 May 1751, granted in his favour by the said William Ralstoun of all and haill the seven roods or thereby of Land call
2 CONC ed the provan, Cowhill, being part of the lands of Whitefoord lying within the Abbey parish of Paisley.
2 CONT
2 CONT William married Jean Ralston , daughter of Robert Ralston and Unknown , on 11 Jul 1719 in Abbey, Paisley, Renfrewshire. Jean was born about 1700 and died after 1753, after age 53.
2 CONT
2 CONT Noted events in her life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • Baptism: Hamilton, Lanarkshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children from this marriage were:
2 CONT
2 CONT   i. Ursulla Ralston was born in 1721.
2 CONT
2 CONT    ii. Janet Ralston was born in 1723.
2 CONT
2 CONT   iii. Robert Ralston was born on 20 Jun 1725 in Abbey, Paisley, Renfrewshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT    iv. Elizabeth Ralston was born in 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT   v. Gavin Ralston was born in 1731 in Paisley, died on 23 May 1818 in Aird, Inch, at age 87, and was buried in 1818 in Kirkcolm, Wigtonshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT   vi. William Ralston was born in 1733 and died in 1803 in Woodhill, Ayrshire, at age 70.
2 CONT
2 CONT     vii. George Ralston was born in 1736. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == WILLIAM RALSTON OF HONEYBOG ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
