1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WALTER STIRLING===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Merchant in Glasgow: Burgess of Glasgow, 1615; Guild Brother of Glasgow, 1618; Bailie of Glasgow; 1630-31; Dean of Guild of Glasgow; 1638-39 and 1639-40'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso43scotuoft#page/46/mode/1up Glasgow Burgesses, 1573-1750: 46]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Mother's Testament Dative===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Walter Stirling's mother died intestate in September 1575. Walter and his siblings were probably minor children at this time for his father gave up his deceased wife's testament dative and inventory as their "father & lawfull a
2 CONC dmstrator". The children are named as Robert, William George, Ninian, Walter, Malcolm, James, Margaret and Elspeth Stirling "lawfull bairnes and execrs dative surogait to their said unqle mother." Confirmation was granted Walter's
2 CONC  father on 21 August 1581. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, Testament Dative of Beatrix Elphingstoun sometyme spouse to John Sterling of Balquharage, reference CC8/8/9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000081862566852& Image of Testament Dative]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000081862221899& Image of Testament Dative]
2 CONT
