2 CONT "Note: 12th chief of the lamont
2 CONT
2 CONT precept of Clare Constat by Colin Earl of Argyle, directed to Robert Stewart of Auchinakaoch, his bailie, for infefting James Lawmonth, now of Inneryne, as heir of the late Duncan lawmonthe of Inneryn, his father, both of old exen
2 CONC t, lying in the Lordship of Cowall, Parish of Killenians in the Kerrerf, and within the sherriffdom of Ergunuine 29 Jul 1579 wit Neil Campbell of Blair, John Stewart of Largvrakana, Charles Campbell of Kylbryde, and John Ogsto
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Precept of sasine directed furth of the Chancery of King James the Sixth to the Sherriff of Argyle for Infefting James Lamond as heir to the late Duncan Lamond his father. In all and haill the Lands and Barrony of Inneryne aft
2 CONC ermentioned vist. The Lands of Inneryne, Drumglasne, Auchinak, Melldalloch, Auchinshelloch and Dowglennan, Craigveoch, Steillage, Ardlamont, Glennan, Auchychoirkbeg, Auchychoirkmore, Darbruiche, Askog, Auchedelvorie, Kilbryde, Cor
2 CONC row. Kilmichsell, Brecklies, Kilmernock, Knockdow, Inchkellen, Strongark, Gortanloisk, Trouster, Colstone, and Strine, and in all hail the Lands of ardcalmasaig and other lands underwritten vist. the two Carrricks, Auchinbowie, Ar
2 CONC dinherrey, Kilmichaellbeg, Ballemore, Duncolgyne, Blairboye, Dowpyne, Monedryn, Druntecormeck, Fernoch, Auchsohoiah. the two Tollartees, Auchinfour, Ardyne, Killenan, Tolasthoustoun, Auchingelzie, with the Advocation of the Chappe
2 CONC ll of Auchingelzie, with the milne, multures annexis connexis parts pendiciles Tennents Tennendries and Service of free Tennets of All and Hail the Lands and others written and pertinents lying in the Bailliary of Cowall and sherr
2 CONC iffdom of Argyle taking security for 239 pounds:6:8 of relief due to the King Dated at Edinburg 5 June 1579
2 CONT
2 CONT Instrument of Sasine proceeding on the aforesaid Precept, in favor of an Honourable and noble man James Lamonthe of Innveryne, son an heir of the late Duncan Lamonthe of innverryne, in The Lands of Inneryne, Drumglasne, Auchinak, 
2 CONC Melldalloch, Auchinshelloch and Dowglennan, Craigveoch, Steillage, Ardlamont, Glennan, Auchychoirkbeg, Auchychoirkmore, Darbruiche, Askog, Auchedelvorie, Kilbryde, Corrow. Kilmichsell, Brecklies, Kilmernock, Knockdow, Inchkellen, 
2 CONC Strongark, Gortanloisk, Trouster, Colstone, and Strine, and in all hail the Lands of ardcalmasaig and other lands underwritten vist. the two Carrricks, Auchinbowie, Ardinherrey, Kilmichaellbeg, Ballemore, Duncolgyne, Blairboye, Do
2 CONC wpyne, Monedryn, Druntecormeck, Fernoch, Auchsohoiah. the two Tollartees, Auchinfour, Ardyne, Killenan, Tolasthoustoun, Auchingelzie, with the Advocation of the Chappell of Auchingelzie with mills, multures, etc lying in the baili
2 CONC ery of Cowal and Sheriffdom of Argyle. Done on the lands of Innerryne, at the principal mansion therfore about noon, on the 7th June 579; wit John bishop of the Isles, John Lamont of Askok. Robert Stewart of Auchinaskye, John, son
2 CONC  and heir apparent of Donald Campbell of Auchevilling, Patrick Campbell, son of the said Donald Campbell of Auchevilling, John Campbell son of the late Duncan Campbell of Ellangreg, and John Stuart of Rosland, notarty public.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 jun1583 Instrument of sasine narrating precept by King James VI in the 17th year of his reign, and a precept by Colin Earl of Argyll, directed to William Mal Cloys his bailie in that part inflefting James Lamont of Inneryne as s
2 CONC on and heir of the Late Duncan Lawmonth of Inneryne in the six merk lands of Auchetyhewins, and four merk lands of Camis in the lordship of Cowal, and the parrish of Killenan in Kerriff and sherrifdom of Argyll. Done at the prinic
2 CONC ipal dwelling house of said lands about the second hour afternoon of 5 June 1583. wit: John McGillein, John Stewart, servitor of the sherrif of Bute, John Pirhe, servitor of John Steuart of Roisland, Gilbert M'Ane, Dowy McAlistar 
2 CONC servitor of said James Lamonthe of Inneryne"
