2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir Patrick MacKie of Larg (1576 - 1645)m., first, Susanna, 3rd dau. of Sir Thomas Kennedy of Culzean, no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m., secondly, Mary, dau. of Sir Uchtred Macdowall of Garthland, issue five : — Alexr., k. at Newburn in 1640; Jean, m. John Houston of Drumastane, by whom she had a son Patrick ; a dau. m Alexr. Murdoch of Cumloden ; Agnes, m. 
2 CONC George, son of John Gordon of Airds ; and Grizel.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m., thirdly, Isobel Kerr, Lady Greenheid, who survived him. Sir Patrick d. in 1645, and was succeeded by his nephew, Patrick M'Kie, bailie in Minnigaf
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *”The book of Mackay”.  Author Mackay, Angus, 1860-1911.  Page 356.   [https://archive.org/details/bookofmackay00mack/page/356 Archive.Org]
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/MacKie-1351
2 CONT *History of the county of Ayr, Volume 2 By James Paterson. Page 288.   [https://books.google.com/books?id=OvEHAAAAQAAJ&lpg=PA289&ots=ImAY7zlUDZ&dq=Sir%20John%20Kennedy%20of%20Culzean&pg=PA288#v=onepage&q&f=true GoogleBooks] Kenned
2 CONC ies of Cidzean.“Sir Thomas Kennedy of Culzean was the third son of Gilbert, third Earl of Cassillis. His immediate elder brother having died in infancy, he was styled Master of Cassillis at the battle of Langside, where he was tak
2 CONC en prisoner. He was knighted at the coronation of James VI. He got a charter of the lands of Culzean from his brother Gilbert, the fourth Earl, in which he was infeft 14th September 1569. He married Elizabeth, daughter of David M'
2 CONC Gill of Cranston-Riddell, widow of Robert Logan of Restalrig, and who afterwards ... According to the History of the Kennedys there was another brother, John, and a daughter, '''Susana''', afterwards Lady Larg.”
2 CONT * Scots Peerage - Page 488 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02paul/page/488 Archive.Org]
2 CONT * Reference: [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=bevangenealogy&id=I70405 RootsWeb's WorldConnect] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 15 2016, 20:33:31 UTC''
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT "The Book of Mackay" pp 355-6 states: "Susanna, 3rd dau. of Sir Thomas Kennedy of Culzean, no issue." 
