2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 February 1622: Discharge by John Fergussone of Kilkerran, in name of Agnes Mvir, daughter of James M., younger of Auchindrain, to Alexander Kennedy of Cragoche, as executor to Elizabeth McGill, lady Culzeane, his mother, of 6
2 CONC 00 merks Scots left to her (whom failing, to John M., her brother) in legacy by the said Elizabeth, her grandmother. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f4%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp
2 CONC =n&k=elizabeth+mcgill&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=1622&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/4/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 March 1653: Discharge by Gilbert Kennedy of Girvane Maynes and Marion K., his spouse, to John K. of Culzeane, as heir and executor to Sir Alexander K. of Culzeane, his father, of "bairn's part" due to the said Marion by dece
2 CONC ase of the said Sir Alexander, her father, or Agnes Kennedy, her mother.[http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f5%2f39&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=agnes+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=1650&
2 CONC di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/5/39]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 October 1654: Discharge and Assignation by Agnes Kennedy, daughter of Sir Alexander K. of Colzeane, and James Hammiltone, son of Archibald H. of Halcraig, her spouse, to John K. of Colzeane, brother of the said Agnes, acknow
2 CONC ledging receipt of 10,300 merks Scots in return for assignation (with two reservations) of "bairn's part" and rights by legacy due to the said Agnes by decease of her said father and Agnes Kennedy, her mother. Craigoch, sheriffdom
2 CONC  of Wigtown. Judicial Ratification of same by the said Agnes Kennedy. [Seal] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f5%2f62&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=agnes+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=
2 CONC 1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/5/62]'''
