1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===THOMAS KENNEDY OF CULZEAN===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sometime Provost of Maybole===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Kennedy of Culzean is the eldest son of Sir Thomas Kennedy of Culzean and his wife Dame Elizabeth Makgill. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f947&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&
2 CONC tp=n&k=elizabeth+makgill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD25/1/947] He is reported to have died unmarried in 1601. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/487/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 487] He was alive on 26 
2 CONC March 1601 but probably died soon after this. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f3%2f1a&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1598&dt=1601&di=n NRS: GD25/3/1a] 
2 CONC He was succeeded by his brother James Kennedy of Blairquharn. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f8%2f157&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD25%2f8%2f15&ro=c&df  NRS: GD25/8/157]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 December 1587: Procuratory by the said William Kennedy of Gilespie to [ ] to resign in the hands of John Earl of Cassillis and Thomas Kennedy of Culean his Tutor, the 40 shilling land of Craigoch, 20 shilling land of Cairnis
2 CONC ton 5 shilling land of Tradonach and half merk land of Knockin, extending to a 5 merk and 20 penny land, with all right and title which he the said William Kennedy had thereto, in favor and for new infeftment thereof to be granted
2 CONC  by the Earl and his Tutor to Elizabeth Makgill wife of the said Tutor in liferent, and Thomas Kennedy their eldest son and his heirs male in fee. Witnesses - John Kennedy of Greenan, Thomas Hay of Park, Uthtred Makdowall of Garth
2 CONC land, and William Baillie of Blairskinnoch. Dated at Inch. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f947&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+makgill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y Nationa
2 CONC l Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/947]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1587: (Incomplete) Procuratory by Sir Thomas Kennedy of Culzeane, Elizabeth Makgill, his spouse, and Thomas K., his son, for resignation in hands of Crown, superior, succeeding to Commendator and Convent of Melrose, in favour o
2 CONC f John, Earl of Cassillis, following on contract. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f2%2f286&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+makgill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records
2 CONC  of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/2/286]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 August 1597: Charter by John Earl of Cassillis to Sir Thomas Kennedy of Culean Knight, his uncle, by which in implement of a Contract entered into between the Earl on the one part, and the said Sir Thomas Kennedy for himself
2 CONC  and taking burden upon him for Dame Elizabeth Makgill his wife and Thomas Kennedy their eldest son, on the other part, dated 18th July then last, the Earl dispones to the said Sir Thomas Kennedy and Dame Elizabeth Makgill his wif
2 CONC e in conjunct fee and liferent and the heirs male procreate between them, whom failling the said Sir Thomas Kennedy his heirs male whatsoever, of the barony of Culean comprehending the 20 pound land of Culean with the manor place 
2 CONC and mill of Culean, 4 pound land of Glenalloway and Auchaltan and 5 merk land of Riddelston all formerly united into a free barony called the barony of Culean, and also the 40 shilling land of Coif with manor place yard and orchar
2 CONC d of the same lying in the parish of Kirkoswald and Earldom of Carrick, and uniting the said barony of Culean, 4 pound land of Glenalloway and Auchaltan, 5 merk land of Riddelston and 40 shilling land of Coif into a free tenandry 
2 CONC to be called the tenandry of Coif and ordaining the manor place of Coif to be the principal messuage of the said tenandry - To be holden feu of the Earl and his successors Earls of Cassillis, for payment yearly of the sums followi
2 CONC ng viz. for the barony of Culean manor place and mill thereof the sum of £80 money of Scotland, for the 4 merk land of Glenalloway and Auchaltan the sum of £16 like money - for the 5 merk land of Riddleston the sum of 20 merks, an
2 CONC d for the 40 shilling land of Coif the sum of £8 money aforesaid, extending in integro to the sum of £120 money aforesaid with 4 merks like money yearly in augmentation of the rental, at two terms in the year Pentecost and St Mart
2 CONC in by equal portions, together with a duplication of the said sums of £120 and 4 merks at the entry of heirs. Witnesses - John Wallace younger of Craig, Thomas Lidderdale younger of Isle, Mr Laurence Makgill Advocate and David Ken
2 CONC nedy in Maxwelston. Dated at Coif. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f1%2f1066&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+makgill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, 
2 CONC Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/1/1066]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 September 1600: Feu-Charter by Thomas Kennedy, provost of Maybole, son of Sir Thomas K. of Culzeaine, to John, Earl of Cassillis, following on contract of 19 January 1598 and containing precept of sasine. [http://catalogue.n
2 CONC rscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f3%2f1a&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1598&dt=1601&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (A
2 CONC ilsa Muniments), reference GD25/3/1a]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 March 1601: Instrument of Sasine by Thomas Kennedy, provost of Maybole, son of Sir Thomas K. of Culzean, in favour of John, Earl of Cassillis, following on charter - GD25/3/1a [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecat
2 CONC alogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f8%2f4a&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+kennedy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1598&dt=1601&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD
2 CONC 25/8/4a]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 August 1624: Charter of Alienation by James Kennedie of Blarquhan, son of Sir Thomas K. of Culzeane, and heir to Thomas K., his brother, and Gilbert Neilsone of Craigcaffie, advocate, to John, Earl of Cassillis, following on 
2 CONC disposition - GD25/8/157, and containing precept of sasine. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f8%2f158&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD25%2f8%2f15&ro=c&df=&dt=&di=n National R
2 CONC ecords of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/8/158]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 August 1624: Letters of Disposition by James Kennedie of Blairqvhan, son of Sir Thomas K. of Culzeane, and brother and heir of Thomas K., provost of Maybole, and Gilbert Neilsone of Craigcaffie, advocate, to John, Earl of Cas
2 CONC sillis, following on contracts of 18 July 1597 and 19 January 1598 and charter of 20 September 1620, and containing procuratory of resignation. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f8
2 CONC %2f157&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD25%2f8%2f15&ro=c&df  National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/8/157]'''
