1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===HELEN LIVINGSTON===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/fastiecclesiaesc04scot/page/291/mode/1up Fasti of the Church of Scotland IV: 291]
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Gordon L. Remington, "The Duncanson Wives  of Four New Netherland Settlers: Glen, Teller, Powell, and Loockermans," RECOlill 128 (1997): 1-10,228. Thomas Powell was also married afterwards to a fifth sister, Janet Duncanson. Alth
2 CONC ough Remington cautiously qualified Mary as a "possible" and Anne as a "probable" member of this family, the indirect evidence he presented that they were sisters of the others is compelling, particularly the fact that Anne's marr
2 CONC iage intention describes her as from "Sterling," accom- panied by a sister "[annetie." Furthermore, Burke (note 8 below) shows that the Rev. James Duncanson and Helen Livingston were married many years earlier than the extant bapt
2 CONC ismal records at Alloa suggest, and that Helen had ten children alive in 1633.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT * https://www.researchgate.net/publication/261286089_Recent_Literature_on_the_Duncanson_Sisters_of_New_Netherland Mary Loockermans, Anne Powell, Margaret Telller, and Katherine Glen were sisters.  They were daughters of the Revere
2 CONC nd James Duncanson, minister of Alloa and Tullibody, Clackmannanshire, Scotland, by his wife Helen Livingston.  Grand daughters of the Reverend John Duncanson, minister  and to the household of King James VI,probably (now known to
2 CONC  be certainly) by John's first wife, Janet Watson.  Helen Livingston was a daughter of the Rev. Helen Livingston, minister of St. Ninian’s, Stirlingshire, by his wife Agnes Gray, and a granddaughter of Henry Livingston of Falkirk 
2 CONC and Margaret Forrester ...
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Livingston-187 has parents as Mr. Henry Livingston & Agnes Gray, and cites 
2 CONT *Adrian Benjamin Burke, The Livingston Ancestry of the Duncanson Sisters of New Netherland, Part II: Identifyng their maternal great-grandmother Margaret Forrester," in The Genealogist, 2013, pp. 172-74. 
2 CONT *Adrian Benjamin Burke, "The Livingston Ancestry of the Duncanson Sisters of New Netherland: Part I: Identifying their mother Helen Livingston," in The Genealogist 2013, pp. 28-50.
2 CONT *click here for Livingstons of Callendar records: [http://www.paperclip.org.uk/kilsythweb/history/archivesources/livingston_line.htm link]
2 CONT * https://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00643172&tree=LEO
2 CONT *[https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/BD2Hdeelfgs “FOUR NEW COLONIAL GATEWAY IMMIGRANTS WITH MEDIEVAL ANCESTRY”] (2013)
