2 SURN Edmonstone
2 _MARNM Edmonstone
2 NICK Marjory
1 SEX F
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MARION EDMONSTONE (otherwise MARION EDMESTOUN) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Edmestoun is the daughter Sir James Edmestoun of Duntreith. [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsofproto10glas#page/76/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols X: protocols numbered 3207-08 on pp. 76-7] She is identified by Sir Archib
2 CONC ald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet, as Marjory Edmonstone. According to him she married "Claude Hamilton of Cocknay"  [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/46/mode/1up The Family of Edmonstone, p. 46] John An
2 CONC derson also calls her Marjory Edmonstone, [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/265/mode/1up Hamilton Memoirs, p. 265] and John Guthrie Smith concurs. [https://archive.org/stream/parishofstrathbl00smit#page/119/m
2 CONC ode/1up Strathblane 119-20]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Marion Edmestoun married Claud Hamilton of Cochno (afterwards Sir Claud Hamilton of Craigleith). She is identified as Claud's future wife in their marriage contract dated 22 November 1599 [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsof
2 CONC proto10glas#page/76/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols, protocol number 3208 on pages 76-7] but they must have married on or before 19 December 1599 when her father-in-law gave her the lands of Wester Cochnoch and others in liferent. [htt
2 CONC ps://archive.org/stream/abstractsofproto10glas#page/76/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols, protocol number 3207 on page 76]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Protocol Book of Archibald Hegate, 1587-1600===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 December 1599: Claud Hammiltoune, junior, son and apparent heir of Claud Hammiltoune, senior, of Cochnocht, roduced a charter whereby James, master of Pasley, commissioner of a noble lord Claud, lord of the barony and regali
2 CONC ty of Pasley, granted to him the lands of Eister Cochnocht, with the castle thereof, extending to a 10 merk land, old extent, with the pertinents, lying in the shire od Dunbartane, parish of Kilpatrik, and regality of Pasley; but 
2 CONC reserving the liferent of Claud Hammiltoune, senior. Charter subscribed at the House of Paisley on 25 November 1599, in presence of Mr. James Hammiltoun of Cander, Thomas Dalzell, Robert Hammiltoun, physician, and Robert Ker, serv
2 CONC itor of the master of Pasley, and writer of charter. Sasine given on the ground of the lands by Patrock Telpheir, bailie in hac parte. Witnesses George Sterling of Balagan, Mr. Walter Stewart, minister of Kilpatrick, Mr. Archibald
2 CONC  Hammiltoun and James Hammiltoun, brothers of the said Claud, junior, and Archibald Johnnestoun, notary.''' [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsofproto10glas#page/75/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols, protocol number 3206 on page 75]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 December 1599: Marion Edmestoun, lawful daughter of Sir James Edmestoun of Duntreith, knight, produced a charter, whereby Claud Hammiltoun, senior of Cochnocht, granted to her, in liferent, (1) the 5 merk land, old extent, o
2 CONC f Huchestoun and Hole (excepting and reserving to the said Claud and his heirs the coals and coa heughs, also the half acre of land occupied by Gabriel Mathew, with the land called Smyddieland, occupied by James Logane, and two ac
2 CONC res of land, occupied by James Paull, together with the muir from the ditch called "the heid dyke upwart;" and (2) the 5 merk 6s 8d. land, old extent, called Westir Cochnocht; both lyong with the parish of Kilpatrik, regality of P
2 CONC aslay and shire of Dunbartane; (3) the lands of Skellington, extending to a 20s. and 20d. land, lying within the parish of Dalserf and barony of machanshire; (4) the 6s. 8d. land called Mos Syde, lying there, with all and sundry p
2 CONC arts, pendicles, and pertinents of the said lands, and that in full satisfaction of terce or other right she may have through the death of Claud Hammiltoun, junior, her spouse. Charter (written by Archibald Heygait, keeper of the 
2 CONC Register of the king's secretary and his depute) subscribed and sealed at Cochnoct on 19 December 1599 in the presence of Archibald Hammiltoun and James Hammiltoun, sons of the granter, George Sterling of Balagane, Alexander Edmes
2 CONC toun, servitor to the said Sir James Edmestoun, Archibald Johnnestoun and Archibald Heygait, notaries.Sasine given with the consent of Claud Hammiltoun, junior, who was personally present, by Patrick Telfeir, as bailie in hac part
2 CONC e, (1) of the lands of Wester Cochnocht to Marion Edmestoun, personally present, and (2) of the lands of Huchestoun and Hole, to George Sterling of Balgray, as attorney and in name of the said Marion. Witnesses: George Sterling of
2 CONC  Balagan, Mr. Walter Stewart, minister of Kilpatrick, Mr. Archibald Hammiltoun and James Hamiltoun, brothers of the said Claud, junior, and Archibald Johnnestoun, notary.''' [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsofproto10glas#page/
2 CONC 76/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols, protocol number 3207 on page 76]
2 CONT
2 CONT                    3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 December 1599: Claud Hammiltoun of Cochnocht, senior, for implement of his part of a marriage contract between him and Claud Hammiltoun, his son and apparent heir, on the one part, Sir James Edmestoun of Duntreith, knight, W
2 CONC illiam Edmestoun, his son, fiar thereof, and Marion Edmestoun, lawful daughter of Sir James, on the other part, dated at Glasgow 22 November 1599, gave, by his own hands,sasine to Claud Hammiltounr, junior, and Marion Edmestoun, h
2 CONC is future spouse, of the lands of Wester Cochnocht and Huchestoun and Hole, as described in number 3207 and under the same reservations, and further reserving the liferent of Claud Hammiltoun, senior.  Witnesses George Sterling of
2 CONC  Balagan, Mr. Walter Stewart, minister of Kilpatrick, Mr. Archibald Hammiltoun and James Hammiltoun, brothers of the said Claud, junior, and Archibald Johnnestoun, notary.''' [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsofproto10glas#page
2 CONC /76/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols, protocol number 3208 on pages 76-7]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 December 1599: Claude Hammiltoune, junior of Cochtnocht gave sasine to Marion Edmestoun, daughter of Sir James Edmestoun of Duntreith, knight, his future spouse, of the liferent of the 10 merk land of old extent of Eister Co
2 CONC chtnocht, lying in the shire of Dunbartane, regality of Paslay and parish of Kilpatrick (but excepting  the castle and yards thereof, and reserving the liferent of Claude Hammiltoune, senior); and that in special warrandice and se
2 CONC curity of the lands mentioned in No. 3208; and also in special warrandice and security of the 20s. and 20d. land of Skellington, lying in the parish of Dalserf and barony of Machanschyre, and in warrandice and security of the 6s. 
2 CONC 8d. land of Mossyd, lying there. Witnesses George Sterling of Balagan, Mr. Walter Stewart, minister of Kilpatrick, Mr. Archibald Hammiltoun and James Hammiltoun, brothers of the said Claud, junior, and Archibald Johnnestoun, notar
2 CONC y.''' [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsofproto10glas#page/77/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols, protocol number 3209 on p. 77]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Published Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/abstractsofproto10glas#page/n8/mode/1up Robert Rewick, Depute Town Clerk, Abstracts of the Protocols of the Town Clerks of Glasgow, Vol. X. Archibald Hegates's Protocls, 1587-1600. John Ros' Protocols
2 CONC , 1588-9. George Hutchesone's Protocols, 1586-91 (Carson & Nicol, Glasgow, MDCCCC), 164 pp. including indexes]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Published Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/n6/mode/1up Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet, Genealogical Account of the Family of Edmonstone of Duntreath (Edinburgh MDCCCLXXV),  95 pp.]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/n8/mode/1up John Anderson, Historical and Genealogical Memoirs of the House of Hamilton with Genealogical Memoirs of Several Branches of the Family (John Anderson, jun., Ed
2 CONC inburgh, MDCCCXXV), 495 pp. including index plus corrections and additions] 
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/parishofstrathbl00smit#page/n8/mode/1up John Guthrie Smith, The Parish of Strathblane and its Inhabitants from Early Times: A Chapter of Lennox History (James MacLehose and Sons, Glasgow, 1886), 394 p
2 CONC p. including index]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Protocol Book of Archibald Hegate ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 December 1599: Marion Edmestoun, lawful daughter of Sir James Edmestoun of Duntreith, knight, produced a charter, whereby Claud Hammiltoun, senior of Cochnocht, granted to her, in liferent, (1) the 5 merk land, old extent, o
2 CONC f Huchestoun and Hole (excepting and reserving to the said Claud and his heirs the coals and coa heughs, also the half acre of land occupied by Gabriel Mathew, with the land called Smyddieland, occupied by James Logane, and two ac
2 CONC res of land, occupied by James Paull, together with the muir from the ditch called "the heid dyke upwart;" and (2) the 5 merk 6s 8d. land, old extent, called Westir Cochnocht; both lyong with the parish of Kilpatrik, regality of P
2 CONC aslay and shire of Dunbartane; (3) the lands of Skellington, extending to a 20s. and 20d. land, lying within the parish of Dalserf and barony of machanshire; (4) the 6s. 8d. land called Mos Syde, lying there, with all and sundry p
2 CONC arts, pendicles, and pertinents of the said lands, and that in full satisfaction of terce or other right she may have through the death of Claud Hammiltoun, junior, her spouse. Charter (written by Archibald Heygait, keeper of the 
2 CONC Register of the king's secretary and his depute) subscribed and sealed at Cochnoct on 19 December 1599 in the presence of Archibald Hammiltoun and James Hammiltoun, sons of the granter, George Sterling of Balagane, Alexander Edmes
2 CONC toun, servitor to the said Sir James Edmestoun, Archibald Johnnestoun and Archibald Heygait, notaries.Sasine given with the consent of Claud Hammiltoun, junior, who was personally present, by Patrick Telfeir, as bailie in hac part
2 CONC e, (1) of the lands of Wester Cochnocht to Marion Edmestoun, personally present, and (2) of the lands of Huchestoun and Hole, to George Sterling of Balgray, as attorney and in name of the said Marion. Witnesses: George Sterling of
2 CONC  Balagan, Mr. Walter Stewart, minister of Kilpatrick, Mr. Archibald Hammiltoun and James Hamiltoun, brothers of the said Claud, junior, and Archibald Johnnestoun, notary.[https://archive.org/stream/abstractsofproto10glas#page/76/m
2 CONC ode/1up Glasgow Protocols, protocol number 3207 on page 76]'''
