1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archibald_Napier,_1st_Lord_Napier
2 CONT
2 CONT == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Archibald Napier, 1st Lord Napier</strong>, the 9th Laird Napier of Merchiston (c. 1576–1645), was a Scottish politician and judge. In 1627 he was created Lord Napier of Merchiston and Baronet of Nova Scotia...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Archibald Napier was the son of John Napier and Elizabeth Stirling. In 1619, he married Margaret Graham, who was a daughter of John Graham, 4th Earl of Montrose and Lady Margaret Ruthven, and sister of James Graham, 1st Marques
2 CONC s of Montrose. They had four children:
2 CONT * John Napier, who died young.
2 CONT * Archibald Napier, who succeeded his father as Lord Napier.
2 CONT * Margaret Napier, who married Sir George Stirling of Keir.
2 CONT * Lilias Napier, who died unmarried."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'Archibald Napier, 1st Lord Napier', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 18 November 2012, 00:55 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Archibald_Napier,_1st_Lord_Napier&oldid=52358
2 CONC 8775> [accessed 27 November 2012]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/422/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VI, page 422-424
2 CONT * [http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Napier,_Archibald_(1576-1645)_(DNB00) Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900], Vol. 40
2 CONT * [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n337/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 318
