2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Edmonstone, here treated, is the son of Sir James Edmonstone of Duntreath and his wife Margaret Colquhoun. He is reported to have died unmarried. [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/46/mode/1up Dun
2 CONC treath: 46]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 April 1609: Extract registered disposition by said William Edmestoun [fiar of Duntreath], with consent of his said spouse in favour of James Edmestoun of Newtoun, his heirs and assignees whomsoever, of the said lands, under 
2 CONC the reversion; to have and to hold of the Superior. Dated at Stirling and Duntreath and registered in the Books of Council and Session, 18 July 1611. Witnesses: Robert Edmestoun, son lawful to Sir James Edmestoun of Duntreath, kni
2 CONC ght, Mr James Stirling, minister at Strablane and others.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/n8/mode/1up Genealogical account of the family of Edmonstone of Duntreath. By Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet (Edinburgh, MDCCCLXXV), 95 pp.]
