1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR MUNGO STIRLING OF GLORAT ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Mungo Stirling of Glorat, here treated, died before 6 July 1678. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD61%2f63&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+stirling+of+glorat&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=
2 CONC &dt=&di=n NRS: GD61/63]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 July 1678: Disposition by Sir George Stirling of Glorat, kt, son and heir of deceased Sir Mungo Stirling of Glorat, in favour of James Macfarlane of Keithtown, of lands called the Allans, and dale called the Elbow Daill, [nea
2 CONC r Ballincleroch]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD61%2f63&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+stirling+of+glorat&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Macfarlane of 
2 CONC Ballancleroch, reference GD61/63]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 August 1678: Inhibition at instance of James Macfarlane of Keithton against Sir George Stirling of Glorat, son and heir of deceased Sir Mungo Stirling of Glorat, relating to disposition of lands of Ballencleroch. Attached: e
2 CONC xecutions dated 15 and 19 August, 1678. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD61%2f64&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+stirling+of+glorat&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Sc
2 CONC otland, Macfarlane of Ballancleroch, reference GD61/64]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 January 1679: Precept of clare constat by James, marquis of Montrose, earl of Kincardine, Lord Grahame and Mugdock, in favour of George Stirling of Glorat, kt., as heir to deceased Mungo Stirling of Glorat, his father, in la
2 CONC nds of Ballancleroch. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD61%2f65&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+stirling+of+glorat&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Macfarlane
2 CONC  of Ballancleroch, reference GD61/65]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/stirlingsofkeirt00fras/page/145/mode/1up The Stirlings of Keir: 145]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4tz/stirling02.php#con2 Stirnet: Stirling 02]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://archive.org/details/stirlingsofkeirt00fras/page/145/mode/1up Biographical Summary Copied from the Sirlings of Keir] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''SIR MUNGO STIRLING OF GLORAT, Knight. he had a precept of sasine in the lands of glorats, as heir to his father, dated July 1642. He was a steady adherent of Charles II and suffered much during the Usurpation, on account of whi
2 CONC ch his son was made a baronet in 1666. He married, 1st., contract dated 11th. August 1614, Margaret, third daughter of Alexander Hamilton of Kinglas and Elizabeth Forrester, his spouse;  2ndly, before 1631, Marion, daughter of Wau
2 CONC chope of Niddrie;  3rdly., contract dated 2nd. October 1641, Margaret Livingston, who was living in 1644. He had two sons and three duaghters:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1. George, who succeeded, and was created a baronet.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' 2. William, who appears to have taken a part against his father during the Commonwealth, and to have circulated reports unfavourable to him. The Commissioners for prisoners investigated these reports, and by the following decl
2 CONC aration, dated 2nd. August 1654, they cleared Sir Mungo.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Whereas severall things was layd to the charge of Sir Mungo Stirling by William Starlinge his second sonne; vpon the examination tharoff, it was Found by the Commissioners for Prisoners at Leith, that the said charge was false 
2 CONC and scandelus"(Original at Glorat)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3. Jean, who was married to George Ross of Galston in 1649.(Ballagan Writs). 4. Margaret, who was married, in 1649, to Thomas Kennedy of Baltersan.(Glorat Writs). 5. Mary married, contract dated  31st. October and 4th. November
2 CONC  1656, John Stirling of Craigbarnet. (Glorat Writs)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/stirlingsofkeirt00fras/page/145/mode/1up The Stirlings of Keir and their family paper. By William Fraser (Privately Printed, Edinburgh, MDCCCLVIII), p. 145]'''
