1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == PATRICK BRUCE OF NEWTON ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Patrick Bruce of Newton, here treated, is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-Bruce/6000000206066875832 who was that son of https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Bruce-Cutler-in-Edinburgh/6000
2 CONC 000206066515821?through=6000000206066875832 whose baptism was registered on 21 December 1595, at Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland.'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Bruce of Newton, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Bruce-of-Airth/6000000002006149255?through=6000000004297770039 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/129/mode/1up RMS 1
2 CONC 620-33: charter number 383] and his spouse https://www.geni.com/people/Jane-Fleming/6000000002005782296?through=6000000004297770039 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/387/mode/1up Ibidem, charter number 1101]
2 CONC '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Bruce of Newton, here treated, is the uncle of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-William-Bruce-2nd-Baronet-of-Stenhouse/6000000009783948279 [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD
2 CONC 122%2f1%2f498A&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD122/1/498A]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Patrick Bruce of Newton. However, he is certainly known to have died before 24 November 1665, the date upon which his widow was interred in Greyfriars burying-ground in Edin
2 CONC burg [https://archive.org/details/registerinterme00socigoog/page/338/mode/1up Greyfriars Interments: p. 338]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Bruce of Newton, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Jackson/6000000000790377048?through=6000000004297770039 [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD90%2f5%2f
2 CONC 13&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD90/5/13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 July 1621: Charter made in favour of Marie Douglas, wife of Alexander, Lord Livingston. Witnessed by Patrick Bruce, son of the deceased William Bruce, feuar of Airth: "Pat. Bruce filio quondam Willelmi B. feodatarii de Airth
2 CONC ." [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/129/mode/1up RMS 1620-33: charter number 383]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 July 1627: Charter issued under the Great Seal of Scotland by which Charles I, King of Scotland, confirms to Patrick Bruce, feudatory of Newtoun, and Jonet Jacksoun, his future spouse, possession of various parts of the land 
2 CONC called Newtoun, in the barony of Bothkenner and Sheriffdom of Stirling. The lands in question had previously been resigned by Patrick Bruce in order to obtain a new grant in favour of himself and his future spouse. His resignation
2 CONC  was made with the consent of Jean Flemyng, who retained her own liferent interest. Patrick Bruce and Jonet Jacksoun were to hold this land in conjunct fee and liferent. The land in question was destined to pass to their lawful ma
2 CONC le heirs, whom failing to the lawful heirs of William Bruce of Stenhous. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/387/mode/1up RMS 1620-33: charter number 1101]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 December 1630: (Extract) Disposition (registered in the Burgh Court Books of Edinburgh, 7 Jan. 1631), by said Rachel, Janet, Helen and Elizabeth Jackson, with consent of Mr. Harie Foulis, Advocate, spouse of said Rachel, and
2 CONC  of Patrick Bruce of Newtoun, spouse of said Janet, to William Baillie, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, and Margaret Jackson, his spouse, of subjects contained in GD90/5/1 hereof. [Note] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonli
2 CONC necatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD90%2f5%2f13&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Yule Collection, reference GD90/5/13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: Tenement of land formerly belonging to deceased William Currour, within the tenement of deceased Nicolas Spathie on the north side of the High Street of Edinburgh and two lower fore booths and two annualrents therefrom.''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 November 1631-32: Registered Disposition by William son and heir of Umq. Sir William Bruce Knight, Baronet of Stenhous, with the assent of his mother Dame Rachell Johnstoun, to Patrick Bruce of Newtoun, of the orcheard of Bo
2 CONC thkennar. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD122%2f1%2f679&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Gilmour fa
2 CONC mily of Craigmillar and Liberton, Midlothian, reference GD122/1/679]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 December 1634: Resignation William, son and heir of Sir William Bruce of Stains Knight, and with the advice of Dame Rachel Johnstoun, his mother, and of Patrick Bruce, his uncle, to Gabriel Ranken, indweeller of Edinburgh, r
2 CONC esignation of the lands. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD122%2f1%2f498A&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers o
2 CONC f the Gilmour family of Craigmillar and Liberton, Midlothian, reference GD122/1/498A]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Register of Interments in Greyfriars Burying-ground ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 November 1665: Jackson. Janet, widow of Patrick Bruce of Newton (above head of Blackfriars Wynd). [https://archive.org/details/registerinterme00socigoog/page/338/mode/1up Greyfriars Interments: p. 338]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1620-1633. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate (H. M. G
2 CONC eneral Register House, Edinburgh,1894), 1096 pp. including indexes and errata]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/registerinterme00socigoog/page/n10/mode/1up Register of Interments in the Greyfriars Burying-ground, Edinburgh, 1658-1700. Edited by Henry Paton, MA., Searcher of Records. (Scottish Record Society
2 CONC , 1902), 722 pp. including index, notanda and glossary]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/bruce08.php Stirnet: Bruce 08] ''' [origins]
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/bruce09.php Stirnet: Bruce 09]''' [descent; does not list a son Patrick]
2 CONT # [https://www.brucefamily.com/lineage.htm#downhill '''Bruce of Downhill: Cowden, Newton and Downhill'''] [Patrick Bruce, of Newton, ancestor of the Bruce of Downhill, married Janet Jackson. They had 3 sons (that I know of): Patri
2 CONC ck, William and Michael."]
2 CONT # [https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I51686&tree=CC '''clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy'''] [does not list a son Patrick]
