2 CONT
2 CONT ===Justice of the Peace===
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam Bellenden is the eldest son of Adam Bellenden of Stenness.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f24&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=adam+Bellenden&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National 
2 CONC Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/24]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Published by the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT 23 July 1621: Instrument of Sasine in favour of '''Robert Bellenden of How, brother to Adam Bellenden of Stanehous, and Jean Smyth, his spouse.''' of the lands of Burgar, in parish of Evie, under reversion. On charter of alienatio
2 CONC n, dated 16 July 1621, by said '''Adam Bellenden, with consent of Adam Bellenden, his eldest son and heir.''' Recorded P.R.S. Orkney 25 July 1621. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%
2 CONC 2f24&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=adam+Bellenden&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/24]
