1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===GEORGE BELLENDEN OF MIDHOUSE===
2 CONT
2 CONT George Bellenden of Midhouse is the son of Adam Bellenden of Stenness, elder. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f167&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+Bellenden&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=
2 CONC y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/167]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT George Bellenden of Midhouse died before 12 March 1658, the date upon which his daughters took possession of the two merk land of Breck in the Orkney parish of Evie as their father's heirs.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrs
2 CONC onlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f45%2f43&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+Bellenden&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Title deeds to lands in Orkney, reference GD1/45/43]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT George Bellenden of Midhouse married Marie Sinclair, daughter of William Sinclair of Tolhoip. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f167&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=+Bellenden&ko=p&r=&
2 CONC ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/167]
