1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ROBERT STEWART OF CULBEG (aka ROB. STEUART de CULBEG)===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sometime Sheriff-depute of Stirling===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Stewart of Culbeg is the eldest son of Robert Stewart of Culbeg, and his wife Isobel Hamilton. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi07scot#page/217/mode/1up RMS: 582 on page 217] In his last will and testament dat
2 CONC ed 26 June 1619, his father instructed him to: "relieve his sd mothr ..... in so far as he is alreddie bound" and to: "gif assistance ..... to the sd Issobell Hamiltoun his mothr in all her affairis." [National Records of Scotland
2 CONC , Commissary Records of Stirling, The Testament Testamentat of Robert Stewart of Culbeg, Confirmed 24 July 1619, reference CC21/5/ pp. 426-29]' For the full text of his father's last will and testament see [https://www.geni.com/do
2 CONC cuments/view?doc_id=6000000077158784515& Image of Testament 3] and [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000077158473417& Image of Testament 4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Stewart of Culbeg died intestate in 1650. His testament dative and the inventory of his goods and gear was given up by Mr. William Crawford, notary public in Gargunnock, to whom he owed six hundred merks Scots money, plu
2 CONC s interest payments and expenses. Crawford was confirmed as executor dative creditor on 21 March 1656. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Stirling, Testament Dative and Inventory of Robert Stewart of Culbeg. refe
2 CONC rence CC21/5/5]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Stewart of Culbeg married Annabella Erskine, the bastard daughter of John, Lord Erskine. In a charter dated 27 February 1623 she is called his future wife. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi08scot#page/157/mode
2 CONC /1up RMS: charter number 452 on page 157] The request for marriage proclamation was booked in their respective home parishes on  2 March 1637, Canongate for her, Gargunnock for him, and they were married either on 19 or 27 March 1
2 CONC 623. The booking at Canongate reads as follows: "Sab: 2 March 1623. 1 Robert Stewart 2 3 Annabell Erskine .......... kirke the 19 March 1623 [National Records of Scotland, Canongate Marriages, 1600-1624, reference OPR.685/3/2] [ht
2 CONC tps://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000077162601653& Image of Marriage Record] The booking at Gargunnock reads as follows: "Upon the 2d Mar: were proclaimed Rot Stuart of Culbeg and Annable Erskine and were married in Edi
2 CONC nburgh the 27 Mar:" [National Records of Scotland, Gargunnock Marriages, 1619-1819, reference OPR.481/1] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000077163345164& Image of Marriage Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Stewart/6000000077101746269
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Isabell-Stewart/6000000077101777236?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521646254358&through=6000000077015408050
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Francis-Stewart/6000000077102087984?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521644812745&through=6000000077015408050
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Stewart-of-Culbeg/6000000077019111452?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521644768257&through=6000000077015408050
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Walter-Stewart/6000000077102137976?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521644725245&through=6000000077015408050
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Stewart/6000000077101792270?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521644583374&through=6000000077015408050
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Stewart/6000000077102013240?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521644553109&through=6000000077015408050
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Stewart/6000000077101835072
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 November 1611: Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that Issobelle Hammiltoun, the wife of Robert Steuart of Culbeg, has quitclaimed her liferent interest in the lands of Nether Culbeg. Likewise, the King confi
2 CONC rms that Robert Steuart of Culbeg has given the five merk lands of Culbeg in the sheriffdom of Stirling to his eldest son Robert Steuart, procreated between him and Isobelle. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi07scot#page
2 CONC /217/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1609-1620, charter number 582 on page 217]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 February 1623: A charter by which Robert Steuart of Culbeg confirms that he has given the lands of Culbeg and others in the sheriffdom of Stirling to his future wife, Annabellam Erskene, for her lifetime. The charter was iss
2 CONC ued in fufillment of a marriage contract between Robert Steuart of Culbeg, who had the consent of his mother Isobelle Hammiltoun, and John, Lord Erskene and his natural daughter Annabellam Erskene. Because his mother held the land
2 CONC s of Nether Culbeg for her lifetime he also gave the lands of Dalbrene to his future wife in compensation. For greater security Annabellam Erskene obtained a charter of confirmation under the great seal of Scotland on 23 April 162
2 CONC 3. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi08scot#page/157/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1620-1623, charter number 452 on page 157]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 May 1631-31 December 1632: Agreement between John, Earl of Mar, on the one part, and Alexander Leckie of that ilk, Adam Cunynghame [Cunningham] of Boquhane [Boquhan] and Robert Stewarte [Stewart] of Culbeg, on the other part,
2 CONC  the Earl ratifying the letters of tack by umquhil Adam, commendator of Cambuskinnethe [Cambuskenneth], of the lands of Leckie, Culbeg and Culmore, they relieving him of the proportional payment of the stipend of the minister of G
2 CONC argunnock. Rental of Gargunnock. Bonds to the Earl by Leckie, Cunynghame, Stewart and Alison Seytoun [Seaton], relict of James Forrester, fiar of Culmoir, to pay their shares of the said minister's stipend.[http://catalogue.nrscot
2 CONC land.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD124%2f9%2f53&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=culbeg&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1500&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, apers of the Erskine Family, Earls of Mar and Kellie, reference
2 CONC  GD124/9/53]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 July 1631: Robert Stewart of Culbeg. sheriif-depute of Stirling, deforced in the execution of a charge. [https://archive.org/stream/registerprivyco06coungoog#page/n373/mode/1up Register of the Privy Council of Scotland, Seco
2 CONC nd Series. VOL. IV., A.D. 1630-1632, pp. 305-06]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 June 1634: Rex : - cum consensu etc. - concessit Waltero Leckie, feoatario de Discheoris, heredibus ejus et assignatis quibuscunque, - 5 mercat terrarum de Culbeg, cum molendinis, vic. de Stirling; - que fuerunt quondam Robe
2 CONC rti Stewart de Culbeg, quond. ducis Jacobi, ejus filii, et Roberti S. tunc de C., ejus filii, de Regi tente per servitum warde, et Regi devenerunt per recognitionem ratione alienationis absque regis consensu facte; - test et in al
2 CONC iis cartis etc. liv. 239. [John Maitland Thomson, M.A., Advoate, Registrum Magnii Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1634-1651, charter number 143 on p. 60]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 July 1655: The Protector grants to William Bell of Nether Cullbeg, his heirs and assignees (subject to the legal reversion), - the five merk lands of Culbeg, mills, milllands, woods, fishings, etc., of the same in the sheriff
2 CONC dom of Stirling; - which lands pertained to the deceased Robert Stewart of Culbeg, and were on 28th Juky 1654 apprised from Francis Stewart, as charged to enter as heir to the said Robert, his father, at the instance of the said W
2 CONC illiam Bell, in  payment to him of 9150 merks, with 454 merks 6s. 8d. of sheriff-fee to Alexander Murray, messenger:- With precept of sasine. P.R. viii. 18. [John Horne Stevenson, M.A., Advocate, and William Kirk Dickson, M.A., Ad
2 CONC vocate (editord), The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland under the Commonwealth, A.D. 1652-1659, charter number 438 on p. 190]'''
