1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===REVEREND WALTER STEWART OF MASSATER===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Dean of Orkney: Minister of the Gospel at South Ronaldsay===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Reverend Walter Stewart of Massater is said to be the son of the Laird of Culbeg. [https://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc07scot#page/230/mode/1up Fasti ,vii, pp. 230-31] The name of his father has not been identified b
2 CONC ut he is treated here as the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Stewart-of-Culbeg/6000000077015893729?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521824257491&through=6000000034605530863 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Isobel-Hamilt
2 CONC on/6000000077015360278?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521824337498&through=6000000034605530863 If this proposition is correct then his paternal grandfather was https://www.geni.com/people/Walter-Stewart-of-Culbeg/6000000077019896467?fr
2 CONC om_flash=1&fsession_id=1521823518658&through=6000000077015893729  and his maternal grandfather was https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Hamilton-of-Inchmachan/6000000023707140843?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521825002585&through=600000
2 CONC 0077015360278 Inchmachan's wife https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Bellenden/6000000023704736979?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521824579589&through=6000000077015360278 was the sister of the Orkney Laird  https://www.geni.com/people/
2 CONC Patrick-Bellenden-of-Stenness/6000000037982860070?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521825018983&through=6000000037982860070
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Reverend Walter Stewart of Masatter died on 8 January 1652. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/browseDetails.aspx?reference=GD195/101&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=massater&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y Nationa
2 CONC l Archives of Scotland, Papers of the family of Stewart of Massater, Orkney, reference GD195/101]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 June 1627: Disposition by William Stewart of Manis to Walter Stewart, provost of Orkney, and Helen Sinclair, his spouse of land in Kirk and Stews disponed to him by William Gray (see GD195/23-24) [http://catalogue.nrscotland
2 CONC .gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD195%2f35-37&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Helen+Sinclair&ko=a&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Stewart of Massater, Orkney, referen
2 CONC ce GD195/35-37]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 August 1637: [https://archive.org/stream/registerprivyco02coungoog#page/n560/mode/1up The Register of the Privy Council of Scotland, Second Series, VOL. VI., A.D. 1635-37, pp. 506-07]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 August 1640: Instrument of sasine in favour of Mr Walter Stewart, minister of Burray and South Ronaldsay, and Helen Sinclair, his spouse, following upon 'letters of disposition and alienation' dated 14 Aug. 1640 by William S
2 CONC tewart of Mains of a rig of land in Kirk, being a part of land disponed to him by Thomas Cromartie (GD195/49) [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD195%2f51&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Hele
2 CONC n+Sinclair&ko=a&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Stewart of Massater, Orkney, reference GD195/51]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 February 1643: Charter by William Stewart of Mains to Mr Walter Stewart and Helen Sinclair, his spouse, of lands in Kirk [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD195%2f56-57&st=1&tc=y&t
2 CONC l=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Helen+Sinclair&ko=a&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Stewart of Massater, Orkney, reference GD195/56-57]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 June 1643: Charter by David Heart of Rusland to Mr Walter Stewart of lands in Gossager and Massater. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD195%2f60%2f1-2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=m
2 CONC assater&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Archives of Scotland, Papers of the family of Stewart of Massater, Orkney, reference GD195/60/1-2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 March 1645: Charter by William, earl of Morton, to Mr Walter Stewart, minister at South Ronaldsay and Burray, of udal land in Kirk, Quoycuise, Stowis, North and South Wydwall, Tarland and Sandwick, South Ronaldsay; with seal 
2 CONC attached. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/browseDetails.aspx?reference=GD195/63&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=massater&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Archives of Scotland, Papers of the family of Stewart of
2 CONC  Massater, Orkney, reference GD195/63]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 August 1654: Testament dative of Mr Walter Stewart, minister at South Ronaldsay, who died Jan. 1652. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/browseDetails.aspx?reference=GD195/101&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=ma
2 CONC ssater&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Archives of Scotland, Papers of the family of Stewart of Massater, Orkney, reference GD195/101]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 November 1654: Inventory of household plenishings of deceased Mr Walter Stewart, minister of South Ronaldsay and Burray, formerly belonging to Helen Sinclair, his first wife, and comprised by David Corner, bailie of Kirkwall,
2 CONC  William Lachtone and James Moirsone, counsellors, John Edmondstoune, chamberlain, and Capt. Robert Irving [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD195%2f103&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Helen+
2 CONC Sinclair&ko=a&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Stewart of Massater, Orkney, reference GD195/103]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
