1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == II. SIR LEWIS CRAIG OF RICCARTOUN ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Master of Arts; Advocate in Edinburgh; One of the Senators of the College of Justice, where he sat as Lord Wrightslands===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''D. Ludovico Craig de Wrichtislandis militi, uni senatorum sui collegii justitie (1610) D. Ludovici C. de Ricartoun militis unius senatorum collogii justitie (1616) D. Lodovico Craig de Ricartoun militi, uni senatoru
2 CONC m collegii justitie (1618) Sir Lewis Craig of Ricartoun (!629)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Lewis Craig of Riccartoun, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Craig-of-Riccartoun/6000000010281232862?through=6000000010281380818 The name of his mother has not been satisfactoril identified. Bru
2 CONC nton and Haig identify him as the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Helen-Heriot/6000000002116161713 [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.35112101615690&seq=300 College of Justice: 244] but the year of birth they proposed 
2 CONC for him suggests that he is more likely to have been the son of  https://www.geni.com/people/Helen-Hamilton/6000000048134948510?through=6000000010281380818 [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/cc4rz/craig01.php Stirnet: Cra
2 CONC ig 01] He is reported by Brunton and Haig to have been born in 1569. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.35112101615690&seq=300 College of Justice: 244]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Lewis Craig of Riccartoun, here treated, is reported to have died before 6 June 1622, the date upon which Thomas Henderson of Chesters was appointed to the College of Justice in his place. [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/
2 CONC pt?id=mdp.35112101615690&seq=300 College of Justice: 244]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
