2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/cc4rz/craig01.php Stirnet: Craig 01]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.35112101615690&seq=300 College of Justice: 244]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=mdp.35112101615690&seq=300 Biographical Summary by George Brunton and David Haig] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Lewis Craig of Wrights Lands. Eldest son of the celebrated Thomas Craig, by Helen, daughter of Heriot of Trabroun, was born in 1569. He was educated at the University of Edinburgh, under the eye of his father, and took his 
2 CONC degree of Master of Arts on 30th July 1597. He afterwards studied the civil law for two years at Poieters ; and returning to his native was admitted an advocate of 11th June 1600. He was knighted and appointed an Ordinary Lord som
2 CONC etime between the 24th February 1604 and 19th June 1605. He died before 6th June 1622, on which date Thomas Henderson of Chesters was promoted in his place. It has been recorded to Sir Lewis' credit, that he always uncovered when 
2 CONC his father was pleading, although the Lords at that period, wore their hats on the bench. '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lewis_Craig&oldid=485564030 Biographical Summary by Wikipedia] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Lewis Craig, Lord Wrightslands (1569-1622), was a Scottish judge.....Craig was the eldest son of Sir Thomas Craig of Riccarton, by Helen, daughter of Heriot of Traboun. He was educated at Edinburgh University, where he grad
2 CONC uated M.A. in 1597. He studied the civil law at Poitiers, was admitted a member of the Faculty of Advocates in 1600, knighted and appointed an ordinary lord of session in 1604-5.'''
