1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===DAME MARION ARNOT===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 July 1589: Burgh of Edinburgh: Instrument of resignation and sasine by Henry Nisbit, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, with consent of Jonet Bannatyne, his spouse, in favour of James Nisbit, his eldest son, and Marion Arnot, sp
2 CONC ouse of the said James, of an annualrent of £20 scots furth of the upper western booth, occupied by Alexander Uddart, merchant, in the said Henry's tenement or foreland on the north side of the High Street of Edinburgh, between th
2 CONC e tenement of the deceased John Fowler on the east, the tenement formerly of the deceased Alexander Cant on the west and the land formerly of Edward Littill on the north, and of the said tenement itself, excepting the booth afores
2 CONC aid, under reservation of liferent of the said Henry and Jonet, and of the said Henry's land late of [blank] Bartilmo, baxter, below the tenement formerly of the deceased Robert Bartane and afterwards of the heirs of Mr Thomas Mar
2 CONC ioribanks, between the dwelling house of the deceased James Bannatyne, writer, on the south and the waste land or yard of the deceased John Arthur on the north, which said tenement was on the north side of the High Street between 
2 CONC the tenement of the said James Bannatyne on the west and the tenement formerly of the deceased Andrew Moubray of Blakbarronry on the east. [Seal of William Smail, bailie, in good condition]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrs
2 CONC onlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f870&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+arnot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Brooke Family of Biel, reference GD6/870]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1616: Procuratory of resignation by John Logan in Restalrig, [owner of the 4 oxgates of lands of town and lands of Restalrig which were of old set by deceased Robert Logan of Restalrig to deceased Marion Skowgall, relict of Mic
2 CONC hael Logan in Restalrig, in liferent, and to deceased William Logan, his son, heritably, and thereafter sold by said deceased William to deceased Gilbert Logan, brother of said deceased William, and son and heir to deceased Michae
2 CONC l Logan, in barony of Restalrig and sheriffdom of Edinburgh,] and Elizabeth Quhippo. his spouse, and with consent of John Arnot of Wodmylne, oy and heir of deceased Sir John Arnot of Barswick, kt., to [blank] to resign said 4 oxga
2 CONC tes in hands of John, lord Balmerino, baron of barony of Restalrig, as in hands of immediate superior, in favour of James Nisbet, merchant, burgess of Edinburgh, and Marion Arnot, his spouse,, in liferent, and to Henry Nisbet, the
2 CONC ir son in fee. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD237%2f1%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=henry+nisbet&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Records of Messrs Tods 
2 CONC Murray and Jamieson WS, lawyers, Edinburgh, Nisbet of Dean, reference GD237/1/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2-18 August 1617:  Sheriffdom of Midlothian: Precept of clare constat by John, Lord Balmerino, in favour of Marion Arnot and Dame Helen Arnot, as heirs to Sir John Arnot of Birswick, their father, in four oxgates in the town of
2 CONC  Restalrig, and instrument of sasine following thereon. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f939&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+arnot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records
2 CONC  of Scotland, Papers of the Brooke Family of Biel, reference GD6/939]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 August 1617- 9 January 1618: Sheriffdom of Midlothian: (a) Charters a nobis and de nobis by James Nesbet, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, Marion Arnot, his spouse, and Henry Nysbet, their son and apparent heir, in favour of t
2 CONC he said Sir John Moresone, of an annualrent (as in no 938). [3 seals, in good condition, appended to either charter]. (b) Instrument of sasine (in duplicate) following thereon. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogu
2 CONC e/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f940&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+arnot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n  National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Brooke Family of Biel, reference GD6/940]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 August 1622: Sheriffdom of Midlothian: Contract whereby Marion Arnot, relict of James Nisbet, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, dispones to Henry Nisbet, her son, her right of conjunct fee or liferent in four oxgates of land in
2 CONC  Restalrig. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f944&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+arnot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n  National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Brooke Family o
2 CONC f Biel, reference GD6/944]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 August 1628: Sheriffdom of Midlothian: Instrument of sasine in favour of Marion Arnot, in liferent, of four oxgates of land in Restalrig. [PRS Edinburgh, 16 August 1628]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogu
2 CONC e/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f946&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+arnot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Brooke Family of Biel, reference GD6/946]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4-11 May 1648: Bond by James, Lord Ogilvie, to Dame Marion Arnot, spouse of Sir Lewis Stewart of Kirkhill, kt., advocate, for £1000 Scots. Edinburgh, 4 & 11 May 1648. [Registered B. of C. & S. 28 May 1649]. [http://catalogue.nr
2 CONC scotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD16%2f42%2f244&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+arnot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Airlie, reference GD16/42/244]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 May 1648: Process of apprising dated 8 Aug 1655, [not included] at the instance of Mr. William Douglas, advocate, against James, Lord Ogilvie, for payment in terms of bond, dated 4, 11 May 1648 [section 42 no. 244], granted 
2 CONC by the said Lord to Marion Arnot, spouse of Sir Lewis Stewart of Kirkhill, kt., advocate, for £1000 Scots, of the lands and baronies of Balloche, Newtoun, Airlie and others. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/d
2 CONC etails.aspx?reference=GD16%2f1%2f83&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+arnot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Airlie, reference GD16/1/83]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 February 1649: Sheriffdom of Midlothian: Discharge by John, Lord Balmerinocht, to Sir Lewis Stuart of Kirkhill, advocate, for the feu duty of two feu rooms in the town of Restalrig belonging in liferent to Marion Arnot, his 
2 CONC spouse, for the said Sir Lewis' lifetime. [Holograph]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f952&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+arnot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records 
2 CONC of Scotland, Papers of the Brooke Family of Biel, reference GD6/952]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 July 1650: Sheriffdom of Midlothian: Extract disposition by Sir George Morisoune of Diesie to Dame Marion Arnot, relict of James Nisbet and Sir Henry Nisbet, her son, of an annualrent (as in no 938). [B of C & S 23 July 1650
2 CONC ]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f953&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=marion+arnot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Brooke Family of Biel, re
2 CONC ference GD6/953]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Marion Arnot married James Nisbet (1557-1621), a son of Henry Nisbet of Dean and brother of William Nisbet of Dean. Marion Arnot inherited Lochend House at Restalrig from her father. James Nisbet was known as James Nisbet of Resta
2 CONC lrig after the marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 - James Nisbet of Restalrig, and burgess of Edinburgh, was the eldest son of Henry Nisbet, provost of Edinburgh 1597-8. On 24th November 1601, he was admitted a guild brother of the city, being designed as "eldest son of Henrie 
2 CONC Nesbet, merchand, lait provost of the burgh." He was a distinguished and successful merchant of the city. He married Marioune, one of the daughters and heirs portioners of sir John Arnot of Birswick, provost of Edinburgh, and trea
2 CONC surer depute to king James VI., by Margaret Craig, his wife, sister of sir Thomas Craig of Riccartoun, the other heir portioner of sir John being Helena, wife of sir George Home of Manderston. James Nisbet died June 1621. Confirma
2 CONC tion of his estate was granted to his relict on 9th January 1622. She subsequently married sir Lues Stewart, a distinguished pleader of the time, who, along with sir John Gilmour and John Nisbet, first of Dirleton, were selected b
2 CONC y the great marquis of Montrose to be his counsel when in 1641 he was prosecuted for treason by the committee of estates. Dame Marioune and her second husband lent large sums of money to sir Alexander Nisbet of that ilk, the grand
2 CONC father of the herald. The children of James Nisbet and Marioune Arnot who have been traced are -
2 CONT * (1.) Henry.
2 CONT * (2.) Robert, who had a daughter Agnes.
2 CONT * (3.) Marion, who married sir Alexander Dalmahoy of that ilk.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.valacar.net/nisbet/origins/plates5.htm]
2 CONT
