3 CITY probably at Edinburgh
3 CTRY Kingdom of Scotland (Not part of the United Kingdom until 1 May 1707)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == RACHEL ARNOT ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rachell Arnot, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Arnot-of-Berswick-Lord-Provost-of-Edinburgh/6000000011233293910?through=6000000002116161860 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Crai
2 CONC g/6000000011233426529?through=6000000002116161860 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Testament Dative and Inventory ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 23 August 1626. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Rachell Arnot, relict of Archibald Johnestoun, Merchant Burgess of Edinburgh, referenc
2 CONC e CC8/8/53]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 November 1643: Signature of the lands of Easter and Wester Shiells of Colbrandspeth etc granted to Janet Arnot, Marion Arnot, Rachel Arnot and Margaret Craig, widow of John Arnot (Arnott). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk
2 CONC /nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SIG1%2f22%2f35&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+craig&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register of Signatures, boxed series, reference SIG1/22/35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rachel Arnot was the daughter of John Arnot and Margaret (Craig) Arnot. Rachel married Archibald Johnston before 15 May 1577 when Archibald was admitted a burgess and guild brother of Edinburgh on 15 May 1577 by right of his wi
2 CONC fe Rachell eldest daughter of the deceased John Arnot burgess and guild brother. Rachel, her father and husband, along with others, appear to have acquired some property from Robert Logan of Restalrig but, by a private Act of Parl
2 CONC iament, were declared innocent of any involvement in the Gowrie Conspiracy. Rachell died before 23 August 1626 when her inventory was confirmed in Edinburgh Commissary Court. They had the following children:  (1) James. married El
2 CONC izabeth Craig. (2) Samuel (3) Joseph. Founder of Johnston's of Hilton. (5) Rachel. married (1) John Jackson, (2) William Bruce. (6)Jonet/Janet. married (1) James Skene, (2) James Inglis.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Johnston-6016 Biographical Summary by WikiTree] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rachel Johnston was born 1588 in Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland, daughter of Archibald Johnston and Rachel Arnot. She was the sister of Joseph Johnston, James Johnston and Janet (Johnston) Inglis.'''
