1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARY GRAY Lady Parbroath===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Marie Gray (1581) Mary Gray (1581) (Mary Gray (1601) Marie Gray (1601) Mary Gray, relict of David Seytone of Parbroth (1602) Mary Gray, elder Lady of Parbroith (1617) Dame Mary Gray, Lady Parbrothe (1623)'''</blockq
2 CONC uote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Fake Genealogy'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''First'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''At least one pedigree published by MyHeritage falsely claims that Mary Gray, daughter of Patrick Gray, fourth Lord Gray, married William Ruthven, Earl of Gowrie. It is true that Williiam and Mary were contacted to m
2 CONC arry, probably when they were children, but the marriage did not actually take place. The same pedigree makes a second false claim, that Mary Gray also married George Seton, fifth Lord Seton, when she did in fact marry David Seton
2 CONC  of Parbroath. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/262/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 262] The fake pedigree published by MyHeritage follows:'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Hon. Mary Ruthven (born Gray), 1547 - 1600. Mary Ruthven (born Gray) was born in 1547, at birth place, to Patrick (Lord Gray Airlie) Gray and Marion Gray (born Ogilvy). Patrick was born Circa March 1508, in Butterga
2 CONC sk, Perth, Perthshire, Scotland. Marion was born in 1514, in Airlie, Angus, Scotland. Mary had 16 siblings: Elizabeth Helen Bruce (born Gray), Isabel Strethan (born Gray) and 14 other siblings. Mary married George (5th Lord of Set
2 CONC on) Baron The Sir Seton, 7th Lord Seton. George was born in January 1531, in Of Seton, Tranent, East Lothian, Scotland. His occupation was Master of the Household to Queen Mary of Scots 1563, waggoner, Scottish Ambassador to Franc
2 CONC e 1583. They had 3 children: George SEATON and 2 other children. Mary married William Ruthven in 1565, at age 18 at marriage place. William was born in 1548, in Ruthven Castle, Perthshire, Scotland. His occupation was 1st Earl of 
2 CONC Gowrie. Mary passed away in 1600, at age 53 at death place. [https://www.myheritage.com/names/mary_ruthven MyHeritage]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Second'''</blockquote> 
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''A second pedigree published by MyHeritage falsely claims that Mary Gray, daughter of Patrick Gray, Lord Gray, and his wife Marion Ogilvy, married William Ruthven, Lord Ruthven. William Ruthven and Mary Gray were con
2 CONC tracted to marry, probably when they were children, but the marriage did not take place. This fake pedigree goes further, and falsely claims that William Ruthven and Mary Gray had a son named William Ruthven. This is wrong. [https
2 CONC ://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/262/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 262] The fake pedigree published by MyHeritage follows:'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Mary Seaton (born Gray), 1540 - 1600. Mary Seaton (born Gray) was born in 1540, at birth place, to Patrick Gray and Marion Gray (born Ogilvy). Patrick was born in February 1508, in Buttergask, Perthshire, Scotland. 
2 CONC Marion was born in 1514, in Airlie, Angus, Scotland. Mary had 9 siblings: Patrick Gray, Katherine Mortimer (born Gray) and 7 other siblings. Mary married David Seton of Parbroath. David was born circa 1535, in Of, Parbroath, Fife,
2 CONC  Scotland. His occupation was Comptroller of Scotland 1589. Mary married William Ruthven. William was born in 1528, in Ruthven, Aberdeenshire, Scotland. They had one son: Williame Ruthven. Mary passed away in 1600, at age 60 at de
2 CONC ath place. [https://www.myheritage.com/names/mary_ruthven MyHeritage]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Question of Identity===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Mary Gray is the daughter of Patrick Gray of Buttergask, afterwards Lord Gray, and his wife Marion Ogilvy. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/282 The Scots Peerage IV: 282-3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Proposed Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Mary Gray was contacted to marry William, Lord Ruthven, afterwards Earl of Gowrie, but the marriage did not take place. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04paul#page/263/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 263]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Mary Gray married David Seton of Parbroath.The marriage contract is dated 12 April 1568. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi05scot/page/94 RMS: 287]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/George-Seton-of-Parbroath/6000000033408495929
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/David-Seton-of-Kinglass-and-Ravenscraig/6000000118410106848?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1578816706694&through=6000000019840324857
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Seton/6000000033516369898?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1578756036216&through=6000000019840324857
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Seton/6000000118409074855?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1578817095827&through=6000000019840324857
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Seton/6000000118409055845?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1578817215221&through=6000000019840324857
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Andrew-Seton/6000000118409244835?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1578816973383&through=6000000019840324857
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Seton/6000000007089307333?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1578816813662&through=6000000019840324857
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Seton/6000000118409467821?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1578816956652&through=6000000019840324857
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Seton/6000000022153757152?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1578756156607&through=6000000019840324857
2 CONT
2 CONT ===EVIDENCE FROM THE NATIONAL RECORDS OF SCOTLAND===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 May 1581: Charter by which David Seton of Parbroath, with the consent of his wife Marie Gray confirms that he has sold the land called the three Urquardis to Master John Scharp, advocate. [https://archive.org/details/registr
2 CONC ummagnisi05scot/page/94 Regrisrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum, Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1580-1593, charter number 287 on p. 94]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 December 1581: Crown Charter confirming charger, dated 30 May 1581, by David Seytoun [Seaton] of Parbroth [Parbroath], with consent of Mary Gray, his spouse, to Mr John Scharp [Sharp], advocate, of the lands called three Urq
2 CONC uhardis [Urquhart], viz., Eistertoun [Eastertown], Lawsounistoun and Lappie [Lappie], lying in the sheriffdom of Fife. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD30%2f264&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp
2 CONC =n&k=mary+gray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Shairp family of Houston, West Lothian, reference GD30/264]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 May 1601: Instrument of sasine in favour of George Seytoun, elder son of David Seytoun of Parbroth, in respect of the barony thereof, under partial reservation of liferent, following on charter by said David and Mary Gray, hi
2 CONC s spouse, of the same date. Registered SRS Fife etc, 1 June 1601. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f218&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mary+gray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n Nati
2 CONC onal Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/218]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: By a charter dated 9 May 1601, David Seton of Parbroath, with the consent of his wife Marie Gray, confirmed that he had given the barony of Parbroath to his eldest son George Seton and his male heirs by his wife Jean Sinc
2 CONC lair. He reserved his own liferent and that of his wife Marie. He also reserved a liferent from the land called Wrquartis to his daughter Elizabeth, His charter was witnessed by his son Robert Seton and William Seton. [https://arc
2 CONC hive.org/details/registrummagnisi06scot/page/419 Regrisrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum, Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1593-1608, charter number 1201 on p. 419]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 June 1602: Extract decree at the instance of Mary Gray, relict of David Seytone of Parbroth, and Robert and Elizabeth Seytoune, her children, against Patrick Glasfurde, notary in Coupar, as haver, and George Seytoun of Parbr
2 CONC othe for registration in B of C and S of a contract, dated 15 and 16 April 1601 by which the said George bound himself to relieve the said David and Mary from various obligations and to confirm certain infeftments in favour of the
2 CONC  said Robert and Elizabeth (Elspeth) and the said David disponed to the said George the barony of Parbroth and other lands. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f220&st=1&tc=y&tl=
2 CONC n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mary+gray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/220]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 March 1617: Extract decree at the instance of John, Lord Lindsy, and his tutors against Jean Sinclare, relict of George Seytoun of Parbroith, Mary Gray, elder Lady of Parbroith, and David Seytoun of Parbroith for delivery of
2 CONC  writs. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f251&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mary+gray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (
2 CONC Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/251]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      6
2 CONT
