2 CONT '''David Seton of Parbroath''' (died 1601) was a Scottish courtier and administrator.
2 CONT He was the son of Gilbert Seton of Parbroath and Helen Leslie, a daughter of the Earl of Rothes.[1] Gilbert Seton was killed during the battle of Pinkie in 1547, making him successor to his grandfather Andrew Seton of Parbroath (d
2 CONC ied 1563).[2]
2 CONT His home was Parbroath Castle in Creich, Fife. '''His surname was sometimes written "Seyton" or Seytoun".'''[2]
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT '''David Seton married circa 1590 Mary Gray''', daughter of Patrick Gray, 5th Lord Gray and Barbara Ruthven. '''Their children included''':[2]
2 CONT *George Seton of Parbroath, who married Jean Sinclair
2 CONT *John Seton, who emigrated to the Virginia Colony in 1635.
2 CONT *Margaret Seton, who married John Scrimgeour, a son of James Scrimgeour of Dudhope, Constable of Dundee. As "Lady Dudhope" she was a friend of Jane Drummond, Countess of Roxburghe, who bought her clothes and visited her at Dudhope
2 CONC  in 1619.[17]
2 CONT *Mary Seton, who married David Skene of Potterton, and became ancestors of the family of Skene of Rubislaw.
2 CONT *Elizabeth Seton.
2 CONT etc.
2 CONT From: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Seton_of_Parbroath
2 CONT _______
