2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the Scots Peerage, James Stewart, here treated, was the son of James Stewart, fifth Lord Innermeath, and his wife Helen Ogilvy. He is said to have been 'at the horn' in 1591. Thereafter, on 26 November 1607, Patric
2 CONC k, Commendator of Coupar, complained to the Privy Council that James Stewart had attacked the Abbey, despoiled it of goods, and removed himself and his family. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/6/mode/1u
2 CONC p The Scots Peerage. Volume V, pp. 6-7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Citing Macfarlane, the Scots Peerage states that James Stewart married Margaret Maule, eldest daughter of Thomas Maule of Panmure. [https://digital.nls.uk/genealogical-collections-concerning-families/archive/74538638#?c=0&m=0&s
2 CONC =0&cv=159&xywh=111%2C1797%2C2596%2C1924 Genealogical Collections made by Walter Macfarlane. Volume II, page 152] In the main text of the Registrum de Panmure the editor identifies her husband as James Stewart, brother-german to Jo
2 CONC hne, Earl of Atholl, but in his additional notes he identifies him as the second son of Stewart, Lord of Innermay. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/7/mode/1up Ibidem: p. 7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft/page/6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage. Volume V, pp. 6-7]'''
