2 CONT <blockquote>'''According to one pedigree published by WikiTree, James Stewart, here treated, is the son of James Stewart, fifth Lord Innermeath, and his wife Helen Ogilvy. He is said to have married Catherine Fyer in Glasgow in 15
2 CONC 88, and to have died there in 1616, although this propositon is not supported by verifiable evidence. [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stewart-5554 Wikitree]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''James Stewart, fifth Lord Innermeath, did have a son named James, but he has no known connection with Glasgow. Moreover, he is said to have married Margaret Maule, eldest daughter of Thomas Maul of Panmure. [https:/
2 CONC /archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05paul#page/6/mode/2up The Scots Peerage. Volume V., note 1 on p. 6] James Stewart, here treated, is said to have married Catherine Fryer.'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
