1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JOHN LINDSAY OF BALLINCHO===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Lindsay of Ballincho is the third son of David Lindsay, Earl of Crawford, and his wife Margaret Beaton. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/29/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 29]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Lindsay of Balinscho is reported to have died on 6 January 1609. https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun03pauluoft/page/30/mode/1up The Scots Peerage III: 30]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Lindsay of Ballincho married Margaret Keith, daughter of Robert Keith, Lord Altrie, and his wife Margaret Lundie. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/171 The Scots Peerage I: 159]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Lindsay of Ballincho married Katherine Lindsay, John Lindsay of Balcarres. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/171 The Scots Peerage I: 159]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of the Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 March 1595-96: Extract Judicial Ratification by Margaret Keythe [Keith] lady Dwne [Dun], then spouse of Sir John Lindsay of Ballinscho [Ballinshoe] knight, one of the two daughters and heirs apparent of Robert lord Altrie, r
2 CONC atifying her father's resignation of the estate (omitting mention of the patronage), in favour of Robert Keythe [Keith] of Benholme [Benholm] brother german of George earl Merschell [Earl Marischal], and renouncing her title there
2 CONC to in his favour; and that in consideration of a contract between lord Altrie on one part and herself and her spouse on the other, of date 18 March 1595/6, whereby a sum of 7000 merks was appointed to be pald to her. Done before t
2 CONC he Commissary of Brechin sitting in judgment in the kirk of Montrose. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f86&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lindsay+of+ballinscho&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1680
2 CONC &di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, reference GD4/86]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 February 1596-97: Instrument narrating that Robert Keithe [Keith] of Benholme [Benholm] in presence of notary and witnesses required Sir John Lindsay of Ballinscho [Ballinshoe] knight to cause Dame Margaret Keithe [Keith] his
2 CONC  spouse to enter as one of the heirs portioners of the deceased Robert lord Altrie her father in the lands and barony of Benholme [Benholm], Manis thereof, tower, fortalice and mills thereof, the lands of Ovir and Nathir Knox, and
2 CONC  the Kirktoune of Benholme [Kirkton of Benholm], conform to contract of 18 March 1595/6. Which Sir John was willing to do, provided that the requisition was lawfully made within year and day of lord Altrie's death, and that the en
2 CONC try should be at Robert's expense. Robert then offered a 5 gold piece to "make the expenses", which Sir John said would not "do the turn". On which both parties asked instruments. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatal
2 CONC ogue/details.aspx?reference=GD4%2f87&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lindsay+of+ballinscho&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1680&di=n  National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott family of Benholm, Kincardineshire and Hedderwick, Angus, refer
2 CONC ence GD4/87]'''
