1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES FOULIS OF COLINTON===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 April 1568: Charter by Alexander Betoun, archdeacon of Lothian and rector of the parish church of Curry alias Killdeleith, to Agnes Heriot, eldest daughter of deceased Mr. Robert Heriot of Lymphoy, and James Fowlis, son and h
2 CONC eir apparent of Mr. Henry Foulis of Colintoun, her spouse, and survivor, and heirs, of said kirklands of Curry, containing a precept of sasine addressed to Mr. John Foulis, rector of Edzell, as bailie. Signed and sealed at Edinbur
2 CONC gh. Witnesses, Mr. Henry Foulis of Colintoun aforesaid, Mr. Edward Henrysoun, advocate, Sir John Richie, prebendary of the collegiate church of St. Mary of Fields near Edinburgh, William Roule, servitor of said Mr. Edward Henrysou
2 CONC n, Adam Haldane, servitor of said Mr. Henry Foulis, and Mr. George Sinclare, notary public.
2 CONT In dorso Note of Sasine following thereon. GD1/208/21.Seal appended. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f208%2f20&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=heriot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1551&dt=1620&di=n 
2 CONC National Records of Scotland, Currie Writs, Midlothian, reference GD1/208/20]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 September 1568: nstrument of Sasine following GD1/208/20. Dated Henry Sinclair acts as attorney for above Agnes Heriot. Witnesses, Andrew Alias Dandle Hering, occupier of said kirklands of Curry, Oliver Hering, his son, Alex
2 CONC ander Weir in Edinburgh, John Dobie in Killeith, Edward Reid, smith in Currie and Robert Sinclare, son of Thomas Sinclare, writer. Notary, Mr. George Sinclare, clerk of the diocese of St. Andrews. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.
2 CONC uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f208%2f21&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=heriot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1551&dt=1620&di=n National Records of Scotland, National Records of Scotland, Currie Writs, Midlothian, reference GD1/20
2 CONC 8/21]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 July 1580: Decreet of Regality Court of Saint Andrews in action at instance of Agnes Hereot and James Fowlis of Colingtoun, her spouse, proprietors of kirklands and glebe of parish church of Curry alias Kyndaleyth with commo
2 CONC n pasture in lands and muir of Kyndaleyth, against John Fynlasoun of Killeith and Matthew Finlasoun, his son, for damage to and wrongful possession of parts of said lands. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/det
2 CONC ails.aspx?reference=GD41%2f214&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hereot&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Dick-Lauder family of Fountainhall, reference GD41/214]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Protocol Books of the Town Clerks of Glasgow===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 April 1590: Michael Leirmonth, attorney and in name of James Fowlis of Colingtoune and Agnes Hereot, spouses, produced a charter whereby Walter, commendator of Blantyre, lord feu-farmer of the barony, lordship and regality o
2 CONC f Glasgow, granted to the said James Fowlis and Agnes Hereot, and l.l., in feu-farm the 33 s. 4 d. land, old extent, of Rammishorne and Medoflatt ; also the 4 merk land, same extent, of Gardorroiche ; with all the pertinents; lyin
2 CONC g in the barony and regality of Glasgow and shire of Lanerk. Charter subscribed and scaled at Edinburgh, on 21 December, 1588, in presence of Alexander Dalnmahoy of that Ilk, Robert Chyrnesyde, burgess of Glasgw, Thomas Fowlis of 
2 CONC Brownysyde, Robert Sinclare, clerk of the privy seal (scriba secreli sigilli), Henry Wardlaw, writer, and George Huchesoun, servant of the commendator (nostro servo). Sasine given on the respective lands by James Thompsone in Lump
2 CONC hoy, as bailie in hac parte, named in the charter. "Witnesses : John Lowthiane, William Hammiltoune, Robert Baird, George Fowlar and John Mayne in Gardorroich, John M'Kynnie, George Pollok, John Drew and John Bar, citizens of Glas
2 CONC gow. [https://archive.org/details/abstractsofproto10glas/page/124/mode/1up Glasgow Protocols X: 3302]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/diaryofsirarchib26scot#page/n23/mode/1up Diary of Sir Archibald Johnston, Lord Wariston. 1639. etc. (Scottish History Society, 1896), p. 4]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/liberprotocollor01glas/page/186 Rental Book of the Diocese of Glasgow, A.D. 1509-1570, p. 186]
2 CONT # [https://books.google.no/books?id=Cq8KAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA491&lpg=PA491&dq=sir+henry+foulis+2nd+baronet&source=bl&ots=fjBVrHWbDG&sig=ZqMeTfccqzJXQEtaLTbgj1lP3WI&hl=no&sa=X&ei=woNYVduFG4PNygOF04CABw&ved=0CE4Q6AEwBg#v=onepage&q=sir%20he
2 CONC nry%20foulis%202nd%20baronet&f=false General and Heraldic Distionary of the Peerage and Baronetage of the British Empire; Burke; 1832:]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
