1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Haldane, 9th of Gleneagles was the son of John Haldane, 7th of Gleneagles and Elizabeth Lundie.2  He died in 1591.2
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He was educated in 1571 at St. Mary's College, St. Andrews, Fife, ScotlandG.1 He was a sympathiser with the perpetrators of the Raid of Ruthven.1 In April 1584 he and his brother-in-law, Sir George Home of Wedderburn, were summone
2 CONC d to appear before the Council, under pain of rebellion, to answer certain charges of connection with the Raids.1 In 1585 he joined the Protestant Lords at St. Ninians to overthrow the Earl of Arran.1 He was Commissioner of the Ge
2 CONC neral Assembly for Dunblane in 1590.1
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, first, to Isobel Home, daughter of Sir David Home, 5th of Wedderburn and Mariota Johnstone.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, second, to Barbara Johnstone, daughter of James Johnstone, 5th of Elphinstone and Margaret Ruthven.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Haldane, 9th of Gleneagles and Isobel Home:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir James Haldane, 10th of Gleneagles+2 d. 1624 m. Margaret Murray
2 CONT # Archibald Haldane2
2 CONT # Isobel Haldane+2 m. William Edmonstone 7th of Duntreath.
2 CONT # Helen Haldane+2 m. Alexander Lindsay 1st of Canterland
2 CONT # Margaret Haldane+2 m. John Home of Blackadder 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Haldane, 9th of Gleneagles and Barbara Johnstone:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Lilias Haldane2
2 CONT # Martha Haldane+2 m. Col. Sir Henry Bruce
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Haldane of Gleneagles, married to Isabel, Haldane, daughter of Sir David Home of Wedderburn, ancestor of the Earls of Marchmont. He appears as one of the Lords of the Congregation standing by the Protestant cause. He had a br
2 CONC other James Haldane, killed in the Raid of Stirling, 1585, who is called by Calderwood " brother-german to the Laird of Gleneagles," and was shot by Colonel Stewart's servant as he was laying hands on the Colonel, brother of the E
2 CONC arl of Arran.
2 CONT
