1 NAME Laurence Oliphant, 1st of Gask
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 24 MAR 1576
2 PLAC Newton of Pitcains, Perthshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 JUL 1632
2 PLAC Findo Gask, Perthshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Not to be confused with his cousin, https://www.geni.com/people/Laurence-Oliphant-5th-Lord-Oliphant/6000000010179043071?through=6000000220018707097, who married Lilias Drummond, and died without male issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Laurence Oliphant, 1st of Gask''' is the son of Laurence Oliphant of Newton and of Thrumster and Mary Rollo.2 He married Lilias Graham, daughter of George Graham, 2nd of Inchbrakie and Marjory Rollo, on 10 June 1606.1
2 CONT
2 CONT He purchased Gask, Perthshire from Laurence Oliphant, 5th Lord Oliphant.1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Maxtone-Graham Ethel.  ''The Oliphants of Gask : records of a Jacobite family'' (1910).  “The House of Gask.” Page 80 - < [https://archive.org/details/oliphantsofgaskr00maxtuoft/oliphantsofgaskr00maxtuoft/page/80/mode/2up Arc
2 CONC hive.Org] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT Laurence Oliphant of Ross and Lamberkin, and afterwards of Cask, eldest son of Lang Laurence, married before 1606, Lilias Graeme of Inchbrakie, the widow of William Colville of Condie. Lilias Graeme was the youngest of the five da
2 CONC ughters of the second Laird of Inchbrakie and his wife, Marjorie Rollo.1 Lilias had two daughters by her first husband, Catherine and Marioni Colville of Condie, and he was alive in 1601, as that was the year in which he sold Cond
2 CONC ie to Laurence Oliphant, servitor of William Oliphant, King's Advocate. Between 1601 and 1606 there is no exact evidence of the events in the life of Lilias,2 but during those years her husband died, and she married Laurence Oliph
2 CONC ant. '''His cousin, the fifth Lord Oliphant''', was disposing of his great estates, and bit by bit Laurence Oliphant bought the lands of Gask ; first, the lands of Ross in 1610, then Lamberkin in 1614, then Keirprow, Clathybeg and
2 CONC  Keirwoodhead. He bought Cowgask from John, Earl of Montrose. His Great Seal charter is dated 1625, from which date he is known as Oliphant of Gask. … Laurence Oliphant, the first Laird of Gask, died 22nd July 1632. He had been po
2 CONC ssessor of Gask only five years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The six children of Laurence Oliphant and Lilias Graham, four boys (3) and two girls, were all probably born at Ross : —
2 CONT
2 CONT #Sir Laurence Oliphant, 2nd of Gask,   d. 20 Jul 1679.  Married his cousin, Lilias Oliphant, daughter of Patrick, sixth Lord Oliphant.
2 CONT # Patrick Oliphant.  Married Margaret Mowat, daughter of James Mowat of Barrafirth. 
2 CONT # James Oliphant.  He was styled of Tomperran, and afterwards of Souterton. Buried at Gask, 5th April 1676.7 Married Janet Riddoch, daughter of Henry Riddoch of Tomperran.  
2 CONT # Thomas Oliphant, 1st of Rossie Hill,   d. Yes, date unknown. Only son Willam.
2 CONT # Jean Oliphant,   d. Yes, date unknown.  Married 1) John Drummond of Pitkellony 2) Gavin Drummond of Culdees 
2 CONT # Margaret Oliphant,   d. 30 May 1663.  Married Alexandrr Inglis of Craigmakerran.
2 CONT
2 CONT (3) There was also an illegitimate son, Alexander, mentioned, in 1621.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # Maxtone-Graham Ethel.  ''The Oliphants of Gask : records of a Jacobite family'' (1910).  “House of Gask. “ Page 80 - < [https://archive.org/details/oliphantsofgaskr00maxtuoft/oliphantsofgaskr00maxtuoft/page/80/mode/2up Archive.O
2 CONC rg] > 
