2 CONT
2 CONT About Sir John Sinclair, of Geanies and Dunbeath Biographical Summary "Sir John Sinclair, of Dunbeath, co Caithness, 2nd son of the Hon. George Sinclair of Mey, by Margaret, daughter of William (Forbes), Lord Forbes [S], which Geo
2 CONC rge was younger son of George, Earl of Caithness [S], is said to have been created a Baronet [S] 3 January 1631, with rem. to the heirs male of his body. He was M.P. [S] for Caithness-shire 1649-50. He married firstly, before 31 J
2 CONC uly 1634 (when she was living as his wife) Christian, daughter of Magnaus Mowat of Buchollie. He married secondly, Catherine (born 1619), daughter of Hugh (Fraser), Lord Lovat [S], by Isabel, daughter of Sir John Wemyss. He was li
2 CONC ving May 1650 (Act Parliament) but died s.p.m. probably shortly afterwards, when the Baronetcy became extinct. His widow married, as his second wife, Robert (Arbuthnott), 1st Viscount Arbuthnott [S], who died 10 October 1655. She 
2 CONC married, thirdly, in 1663, Andrew (Fraser) 3rd Lord Fraser [S], who died 22 May 1674." SOURCE: Complete baronetage; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 391
