1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 4th Earl of Montrose
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT John Graham, 4th Earl of Montrose (1573–1626) was a Scottish nobleman, Earl of Montrose from 1608 to the 1620s. He was for a time Lord President of the Privy Council of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Catholic, as the English ambassador William Asheby noted in November 1589, on the death of his uncle Mungo Graham, Master Household to James VI.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 31 January 1595, in a feud following the death of his kinsman John Graham of Hallyards, he fought with James Sandilands on the Royal Mile. There were over 100 pistol shots and Sandilands was wounded. In the confusion, a rumour 
2 CONC spread that King James was besieged in Holyrood Palace.[2] Sandilands' brother-in-law William Crauford, brother of the laird of Carse was killed.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was at court in Royston in England in 1614 and the court physician Théodore de Mayerne treated him for melancholy.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and Family
2 CONT Edit
2 CONT He married Margaret Ruthven, daughter of William Ruthven, 1st Earl of Gowrie and Dorothea Stewart. Their children included:
2 CONT
2 CONT James Graham, 5th Earl of Montrose, later 1st Marquess of Montrose.
2 CONT Lilias Graham, married Sir John Colquhoun of Luss, 1st Baronet.
2 CONT Elizabeth Graham
2 CONT Margaret Graham married Archibald Napier, 1st Lord Napier of Merchiston
2 CONT Dorothea Graham married Sir James Rollo, Younger of Duncrub.
2 CONT Katherine Graham
2 CONT Beatrix Graham married David Drummond, 3rd Lord Maderty.
