1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir William Graham of Braco, Knight and Baronet</strong>, who had a blench charter from his father of the lands of Braco, Drummawhance, and others, dated in 1585, and a liferent grant from his elder brother of the lands o
2 CONC f Killearn Ibert and Wester Carleston in 1590. He was created a Baronet of Nova Scotia 28 September 1625...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He married, first, Margaret Keith, daughter of William, Lord Keith, and widow of the Laird of Ludquhairn, by whom he had no children; and secondly, after 1609, Mary Edmonstone, daughter of Sir James Edmonstone of Duntreath, and
2 CONC  widow of John Cunningham of Cunninghamhead, by whom he had an only son."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/236/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VI, page 237-238
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n321/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 302
2 CONT --------------------
