2 CONT
2 CONT (98) Sir John Murray of Tullibardine , died 1613. He was served heir to his father 15th May, and to his grandfather 27th June, 1583. In 1590-92 he was M.P. for Perthshire. On 25th April 1604 he was created Lord Murray of Tullibard
2 CONC ine, and on 10th July 1606 Earl of Tullibardine, Lord Murray, Gask, and Balquhidder. He married, before 20th December 1576, Catherine, daughter of David, second Lord Drummond, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT 98(a) William (No. 99).
2 CONT
2 CONT 98(b) Captain John Murray, died before 13th February 1607. 98(c) Sir Patrick, Earl of Tullibardine (No. 124 below). 98(d) '''Sir Mungo, second Viscount Stormont''' (No. 126 below). 98(e) Robert Murray, living 1618.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT (126) '''Sir Mungo Murray OF Drumcairn''', fourth son of John, first Earl of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Tullibardine (No. 98), died s.p. March 1642. Under the special remainder {see first Viscount, No. 133) he became, in 163 1, SECOND Viscount Stormont and Lord Scone. He married, first, Anne, daughter of Sir  Andrew Murray of Arngos
2 CONC k and Balvaird (No. 132, a). She died 13th May 1639, and her Will was recorded at St. Andrews 13th January 1640. He married, second, 1639, Anne, daughter of John, first Earl of Wemyss, and widow of Alexander Lindsay of Edzell.
2 CONT --------------------
