1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JANET STEWART (OTHERWISE JONET STEWART)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Janet Stewart is the daughter of Sir Matthew Stewart of Minto [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/255/mode/1up Memoirs of the House of Hamilton]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Janet Stewart (Otherwise Jonet Stewart) married John Hamilton of Cambuskeith [https://archive.org/stream/heraldryofhamils00john#page/121/mode/1up Heraldry of the Hamiltons] They were married before 1 April 1538.  [http://catalo
2 CONC gue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f179%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hamilton+of+cambuskeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Birkwood writs, Lesmahagow, Lanarkshire, refe
2 CONC rence GD1/179/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to John Anderson, Janet Stewart (Otherwise Jonet Stewart) is the mother of three children: John Hamilton,  William Hamilton and David Hamilton [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/255/mode/1up Hamil
2 CONC ton Memoirs] G. Harvey Johnston, on the other hand, says that she is the mother of David Hamilton of Ladieton, and Thomas Hamilton of Monktonhill [https://archive.org/stream/heraldryofhamils00john#page/121/mode/1up Heraldry of the
2 CONC  Hamiltons]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 April 1538: Precept of sasine by William Cunynghame [Cunningham], knight, fiar of the earldom of Glencarne and lord of Kilmawris [Kilmaurs] in favour of John Hammiltoun [Hamilton] of Cambuskeith and Janet Stewart, his spouse,
2 CONC  of the lands of Ovirmure and Carlingcraig in the lordship of Lowdoun [Loudoun], bailiwick of Cunynghame, and sheriffdom of Ayr. At Edinburgh, 1 Apr, 1538. Witnesses: Patrick Hammiltoun of Bogsyd [Bogside], William Hammiltoun, bro
2 CONC ther of the said John Hammiltoun of Cambuskeith, Robert Ormstone [Ormiston], Sir James Walker, and Andrew McTene [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f179%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&
2 CONC k=cambuskeith&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Birkwood writs, Lesmahagow, Lanarkshire, reference GD1/179/1]'''
