1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lilias Drummond''' was the daughter of James Drummond, Lord Inchaffray, 1st Lord Maderty.2 and his wife Jean Chisholm.
2 CONT
2 CONT A contract for the marriage of Lilias Maderty and Laurence Oliphant, 5th Lord Oliphant was signed on 29 October 1603.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Laurence Oliphant, 5th Lord Oliphant and Lilias Drummond
2 CONT # Anne Oliphant+1 married Sir James Douglas, 1st Lord Mordington
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Genealogical memoir of the most noble and ancient house of Drummond" by David Malcolm 1808
2 CONT
2 CONT >Lilias Drummond, married to Lawrence, 5th Lord Oliphant, a man of a vast estate, who received 40,000 merks as her tocher, but who spent most of his immense fortune; to him she bore only one daughter, Anne Oliphant.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Article about the Oliphant clan, past and present: https://www.scottishfield.co.uk/culture/scottish-clan-is-like-a-phoenix-from-the-flames/
2 CONT
2 CONT >However, despite inheriting this vast and impressive wealth, the spendthrift nature of Laurence, the 5th Lord Oliphant (1583-1603) meant that every last acre was lost in his lifetime. For instance, Muirhouse was sold in 1605, fol
2 CONC lowed by the Caithness estates and Glensaugh the following year.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
