1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir Donald IV Mackay Kt, (1590-1649 in Denmark). Cr: Baronet 18 may 1627 with remainders to heirs male whatsoever and 1st Lord Reay created 20 June 1628 with remainder to his heirs male for ever bearing the name an
2 CONC d arms of Mackay. A further patent creating him Earl of Strathnaver was never completed owing to the Civil war., Fought under Christian IV of Denmark's Thirty year War against Germany Also under Gustavus Adolphus of Sweden 1629-30
2 CONC ; Royalist Civil war. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married (1) 1610 to Barbara, sister of 1st Earl of Seaforth, 
2 CONT
2 CONT married (2) 1631 (Annulled) to Rachel Winterfield,
2 CONT >1.1.1.1.2.1.1.1.2.3. (Second Marriage) Hon Donald Mackay, (1658-1680), Master of Reay, married 1677 to Anne Munro, with issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT  married  (3) 1631 to Elizabeth Thomson, married 
2 CONT
2 CONT (4) to Marjorie Sinclair of Stirkoke, and 
2 CONT
2 CONT also held a mistress, Lady Mary Lindsay, daughter of 11th Earl of Crawford
2 CONT >1.1.1.1.2.1.1.1.13. (illegitimate with Lady Mary Lindsay) Donald Mackay of Dysart, (1620 - 1659 Dysart), married  1640 to Isobel Ramsay, (illegitimate daughter of William Ramsay, 1st Earl of Dalhousie d. 1672), with issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.maltagenealogy.com/Libro%20d'Oro%20della%20Mediterranean/Mackay.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ====================
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a natural son by Mary Lindsay, daughter of David, eleventh Earl of Crawford." Complaint was made by his wife to the Privy Council in 1617 as to Lord Reay's ill-treatment of her in connection with his intimacy with Mary Lind
2 CONC say."
2 CONT
2 CONT Scottish Peerage Vol 7 pg. 167-169
2 CONT
2 CONT ==================
