2 CONT
2 CONT Donald Mackay, 1st Lord Reay1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #109197, b. March 1590/91, d. 1649
2 CONT Last Edited=21 Aug 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT      Donald Mackay, 1st Lord Reay was born in March 1590/91.2 He was the son of Hugh 'Du' Mackay and Lady Jane Gordon.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, fourthly, Marjorie Sinclair, daughter of Francis Sinclair of Stirkoke.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Barbara Mackenzie, daughter of Kenneth Mackenzie, 1st Lord Mackenzie of Kintail and Anne Ross, in August 1610.3,4 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, thirdly, Elizabeth Thomson in 1631.2 He died in 1649.1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He and Lady Jean Lindsay were associated'''.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT With remainder to heirs male whatsoever.2 With remainder to his heirs male for ever bearing the name and arms of Mackay (a further patent creating him Earl of Strathnaver was never completed owing to the Civil War).2 Royalist Civi
2 CONC l War England and Scotland.2 He was Justice of the Peace (J.P.) (Inverness and Cromarty in 1610.2 In 1612 Sutherland ).2 In 1616 knighted.2 In 1627 fought under CHRISTIAN IV OF DENMARK Thirty Years War Germany , such service proba
2 CONC bly winning him his peerage in that CHRISTIAN's n was CHARLES I, and 1629–30 under GUSTAVUS ADOLPHUS OF SWEDEN.2 He was created  1st Baronet Mackay on 18 May 1627.2 He was created  1st Lord Reay [Scotland] on 20 June 1628.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Donald Mackay, 1st Lord Reay and Elizabeth Thomson
