1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN SOMERVILLE OF CAMBUSNETHAN ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Liferenter of Over Mains and other lands in the Barony of Cambusnethan; afterwards John Somerville, junior of Cambusnethan, and then John Somerville of Cambusnethan'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Somerville of Cambusnethan, here treated, is the son and apparent heir of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Somerville-of-Cambusnethan-elder/6000000181021808823?through=6000000181112800898 On 23 December 1620 he gave his c
2 CONC onsent to a charter by which his father conveyed an annualrent of fifty pounds Scots from the lands and barony of Cambusnethan to Jean Somerville, daughter of the deceased Sir John Somerville of Carswell. [https://catalogue.nrscot
2 CONC land.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1207&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Jean+Somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD109/1207]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Somerville of Cambusnethan was served as heir to his deceased father, James Somerville of Cambusnethan, on 27 March 1630, and to his deceased grandfather, John Somerville of Cambusnethan, on the same date.  [https://books.
2 CONC google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=%20somervell&f=false Inquisitionem
2 CONC  Ad Capellam Domini Regis Tetornatarum etc. II]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stirnet reports that John Somerville of Cambusnethan, here treated, died in 1635. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ss4as/somerville02.php Stirnet: Somerville 02] It would appear that this may be wrong, however, becau
2 CONC se his youngest son Patrick Somerville stated that he died in March 1640, when he gave up his testament dative on 1 February 1672. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The Testament Dative of John Sommervell of
2 CONC  Cambusnethan, reference CC9/7/39]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Testament Dative and Inventory ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The testament dative and inventory of John Somerville of Cambusnethan, here treated, was given up by: "Patrick Somervell youngest lawfull son to the defunct as lawll creditor to him in suo far as the defunct was justlie adebted
2 CONC  & awand to him the sowm of 2000 mks Scots mony prinll sown 500 lbs mony foirsd of liquidat expenss with the @rent of the said prinll sowm frme the terme of Whitsunday 1634 yeirs extending now to the sowm of 265 lbs mony foirsd co
2 CONC nteinit in and band & obligatioune mad & granted be the defund to the said Patrick Somervell of the dait the [ blank ] day of Junij 1634 yeirs.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''At the time of his death, John Somerville of Cambusnethan was owed £400 Scots money, with £10 of liquidate expenses, by Sir John Hamiltoun of Bargany, knight, Sir John Hamiltoun of Carridden, knight, Sir John Hamiltoun of Broom
2 CONC hill, knight, and Gavin Hamilton of Raploch. [Note] William Hendersoun, merchant burgess of Glasgow, acted himself as cautioner for Patrick Somerville, and confirmation was granted to him on 2 February 1672. [National Records of S
2 CONC cotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The Testament Dative of John Sommervell of Cambusnethan, reference CC9/7/39]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000181317449028 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000181331996835 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000181317224997 Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: The bond for £400 mentioned here was subsequently assigned by Patrick Somervill, who is identified in the assignation as the brother of the deceased Sir James Somerville of Cambusnethan. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.
2 CONC uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1488&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+james+somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=&di=n NRS: GD109/1488]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 December 1620: Charter by James Somervell of Cambusnethem, with consent of John Somervell, his son and apparent heir, and James Somervell, son of said John, in favour of Jean Somervell, daughter of deceased Sir John Somervel
2 CONC l of Kerswell, kt., of annualrent of £50 scots from lands and barony of Cambusnethem, in sheriffdom of Lanerk. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1207&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=
2 CONC Jean+Somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/1207]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 March 1621: Signature of the lands of Over Mains of Cambusnethan granted to John Somerville (Somervell, Somervile, Somervill, Sommervell, Sommervile, Sommervill, Summervile). [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecat
2 CONC alogue/details.aspx?reference=SIG1%2f144%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+somerville&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register of Signatures, boxed series, reference SIG1/144/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 December 1620 and 15 February 1642: Extract bond by James Somervell, elder of Cambusnethan, John Somervell, his son, and James Somervell, his eldest son now living [Note], to infeft Jean Somervell, said James, elder's, prone
2 CONC voy, daughter of deceased Sir John Somervell of Kerswell, kt., eldest son of said John, in annualrent of £500 from lands and barony of Cambusnethan, reg. B. of C. and S., 24 January, 1624; with bond of relief by said Sir James Som
2 CONC ervell to Sir John Hamiltoune, elder, of Bargany, kt., Sir John Hamiltoune, younger, of Carridden, kt., his eldest son, Sir James Hamiltoune of Broomhill, kt., and Gavin Hamiltoune of Raploch, his cautioners, over £4 land of Nethe
2 CONC rtoun of Cambusnethan, premonition, renunciation, and ratification thereof, with consent of James Kincaid of that ilk, her spouse. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1208&st=1&tc
2 CONC =y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/1208]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: It is supposed that James Somervell, son of James Somerville, elder of Cambusnethan, was the eldest son living on 15 February 1642 and that his elder brother, John Somerville, must have died before this date. John's son, 
2 CONC Sir John Somervell of Carswell, died on 12 April 1621. [NRS: CC9/7/17]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 March 1621: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands of Over Mains of Cambusnethan in the Sheriffdom of Lanark, and various other lands in Cambusnethan, 
2 CONC to JOHN SOMERVILLE, junior of Cambusnethan, who is identified as the son and apparent heir of James Somerville, senior of Cambusnethan. These lands were to be held by the said John Somerville, junior, for his lifetime, following t
2 CONC he death of his father. James Somerville, senior of Cambusnethan, also resigned the lands and barony of Cambusnethan in favour of his grandson, identified as James Somerville, junior, son of the said John Somerville, junior of Cam
2 CONC busnethan. James Somerville, senior of Cambusnethan, reserved his own liferent, and an annualrent from the lands of Over and Nether Mains of Cambusnethan for his daughter-in-law, MARIE HAMMILTOUN, identified as the wife of John So
2 CONC merville, junior of Cambusnethan. The land and barony of Cambusnethan thus conveyed was to be held by James Somerville, junior, and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by his brother german Thomas Somervill and his lawful male hei
2 CONC rs, whom failing by his brother german Patrick Somerville and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by the nearest male heir of James Somerville, junior, bearing the name and arms of Somerville. [https://archive.org/details/registru
2 CONC mmagnisi08scot/page/48/mode/1up RMS 1620-33: charter number 148]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 December 1627: Bond by John Somervell of Cambusnethane and Sir James Somervell, fiar thereof, his son, to Sir John Hammiltoun of Lettrik, kt., to relieve him of bond by said John Somervell to Robert Mcoll, tailor, burgess of
2 CONC  Edinburgh, for 500 merks, to which said Sir John is cautioner. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1475&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+james+somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=&di
2 CONC =n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/1475]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 April 1629: Precept of Clare Constat granted by John, Earl of Mar Lord Erskine and Gareoche etc, liferenter of the barony of Carnewathe, and by James, Earl of Buchen, Lord of Ouchterhous, his son, fiar thereof, for infefting
2 CONC  John Somervell of Cambusnethane, son of the deceased James Somervell of Cambusnethane, as heir of his said father, in the lands of CARSWELL, lying within the barony of Carnewathe and sheriffdom of Lanark, the Over Lands of the to
2 CONC wn of Quodquen, and one cottage land of the lower town of Quodquen, those 44 acres of land lying in the north part of the common pasture and ground of the lands of Quodquen commonly called Newmaynes, and also in those 2 oxgates of
2 CONC  land commonly called Haisties Land, in the town of Newbiging, all lying within the said barony and sheriffdom. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD118%2f147&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=
2 CONC &ko=p&r=GD118%2f147&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Chancellor family of Shieldhill, Lanarkshire, reference GD118/147]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''(1593) 27 March 1630. JOANNES SOMERVELL de Cambusnethanm haeres Jacobi Somervell de Cambusnethan, patris.  xi. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=Hy
2 CONC jCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=%20somervell&f=false Inquisitionem Ad Capellam Domini Regis Tetornatarum etc. II]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''(1594) 27 March 1630. JOANNES SOMERVELL de Cambusnethan. haeres Joanni Somervell de Cambusnethan, avi. Xi. 232. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=H
2 CONC yjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=%20somervell&f=false Inquisitionem Ad Capellam Domini Regis Tetornatarum etc. II]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 February 1637 and 12 December 1672: Bond by Sir John Hamiltoun of Bargany, kt., Sir John Hamiltoun of Carridden, kt., Sir John Hamiltoun of Brumhill, kt., and Gavin Hamiltoun of Ropploche, to John Somervell of Cambusnethen, 
2 CONC for £400 scots, with assignation thereof by Patrick Somervell, brother of deceased Sir James Somervell of Cambusnethen, son of said John, to [blank]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=G
2 CONC D109%2f1488&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+james+somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/1488]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Nickname ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Somerville of Cambusnethan, here treated, was nicknamed "Harie Hott Spures" for his quarrelsome disposition.[https://archive.org/details/memorieofsomervi1815some/page/89/mode/1up Memorie of the Somervilles II: page 89]'''
2 CONT
