2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 December 1620 and15 February 1642: [Note 1] Extract bond (dated 23 December 1620) by James Somervell, elder of Cambusnethan, John Somervell, his son, and JAMES SOMERVELL, HIS ELDEST SON NOW LIVING [Note 2], to infeft Jean So
2 CONC mervell, said James elder's pronevoy, daughter of deceased Sir John Somervell of Kerswell, kt., eldest son of said John, in annualrent of £500 from lands and barony of Cambusnethan, reg. B. of C. and S., 24 January, 1624; with bon
2 CONC d of relief (dated 15 February 1642) by said Sir James Somervell  to Sir John Hamiltoune, elder, of Bargany, kt., Sir John Hamiltoune, younger, of Carridden, kt., his eldest son, Sir James Hamiltoune of Broomhill, kt., and Gavin H
2 CONC amiltoune of Raploch, his cautioners, over £4 land of Nethertoun of Cambusnethan, premonition, renunciation, and ratification thereof, with consent of James Kincaid of that ilk, her spouse. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrs
2 CONC onlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1208&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+kincaid&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/
2 CONC 1208]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note 1: Two quite separate documents are mentioned here. The first is an extract or copy of a document dated 23 December 1620, that was registered on 24 January 1624. The second document is a bond of relief dated 15 February 16
2 CONC 42. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note 2: It is supposed that James Somervell, son of James Somerville, elder of Cambusnethan, was the eldest son living on 15 February 1642 and that his elder brother John Somerville must have died before this date. John's son, 
2 CONC Sir John Somervell of Carswell, died in August 1620.'''
