2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1612: Assignation by John Stewart, lawful son to Walter, Lord Blantyre, to Sir Thomas Boyd of Bonschawe, knight, of that part of the decree obtained at the granter's instance on the 27 Feb 1612, against John Lowgie in Lochwood,
2 CONC  Gavin Lowgie, Arthur Lowgie there, James Paterson there, John Jackson and David Shanks, whereby they were decerned to restore to the complainer the Teind Sheaves of the Crown of the Sub-Deanery of Glasgow, parsonages of Cadder an
2 CONC d Monkland. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f544&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Walter+Lord+Blantyre&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1580&dt=1620&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burg
2 CONC h of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/544]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1612: Tack by John Stewart, lawful son to Walter, Lord Blantyre to Sir Thomas Boyd of Bollinschawe, knight, the Teind Sheaves, called 'The Parsonage Teinds' in the lands of Lochwood, Holmhead, Meddrois, etc for 19 years. Dated 
2 CONC St Andrews and Edinburgh, 30 Jun and 3 Jul 1612. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f545&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Walter+Lord+Blantyre&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1580&dt=1620&di=n National R
2 CONC ecords of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/545]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
