1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == REVEREND MR. JOHN SOMERVELL MA ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to the Memorie of the Somervilles, the Reverend Mr. John Somerville, here treated may be the fourth son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Somerville-of-Cambusnethan/6000000181364612826 : "The fourth from this gentle
2 CONC man is now Master John Somervill, minister of the gospell att Cramond in Mid-Lothian". [https://archive.org/details/memorieofsomerv11815some/page/449/mode/1up Memorie of the Somervilles I: 449]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary by the Fasti of the Church of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''JOHN SOMERVILLE [SOMERVELL],  a cadet of the family of S. of Cambusnethan ; M.A. (Edinburgh, July 1642); ord. to St Boswells 1662; trans, to Kirkcowan 1666 ; trans, to Glasserton 1667 ; trans, to West Calder 1668 ; trans, to Mi
2 CONC d-Calder 1672 ; trans, and adm. 1675 (G. R. Horn., 22nd Aug. 1678) ; deprived 2nd May 1689 for not reading the Proclamation of the Estates, etc. ; died at London, 1692. He marr. (1) Esther Scougall, and had issue — Janet (G. R. Sa
2 CONC s., xxix., 11): (2) 5th Feb. 1674, Katharine, daugh. of James Brown, merchant, burgess of Edinburgh (G. R. Sas., xli., 204), who survived him, and in whose right he entered burgess and guild- brother of Edinburgh, 27th Feb. 1689 ;
2 CONC  she succeeded to his estate, 12th Feb. 1692, and had issue — Margaret, born 30th Aug. 1675 ; James, born 17th May 1679 ; Hugh, born 7th July 1681 ; William, born 10th Dec. 1682; Anne, born 9th Jan. 1685 (marr., cont. 21st Aug. 17
2 CONC 04, George Dundas, surgeon - apothecary, Edinburgh : Edin. Sas., lxxvi., 230) ; John, born 19th Sept. 1686, died 24th March 1689 ; Robert, born 1st Oct. 1689; and three children who died in infancy. [https://archive.org/details/fa
2 CONC stiecclesiaesc01scot/page/11/mode/1up Fasti of the Church of Scotland I: 11]'''
