1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MR. JOHN DUNLOP OF THAT ILK (afterwards OF GARNKIRK) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Mr John Dunlop (1624) Mr John Dunlop of that ilk (1631) Mr. John Dunlop, merchant burgess of Glasgow (1634) Mr John Dunlop of Gartinkirk (1638) the late Mr John Dunlop of Garnkirk (1669) Magistri Joannis Dunlop de G
2 CONC arnkirk (1672)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Master John Dunlop, here treated, is brother of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Dunlop-of-that-Ilk/6000000223358701883?through=6000000223358984827. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/329/mode/1up RMS 162
2 CONC 0-1633: charter number 916] It follows that he is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Dunlop-of-that-Ilk/6000000223359039891. [NRS: GD3/1/1/56/7]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Dunlop of that Ilk ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''With regard to Mr. John Dunlop and the Dunlop estate, James Paterson said this. When his brother James was resisting the attempt of Charles I. to introduce Episcopacy: "the estate of Dunlop had been made over to John of Garnkir
2 CONC k, for the purpose of security. This deed was acted upon in 1633, when his brother took possession, and in five years after made resignation to his nephew. [https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyo02pateuoft/page/47/mode/1up A
2 CONC yr: 47] He is noticed as Mr. John Dunlop of that Ilk in 1631. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f683&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Dunlop&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1630&dt=1640&di=n NRS: G
2 CONC D8/683]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Dunlop of Garnkirk ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''With regard to Mr John Dunlop and the Garnkirk estate, the late Donald Whyte had this to say: John obtained the lands of Garnkirk and other subjects within the parish of Cadder in 1634, confirmed under the Great Seal , 27th Jun
2 CONC e 1636. [Newsletter of the Glasgow and West of Scotland Family History Society, No. 47 Autumn 1996, pp. 11-16 for the first part of Donald Whyte's scholarly account of the family of Dunlop of Garnkirk]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Foreign Merchant in Glasgow ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Dunlop of Garnkirk is third son of James Dunlop of that Ilk, and his wife Jean Sommerville. The date and place of his birth is not known. [Newsletter of the Glasgow and West of Scotland Family History Society, No. 47 Autum
2 CONC n 1996, pp. 11-16 for the first part of Donald Whyte's scholarly account of the family of Dunlop of Garnkirk]. Besides being a merchant, John Dunlop of Garnkirk appears to have been a banker. He built the original mansion house of
2 CONC  Garnkirk. [http://www.clandunlop.com/dunlop_manor_houses.htm Dunlop Manor Houses]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Burgess and Guild Brother of Glasgow ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 28 July 1631 Mr. John Dunlop, merchant was enrolled as as a burgess and guild brother of Glasgow by purchase [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso43scotuoft#page/81/mode/1up James R. Anderson, The Burgesses & Guild Br
2 CONC ethren of Glasgow, 1573-1750 (Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh, 1925), p. 81].'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Dunlop of Garnkirk died in March 1662. [https://archive.org/stream/exhibitionillust00glas#page/21/mode/1up Exhibition Illustrative of Old Glasgow 1894 (Glasgow Institute of Fine Arts), exhibit number 53 on page 21]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Testament Dative and Inventory ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 4 April 1665. [National Records of Scotland Hamilton and Campsie Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of John Dunlop of Gartinkirk, parish of Calder, reference CC10/5/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Additional Testament Dative ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 15 September 1668. [National Records of Scotland Hamilton and Campsie Commissary Court, Eik to the Testament Dative and Inventory of John Dunlop of Gartinkirk, parish of Calder, reference CC10/5/7]''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Dunlop of Garnkirk married Bessie Dunlop, daughter of Archibald Dunlop, merchant burgess of Glasgow, who was the widow of John Mackildune, merchant burgess there. The late Donald Whyte suggested that they were probably mar
2 CONC ried soon after he became a burgess and guild brother on 28 July 1631. [Newsletter of the Glasgow and West of Scotland Family History Society, No. 47 Autumn 1996, p. 11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/James-Dunlop-2nd-of-Garnkirk/6000000001499754914?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1508594594206&through=6000000009967091365
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Dunlop-of-Garnkirk/6000000069290346929?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1508594731973&through=6000000009967091365
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 April 1624: Obligation granted by James Dunlop of that ilk whereby on the narrative that he was indebted to Mr John Hutchisone, merchant in Glasgow in 4000 merks; he as son and heir to James Dunlop, his father, the deceased 
2 CONC becomes bound to obtain himself infeft in the said annualrent and being so infeft to infeft the said Mr John Hutchison, his heirs and assignees therein Dated at Glasgow Witnesses: Mr John Dunlop, his brother german and others [htt
2 CONC p://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f56%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+dunlop&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Ea
2 CONC rls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/1/56/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 July 1624: Charter by which James Dunlop of that Ilk confirms that he has given the lands of Hunthall and Over Auldhall to his brother german Master John Dunlop: "M. Joanni Dunlop". This charter was confirmed under the Great
2 CONC  Seal of Scotland on 7 December 1625. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/329/mode/1up RMS 1620-1633: charter number 916]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1631: Extract Assignation by William, Lord Blantyre, son and heir of the late Walter, Lord Blantyre, and taking burden on him for Mr John Stewart, his brother and with the consent of Sir Archibald Stewart of Finnart, in favour 
2 CONC of Robert Hamilton of Torrens, and Mr John Dunlop of that ilk, of a contract between the said Walter, Lord Blantyre, on the one part and Mr Patrick Walkinshaw, sub-dean at Glasgow, on the other part. The Assignation is dated at Ed
2 CONC inburgh and Glasgow, 28 Mar and 6 and 8 Apr 1633. Registered at Edinburgh, 19 Jun 1633. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f683&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Dunlop&ko=p&r=&ro=s&d
2 CONC f=1630&dt=1640&di=n National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/683]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 March 1634: "Robert Stirling in Garnkirk and John Stirling, his eldest lauchful sone," conveyed "the town and lands of Garnkirk" to "Mr. John Dunlop, merchant burgess of Glasgow, and Elizabeth Dunlop his spouse, and longest 
2 CONC liver." [http://www.clandunlop.com/dunlop_manor_houses.htm Dunlop Manor Houses]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 February 1638: Tack by Robert Hamilton of Torance and Mr John Dunlop of Gartinkirk to Robert, Lord Boyd of the parsonage teinds of the lands of Lochwood, Medros, Myvattis, etc. Dated at Edinburgh and Glasgow, 27 Feb and 6 Ap
2 CONC r 1638. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f692&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+dunlop&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, r
2 CONC eference GD8/692]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 November 1669: Renunciation by James Dunlop, now of Garnkirk, only son and heir to the late Mr John Dunlop of Garnkirk, to William, Earl of Kilmarnock, of an annual rent corresponding to the principal sum of 5,000 marks. [ht
2 CONC tp://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f854&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=garnkirk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/8
2 CONC 54]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 September 1672: JACOBUS DUNLOP, haeres Magistri Joannis Dunlop de Garnkirk, patris. xxxi. 108. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82
2 CONC Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=snippet&q=dunlop&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc., ii, Inquisitiones Gererales., entry number 5574]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/genealogicalheral01burk/page/434/mode/1up A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great Britain etc. By John Burke, Volume I. (Henry Colburn, London, MDCCCXXXV), pp. 434-6 for Dunl
2 CONC op of that Ilk]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/historyofcountyo02pateuoft/page/46/mode/1up History of the County of Ayr etc., By James Paterson. Vol. II (Thomas George Stevenson, Edinburgh, M.DCCC.LII), pp. 46-9 for Dunlop of that Ilk]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/dd/dunlop01.php Stirnet: Dunlop 01]'''
2 CONT # '''[Newsletter of the Glasgow and West of Scotland Family History Society, No. 47 Autumn 1996, pp. 11-16 for the first part of Donald Whyte's scholarly account of the family of Dunlop of Garnkirk]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://www.clandunlop.com/ Biographical Summary by Clan Dunlop] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John DUNLOP, 1st. of Garnkirk. Born in 1594 in Paisley, Renfrewshire, Scotland, John died in March 1662; he was 68. Before 10 November 1631, when John was 37, he married Elizabeth DUNLOP. They had the following children: 1. Jea
2 CONC n 2. James (1633-1695)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Critical Commentary: The birth date and place cited here are entirely speculative, as is his age at death and the date of his marriage, as also the birth of a daughter named Jean.'''
