2 CONT '''9 June 1648: Obligation by John Park in Househill for himself and others, to obey the Act of Parliament anent the levies of horse and foot to be provided by the tenants of Thomas Dunlop of Househill. At Paisley. [http://catalog
2 CONC ue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f288&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Thomas+Dunlop+of+Househill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/288]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 July 1692: Signet letters at instance of Thomas Dunlop, brother of deceased James Dunlop of that ilk, charging John, lord Bargeny, son and apparent heir of deceased Sir John Hammiltone of Bargeny, kt. to enter heir to his sa
2 CONC id father, to be pursued for payment of bond, (undated) by said deceased Sir John as cautioner for £1,000 scots. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f2167&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k
