2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 April 1623: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms possession of the five merk land of Crevoch in the Cunningham division of Ayrshire to John Lindsay of Crevoch-Lyndsay. The lands
2 CONC  in question had previously been resigned by James Dunlop of that Ilk, son of the deceased James Dunlop of that Ilk: "quas Jac. Dunlope de eodem filius et heres quondam Jacobi D. de eodem resignavit". James Dunlop of that Ilk's ch
2 CONC arter of resignation is dated 6 June 1617: "cum instrumento sasine diet,  terrarum date dicto Jac. D. tunc de eodem tanquam heredi dicti ejus patris,de data 6 Jun. 1617 [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/271/
2 CONC mode/1up RMS 1620-1633: charter number 748]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''23 July 1624: Charter by which James Dunlop of that Ilk confirms that he has given the lands of Hunthall and Over Auldhall to his brother german Master John Dunlop. This charter was confirmed under the Great Seal of Scotland on
2 CONC  7 December 1625. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/329/mode/1up RMS 1620-1633: charter number 916]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14, 26 and 30 July 1633: Extract bond by Sir James Somervell of Cambusnethane, kt., to Thomas Dunlop, brother of James Dunlop of that ilk, for £1,000 scots. Reg. B. of C. and S., 26 October, 1640. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.
2 CONC gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1213&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+Dunlop&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1601&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire,
2 CONC  reference GD109/1213]'''
