2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1626-36: Receipts, renunciations, contracts and related documents (mainly dated Nov-Dec, 1634) Being warrants of payments made by various individual including John Buchannan, son and heir of deceased James Buchannan of Sherifha
2 CONC ll [Sheriffhall] [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD124%2f17%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Sheriffhall&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ers
2 CONC kine Family, Earls of Mar and Kellie, reference GD124/17/6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 November 1628: REX, pro se et tanquam dominus dominus et regalitatis de Dumfermling, — cum consensu etc. (1. 8.), — confirmavit cartam quondam Jacobi Buchannan de Schirrefhall, — [qua, pro perimpletione literarum obligatoria
2 CONC lium de data presentium, concessit JOANNI BUCHANNAN filio suo legit, secundogenito inter se et Jeannam Lundie sponsam suam procreato, heredibus ejus et assignatis quibuscunque, — terras suas de Schirrefhall, cum manerie et carboni
2 CONC bus, in dominio de Mussilburghschyre, regalitate de Dumfermling, vic. de Edinburgh :— Reddend. regi tanquam domino etc. (ut sup.) 2 libras piperis nomine albe firme : — cum precepto sasine : — Salvo vitali redditu dictis Jac. et J
2 CONC ean.: — Proviso quod quandocunque dictus Jac. in vita sua duntaxat unum lit rois-noble (vel 16 mere.) in magna ecclesia Divi Egidii burgi de Edinburgh super premonitione 8 dierum (apud ecclesiam parochialem de Neatoun die Sabbathi
2 CONC  facta si dictus Joannes extra Scotiam fuisset) persolviaset, aut in manibua thesaurarii aut decani gilde dicti burgi consignasset, haberet regressum ad suprascripts ; et quod liceret  dicta suprascripta impignorare pro  . . . . .
2 CONC  Test. Dunc Buchaunane fratre dicti Jacobi, Antonio Quliyte scriba signeti regii, Alex. Blair ejus servitore (scriptore carte): — Apud Schirefhall, 14 Jan. 1627] [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/451/mode/1u
2 CONC p RMS 1424-1513, charter number 1322 on pp. 451-2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 January 1631: REX confirmavit cartam Joannis Buchanane de Schirefhall, — [qua, pro perimpletione literarum dispositions de data presentium, vendidit JOANNI STIRLING filio legit. Willelmi S. de Auchyle, heredibus ejus et assi
2 CONC gnatis quibuscunque, absque reversione, — terras de Schirefhall, cum manerie et carbonibus, in dominio de Mussilbrugh, regalitate de Dumfertnling, vic. Edinbrugh: — Salvo vitali redditu Jeanne Lundie matri dicti Jo. B.: — Reddend.
2 CONC  regi tanquani domino dominii et regalitatis de Dumfermling 2 librae piperis nomine albe firme : — cum precepto sasine : — Test. M. Wil. Stirling scriba, Jo. Williamsoun scriba signeto regio, Hen.W. ejus filio (scripture carte), J
2 CONC ac. Keir servitore dicti Jo. W. : — Apud Edinbrugh, 9 Dec. 1 630] [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/572/mode/1up RMS 1424- charter number 1701 on p. 572]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 November 1635: Discharge by John Buchanan, son of umquhil James Buchanane of Schirrefhall [Sheriffhall] to John, Earl of Mar, of annual-rent conform to a bond by the Earl to William Drummond of Riccartoune [Riccarton], assig
2 CONC ned to the said John Buchanan and Jean Drummond, his spouse. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD124%2f2%2f44&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Sheriffhall&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y Nat
