2 CONT ===The Kirklands of Staynlie===
2 CONT
2 CONT On 3 August 1611: '''William Porterfield and Alexander Porterfield on the one part and '''Gabriel, George, Jean, Agnes, Marion and Mary Porterfield,''' on the other part, entered into an agreement which led to a charter by which '
2 CONC ''William Porterfield of that Ilk transferred the Kirklands of Staynlie '''to his grandson George Porterfield, son of the deceased Alexander Porterfield younger of that Ilk.''' The charter was issued at the Manor House of Duchall 
2 CONC on 16 February 1616 and was witnessed by '''Alexander Porterfield, younger of that ilk,''' Robert Hamilton, apparent of Torrens, Master Daniel Cunynghame, minister at Kilmalcolm, Alexander Hamilton, apparent of Kirkton and '''Gabr
2 CONC iel Porterfield, his grandson.''' [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f7%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+hamilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland,
2 CONC  Montgomerie Papers, reference GD3/1/1/7/6] 
2 CONT
