1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===GEORGE PORTERFIELD===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Merchant: Lord Provost of Glasgow 1645-49===
2 CONT
2 CONT George Porterfield is the son of Alexander Porterfield of that Ilk, younger, and his wife Agnes Houston His date of birth is not known but he must have been of perfect age when he was enrolled as a burgess and guild brother of Gla
2 CONC sgow on 21 March 1623, and this suggests that he was born before 21 March 1602. [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso43scotuoft#page/60/mode/1up The Burgesses and Guild Brethren of Glasgow, p. 60]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Burgess and Guild Brother in Glasgow===
2 CONT
2 CONT George Porterfield was enrolled as a burgess and guild brother of Glasgow on 21 March 1623. The town council admitted him in right of his marriage to Jonat Patoun, the daughter of a deceased burgess. [https://archive.org/stream/sc
2 CONC ottishrecordso43scotuoft#page/60/mode/1up The Burgesses and Guild Brethren of Glasgow, p. 60]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT George Porterfield died in Rotterdam in 1675 and was buried in the French Church there. [http://www.theglasgowstory.com/story/?id=TGSBH07 The Glasgow Story: George Porterfield]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT George Porterfield married Jonat Patoun, daughter of James Patoun, merchant in Glasgow. [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso43scotuoft#page/60/mode/1up The Burgesses and Guild Brethren of Glasgow, p. 60] The marriage was b
2 CONC ooked at Glasgow on 14 November 1622. [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:XTYY-T2Q Glasgow Marriage Records]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/N-N-Porterfield/6000000055173156869
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Porterfield/6000000055171383153?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1488274807921&through=6000000045582690031
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Kirklands of Staynlie===
2 CONT
2 CONT On 3 August 1611: '''William Porterfield and Alexander Porterfield on the one part and Gabriel, George, Jean, Agnes, Marion and Mary Porterfield, on the other part, entered into an agreement which led to a charter by which William
2 CONC  Porterfield of that Ilk transferred the Kirklands of Staynlie to his grandson George Porterfield, son of the deceased Alexander Porterfield younger of that Ilk.''' The charter was issued at the Manor House of Duchall on 16 Februa
2 CONC ry 1616 and was witnessed by Alexander Porterfield, younger of that ilk, Robert Hamilton, apparent of Torrens, Master Daniel Cunynghame, minister at Kilmalcolm, Alexander Hamilton, apparent of Kirkton and Gabriel Porterfield, his 
2 CONC grandson. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f7%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+hamilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Montgomerie Papers, ref
2 CONC erence GD3/1/1/7/6] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Account===
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.theglasgowstory.com/story/?id=TGSBH07 The Glasgow Story: George Porterfield]
