1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  
2 CONT ===JEAN PORTERFIELD===
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Porterfield is the eldest daughter of Alexander Porterfield She was born in about 1588. [Lieutenant-Colonel George Hamilton, The House of Hamilton (Edinburgh, 1933), see pages 850-58 for an account of the Hamiltons of Torranc
2 CONC e] According to John Anderson, her father was Porterfield of that Ilk. [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/388/mode/1up Hamilton Memoirs, page 388]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Kirklands of Staynlie===
2 CONT
2 CONT On 3 August 1611 William Porterfield and Alexander Porterfield on the one part and Gabriel, George, Jean, Agnes, Marion and Mary Porterfield, on the other part entered into an agreement which led to a charter by which William Port
2 CONC erfield of that Ilk transferred the Kirklands of Staynlie to his grandson George Porterfield, son of the deceased Alexander Porterfield younger of that Ilk. The charter was issued at the Manor House of Duchall on 16 February 1616 
2 CONC and was witnessed by Alexander Porterfield, younger of that ilk, Robert Hamilton, apparent of Torrens, Master Daniel Cunynghame, minister at Kilmalcolm, Alexander Hamilton, apparent of Kirkton and Gabriel Porterfield, his grandson
2 CONC . [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f1%2f7%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+hamilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Montgomerie Papers, reference G
2 CONC D3/1/1/7/6] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Porterfield married Robert Hamilton of Torrance. [https://archive.org/stream/heraldryofhamils00john#page/90/mode/1up Hamilton Heraldry] She was his future wife on 5 July 1611 [Lieutenant-Colonel George Hamilton, The House of 
2 CONC Hamilton (Edinburgh, 1933), see pages 850-58 for an account of the Hamiltons of Torrance]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===She lends fifteen hundred merks to James Hamilton of Aikenhead===
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Porterfield lent fiftteen hundred merks to James Hamilton of Aikenhead. She mentions this fact in her last will and testament which was made at Glasgow on 28 December 1658: "Item thr being adebtd & awand to me be James Hamilt
2 CONC on of Aiknheid the soume of ane thousand merks conform to his band grantit to me thranent of the dait the sexteint day of November Jajvjc & fifty seven yeirs ..... Item thr being ane uthr ffyve hundreth merks in the hands of the s
2 CONC d James Hamiltoun for the qch he hes given band to Margaret & Agnes Hamiltouns his sisters at my desyre"[National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, reference CC9/7/32]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Porterfield died without having had any children. [Lieutenant-Colonel George Hamilton, The House of Hamilton (Edinburgh, 1933), see pages 850-58 for an account of the Hamiltons of Torrance] She was alive on 28 December 1658 b
2 CONC ut died before 7 February 1659. She probably died on or soon after 28 December 1658, at Glasgow in Lanarkshire, Scotland. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, reference CC9/7/32]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Her Testament Testamentar===
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean Porterfield made her last will and testament at Glasgow on 28 December 1658. The opening sentence identifies her as the: '''relict of the deceist Rot Hamilton of Torrence'''. She left the following legacies: "Item thr being a
2 CONC debtd & awand to me be James Hamilton of Aiknheid the soume of ane thousand merks conform to his band grantit to me thranent of the dait the sexteint day of November Jajvjc & fifty seven yeirs of the qlk soum I heirby leive in leg
2 CONC acy to '''Elisabeth & Mary Porterfield dochts laull to umqle Gabriell Porterfield of Hapland''' the sumn of sex hundreth merks mony eqlly betwext them vix three hundreth merks to each of them Item ane hundreth merks of the forsd t
2 CONC housand merks I heirby leive in legacy to Jeane Wallace dochter to umqle Wm Wallace sometyme of Johnstoun Iem ane uther hundreth merks throf I leive in legact to Jeane Fergushill dochter to the lait Laird of Fergushill Item thr be
2 CONC ing anu uthr ffyve hundreth merks in the hands of the sd James Hamiltoun for the qch he hes given band to Margaret & Agnes Hamiltouns his sisters at my desyre I heirby declair that they sall have each of them the eqll half throf I
2 CONC tem as for the rest of the forsd soume of ane thousand merks money eftir my debts ar payed & the charges of my funeral defrayed I leive the haill remenant throf to Mr George Wallace son to the sd umqle Wm Wallace". [National Recor
2 CONC ds of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, reference CC9/7/32]
