2 CONT On 3 August 1611 William Porterfield and Alexander Porterfield on the one part and Gabriel, George, Jean, Agnes, Marion and Mary Porterfield, on the other part, entered into an agreement which led to a charter by which William Por
2 CONC terfield of that Ilk transferred the Kirklands of Staynlie to his grandson George Porterfield, son of the deceased Alexander Porterfield younger of that Ilk. The charter was issued at the Manor House of Duchall on 16 February 1616
2 CONC  and was witnessed by Alexander Porterfield, younger of that ilk, Robert Hamilton, apparent of Torrens, Master Daniel Cunynghame, minister at Kilmalcolm, Alexander Hamilton, apparent of Kirkton and Gabriel Porterfield, his grandso
