1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 79. John Doig of Cessintullie  (James, Paul, James, James, James, Walter, John, Walter) was born about 1595 in Of Kilmadock, Perth, Scotland. Source: https://www.doig.net/DOIGK.htm. See also: https://www.wikitree.c
2 CONC om/wiki/Doig-57
2 CONT
2 CONT John acquired the Mill of Cessintully by assignation of his father on 11 Feb 1634.  Thereafter the tenants of the local farms did not cooperate in using the mill, a monopoly, and making proper payments.  In 1637 John Dog brought s
2 CONC uit against the local farmers to exclusively use his mill and pay the required portion. Included as defendants in his suit were John Dog, portioner of Murdieston, and David Dog of Ballingrew. In 1642 James Dog of Gartincaber claim
2 CONC ed Cessintully.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was a witness to christenings in 1634 and 1647. A bond is recorded about 1647 by John Dog at the Mill of Cessentullie, brother germain to Paul Dog, there, to John Johnston of Stirling. [General Register of Deeds, Vol. 533.]
2 CONT
2 CONT John had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # +      116 M        i.  John Doig  was born about 1638.
