1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Patrick Jr McKie (Patrick Sr), b. aft. 1520 in Minnigaff Kirkcudbright Scotland;  deceased aft. 1591 in Scotland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in 1550 in Garlies, Wigtown, Scotland, Margaret Stewart , b. in Garlies Wigstownshire Scotland; deceased in unknown, daughter of Alexander Stewart [born in Of, Garlieston, Wigtownshire, Scotland. He was the son of Alexa
2 CONC nder STEWART and Elizabeth KENNEDY and Margaret Dunbar [born Abt. 1511 in Clugston, Scotland]. Children of Patrick Jr McKie and Margaret Stewart were as follows:
2 CONT * Duncan McKie
2 CONT * Patrick McKie
2 CONT * Alexander McKie 
2 CONT * Anne Mackie, b. 1560, Larg, Dumfriesshire, Scotland1  d. date unknown.She married Alexander Hannah on 1582 in Sorbie Castle, Scotland   , son of Donald Hannah.
2 CONT =================
2 CONT
2 CONT Chart from "The Clan Mackay" - families of McKee or McKie or Mackie living in Galloway; living in time of Mary, Queen of Scots - 1542-1569; succeeded by grandson Alexander in 1591; "The Book of Mackay" states that he was married i
2 CONC n 1550 to Margaret, dau of Alexr Stewart of Garlies and had sons Alexr, Duncan of Palgown, and Patrick
2 CONT
2 CONT History of the Lands and Their Owners in Galloway FHL 941.49 H2m 1994 states that Patrick M'Kie married three times, and Margaret Stewart was his third wife, and mother of two children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Book of McKee, p 233 states that Patrick McKe was burgess of Wigtoun, 1575
2 CONT
2 CONT Kirkcudbright Sheriff Court: P 271 1591 "The quhilk day the customes of Monygolff within the Clauchane and parrochin thairof with the commodetie of the regratoris thairin is set for ane yeir to Patrik McKie of Larg for the payment
2 CONC  of xx merkis money at Candilmes and Lambes be equall portiouns and Thomas Hall is become cawtionar theirfoir and he to releif him."
2 CONT
2 CONT Charter 1574 - History of Galloway - Edinburgh; in Rough Sketch of M'Kie family 1911, he states: "He [Patrick M'Kee] married Margaret daughter of Sir Alexander Stewart of Garlies, and Margaret daughter & heiress of Sir Patrick Dun
2 CONC bar of Clugston, as appears from a grant by him to her dated 2d May 1582, and confirmed 1st August 1595. Her tocher was 1000 merks." 
2 CONT
2 CONT =================================
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Patrick of Larg, m. in 1550 Margaret, dau. of Alexr.
2 CONT Stewart of Garlies, and by her had issue :—
2 CONT * Alexr., of whom follows
2 CONT * Duncan of Palgown ; and 
2 CONT * Patrick.
2 CONT
2 CONT pg. 354
2 CONT
