1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir John Vans of Barnbarrock and Ulster, Ireland.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT James Gordon of Barncrosh, parish of Tongland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret, daughter of Sir John Vaus of Longcastle, parish of Kirkinner, and had issue— John and Robert afterwards in succession, Viscount Kenmure.
2 CONT
2 CONT  In 1621 she pursued him for a divorce for sundry adulteries said to have been committed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lands & Their Owners - Buittle Parish  By P. H. McKerlie - Published in 1877. http://www.buittle-and-kelton-churches.org.uk/buittleHistory/lands.asp
2 CONT
2 CONT  Lived at Barnbarroch, Wigtownshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Sir Patrick Vans of Barnbarroch, II and Catherine Vans (Kennedy)
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Margaret Vans of Barnbarroch (MacDowall of Garthland)
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Rev. John Vans; Joseph Vance and Margaret Vans
2 CONT
2 CONT  Brother of Patrick Vans, III; Alexander Vans; Robert Vans; Eupheme Vans; Catherine Vans; Florence Vans; Mary Vans; Elizabeth Vans and Jean Vans 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Half brother of Isobel Vans; Grissell Vans; Margaret Vans and Janet Vans
2 CONT
2 CONT ========================
2 CONT Sir John Vans of Barnbarroch1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #132695, b. circa 1574, d. 1642
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=3 Nov 2010 Consanguinity Index=0.51%
2 CONT      Sir John Vans of Barnbarroch was born circa 1574.2 He was the son of Sir Patrick Vaus, Lord Barnbarroch and Katherine Kennedy.1 He married Margaret Macdowall, daughter of Uchtred Macdowall, 10th of Garthland and Margaret Stew
2 CONC art, before 1597.1,2 He died in 1642.1
2 CONT      He was Commendator of Crossraguel in 1587.2 He held the office of Gentleman of the Chamber, to King James VI and I.1 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Wigtownshire between 1617 and 1621.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir John Vans of Barnbarroch and Margaret Macdowall
2 CONT  1.Sir Patrick Vans of Barnbarroch+1 d. 1673
2 CONT  2.Andrew Vans of Craigdhu+3 d. c 1661
2 CONT  3.Janet Vans1
2 CONT  4.Margaret Vans+1
2 CONT  5.Grizzell Vans+1
2 CONT  6.Florence Vans+1
2 CONT  7.Joanna Vans1
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT  1.[S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 263. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pe
2 CONC erage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT  2.[S2127] Jamie Vans, "re: Agnew Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 5 February 2007. Hereinafter cited as "re: Agnew Family."
2 CONT  3.[S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 2483.
2 CONT
