2 CONT History of the Lands and Their Owners in Galloway, FHL #941.49 H2m 1994, v 1, pg 364: "Helen Vaus, was then under age [at the death of her father in 1567], and became a ward of the crown, the lands being held from the Sovereign. T
2 CONC he wardship, &c,., were given to Sir John Bellenden of Auchinvole. Under this authority, Sir John gave her a choice of husband from the elder sons of four of the proprietors in the district, all of whom she refused....[he] gave th
2 CONC e said Helen to choose whether she would marry one of these four persons underwritten, equal to her in living and blood; that is to say--" Uchtred M'Dowall son of Wm, Andro Agnew, son of Patrick, William M'Culloch, son of Symon of
2 CONC  Mertoun, and John M'Culloch, son of John of Torhouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wigtown Inquisitions Speciales Q941 A21 Vol 1 list Helena Vaus (vel Vans) Jun 23 1574, haeres Alexandri Vaus (vel Vans) de Barnbarroch, patris--Drumgorgane in parochia de Kirkinver. 
