1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR THOMAS DALYELL OF THE BINNS Baronet ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Thomas Dalyell of the Binns, Baronet, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Katharine-Drummond/6000000008948330907?through=6000000008947218574
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Thomas Dalyell of the Binns, Baronet, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-Murray/6000000222308210866?through=6000000008947218574. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54s
2 CONC cotuoft/page/76/mode/1up The Binns Papers I: 383] The marriage was booked on 18 April 1682, at Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Marriages, reference OPR.685/1] They were married by Mr. Jo
2 CONC hn Robertson. They were married by Mr. John Robertson. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso16scotuoft/page/173/mode/1up Edinburgh Marriages 1595-1700: 173]''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Binns Papers ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 April 1682: Marriage Contract between Captain Thomas Dalyell, younger of Binns, and Agnes Murray, widow of Mr. John Ellies, younger of Eliestoun, whereby the said Agnes assignes to the said Captain Thomas an annualrent of 18
2 CONC 00 merks on the lands of Eliestoun, lying in the lordship of Kilpunt and sheriffdom of Linlithgow, and further the said Agnes renounces any terce that may fall to her on the death of the said captain Thomas, unless he provide one 
2 CONC willingly during his lifetime. Dated at Edinburgh 17 April 1682: Witnesses, John Elies of Eliestoun, younger, John Murray, brother to the laird of Levingsloun, Captain Thomas Dalyell in Colonel James Douglas's Regiment under the P
2 CONC rince of Orange, James Hay, W.S., and John Gourlay his servitor (writer of the contract). (Signed) "Thomas Dalyell. Agnes Murray," and the witnesses. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft
2 CONC /page/76/mode/1up The Binns Papers I: 383]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: Captain Thomas Dalyell in Colonel James Douglas's Regiment under the Prince of Orange', here mentioned, is the younger brother of Captain Thomas Dalyell, younger of Binns.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Agreement between Dame Agnes Murray, widow of the late Mr John Eleis of Eleistoun, and now wife of Sir Thomas Dalyell of Binns, and the said Sir Thomas for his interest on the one part, and Elizabeth and Christian Eleis, daught
2 CONC ers and heirs portioners of the said late Mr. John Eleis, with consent of David Scot of Scotstarvet, husband of the said Elizabeth, and Lieutenant-Colonel John Dalyell, husband of the said Christian, on the other part, whereby the
2 CONC  said Sir Thomas and his wife discharge the said Elizabeth and Christian Eleis and their husbands of the sum of 600 merks yearly, being a part of the sum of 1800 merks claimed by the said Dame Agnes Murray under her marriage contr
2 CONC act with her first husband, and in virtue of a clause of reservation in a bond of tailyie and provision made by her said first husband in favour of John Eleis her son, with destination to her said daughters ; and they assign the r
2 CONC emaining 1200 merks yearly to the said David Scot and John Dalyell during the lifetime of Mr. John Eleis of Eleistoun, and the sum of £1000 after the said Mr. John's death, payable during the lifetime of the said Dame Agnes Murray
2 CONC . Dated at Edinburgh 15 December 1691, and written by William Trent, servant of James Hay of Carribber. Witnesses, Thomas Johnston, writer in Edinburgh, and the said William Trent. (Signed) "Thomas Dalyell, Agnes Murray, Elizabeth
2 CONC  Eleis, David Scot, Jo. Dalyell, Christ. Eleis," and the witnesses. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/91/mode/1up The Binns Papers II: 435]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 November 1685:  Patent of Baronetcy in favour of Captain Thomas Dalyell of Binns 7 November 1685 In Latin : Translation) James, by the Grace of God King of Great Britain, France and Ireland, Defender of the Faith, to all hone
2 CONC st men to whom our present letters shall come, Greetings. . . . . We give, grant and confer, on the said Captain Thomas Dalyell and after his death on Thomas Dalyell, his eldest son and his heirs male and of tailyie following him 
2 CONC in hereditary right to the estate and family of Binns, the Title, rank, degree and honour of Knight Baronet, and by these presents We make, constitute and appoint them Knights Baronets for all time . . . . . In witness whereof We 
2 CONC have ordered Our Great .Seal to be appended to these presents. Given at Our Court of Whythall, 7 November 1685 and of our reign the 1st year. Sealed at Edinburgh the seventh day of December 1685. [https://archive.org/details/scott
2 CONC ishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/80/mode/1up The Binns Papers I: 396]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 November 1697: Renunciation by Sir Thomas Dalyell of Binns and Dame Agnes Murray, his second wife, of her jointure of 12 chalders victual, to which, as his second wife, she was entitled under the provisions of a bond of taily
2 CONC ie and provision granted by the late General Thomas Dalyell of Binns, of date 5 May 1673. When the said bond was granted, the said Thomas Dalyell's first wife, Katherine Drummond, was still alive. Dated at Binns, i November 1697. 
2 CONC Witnesses and signatures as in No. 455. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/95/mode/1up The Binns Papers II: 485]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 August 1687: Signature of the lands of Meikle Parklie granted to Sir Thomas Dalziel, Agnes Murray, his wife and William Dalziel (Dalyel, Dalyell, Dalzell, Dalziel). [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/det
2 CONC ails.aspx?reference=SIG1%2f41%2f18&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=agnes+murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Register of Signatures, boxed series, reference SIG1/41/18]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 June 1711: Letter to the laird of Houstoune [Houstoun] from David Scott [of Scotstarvet], concerning the funeral of "Lady Binns" [Dame Agnes Murray, 2nd wife of Sir Thomas Dalyell [Dalziel], 1st baronet of Binns], mother-in-l
2 CONC aw of said David and Aunt of said laird of Houstoune [Houstoun].Dated at Edinburgh. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD30%2f1779&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+dalyell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&
2 CONC df=1700&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Shairp family of Houston, West Lothian, reference GD30/1779]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Marriage Records of Edinburgh ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 April 1682: Dalziel (Daliell, Dalyale, Dalyell, Dalzell, Dalziell) of Binnes, Thomas, younger ; Agnes Murray, widow of Mr, John Eleis, younger, advocate, married by Mr. John Robertson 18 Apr. 1682. [https://archive.org/detai
2 CONC ls/scottishrecordso16scotuoft/page/173/mode/1up Edinburgh Marriages 1595-1700: 173]'''
2 CONT                      2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 April 1682: Murray. Agnes, widow of Mr. John Eleis, younger, advocate ; Thomas Daliell of Binnes 18 Apr. 1682. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso16scotuoft/page/504/mode/1up Edinburgh Marriages 1595-1700: 504]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/n2/mode/1up The Binns Papers 1320-1864. Part I. 1320-1685( Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh, 1936), pp. pp. 1-80]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/n86/mode/1up The Binns Papers 1320-1864. Part II. 1686-1864. (Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh, 1936), pp. 81-146]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso16scotuoft/page/n6/mode/1up The Register of Marriages for the Parish of Edinburgh, 1595-1700. Edited by Rev. Henry Paton, MA., General Register House (Scottish Record Society, Edin
2 CONC burgh, 1908), 770 pp.]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://archive.org/details/cu31924092524408/page/n353/mode/1up Biographical Summary] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''"Captain Thomas Dalziell [or Dalyell] of Binns, co. Linlithgow, s. and h. of Gen. Thomas Dalyell, of the same, a distinguished cavalier, held a command at the battle of Worcester, and who, after the Restoration, was Commander i
2 CONC n Chief of the forces in Scotland, by Agnes, da. of John Ker, of Cavers, was a Capt. in the army; suc. his father 1 Oct. 1685, on account of whose services, apparently, he was, a month later, cr. a Baronet [S.], 7 Nov. 1685, as ab
2 CONC ove "provydit to his eldest son and heirs male and tailzie succeiding him in estate of Binns". He m. Katharine, da. of Sir William Drummond, of Riccaton, by Magdalen, da. of Thomas Dalyell, of Binns." [https://archive.org/details/
2 CONC cu31924092524408/page/n353/mode/1up Complete Baronetage; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 334]'''
