1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MARGARET DALYELL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Binns Papers ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 September 1695: Marriage Contract between James Bell, younger, tenant in Easter Auldcathie, and Margaret Dalyell, natural daughter of General Thomas Dalyell of Jjinns, with consent of Sir Thomas Dalyell of Binns, her brother,
2 CONC  whereby the said James Bell binds him to provide 200 merks to each child of the marriage, and the said Sir Thomas binds him to pay 1000 merks as tocher with another 1000 merks, being half of the 2000 merks left by the will of the
2 CONC  said late General to the late Jean Drummond, sister of the laird of Riccartoune, and left in legacy by the said Jean to the said Margaret Dalyell. Dated at Binns, 7 September 1695, and written by Robert Masterton, writer in Edinb
2 CONC urgh. Witnesses, William Dalyell, younger son of the said Sir Thomas, James Allan, his gardener, and the said Robert Masterton. (Signed) "James Bell, Tho. Dalyell, Margaret Dalyell (could not write)," and the witnesses. [https://a
2 CONC rchive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/93/mode/1up The Binns Papers II: 447]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/n2/mode/1up The Binns Papers 1320-1864. Part I. 1320-1685( Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh, 1936), pp. pp. 1-80]'''
