1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Cavendish, 1st Duke of Devonshire KG PC (25 January 1640 – 18 August 1707) was a soldier and Whig statesman, the son of William Cavendish, 3rd Earl of Devonshire and Lady Elizabeth Cecil.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Cavendish became Member of Parliament for Derby in 1661. A Whig under Charles II of England and James II of England, he was leader of the anti-court and anti-Catholic party in the House of Commons, where he served as Lord 
2 CONC Cavendish. He was a strong supporter of the "Glorious Revolution" of 1688 which brought William III of Orange to the throne, signing as one of the Immortal Seven the invitation to William. After the revolution, he was a leading Wh
2 CONC ig, serving as William's Lord Steward, and was created the Duke of Devonshire (1694) and also Marquess of Hartington in recognition for his services. He married Lady Mary Butler (1646–1710), daughter of James Butler, 1st Duke of O
2 CONC rmonde and his wife, Lady Elizabeth Preston, on 26 October 1662. He rebuilt Chatsworth House. He was also a famous womaniser.
2 CONT
2 CONT Devonshire and Lady Mary Butler had four children:
2 CONT *Lady Elizabeth Cavendish (1670–1741), married Sir John Wentworth, 1st Baronet and had issue
2 CONT *William Cavendish, 2nd Duke of Devonshire (c. 1672 – 4 June 1729)
2 CONT *Lord Henry Cavendish (1673 – 10 May 1700)
2 CONT *Lord James Cavendish (d. 14 December 1751)
2 CONT
2 CONT Cavendish was given an honorary MA by Cambridge University in 1705.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT See also
2 CONT *Chatsworth House – includes an account of the Duke's reconstruction of the house.
2 CONT *List of deserters from James II to William of Orange
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT *1.^ Venn, J.; Venn, J. A., eds. (1922–1958). "Cavendish, William". Alumni Cantabrigienses (10 vols) (online ed.). Cambridge University Press. 
2 CONT *Leo van de Pas genealogies From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Cavendish,_1st_Duke_of_Devonshire
2 CONT *____________________
2 CONT *''''''William Cavendish, 1st Duke of Devonshire1
2 CONT *''''''M, #10208, b. 25 January 1640/41, d. 18 August 1707
2 CONT *Last Edited=31 Dec 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.0%
2 CONT *''''''William Cavendish, 1st Duke of Devonshire was born on 25 January 1640/41.1 He was the son of William Cavendish, 3rd Earl of Devonshire and Lady Elizabeth Cecil.1 He married Lady Mary Butler, daughter of James Butler, 1st Du
2 CONC ke of Ormonde and Elizabeth Preston, Baroness Dingwall, on 26 October 1662.1 He died on 18 August 1707 at age 66.1
2 CONT *''''''     He succeeded to the title of 4th Baron Cavendish of Hardwick, co. Derby [E., 1605] on 23 November 1684.1 He succeeded to the title of 4th Earl of Devonshire [E., 1618] on 23 November 1684.1 He was one of the seven who 
2 CONC signed the invitiation to William of Orange to come to England,a dn was one of the first to take up arms on his behalf on his arrival.1 He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) in 1689.1 He was invested as a Privy C
2 CONC ounsellor (P.C.) in 1689.1 He held the office of Lord Steward of the Household between 1689 and 1707.1 He succeeded to the title of 1st Marquess of Hartington, co. Derby [England] on 12 May 1694.1 He succeeded to the title of 1st 
2 CONC Duke of Devonshire [England] on 12 May 1694.1 He has an extensive biographical entry in the Dictionary of National Biography.3    
2 CONT *''''''Children of William Cavendish, 1st Duke of Devonshire and Lady Mary Butler
