1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.ebooksread.com/authors-eng/alexander-mackenzie/history-of-the-munros-of-fowlis-with-genealogies-of-the-principal-families-of-th-kca/page-40-history-of-the-munros-of-fowlis-with-genealogies-of-the-principal-familie
2 CONC s-of-th-kca.shtml Alexander Mackenzie. History of the Munros of Fowlis with genealogies of the principal families of the name: to which are added those of Lexington and New England. (page 40)]
2 CONT
2 CONT THE MUNROS OF KATEWELL
2 CONT
2 CONT I. George Munro, fifth son of Robert Munro, fourteenth  Baron of Fowlis, killed at the battle of Pinkie in 1547, was 
2 CONT the first of this family. He married with issue, among  others — 
2 CONT
2 CONT n. '''George Munro''', who received the lands of Katewell, and married, first, Catherine, daughter of Hector  Mackenzie, IV. of Fairburn, with issue —
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Hector, who died before his father, unmarried. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Catherine, who married with issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Euphemia, daughter of John  Munro, I. of Pittonachy, progenitor of Novar, with issue —
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Andrew, who died before his father, unmarried. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. David, who succeeded his father. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Florence, who married Murdo Mackenzie, Lord  Kintail's Chamberlain of the Lewis, and natural son of  Kenneth Mackenzie, HL of Davochmaluag, with issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Ann. 
2 CONT
2 CONT George married thirdly, Agnes, only daughter of Hugh  Munro, V. of Coul, and IV. of Balconie, with issue — 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Agnes, who married Hugh Munro, H. of Mid- Swordale, with issue — George, who went to the German  wars and died there. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his third and only surviving son,  HL David Munro
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
