2 DATE BEF 4 JUN 1616
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "II. <strong>Hector Munro</strong>, who entered the army, and rose to the rank of Major. He married Isabel, daughter of James Dunbar of Tarbat, with issue — 
2 CONT * Robert, his heir and successor. 
2 CONT * John, who, like his father, entered the army
2 CONT * Christian, who married Alexander Mackenzie, progenitor of the Mackenzie families of Applecross and Coul, with issue. 
2 CONT * Helen, who married Robert Munro, VI. of Coul, and V. of Balconie. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hector appears to have sold or " tochered " the Assynt estate to his son-in-law Alexander Mackenzie of Coul, who gave it to his son, Kenneth, who in 1644, appears as proprietor. Hector however had purchased for his son the lands o
2 CONC f Inveran and of Achness, from John Gordon of Embo. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at Inveran before the 4th of June, 1616, and was succeeded by his son."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmunroso00mack#page/470/mode/2up History of the Munros of Fowlis: with genealogies of the principal families of the name to which are added those of Lexington and New England]; Alexander
2 CONC  Mackenzie; 1898; page 470
