1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William, of Mid-Swordale, parish of Kiltearn, who married Euphemia, daughter of Hugh Ross, I. of Achnacloich, with issue - 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1, Hugh, who married Agnes, daughter of George Munro, II. of Katewell, with issue - George, who went to the German Wars with his father and his chief the Black Baron of Fowlis in 1626, where father and son died. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2, George, who married Marjory, daughter of Hugh Ross, with issue - Hugh, and John, "who went to the battle of Worcester with the army," and Donald. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3, Hector 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4, Robert, who also fought at Worcester, and his two nephews, Hugh and John, and several others were banished by Cromwell to the New England States of North America, in 1652. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmunroso00mack#page/466/mode/2up/ History of the Munros of Fowlis with genealogies]  
