1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Colin Falconar</strong>, born 1623, son of William F. of Dunduff and Beatrix Dunbar ; educated at St Leonard's College, St Andrews ; ord. to Essil 2nd Oct. 1651 ; trans, to Forres 24th March 1658 ; promoted to Bishopric o
2 CONC f Argyll 5th Sept. 1679 ; trans. 7th Feb. 1680 ; app. to Bishopric of Moray 15th April and installed 5th Sept. 1680 ; sat in the Parliaments of 1681, 1685, 1686; died at Spynie Castle 11th Nov. 1686, and was buried in St Giles Chu
2 CONC rch, Elgin. His portrait is at Eden Court, Inverness. He marr. 24th July 1648, Lilias (died at Elgin 6th May 1688), daugh. of William Rose of Clava, and had issue — 
2 CONT * William, min. of Dyke
2 CONT * Alexander, apprenticed to Andrew Home, merchant, Edinburgh, 11th Feb. 1674
2 CONT * Isobel
2 CONT * Jean (marr. 15th Aug. 1678, Beroald Innes, Min. of Alves)
2 CONT * Hugh, commissary clerk of Inverness."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc00scot#page/352/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. VII, page 352
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft#page/244/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. V, page 245
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT  	Minister and Archdeacon of Moray Colin Falconer
