1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/n/i/c/Garrett-C-Nicholson/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0503.html /familytreemaker.genealogy.com....]; 
2 CONT ===Elizabeth Cochrane (b. 1580, d. date unknown)===
2 CONT Elizabeth Cochrane (daughter of William Cochrane and Margaret Montgomerie) was born 1580 in Cochrane, Abbey, Renfrewshire, Scotland, and died date unknown. She married Alexander Blair on 24 Jul 1593 in ,,Renfrewshire, Scotland, so
2 CONC n of John Blair and Grizel Semple.
2 CONT ===More About Elizabeth Cochrane and Alexander Blair:===
2 CONT * Marriage: 24 Jul 1593, ,,Renfrewshire, Scotland.
2 CONT * Children of Elizabeth Cochrane and Alexander Blair are:
2 CONT >* +William Cochrane, b. 1605, Cowdon, Ayrshire, Scotland, d. 1685, Dundonald, Ayrshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://quod.lib.umich.edu/e/ecco/004896980.0001.000/1:93?rgn=div1;view=fulltext
2 CONT
2 CONT XIV. ELIZABETH, daughter and heiress
2 CONT of William Cochran of that ilk, married to her cousin Alexander Blair, a younger son of John Blair of that ilk, (an ancient and honou∣rable family in the shire of Renfrew) by Gri∣zel his wife, daughter of Robert lord Semple, who, 
2 CONC immediately after his marriage, assumed the name and arms of Cochran, according to the above entail; all which appears from a charter under the great seal of king James VI. of the lands and barony of Cochran,*&c. to and in favours
2 CONC  of Alexander Cochran, alias Blair, third lawful son of John Blair of that ilk, and Elizabeth Cochran his spouse, third lawful daughter of William Cochran of that ilk, dated 7th February 1601. He got also a charter under the great
2 CONC  seal,* of several other lands, Alexandro Cochran de eodem, dated anno 1618. He was a man of singular virtue and probity, and greatly improved the estate of the family. By the said Elizabeth Cochran, he left is∣sue seven sons and 
2 CONC two daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sir John his heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Sir William of Cowdon, who succeed∣ed his brother.
