1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Lady Sophia Lindsay:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p2051.htm#i20501
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Sophia Seton [1]
2 CONT *F, #20501
2 CONT *Last Edited=24 Mar 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.41%
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Sophia Seton married Sir David Lindsay, 1st Lord Lindsay of Balcarres, son of John Lindsay of Balcarres, Lord Menmuir and Marion Guthrie, on 16 February 1611/12 at Dunfermline, Fife, Scotland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Alexander Seton, 1st Earl of Dunfermline and Lilias Drummond.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT From 16 February 1611/12, her married name became Lindsay.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Lady Sophia Seton and Sir David Lindsay, 1st Lord Lindsay of Balcarres
2 CONT *1. Alexander Lindsay, 1st Earl of Balcarres+[1] b. 6 Jul 1618, d. 30 Aug 1659
2 CONT
