2 CONT
2 CONT MR. HUGH LEE, 1100 acs, in Petomeck freshes above Puscatoway, on the Wwd. side of the river, bounding Sly. upon Mr. Claies land, Nly, along the river & parallel to Mr. Cley. 15 July 1657, p. 114, (170). Trans. of 22 persons: Jonat
2 CONC han Marrow, Mary Marrow, Dorithy Marrow, Wm. Browne, Wm. Hanniver, Geo. Wilson, Hannah Lee, Mr. David Linsey, Anne Murrall, Joshua Esto, Anne Moore, Junr., Anne Moore, Senr., Dan Lile, Jno. Carr, Eliz. Parry, Mary Harris, Eliz. Ha
2 CONC rdinge, Mary Barkinton, Anne Murrall, Joshua Estoe, Wm. May, Rob. Smart.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Note by compiler: Thousands of Virginia's early settlers arrived in the colony as a result of the headright system. Under this system, anyone who paid for his transportation (or someone else's transportation) to Virginia was enti
2 CONC tled to receive 50 acres of land for each immigrant transported to Virginia at his expense. In order to receive a land patent under the headright system, an individual would petition the county court for certification of these rig
2 CONC hts. The certificate was then recorded in the county court minute books. The petition for a certificate was usually filed soon after the arrival of the immigrants, while proofs of the claim where fresh. The documents certifying th
2 CONC ese rights, formally termed "transportation rights," but commonly called "headrights," were used as paper currency and freely sold, bartered or assigned to others at or near the time of certification. For that reason they could ha
2 CONC ve remained in circulation for a considerable time before ultimately being "tendered" for land. Before 1705, these rights could have been claimed for multiple arrivals of the same person. Assuming that Mr. David LINSEY, who was tr
2 CONC ansported to VA by Mr. Hugh LEE, was the same person as Rev. David LINDSAY, he arrived in VA no later than July 15, 1657, when Mr. Hugh LEE was granted a patent for transporting 22 persons, including David LINSEY, to Virginia. How
2 CONC ever, as shown elsewhere in these notes, the Rev. David LINDSAY was in VA before July 15, 1657.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Cavaliers and Pioneers, Patent Book 4, pp. 374-375:
2 CONT
2 CONT MR. DAVID LINDSEY, 236 acs. Northumberland Co. upon Perries Cr, 23 Mar. 1657, p. 207, (302). Beg. on sd. Cr., running to head of the branch parting this from land in possession of Richard White, Carpenter. 210 acs. granted unto Th
2 CONC omas Willford 10 Nov. 1651, assigned to Edward Henly, reassigned to sd. Wilsford, who assigned to sd. Lindsey; 26 acs. granted Thomas Wilsford 1 Aug. 1653 & assigned as above noted. Trans. of 1 pers. Renewed 18 Mar. 1662.
2 CONT
