2 CONT David Lindsey
2 CONT Son of Sir Hierome Lindsey of the mount. Lord Lyon-king-at-arms of Scotland, was born at South Leith, Scotland, Jan 2, 1603, and was rector of Yeocomico parish, Northumberland county, Virginia. He died April 3, 1667, leaving an on
2 CONC ly daughter Helen, who married Captain Thomas Opie, who has descendants in Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT This stone was put over him replacing the original stone, when his grandson Capt. Thomas Opie was interred with him having died on the 16th November of 1702.
2 CONT
2 CONT The original stone marking Lindsey appears lost to history although a report from 1904 suggests that the Smithsonian accepted it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birthdate: January 2, 1603
2 CONT Birthplace: Annatland, , Angusshire, Scotland
2 CONT Death: Died April 3, 1667 in Northumberland, VA, USA
2 CONT Immediate Family:
2 CONT Son of Sir Jerome Lindsay of Annatland and Margaret Lindsey
2 CONT Husband of Susanna Lindsey
2 CONT Father of James Lindsay and Helen Lindsay
2 CONT Brother of Robert Lindsay and Helen Muirhead
2 CONT Half brother of Annas Lindsay; Margaret Lindsay; Marjory Lindsay; Rachel Lindsay; Alexander Lindsay and 5 others
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT According to an account done by a relative of the Lindsay family in 1849, the
2 CONT epitaph read as follows:
2 CONT Here lyeth ye body of that Hold and Reverent Devine Mr. David Lindsay
2 CONT late Minister of Yeocomico, born in the Kingdom of Scotland, ye first and
2 CONT lawful sonne of ye Rt. Honorable Sir Hierome. Lindsay K'nt of ye Mount
2 CONT Lord-Lyon_king-at-Arms, who departed this life in ye 64th year of his age
2 CONT ye 3rd April Anno Dom 1667
2 CONT as well as the following:
2 CONT Here also lyeth the body of Capt. Thomas Opie Jr. of Bristol, grandson of
2 CONT Mr. David Lindsay who departed this life 16 Nov 1702..
