1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James Lindsay (1623 - 1674) was the son of Sir Jerome Lindsay (1565 - 1642) and his second wife Agnes (1590 - 1624), who he married in 1606.   James' half brother David was born in 1603, and reached America in 1645
2 CONC .  James arrived in America between 1635 and 1647.
2 CONT * http://rootedinfoods.com/52-ancestors-15-the-conundrum-of-james-lindsay/
2 CONT * https://www.genealogieonline.nl/en/genealogie-richard-remme/I533035.php
2 CONT * https://www.geni.com/people/Lady-Agnes-Lindsay-Of-Belstane/6000000001089706084?through=6000000007237425318.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The wife of James Lindsay is unknown, but they had four children: Caleb, Joshua, Adam and William.  Some records show that they were born in Scotland, while others suggest that they were born in Essex, Virginia.  James had a land 
2 CONC grant  for 390 acres in Gloucester County, Virginia (Patents6, 1666-1679 Reel 6, page 549, Virginia State Library, Richmond, Virginia.).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # +Caleb Lindsay, b. 1664, Scotland159, d. August 20, 1717, St Mary, Essex /  Gloucester County, Virginia.
2 CONT # JOSHUA LINDSEY, b. 1666; d. 1720.
2 CONT # ADAM LINDSEY, b. 1668; d. 1751.
2 CONT # WILLIAM LINDSEY, b. 1670.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT # Quoted from June Hunt's book, "The Family of James Lindsay".....June states; this material was taken from Scott's Peerage by Paul, Pioneers and Makers of Arkansas by Josiah Shinn, Virginia Magazine of Biography and History, Mrs.
2 CONC  Kearney's Papers on file in the Mississippi Archives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.clanlindsay.com/sln_v1_n4.pdf
2 CONT * http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/h/e/n/Lori-Henshaw-Bessemer/FILE/0016text.txt
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lindsey of the Mount, Fife
