1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ANNA MURRAY Lady Kennet ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Agnes Murray (1627) Annas Murray 1628) Annas Murray (1629) Annas Murray (1631) Anna Murray (1633) Annas Murray (1635) Anna Murray (1638) Anna Murray (1640) Annas Murray (1641) Annas Murray (1642)  Anna Murray (1644)
2 CONC  Anas Murray (1646) Anna Murray (1647) Anna Murray (1664) Annas Murray (1656) Anna Murray (1671)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 March 1627: Charter by Mr Robert Bruce of Wester Kennet, (in implement of a Contract of Marriage, entered into between him, and Margaret Colvill, relict of Patrick Murray of Perdewis, on behalf of Agnes Murray their daugter; 
2 CONC with consent of James Colvill of Balbedie, Mr Robert Colvill Minister of Culross and Mr Alexander Colvill of Blair, Justitiar Depute of Scotland, her Trustees;) to the said Agnes Murray, his future spouse, in liferent, of the half
2 CONC  of the lands of Wester Kennet, lands called the Cruiked lands, and Petfoulden, lying in the barony and bounty of Clackmannan - To be holden of the said Robert Bruce, of and under Sir Robert Bruce of Clackmannan Knight, and Robert
2 CONC  Bruce, fiar thereof, his son, for payment of a half penny yearly, as the proportion of a penny, for the whole lands of Wester Kennet. Witnesses Mr Robert Colvill Minister of Culross, Mr Bernard Gib, son of John Gib of Knoch, Norm
2 CONC an Blackadder, son of Patrick Blackadder of Milnhills, and George Lundie, son of the deceased Robert Lundie, in Dysart -Dated at Dunfermline. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD11%2f115
2 CONC &st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=agnes+murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Bruce Family of Kennet, Clackmannanshire., reference GD11/115]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 March 1627: Charter by Sir Robert Bruce of Clackmannan Knight and Robert Bruce fiar thereof, verbatim ratifying and confirming the foregoing Charter, GD11/115, by Mr Robert Bruce of Wester Kennet, to Agnes Murray his future s
2 CONC pouse, in liferent, of the half of the lands of Wester Kennet, and others, therein mentioned. Witnesses Robert White Junior in Clackmannan, Mr David Kinghorn Writer in Dysart, and David Wightman, servant of the said Sir Robert Bru
2 CONC ce Dated at Clackmannan. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD11%2f116&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=agnes+murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Br
2 CONC uce Family of Kennet, Clackmannanshire, reference GD11/116]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 November 1640: Renunciation by Anna Murray spouse of Mr Robert Bruce of Wester Kennet (vide GD11/115) bearing that by Contract Matrimonial, entered into between her and her said husband, she stood infeft in liferent in the h
2 CONC alf of the lands of Wester Kennet, but she having, in consideration of her said husbands estate, and the debts contracted upon the said lands, in winning and drying of the Coal therein, as also in consideration that Elizabeth Gaw,
2 CONC  mother of the said Robert Bruce, was also infeft in the other half of said lands of Wester Kennet, and others, Therefore, and for the love she has and bears to David Bruce, apparent of Wester Kennet, her son, and for the well-bei
2 CONC ng of the House thereof, she renounces her said liferent on said land, and restricts herself to the rents thereof, and her right to the coal, competent to her, by said contract, except what she shall use in her own house. Witnesse
2 CONC s Mr Edward Wright Minister of Clackmannan, Robert Masterson of Parkmill, sheriff Depute of Clackmannan, and Mr Patrick Morrison Notary - Dated at Clackmannan. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?re
2 CONC ference=GD11%2f133&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=anna+murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Bruce Family of Kennet, Clackmannanshire, reference GD11/133]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 November 1664: Testament of Anna Murray, spouse of Mr Robert Bruce of Wester Kennet, in the parish of Clackmannan and diocese of St Andrews; who died in the month of March last, given up by the said Mr Robert Bruce her Execu
2 CONC tor Dative, and confirmed by Alexander Monro, Commissary of Stirling - Dated at Stirling. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD11%2f169&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=anna+murray&ko=p&r=&ro=s
2 CONC &df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Bruce Family of Kennet, Clackmannanshire, reference GD11/169]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 June and 25 June 1656: Clackmannanshire: Disposition by David Bruce of Kennets, eldest son and apparent heir of Robert Bruce of Schanbody, to Annas Murray, lady Kennet, his mother, of the Wodebank and other lands lying in th
2 CONC e lands of Easter Kennet, in implement of his marriage contract with Marjory Young, daughter of David Young of Kirktoun, 12-25 June 1656. Because his father "intends and purposes to use policy and mak industry" in the lands of Cra
2 CONC igtoun "by erecting and building of some saltpannes and salter houses"; the said David being also obliged after his father's death to furnish his mother with "two carts of small coalles and one cart of great coalles for her awin f
2 CONC yre weeklie and for brewing of her awin and her childrens drink ... she alwayis payand the expenses of hewing and bearing allennerly and careying them home to her awin durre". [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue
2 CONC /details.aspx?reference=GD214%2f151&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=David+Young&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of Professor Robert K. Hannay, reference GD214/151]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 December 1671: Charter by King Charles II ratifying and confirming Contract Matrimonial, and Disposition therein contained; entered into between David Bruce now of Kennet, with consent of the now deceased Mr Robert Bruce of K
2 CONC ennet, his father, and Anna Murray his mother, on the one part, and Marjory Young, with consent of David Young of Kirktoun, her father, on the other part (vide GD11/158), in the whole heads and articles thereof - Dated at Edinburg
2 CONC h. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD11%2f180&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+bruce+of+kennet&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Bruce Fami
2 CONC ly of Kennet, Clackmannanshire, reference GD11/180]'''
