1 NOTE {geni:about_me} David Forrester of Little Denovan, who had the lands of Arngibbon  apprised from him by Duncan Forrester of Kilhorn who thereafter had a  confirmation under the Great Seal dated 18 June 1631.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. firstly, Margaret, natural daughter of James Erskine of Balgounie, by whom he  had issue ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT secondly, to Janet, daughter of Mr. James Forrester of Logie, by whom he had no apparent issue, and
2 CONT
2 CONT  thirdly, Margaret Marshall, (she was widow of Robert Burne, Merchant in Stirling). 
2 CONT
2 CONT By his first wife he was father of 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 b Thomas Forrester of Little Denovan
2 CONT
2 CONT 2b} David Forrester, became a Merchant in Stirling and d. before 22  February 1672. He was father of : 2c} Margaret Forrester, to whom Mr. Thomas Forrester, Minister at  Alva, was appointed Tutor-at-law on 22 February 1672.3
2 CONT
2 CONT 2b} Margaret Forrester, whom Charles II. is said to have fallen in love  with when he came to Stirling. She m. firstly, to Napier of  Boquhapple, and secondly, to Gavin Norrie of Norrieston.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2b} Mary Forrester, m. Robert Stevenson, Provost of Stirling.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2b} Jean Forrester, who dsp.
