2 CONT From: "Joe Slavin" <jsla@loc.gov>  Subject: [LIVINGSTON-L] Ann Livingston -Reply  Date: Wed, 17 Mar 1999 15:21:08 -0500 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Well this is interesting, because the Thomas Livingston who
2 CONT  married Mary Chiles and another Chiles since he had two wives was of
2 CONT  the Livingston line of Poropotank Creek, King & Queen Co., VA... and
2 CONT  was son of Thomas Livingston I (b 1731 in Caroline Co., VA) who was
2 CONT  son of Cornelius Livingston (b abt `710 in King & Queen Co., VA) who
2 CONT  was son of John Livingston III who was son of John Livingston II who
2 CONT  was son of John Livingston I all of Poropotank Creek in Stratton Major
2 CONT  Parish in King & Queen Co., VA.. John I being first transported into
2 CONT  VA before or in the year 1650.. allegedly being born in Scottland...
2 CONT
2 CONT  Thomas Livingston II (who married Mary Chiles and the other
2 CONT  Chiles) was born in Caroline Co., VA, but the family moved to South
2 CONT  Carolina.. where he and his brother James Todd Livingston lived...
2 CONT **** Discussion anyone..?? 8-) 8-)
2 CONT  Joe jsla@loc.gov
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LBKZ-4SY
2 CONT
2 CONT During the last few years of his life, his father Sir David must have lost most of his property, as John inherited nothing from him, and does not appear to have assumed the baronetcy. SIR JOHN, 6th of Dunipace, married Annabella (
2 CONC sic Arabella) Young, succeeded his father in 1634, and that same year sold the estate to Sir Robert Spottiswoode. (THE LANDS AND LAIRDS OF DUNIPACE by John C. Gibson 1903). Hence, his immigration to America.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ** Many more generations to add. (8/30/20)
