1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jan. 24. 1640 Alexander Erskyne de Barnes, patruus Marjorie Erskyne filiae quondam Willielmi Erskin burgensis de Aberdein, propinquior agnatus, id est consanguineus ex parte patris dictae Marjoriae - Inquisitionum 
2 CONC ad Capellam domini regis retornatorum, quae in publicis archivis Scotiae adhuc servantur, abbreviatio, Volume 2
2 CONT
2 CONT 1642. Feby. 18. Exhibition and Delivery. Marjorie Erskine, daughter and heir or apparent heir to Wm. Erskine, burgess of Abd., and Alexr. Erskine of Barnes her Tutor v. Patrick Straquhan in Kinaddie. Decree for exhibition and deli
2 CONC very of a number of Bonds granted in favor of the Pursuer's father was pronounced. Letters of Tutory, dated 8 Dec., 1641, and a Receipt by the Defender for the Bonds in question, dated 22 June, 1639 were produced. The Defender was
2 CONC  cited to give his oath of verity, but did not appear. - Decree Books : Vol. VIIl., Contents
