1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Leslie-3021
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine Leslie was born in 1640.   Catherine Leslie was the  sister of Rev Dr John Leslie, Rector of Derricolan, who was also R. of Urney.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Rev James Hamilton, MA of Montgavelin Castle, co. Donegal ''eldest son of Rev Andrew Hamilton, Preb of Kilskerry.''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/hh4aa/hamilton50.php Stirnet - 'Hamilton50']
2 CONT
2 CONT *i.	'''James Hamilton of Mountgavelin''' (b 1638, d 1690, Donagheady & Taghboyne, Archdeacon of Raphoe) 	m. '''Catherine''' '''Leslie''' (dau of James Leslie by Catherine, dau of Alexander Conyngham, Dean of Raphoe)
2 CONT **a.	'''Andrew Hamilton''' (b 1669, d 22.09.1753, rector of Donagheady & Taghboyne, Archdeacon of Raphoe) 	Andrew's wife is named Anne by 'HamiltonHistory' but Sarah by TCB. m. (before 1703) Anne or Sarah Conynghame (dau/heir of H
2 CONC enry (not Sir William) Conynghame of Castle Conynghame)
2 CONT **b.	'''William''' Hamilton (d 1729, Archdeacon of Armagh) 	m. (1701) Catherine Leslie (b 1682, d 1740, dau of Henry Leslie, Archdeacon of Down ('grandson (not son) of Henry, Bishop of Meath'))
2 CONT **c.	'''Judith''' Hamilton 	m. (c1700) '''Alexander Colhoun''' (rector of Templecarne)
2 CONT **d.+	other issue including '''James''' (b 1765, a 1693), '''Ezekeal''' (b 1680, a 1703)
2 CONT
2 CONT Validated https://www.geni.com/people/Jane-Hamilton/6000000012060174275 married https://www.geni.com/people/Oliver-McCausland-MP/6000000008973472352?through=6000000008973773298 as child - her husband named her brothers in his Will
2 CONC .
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT The House of Leslie Records say daughter of John Leslie, Burke’s Irish records say daughter of Col. James Leslie. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Leslie-3021 claims:
2 CONT
2 CONT “Catherine was born in 1640. She is the daughter of James Leslie and Isabella Conyngham.”
2 CONT
2 CONT However, according to “THE FAMILY OF LESLIE OF TARBET”
2 CONT
2 CONT Historical Records of the Family of Leslie from 1067 to 1868-9 ..., Volume 3 By Charles Joseph Leslie Page 330 [http://books.google.com/books?id=lyENAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA330#v=onepage&q=&f=false GoogleBooks] 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT “II.   John Leslie, married Catherine Cunningham, and had issue -
2 CONT
2 CONT * I. The Rev. Dr. John Leslie.
2 CONT *  II. '''Catherine, married to '''Archdeacon''' Hamilton'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT “John Leslie died 26th December 1648."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikitree is citing From _Burke's Irish Family Records_ American Edition, London, 1976? Leslie (Co. Kerry)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT This family is a cadet branch of the LESLIES of Wardis (see Burke's Peerage, LESLIE of Wardis, Bt) JAMES LESLIE, of Milltown; 4th son of William Leslie, 4th of Wardis, Falconer to King James VI and I (see Burke's Peerage, LESLIE o
2 CONC f Wardis, BT); m Margaret Erksine, dau of the Laird of Pittodrie, and d in hosp in Aberdeen 1620, leaving issue (with a yr son) COL JAMES LESLIE, served in King Charles I's Army in Ireland, and in Civil War 1641, m Isabella, dau (
2 CONC one of 27 children by one wife) of Rev. Alexander Conyngham, Dean of Raphoe (see Burke's Peerage, CONYNGHAM, M) and had issue, JOHN (Rev) of whom presently.
2 CONT * Catherine, m. Rev. James Hamilton, MA, of Montgavelin Castle, Co Donegal, eldes son of REV. ANDREW HAMILTON, Pres of Kilskerry, and had issue. He d 1689. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.dib.ie/biography/hamilton-william-a3764 DICTIONARY OF IRISH BIOGRAPHY] Contributed by
2 CONT Bergin, John
2 CONT
2 CONT >Hamilton, William (d. 1729), clergyman and author, was the second son of James Hamilton (1638–c.1689), archdeacon of Raphoe and chaplain to the earl of Arran (qv). James was at the siege of Derry, and took a prominent part in neg
2 CONC otiations in the spring of 1689 between Derry leaders and Jacobite commanders.  William, '''who had at least two brothers and two sisters''', attended TCD, graduating BA 1691, MA 1696 and LLB 1700 …  … 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
