2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Leslie-3019
2 CONT
2 CONT Leslie of Tarbet Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Col James Leslie and Isabella Conyngham, daughter of Rev Alexander Conyngham, Dean of Raphoe.
2 CONT
2 CONT He raised in 1688, a company of Foot and a troop of Dragoons, and at their head performed services so important that the King rewarded him by grants of estates.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the owner of considerable property in Ireland, much of which he acquired through support of King William III cause. He was ordained 30 October 1661. Appointed Rector of Urney, county Tyrone 1672
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marion (Mariana), daughter of Rev. H Galbraith
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT # John, who fell at Aughrim, died unmarried
2 CONT # James, settled in Kerry, married Sarah, daughter of Col. Kellie, and had a daughter and three sons.
2 CONT # George who left issue
2 CONT # Elizabeth died young
2 CONT # Isabella married Thomas Knox
2 CONT # Lettice married Walter Johnson
2 CONT # Catherine married Thomas Enraght
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1700.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Leslie-3019
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine Leslie, sister of Rev Dr John Leslie, Rector of Derricolan, was also R. of Urney.  She married Rev James Hamilton, MA of Montgavelin Castle, co. Donegal eldest son of Rev Andrew Hamilton, Preb of Kilskerry.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Col James Leslie and Isabella Conyngham, daughter of Rev Alexander Conyngham, Dean of Raphoe.
