1 NOTE {geni:about_me} III.— Mr. Alexander Skene of Newtyle.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 15th January, 1625, Alexander Skene, eldest son of Robert Skene, burgess of Aberdeen, is admitted burgess "jure paternitatis et dispens. cum jure jurando quia pupillus est et infra setatem " ; and, on 20th June, 1648, he served
2 CONC  heir to his father, Robert Skene, and is infeft
2 CONT in the tenement " in vico lemurum."
2 CONT
2 CONT On 26th August, 1646, he was married at Kirkaldie to Lilias Gillespie, daughter of Mr. John Gillespie, minister of Kirkaldie who died soon after.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1656 we find him one of the magistrates of Aberdeen ; and in 1657 he acquired, from Sir Alexander Forbes of Foveran, the lands of Newtyle, in the Parish of Foveran.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1669 "Alexander Skene, a magistrate in Aberdeen, his wife Lilian became a quaker, also Alexander Skene himself. He narrates of him-self that having once before his conversion to quakerism bitterly reviled the quakers, he became
2 CONC  seized with the complaint called Cynicus Spasmus, by which his mouth continually turned about, which lasted sometime" (MS.E). In 1677 he published a pamphlet with the title " The Way Cast up," and on the 5th of the fifth month, 1
2 CONC 679, he wrote an address to the Presbyterians, entitled "'' A^Plain and Peaceable Advice to those called Presbyterians in Scotland,''" by Alexr. Skene (London, 1681).
2 CONT
2 CONT His other literary works, including MS.A., are noticed in the Introduction.
2 CONT
2 CONT The arms of "Mr. Alexander Skene of Newtyle" are thus recorded in the Lyon Register? " Parted per chief azur and gules three skenes argent hefted and pomelled or, surmounted of as many woolf-heads couped of the third." Crest : " A
2 CONC  dexter hand holding a corona triumphalis." Motto : " Sors mihi grata cadet."
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife, Lilias Gillespie, who died in 1697, he had the following
2 CONT children : —
2 CONT
2 CONT # I. Robert Skene, born 29th October, 1647 ; died young.
2 CONT # ' II. John Skene.
2 CONT # III. Lilias Skene, baptised 31st August, 1651.
2 CONT # 
2 CONT
2 CONT
