2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Oxford, Maryland
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Oxford is one of the oldest towns in Maryland. While Oxford officially marks the year 1683 as its founding because in that year it was first named by the Maryland General Assembly as a seaport, the town began between 1666 and 1668
2 CONC  when 30 acres (120,000 m2) were laid out as a town called Oxford by William Stephens, Jr.. By 1669 one of the first houses was built for Innkeeper Francis Armstrong (see Talbot County Land Records, A 1, f. 10/11).
2 CONT ===
2 CONT "Weeping Spring" - 200 a., surveyed 10-13-1663 for Francis Armstrong
2 CONT
2 CONT 13 Aug 1665 - Francis Armstrong, planter, and Frances, his wife, to William Killman, planter, 400 Acres on the north side of James Island, Dorchester County. this was witnessed by Thomas Paddison (sic) (Talbot County Land Records,
2 CONC  by Leonard. page 5)
2 CONT
2 CONT Mar. 17, 1667: Francis Armstrong Gent. to William Bennett, planter, 50 a. at head of branch of Tredhaven Creek adj Egberd Garrison and Capt. Robert Morris. Wt.: Ralph Dawson & Andrew Skinner. Vol. I:29.
2 CONT
2 CONT 13 Aug 1669 - "Francis Armstrong and Frances Armstrong, his wife, to Thomas Paterson (sic) of Rappahannock: 400 a. called "Armstrong's Hoggpenne" on Oyster Creek in James Island, patented 1663. ( Dor. co. Land Records Vol. B 8-157
2 CONC )
2 CONT
2 CONT ===
2 CONT http://www.combs-families.org/combs/families/c-enoch.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Nov 1663 Talbot County, Maryland and Old Rappahannock County, Virginia. Enoch COMES and Henry SEWELL witness an agreement recorded in Talbot between William JOHNSON of Old Rappa and Francis ARMSTRONG of Talbot.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
