1 TITL Captain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Of Longfield; 1689 is date of death in http://www.antonymaitland.com/irisharmf.htm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Being possessed of a plentifull fortune lived in great reputation at Longfield in the County of Cavan, and upon the breaking out of the war in Ireland soon after the abdication of King James II, he joined himself to the Inniskill
2 CONC iners and raised a large body of Horse at his own expence;" routed a superior force near Lisnaskea; marched to Cavan and was killed in a pursuit - John Armstrong, 'The Pedigree of the family of Armstrong', continued by the Rev. W.
2 CONC  A. Armstrong (no imprint, 1813), p. 5 (attached as Source WAArmstrong p5). This gives date of death as the day after 12 February 1689/90, presumably 1690 in the new calendar, and states he was the eldest son of John.
