0 @I6000000086733905824@ INDI
1 NAME Anna /Graham/
2 GIVN Anna
2 SURN Graham
2 _MARNM Graham
1 SEX F
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ANNA GRAHAM===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Anna Graham is the eldest daughter of Sir John Graham of Knockdolian. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f7%2f6%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+john+graham+of+knockdo
2 CONC lian&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD220/1/A/7/6/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 June 1614: Discharge by Anna Graham, lawful daughter of the deceased Sir John Graham of Knockdolian having reached 21 years of age, in favour of John, Earl of Montrose as principal and Robert Graham of Gartmore as cautioner,
2 CONC  of the sum of 5000 merks which the Earl and Robert Graham had, by their bond dated at Glasgow 5 Nov 1607, obliged themselves to make forthcoming to her by Robert Graham of Grugar, now of Auchincloich, in full satisfaction of all 
2 CONC her rights through the decease of her father, Sir John or the decease of her grandfather, Robert Graham of Knockdolian, as one of their heirs portioners; discharging the said Earl and his cautioner of the said bond and the said Ro
2 CONC bert Graham of Auchincloich; at Glasgow. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f7%2f6%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+john+graham+of+knockdolian&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y N
2 CONC ational Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/A/7/6/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 June 1614: Discharge by Robert Graham of Auchincloich and Robert Graham his son with consent of his curators, in favour of John, Earl of Montrose as principal and Robert Graham of Gartmore as cautioner, of an obligation gran
2 CONC ted by them obliging them to cause Anna Graham, eldest lawful daughter of Sir John Graham of Knockdolian, upon reaching 21 years of age, to renounce (as one of the three heirs portioners of the said Sir John and Robert, his father
2 CONC ) in favour of the said Robert Graham of Auchincloich her right as heir foresaid, and granting them to have received the said renunciation from the said Anna Graham in the terms of the obligation; at Glasgow. [http://catalogue.nrs
