2 CONC ugh=6000000086732679308. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/gg/graham05.php Stirnet: Graham 05]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 March 1616: Decreet before the Lords of Session at the instance of Helen Graham, one of the three female heirs of the deceased John Graham of Knockdolian, born of the marriage between John and Dame Helen Kennedy, Countess of
2 CONC  Eglinton, his wife, and at the instance of Robert Dunbar, brother to David Dunbar of Enterkine, her husband, against Robert Graham of Grugar, brother and male heir of tailzie to the deceased John Graham, and against Mr Alexander 
2 CONC Gibson of Durrie, one of the clerks of Session in whose hands the contract of marriage (GD220/1/B/1/5/1) was waiting to be registered that diligence might pass thereupon at the instance of the said Helen and her husband for recove
2 CONC ry of her third of the £10,000 thereby provided to the three female heirs born of the marriage; the contract is insert in the decreet. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f
2 CONC 1%2f5%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=helen+graham&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1610&dt=1630&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose , reference GD220/1/B/1/5/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 November 1616: Charter under the Great Seal of Scotland by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that he has given the lands of Growgar in the Cunningham division of Ayrshire, to Helene Graham, one of the three daughters of
2 CONC  the deceased John Graham of Knockdoliane, and wife of Robert Dunbar, brother of David Dunbar of Enterkyne. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi07scot/page/557/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, 1609-20, cha
2 CONC rter number 1539]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 December 1618: Extract bond by Robert Graham younger of Auchincloich in favour of William Montgomery of Bridgend for £8000, and that in satisfaction of several sums paid to Robert's creditors: 5000 merks to Helen Graham, law
2 CONC ful daughter to Sir John Graham of Knockdolian and 4000 merks to Margaret Graham, sister to the said Robert and 500 merks to John Graham, natural son to the said Sir John etc; dated 30 Dec 1618 and registered in the Books of Sessi
2 CONC on 25 Mar 1620. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f1%2f1%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+john+graham+of+knockdolian&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotla
2 CONC nd, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose , reference GD220/1/B/1/1/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 June 1619 and 15 September 1619: Contract between William Montgomery of Bridgend and John Montgomery of Cocklebie with consent of Neill Montgomery of Langshaw on the one part and James Graham of Drumfad on the other part, men
2 CONC tioning that whereas Robert Graham of Auchinhowie had by his charters, GD220/1/B/1/1/2 and GD220/1/B/1/1/8 sold to the said William the £10 land of Auchincloich, Hilltoun and Auldmarrock to be held of the laird of Houston, superio
2 CONC r, and by his disposition, GD220/1/B/1/1/6, had sold the said lands and the lands of Auchinhowie, Douan and Blairskeith to the said William, and by his bond, GD220/1/B/1/1/5 obliged him to pay the said William £8000, whereupon inh
2 CONC ibition had been served and by his tack, GD220/1/B/1/1/4, had set the whole lands to Neill Montgomery of Langshaw; and whereas Ludovick Houston of that ilk by his bond had obliged him to confirm any charters that should be made by
2 CONC  the said Robert to the said William of the £10 lands, as also whatever charters the said William should give thereof, paying such composition as two named friends should modify; as also that the said William had right by assignat
2 CONC ion from Robert Dunbar and Helen Graham, his spouse of an apprising led at their instance upon the barony of Grugar for the sum of 600 merks and mentioning the ratification (GD220/1/B/1/2/3) of the above rights by John, Earl of Mo
2 CONC ntrose at whose instance the said Robert interdicted, and that the said James Graham of Drumfad had paid to them certain sums of money; therefore the said John and William with consent of the said Neill disponed to the said James 
2 CONC the £10 land of Auchincloich, Hiltoun and Auldmarrock, with all right they have thereto by virtue of the above charters and securities, or any other way; with all right and title they had to the lands of Auchinhowie, Douan and Bla
2 CONC irskeith with warrandice from their own proper facts and deeds; and assigning him to the whole rights and securities, excepting from the said warrandice the contract, GD220/1/B/1/1/10, which the said James Graham obliges him to pe
2 CONC rform to the said Robert Graham; and the said James grants the receipt of the whole titles and evidents of the said lands conform to a signed inventory of the date of this contract. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlineca
2 CONC talogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f1%2f2%2f6&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f1%2f2%2f6&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose , reference GD220
2 CONC /1/B/1/2/6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 March 1620 and 9 April 1620: Summons of apprising at the instance of James Graham of Drumfad against Robert Grahams, elder and younger of Auchinhowie for the sums aftermentioned: 5000 merks due to Helen Graham as one of the 
2 CONC three female heirs of the deceased John Graham of Knockdolian by his contract of marriage, GD220/1/B/1/5/1, which was assigned by Robert Dunbar, her husband, taking burden on him for her to William Montgomery of Bridgend by assign
2 CONC ation dated 30 Dec 1618; also for the sum of £8000 due by the said Robert Graham younger to William Montgomery by his bond, GD220/1/B/1/1/5, both sums being assigned to the said James by the contract, GD220/1/B/1/2/6. The summons 
2 CONC is signeted 31 Mar 1620 with three executions dated 5, 6, 8 and 9 Apr 1620. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f1%2f5%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=William+montgomery+of+b
2 CONC ridgend&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/B/1/5/3]'''
