1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ROBERT GRAHAM OF GROUGAR (aka ROBERT GRAHAM OF AUCHINCLOICH)===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 March 1617: Renunciation and discharge by Robert Graham younger of Auchinhowie with consent of his curators, in favour of John, Earl of Montrose, of the wadset right of the lands of Balmore, Sommerstoun and Malichen lying in
2 CONC  the parishes of Campsie and Kilpatrick, sheriffdoms of Stirling and Dunbarton, granted to the deceased Margaret Montgomery, mother to the said Robert, in liferent and to the said Robert himself in fee by the Earl, and set back by
2 CONC  them to the Earl by payment of the back tack duty of £1000 scots yearly, redeemable by payment of £10,000 for which Robert now grants receipt and declares the infeftment to be extinguished; at Glasgow. [http://catalogue.nrscotlan
2 CONC d.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f7%2f7%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=malichen&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD2
2 CONC 20/1/A/7/7/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 June 1617: Disposition and assignation by Robert Graham, younger of Auchincloich, eldest lawful son of Robert Graham, sometime of Grugar and now of Auchincloich and deceased Margaret Montgomery, his spouse, upon reaching the
2 CONC  age of 21 years, in favour of John Montgomery of Cocklebie, his uncle, of a wadset right for an annualrent of £1000 out of the lands of Balmore, Sommerstoun and Malichen, redeemable by payment of £10,000 after the said Robert rea
2 CONC ches the age of 22 years at two terms; to which he had right by virtue of a contract made between the said Margaret Montgomery, his mother, and the said Robert Graham of Auchincloich, his father, as administrator to him on the one
2 CONC  part and John, Earl of Montrose on the other part, dated at Edinburgh 25 Nov 1611. By which contract it is declared that John Montgomery of Cocklebie, his uncle, had in his name and on his behalf and his mother's, paid the said s
2 CONC um of £10,000 and therefore the said annualrent and sum of £10,000 was provided to the said Margaret in liferent and to him, the said Robert, in fee. This disposition and assignation is dated at Edinburgh, with a ratification at t
2 CONC he foot of it by John, Earl of Montrose, at whose instance the said Robert stood interdicted. The consent is dated at Kincardine 17 Jun 1618. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%
2 CONC 2fA%2f8%2f5%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=malichen&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/A/8/5/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 November 1617: Disposition and assignation by Robert Graham, younger of Auchincloich, eldest lawful son of Robert Graham, sometime of Grugar and now of Auchincloich and deceased Margaret Montgomery, his spouse, upon reaching
2 CONC  the age of 21 years, in favour of John Montgomery of Cocklebie, his uncle, of a wadset right for an annualrent of £1000 out of the lands of Balmore, Sommerstoun and Malichen, redeemable by payment of £10,000 after the said Robert
2 CONC  reaches the age of 22 years at two terms; at Edinburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fA%2f8%2f5%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=malichen&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y Nationa
2 CONC l Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose, reference GD220/1/A/8/5/3]'''
