2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Stirnet, Ursula Ralston, here treated, was dead by 1698. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/hh4aa/hamilton46.php Stirnet: Hamilton 46] This may be true but it is misleading. For example, her husband, Sir J
2 CONC ohn Hamilton of Halcraig, appears to have married his second wife, https://www.geni.com/people/Isobel-Menzies/6000000212946424826, before 20 May 1685. [See Evidence and Note cited below] It follows, therefore that Ursula Ralston, 
2 CONC here treated, the putative first wife of Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig, must have died before 20 May 1685.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Stirnet, Usula Ralston, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/John-Hamilton-of-Halcraig-Senator-of-the-College-of-Justice/6000000017552481415?through=6000000023942470532 in 1663. [https://www.stirnet.co
2 CONC m/genie/data/british/hh4aa/hamilton46.php Stirnet: Hamilton 46]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Possible Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/James-Hamilton-of-Halcraig/6000000212795688842?through=6000000023942470532 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/John-Hamilton-of-Halcraig/6000000212795729825?through=6000000023942470532 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Isobell-Hamilton/6000000014827155183?through=6000000023942470532 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Sasine Registers ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 August 1679 x 20 May 1685: Isobel Menzies, spouse of John Hamilton, younger of Halcraig. [Register of Sasines for the Sheriffdom of Lanark, reference RS42/VII/338]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: Isobel Menzies married Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig. This is proved by the baptismal record of their daughter Elisabeth Hamilton, which reads as follows: "Mr John Hamilton of Hallcraig one of the Senators of the College 
2 CONC of Justice and Dame Issobell Meinzies a. d. n. Elisabeth W. William Baillie of Lamingtoun Alexr. Meinzies of Coulteralers, Mr John Meinzies, Advocat, William Meinzies, merchant, Mr James Meinzies, writer to the Signet, Mr William 
2 CONC Carstairs & Mr William Dunlop, ministers of the Gospel George Stirling Deacon Conveener Chirurgeon. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Baptisms, reference OPR.685/1/11] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=60000002132
2 CONC 59327824 Image of Baptismal Record] It follows therefore, that her husband is the man identified as John Hamilton, younger of Halcraig, in the Lanark Sasine Register.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
