1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM WALLACE OF ELDERSLIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Spurious Pedigree'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''According to the Reverend Charles Rogers, William Wallace of Elderslie here treated is the son of Katherine Crawford but there is no doubt that he confused this lady with Katherine Wallace. [https://archive.org/stre
2 CONC am/bookofwallace01roge#page/n84/mode/1up The Book of Wallace, i, p. 28]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Question of Ancestry===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie here treated is the son of William Wallace, younger of Elderslie, and his wife Katherine Wallace. [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n84/mode/1up The Book of Wallace, i, p. 28] On 
2 CONC 24 June 1610 he and his sister Elizabeth were confirmed as her executors dative to their deceased mother. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Records, Testament Testamentar of "Katherine Wallace spous to Williame Wal
2 CONC lace younger of Ellirslie", reference CC9/7/7 pp. 253-55] William and Elizabeth were still minor children at this time but William probably reached the age of majority before 3 May 1627, the date upon which he was served heir to h
2 CONC is deceased father in the lands of Helington and Langlands. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f4%2f15%2f21&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=wallace+of+elderslie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&d
2 CONC i=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/4/15/21]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Mother's Testament Testamentar===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Katherine Wallace made her last will and testament at Hellingtoun on 24 June 1610. She nominated her children, William and Elizabeth Wallace, to be her only executors and intromitters with her goods, and nominated her husband t
2 CONC o be their administrator. When confirmation was granted to the children on 6 November 1611 their father: "made fayth as use is. jure [specit] for the excrs testamentaris above menit thair minotitie & les age." On the same day Hew 
2 CONC Pollick in Kilmarnock acted himself as cautioner for the children, and William Wallace younger of Elderslie, their father, took burden upon himself for "the said excrs minoris" and promised to keep Hew Pollick skaithless and free 
2 CONC of any damage for his trouble. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Records, Testament Testamentar of "Katherine Wallace spous to Williame Wallace younger of Ellirslie", reference CC9/7/7 pp. 253-55]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076560259054& Image of Testament 1]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076560234089& Image of Testament 2]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076560102054& Image of Testament 3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie died before 28 March 1637, the date upon which his son Hugh Wallace was served heir to his grandfather William Wallace of Elderslie. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR1
2 CONC 7&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=ellerslie&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc., II Inqu
2 CONC isitiones Speciales. Renfrew]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie married Helen Wallace. She died in June 1621 and on 23 May 1622 he gave up her testament dative in name and behalf of their three children. Confirmation was granted on 28 May 1622. [National Records
2 CONC  of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, The Testament Dative of umqlw Helein Wallace Lady Elerslie, reference CC9/7/18, pp. 485-86]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of the First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Hugh-Wallace-of-Elderslie/6000000025804520850?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520172375154&through=387587471080005704
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Wallace/6000000076500100841?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520172497868&through=386425570480011365
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Esther-Wallace/6000000076499878998?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1520172646693&through=6000000076500100841
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Wallace of Elderslie married Agnes Wallace. She is identified as his future wife in a marriage contract date 14 June 1627. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi08scot#page/485/mode/1up Great Seal Register, A.D. 1
2 CONC 620-1633, charter number 1436 on p. 485]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 May 1627: Extract special service of William Wallace of Elderslie as heir to his father William Wallace in the lands of Helington and Langlands alias 40 acres in the bailliary of Kylestewart [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.u
2 CONC k/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f4%2f15%2f21&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=wallace+of+elderslie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, referen
2 CONC ce GD3/1/4/15/21]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 June 1627: Charter by which William Wallace of Elderslie confirms that he has given ro Agnes Wallace, his future spouse, for her lifetime, the Mains of Ellingtoun and other lands, including the tower and manor of Elingtoun, 
2 CONC in the parish of Symington in Kyle-Stewart, Ayrshire. His charter follows from a contract of marriage  dated 14 June 1627 between him and Robert Wallace of Galriggs, M. William Wallace Robert's son and heir, and Agnes Wallace,  Ro
2 CONC bert's daughter, the widow of John Blair of Hilhouse. For greater security a charter of confirmation under the Great Seal of Scotland was obtained on 26 June 1629. [https://archive.org/stream/registrummagnisi08scot#page/485/mode/1
2 CONC up Great Seal Register, A.D. 1620-1633, charter number 1436 on p. 485]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 January 1631: [https://archive.org/stream/registerprivyco06coungoog#page/n178/mode/1up Register of the Privy Council of Scotland, Vol. IV, A.D. 1630-1632, p. 110]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1631: [https://archive.org/stream/registerprivyco06coungoog#page/n247/mode/1up Register of the Privy Council of Scotland, Vol. IV, A.D. 1630-1632, pp. 179-80]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 January 1632: [https://archive.org/stream/registerprivyco06coungoog#page/n485/mode/1up Register of the Privy Council of Scotland, Vol. IV, A.D. 1630-1632, p. 417]'''
2 CONT
