1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ELIZABETH WALLACE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Wallace here treated is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Caldwell/6000000003016384215?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1519936127640&through=6000000076619929891
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Wallace here treated is the daughter of William Wallace of Elderslie and his wife Katherine Wallace. The Reverend Charles Rogers believed that Katherine Wallace was the same person as Katherine Craufurd but he was mis
2 CONC taken. [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n84/mode/1up The Book of Wallace, i, p. 28]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Wallace here treated and her brother William were minor children on 24 June 1610, when their mother nominated them as her executors, and her husband as their administrator. Elizabeth's brother William probably reached
2 CONC  the age of majority before 3 May 1627, the date upon which he was served heir to his deceased father in certain lands in Ayrshire, [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f4%2f15%2f2
2 CONC 1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=wallace+of+elderslie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD3/1/4/15/21] and it might reasonably be supposed, therefore, that Elizabeth, if she survived beyond 6 November 1611, might also have reached the ag
2 CONC e of majority at about the same time.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Her Mother's Testament Testamentar===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Katherine Wallace made her last will and testament at Hellingtoun on 24 June 1610. She nominated her children, William and Elizabeth Wallace, to be her only executors and intromitters with her goods, and nominated her husband t
2 CONC o be their administrator. When confirmation was granted to the children on 6 November 1611 their father: "made fayth as use is. jure [specit] for the excrs testamentaris above menit thair minotitie & les age." On the same day Hew 
2 CONC Pollick in Kilmarnock acted himself as cautioner for the children, and William Wallace younger of Elderslie, their father, took burden upon himself for "the said excrs minoris" and promised to keep Hew Pollick skaithless and free 
2 CONC of any damage for his trouble. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Records, Testament Testamentar of "Katherine Wallace spous to Williame Wallace younger of Ellirslie", reference CC9/7/7 pp. 253-55]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076560259054& Image of Testament 1]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076560234089& Image of Testament 2]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000076560102054& Image of Testament 3]
