1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ROBERT DOUGLAS Viscount Belhaven ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Sir Robert Douglas of Spot (1631)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/36/mode/1up The Scots peerage  II: 36-7]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/36/mode/1up The Scots peerage  II: 36-7]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Douglas, Viscount Belhaven, is reported to have died, aged sixty-six, on 14 January 1639, at Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland. He was buried in the vestry of the Abbey of Holyroodhouse, where a fine monument was erected
2 CONC  to his memory by his nephews, Sir Archibald and Sir Robert Douglas. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/36/mode/1up The Scots peerage  II: 36-7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Douglas, Viscount Belhaven, married Nicolas Moray in May 1611. She was the eldest daughter of Robert Moray of Abercairny. She died in November 1612, after giving birth to a child who did not survive, and was buried in th
2 CONC e Savoy Chapel, where there is a monument to her memory surmounted with a recumbent figure of her husband. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/37/mode/1up The Scots Peerage II: 3
2 CONC 7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Illegitimate Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''By a Miss Whalley of the county of Nottingham, Robert Douglas, Viscount Belhaven, had two natural children, John Douglas and Susanna Douglas, who had letters of legitimation under the Great Seal 30 July 1631. Susanna, then aged
2 CONC  eighteen, had a licence from the Bishop of London to marry at St. Andrew's, Holborn, on 2 February 1635-36, a widower, aged thirty-four, Robert Douglas, afterwards Sir Robert Douglas of Blackerston, to whom and his spouse, Lord B
2 CONC elhaven, in 1636, made over the barony of Gorbals, reserving his own liferent. By them it was sold in 1650 to the Corporation of Glasgow. They had issue a large family.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 July 1631: Apud Halyrudhous, 30 Jul. REX dedit literas legitimatiouis JOANNI DOUGLAS et SUSANNE DOUGLAS, filio et filie naturalibus D. Roberti D. de Spott militis ; ordinando ut alter eorum alteri succederet in hereditatibus
2 CONC  et bonis. P.R, iii. 112 (i). [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/629/mode/1up RMS: charter number 1839]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland. A. D. 1620-1633. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate (H. M. Gen
2 CONC eral Register House, Edinburgh,1894), 1096 pp. including indexes and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft/page/n6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility o
2 CONC f that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume II. (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1905), 602 pp.]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Douglas,_1st_Viscount_of_Belhaven Biographical Summary by Wikipedia] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Douglas, 1st Viscount of Belhaven PC (1573 – 14 January 1639), was a Scottish courtier. The second son of Malcolm Douglas of Mains (executed 1584), by Janet Cunningham, daughter of John Cunningham, of Drumquhassil. He wa
2 CONC s Master of the Horse to the Henry Frederick, Prince of Wales, a Gentleman of the Bedchamber to James VI and Charles I and Master of the Household to Charles I. He was knighted in 1609 and subsequently sworn of the Scottish Privy 
2 CONC Council. In 1633, on the coronation of Charles I, he was raised to the Peerage of Scotland as Viscount of Belhaven, in the County of Haddington.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lord Belhaven married Nicola Moray, daughter of Robert Moray, in 1611. She died in childbed in November 1612. He had two children by his mistress, Elizabeth Whalle, the sister of Edward Whalley, who was subsequently to be a reg
2 CONC icide. They were both legitimised by Act of Parliament when he became a viscount at Charles I's coronation in 1633. His son John is assumed to have predeceased him, but his daughter Susanna Douglas married her cousin, Robert Dougl
2 CONC as of Blackerston. On his death, his estate including the Gorbals Mansion House passed to his nephew and son-in-law. Lord Belhaven died at Edinburgh in January 1639 and was buried in Holyrood Abbey in Edinburgh where his monument 
2 CONC remains today. As he had no sons the viscountcy died with him.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://deriv.nls.uk/dcn23/9528/95281270.23.pdf Biographical Summary by Heraldry of the Douglases] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Douglas of Spott, created VISCOUNT OF BELHAVEN, 24th June 1633, died 14th January 1639. He married, May 1611, Nicolas, daughter of Robert Moray of Abercairny, who died November 1612. By a Miss Whalley he had a natural so
2 CONC n : (1) John Douglas, legitimated 1631.'''
