1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From “The house of Argyll and the collateral branches of the clan Campbell, from the year 420 to the present time” (Publication date 1871). CAMPBELLS OF LOCHNELL.  Page 166-167.  < [https://archive.org/details/houseofargyllcol00in
2 CONC glas/page/n347/mode/2up?q=Lochnell Archive.Org] >
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Archibald is said to have had four wives, at or about the same time. 1st. Janet, daughter to Duncan na-mein Macdougall of Dunollie, chief of the Macdougalls; by her he had—
2 CONT 1st. Alexander, his heir, and
2 CONT 2nd. Cailen-na-kille of Kilekolmldll, in Benderloch, who was married to a daughter of Stirling of Keir, relict of Buchanan of Leni, extinct.
2 CONT
