1 NAME John "Ian Connelach" /Campbell/
2 GIVN John "Ian Connelach"
2 _MARNM Campbell
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From Burke’s (1879), “CAMPBELL OF LOCHNELL.” Page 255.  < [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera01byuburk#page/254/mode/2up Archive.Org] >
2 CONT
2 CONT >The eldest son, Archibald Campbell, 2nd of Lochnell, m. 1st, Janet, dau. of Duncan Macdougall, of Dunolly, and had, Alexander, his heir; and Colin, whose issue is extinct. He m. 2ndly, a dau. of Maclean of Dowart, and had issue ;
2 CONC  3rdly, a dau. of Cheyne, and had a son, John, ancestor of Coreleigh ; and 4tlhly,Sibella, dau. of John Drummond, of Colquhalzie, and had a son, James, of Cruachan, ancestor of Stonefield and Balemo.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 - Jessie, the third [wife], was daughter to Chuin O'Donell, Ireland. She was mother to Ian Connelach, married to Loup's daughter; of them are the Campbells of Corrieleigh.
2 CONT (Campbell-The House of Argyll and the collateral branches of the clan.pdf)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a very tight web of connections between the descendants of Conn and this particular branch of the Campbells that lasted into the middle of the 17th century. For example, the byname of Ian "Connelach", son of Archibald Cam
2 CONC pbell, 2nd of Lochnell, suggests that he was fostered in Donegal. [E-mail from Jack Mason rec: 17 Feb 2020]
2 CONT ----
