1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Captain Andrew Stewart of Gortigil, who in or about the year 1620, accompanied Andrew Stewart, 3rd Lord Ochiltree & 1st Lord Castlestewart, from Scotland  Of Gortigal Andrew Stewart, (commonly styled captain Andrew
2 CONC  Stewart,) who, with lord Castle Stewart, to whom he was related, and his (Andrew’s) brother James, who afterwards fixed his residence at Ballymona, co. Tyrone, went from Scotland to Ireland about the year 1627 : on his marriage, 
2 CONC (as hereafter mentioned) he obtained from lord Castle Stewart the greater part of the manor of Castle Stewart; but he afterwards built, and resided on, another seat, called Gortigill, near Stewart’s Town, co. Tyrone, (at a spot im
2 CONC mediately adjoining the present residence of the Castle Stewart family-) which has ever since been in possession of captain Stewart’s descendants: he served with colonel Robert Stewart, of Fry, in defence of the forts of Dungannon
2 CONC  and Mountjoy in 1641; and at the rising of the rebels at Artrea, or Ardtreigh, co. Tyrone, for the purpose of destroying the protestant families of that county, his house was attacked, but with a few Scots’ followers he defended 
2 CONC it for two days, when assistance was sent to him from Mount_joy Fort. Captain Stewart m. Sarah, eldest daughter of lord Castle Stewart,(commonly styled lordOchiltree, and sister to Mary, countess of Suffolk,) by whom (who survived
2 CONC  him and d. in 1687,) he had issue, 1. Robert, who had an only child, Janet, who m., in 1684, John Bell, of Mullnntear, esq.; 2. Hugh, (of whom hereafter); 3. James, an oflicer R.N., who m. _, daughter of admiral sir Clondesley Sh
2 CONC ovel, and d. gallantly in‘ battle. Captain Stewart having long been an object devoted to vengeance for the zeal and loyalty he evinced in the royal cause, was, at length, put _to death byrebels about the year 1650. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.	Andrew Stewart of Gortigal, co Tyrone (a 1620, d before 06.10.1658, Captain)
2 CONT  	m. Sarah (a 1658) Children:
2 CONT  	A.	Robert Stewart
2 CONT  	i.	Janet Stewart
2 CONT  	m. (1684) R. Bell
2 CONT  	B.	Hugh Stewart of Gortigal
2 CONT  	m. Margaret Morris (dau of Thomas Morris of Mountjoy Castle) i.	Hugh Stewart (2nd son)
2 CONT  	a.	son (dsp)
2 CONT  	ii.	John Stewart of Gortigal (youngest son)
2 CONT  	m. (1710) Mary Kennedy ("a Scotch lady")
2 CONT  	a.	Hugh Stewart (b 1711, d 01.1800, rector of Termon, co. Tyrone)
2 CONT  	m. (1755) Sarah Hamilton (dau of Rev. Andrew Hamilton (by Sarah, dau/heir of Henry Conyngham of Castle Conyngham), sister/coheir of Sir Henry, Bart of Castle Conyngham)
2 CONT  	(1)	Sir John Stewart 'of Ballygawley', 1st Bart of Athenree (co Tyrone) (b 1757, d 22.06.1825, MP, Attorney General for Ireland)
2 CONT  	m. Mary Archdale (d 28.05.1795, dau of Mervyn Archdale of Castle Archdale)
2 CONT  	(A)	Sir Hugh Stewart, 2nd Bart of Athenree (b 14.05.1792, d 19.11.1854, MP) had issue
2 CONT  	m1. (19.01.1826) Julia Gage (d 11.1830, dau of Marcus McCausland Gage of Bellarena)
2 CONT  	m2. (28.02.1837) Elizabeth St. George (d 02.09.1902, dau of Rev. Henry Lucas St. George of Dromore) (B)	Mervyn Stewart of Martray House, Sheriff of Co Tyrone (b 27.05.1794, d 1885) had issue
2 CONT  	m. (17.06.1822) Frances Vesey (dau of Rev. George Vesey of Derrabard House)
