1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://dn790008.ca.archive.org/0/items/historyofclanmac00macf/historyofclanmac00macf.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT History of Clan MacFarlane (1914), says that Walter, 16th Chief, married Margaret, daughter of Sir James Semple of Beltrees, and that they had “John, who succeeded as 17th Chief,” plus Andrew of Ardess and Giles. That is solid evi
2 CONC dence that the succeeding chief’s mother was a Sempill/Semple of Beltrees.
2 CONT
2 CONT The same book then opens its next chapter as “John—17th Chief. 1664–1679”, identifying him as Walter’s successor, and adds that John married Grizel, daughter of Sir Colin Lamond of that Ilk. In other words, the printed history sup
2 CONC ports John MacFarlane as the 17th chief/baronial holder in question.
2 CONT
2 CONT A second older source, an article in The Scottish Antiquary on the pedigree of Walter MacFarlane of that Ilk, agrees with that structure: it states that “Walter, 11th laird, married Margaret, daughter of James Semple of Beltrees, 
2 CONC and by her had two sons—John and Andrew, both of whom succeeded.” That independently supports Margaret Sempill/Semple of Beltrees as the mother of the succeeding John.
