1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ? HAMILTON ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This lady's forename has not been identified. She was the daughter of  https://www.geni.com/people/John-Hamilton-of-Lettrick-and-Bargany/6000000002116164386 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Campbell/600000000278553
2 CONC 9567?through=6000000005066692952, [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02paul#page/27/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 27] and the sister of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Hamilton-Lord-Bargany/6000000017530063772?through=60
2 CONC 00000005066692952. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1529&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+weir&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y NRS: GD109/1529]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This lady married https://www.geni.com/people/William-Weir-of-Stanebyres/6000000063923442087?through=6000000005066692952. Her husband is identified as the brother-in-law of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Hamilton-Lord-Bargany
2 CONC /6000000017530063772?through=6000000005066692952 in a bond dated 9 June 1640. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1529&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+weir&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1
2 CONC 700&di=y NRS: GD109/1529]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/James-Weir-of-Stanebyres/6000000025171472648 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/George-Weir-of-Stanebyres/6000000063819867856?through=6000000005066692952 '''
2 CONT # ''' https://www.geni.com/people/Katharine-Fergusson/6000000048697163043?through=6000000005066692952 '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 June 1640: Bond by John, lord Bargany, to Sir William Weir of Stanebyres, kt., his brother-in-law for 3,000 merks Scots [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1529&st=1&tc=y&tl=n
2 CONC &tn=n&tp=n&k=william+weir&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/1529]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Critical Commentary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It has been suggested that William Weir of Stonebyres married a lady named Elizabeth Hamilton and that they were the parents of Thomas Weir of Kirkton but proof of this is wanting. [http://newsfeed.rootsweb.com/th/read/WEIR/200
2 CONC 4-09/1094570296 RootsWeb: Weir] See also [http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/weir/2098/ Genealogy.com: Thomas (The Witch) Weir] This proposition appears to have been accepted by Electric Scotland, who say "Thomas Weir 
2 CONC of Kirkton was the son of William Weir de Vere of Stonebyres and his wife Elizabeth Hamilton" [http://www.electricscotland.com/webclans/stoz/weir2.html Electric Scotland: Weir] and by the author of the Wikipedia article on Major T
2 CONC homas Weir, who say this of him: "His grandfather was William Weir, or Vere, of Stonebyres Castle who married Lady Elizabeth Hamilton." [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Weir Wikipedia: Thomas Weir]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It should not be regarded as certain but it is possible that the proposition mentioned above has its origin in an online article by Nicholas Thomas de Vere Von Drackenberg entitled "The Duchy of Angiers and the Royal House of V
2 CONC ere." According to him, James Weir of Vere, 7th Baron Blackwood, married Lady Euphemia Hamilton, (Merovingian descent) sister of the Duke of Chatelherault, Marquess of Hamilton, 5th Grandson of King Edward III Plantagenet. The Ham
2 CONC iltons were the Heirs Presumptive to the Throne of Scotland during this period. James lived to a great age. He died in 1595. Had sons: 1. James Weir 2. William Vere of Stonebyres who married Elizabeth Hamilton. 3. Robert Weir [htt
2 CONC ps://www.bibliotecapleyades.net/dragons/esp_sociopol_dragondescent2.htm The Duchy of Angiers and the Royal House of Vere]'''
