1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Patrick MacGregor of Ardchoille''' (called '''Aberach''' after his father), Chieftain of the Children of the Mist and is also said to have fought under Montrose at Kilsyth in 1645. He would, of course, have been
2 CONC  subordinate to the other Patrick who was his Chief. He married Marian MacDonald of Auchatrichatan in Glencoe member of the family of the MacDonalds of Glencoe and, perhaps, a distant relative of the MacDonalds of Sleat. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the latter half of the 16th Century this branch of the Clan led such wild and hunted lives in the misty mountains that they became known as MacEagh or "Sons of the Mist". 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Patrick MacGregor aka 3rd Chief of the Children of the Mist Born about 1582 in Montrose, Angus, , Scotlandmap Son of Duncan Aberach MacGregor and Dau. MacFarlane Brother of Robert Aberach MacGregor of Lochabe and	Gregor MacGregor 
2 CONC Husband of Marian MacDonald — married [date unknown] [location unknown] Father of Duncan MacGregor, William MackGayhe, Iain John MacGregor, James MacGregor Maj., William MacGregor and	Iain MacGregor Died 1648 in Glenstrae, , , Sco
2 CONC tlandmap
