2 CONT Henry Stewart, 1st Lord Saint Colme1  M, #25175, d. 12 July 1612 Last Edited=6 Oct 2012 Consanguinity Index=0.6%
2 CONT      Henry Stewart, 1st Lord Saint Colme was the son of James Stewart, 1st Lord Doune and Lady Margaret Campbell.1 He married Lady Jean Stewart, daughter of John Stewart, 5th Earl of Atholl and Lady Mary Ruthven, in December 1603.
2 CONC 2 He died on 12 July 1612.1
2 CONT      He held the office of Constable of Doune Castle from 1591/92 to 1593.1 He held the office of Justice of the Peace (J.P.) for Fife and Kinross in 1610.1 He was created 1st Lord Saint Colme [Scotland] on 7 March 1610/11.1 Child
2 CONC  of Henry Stewart, 1st Lord Saint Colme and Lady Jean Stewart James Stewart, 2nd Lord Saint Colme1 d. c 1620 Citations [S37] BP2003 volume 2, page 2768. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37] [S37] 
2 CONC BP2003. [S37] __________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Stewart,_1._Lord_St._Colme
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Stewart, 1st Lord St. Colme Jumptonavigation Jumpto search Henry Stewart, 1st Lord Saint Colme (* before 1561, † July 12, 1612 ), was a Scottish peer .
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the second born son of James Stewart, 1st Lord Doune . His mother was Lady Margaret Campbell, daughter of Archibald Campbell, 4th Earl of Argyll .
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1576 he owned lands in Emycreichan and Crostinterray in Strathearn . From 1581 he was administrator ( Commendator ) of the Abbey of Saint Colme's Inch in Fifeshire . Between 1591 and 1593 he also held the office of Constable of
2 CONC  Doune Castle . In 1584 he was given the life of the Priory of St. Colmoc's in Perthshire . In 1607 he owned more land near Invermay in Perthshire. In 1610 he became justice of the peace for Fifeshire and Kinross-shire .
2 CONT
2 CONT King James VI. on March 7, 1611, gave him the Abbey of Saint Colme's Inch, including its lands, converted it into a secular Lordship of Parliament , and gave it the hereditary title Lord St. Colme .
2 CONT
2 CONT In December 1603 he married Lady Jean Stewart, daughter of John Stewart, 5th Earl of Atholl . With her he had a son and heir, James Stewart († after 1620).
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1612 and was buried in Holyrood Abbey .
2 CONT
2 CONT Web links  Henry Stewart, 1st Lord Saint Colme on thepeerage.com Saint Colme, Lord (S, 1610/11) at Cracroft's Peerage predecessor	office	successor Title created new	Lord St. Colme 1611-1612	James Stewart __________________________
2 CONC _____________________
