1 NAME Fionnvola /MacLeod/
2 GIVN Fionnvola
2 SURN MacLeod
2 NICK MacLean
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1583
2 PLAC Dunvegan, Inverness-shire, Scotland 
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1642
2 PLAC Isle of Coll, Argyll, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/MacLeod-667
2 CONT
2 CONT Fionnvola MacLeod was born between 1580 and 1585, the daughter of Tormod MacLeod of Dunvegan and his second wife Lady Janet Campbell, daughter of the Earl of Argyll.[1] [2] [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Fionnvola married Lachlan MacLean about 1602, probably on the Isle of Coll where they spent their lives. Lachlan was the grandchild of Lady Janet Campbell, Fionnvola's mother, making him Fionnvola's nephew.[1] [2] [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had six children together [4] including:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Garbh MacLean born before 1603
2 CONT # Hector MacLean born before 1628
2 CONT # Neil MacLean born about 1600
2 CONT # Katherine MacLean born about 1608
2 CONT # Janet MacLean born before 1631
2 CONT # Lachlan died about the beginning of 1642.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT *John Garbh succeeded his father in Coll. Hector was the progenitor of the MacLean's of Muck. Neil was the progenitor of the MacLeans of Drimnacross. Catherine was married, in 1627, to John Balbh, chief of the Clan Fingon, or MacK
2 CONC innons. Janet was married to the Rev. Farquhar Fraser, minister of Tiree. Birth dates taken from profiles.Lemon-3042 23:49, 5 December 2025 (UTC)
2 CONT *Lachlan "was a man of ability and prudence, and possessed a good deal of influence in his time. He was a Presbyterian. He was probably the last Laird of Coll who could not sign his name."[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT # Gordon MacGregor, The Red Book of Scotland, "Norman MacLeod of Dunvegan", Volume 6, p.609-611 (Lin-Mer, published 2022), citing MacLeod of Dunvegan and MacLeod; "Scotland, Red Books of Scotland, 1600-1939", database with images,
2 CONC  (Red Book of Scotland vol. 6, p. 609-611 : viewed 3 December 2025); Ancestry Sharing Link - Ancestry Image
2 CONT # MacKenzie, Alexander; History of the Macleods with genealogies of the principal families of the name, p. 54. (A. & W. Mackenzie in Inverness.1889),(History of the Macleods : accessed 3 December 2025).
2 CONT # MacKinnon, Donald and Morrisson, Alick, The MacLeods - The Genealogy of a Clan, "MacLeod Chiefs of Harris and Dunvegan", Volume 1, frontpiece, p.20, (Clan MacLeod Society), images, (MacLeod Chiefs of Harris and Dunvegan : access
2 CONC ed 3 December 2025). Norman MacLeod c.1509 - c.1585; son William c 1560 - c 1590; Rory Mor c 1562 - c 1626; Alexander.
2 CONT # Sinclair, Alexander MacLean. The Clan Gillean. p.372-373. (Charlottetown: Haszard and Moore, 1899). (The Clan Gillean : accessed 6 December 2025).
