1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maritje was born in Antwerpen.  [?.] At least 5 of her childreen were born in Albany during the years 1638 & 1652.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Duncanson-15
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Duncanson (also Donchesen, Donckesen, and other variants) was born in Scotland about 1614. In about 1650, she was living in New Netherland, where she became the second wife of Pieter Loockermans.[1] In view of her age, Piete
2 CONC r is likely to have been Maria's second husband. A possible record of her first marriage exists in the form of banns posted in January 1640 for the marriage in Amsterdam, Holland, of a 25-year-old Maria Donckes and a James Macfass
2 CONC e, both from Scotland.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT The identity of Loockermans' second wife Maria has been the subject of some debate.[3] In preparation for his second marriage, in 1664, to Maria Varleth, Willem Teller made provision for his children by his first wife and appointe
2 CONC d as their guardians "Sander Leendertse Glen and Pieter Loockermans, uncles of said children." This is interpreted as indicating that Pieter Loockermans' wife Maria was the sister of either Willem Teller or his deceased wife "Marg
2 CONC ariet Donckesen" (Duncanson).[4] Because Margaret Duncanson had a sister Maria born about the same time as Pieter Loockermans, others Duncanson sisters lived in New Netherland, and there is no record of Willem Teller having any si
2 CONC sters in New Netherland,[5][4] it is most likely that it was Maria Duncanson who was Pieter Loockermans' second wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pieter and Maria are recorded as the parents of four daughters, Maria, Annetje, Hilletje, and Catharina (Catelyntje).[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT On the Albany census of 1697, Maria was listed as a widow and the head of a household that included one child. The last record of her is from February 1700, when she assisted at a burial in Albany.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *https://www.researchgate.net/publication/261286089_Recent_Literature_on_the_Duncanson_Sisters_of_New_Netherland Mary Loockermans, Anne Powell, Margaret Telller, and Katherine Glen were sisters. They were daughters of the Reverend
2 CONC  James Duncanson, minister of Alloa and Tullibody, Clackmannanshire, Scotland, by his wife Helen Livingston. Grand daughters of the Reverend John Duncanson, minister and to the household of King James VI,probably (now known to be 
2 CONC certainly) by John's first wife, Janet Watson. Helen Livingston was a daughter of the Rev. Helen Livingston, minister of St. Ninian’s, Stirlingshire, by his wife Agnes Gray, and a granddaughter of Henry Livingston of Falkirk and M
2 CONC argaret Forrester ...
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/42722996/person/28665523976 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 20 2017, 16:13:14 UTC''
2 CONT * http://bowergenealogy.ca/1184.htm
