1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography
2 CONT Robert Galbraith, 11th Laird of Culcreuch and 17th Chief of Clan Galbraith. Robert Galbraith was the cause of the fall of the Galbraith Clan. During the 16th century the 17th Chief of the Galbraiths, Robert, was renowned for his m
2 CONC isdeeds, including the attempted murder of his brother-in-law, Alexander Seton of Gargunnock, to whom he owed money and the abuse of his power to pursue the Clan Gregor to attack the chief of MacAulay who had married his widowed m
2 CONC other against his will. Finally he was denounced a rebel and fled to Ireland sometime before 1642. His heir James, 18th chief was the last traceable member of the line. The Galbraiths who moved to Gigha held the island for the Mac
2 CONC Donalds of the Isles till after 1590 but later took their protection.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Galbraith, the 17th Chief, proved to be a drunken scoundrel who brought nemisis upon his house. His subsequent misdeeds led finally to his being arrested and denounced as a rebel. In 1622, he fled from an order for his arre
2 CONC st, and died in Ireland sometime before 1642. His heir, james Sr., inherited nothing and his grandson, James Jr., the 19th Chief, is the last traceable member of his line.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eventually it was financial hardship which forced Robert Galbraith to pass over Culcreuch Castle and the rest of the family's estate in settlement of his debts to brother-in-law Alexander Seton of Gargunnock, a Lord of the Session
2 CONC , in 1624.
2 CONT
2 CONT Penniless, Robert Galbraith, 11th Laird of Culcreuch and 17th Chief of Clan Galbraith, fled to Ireland and disappeared into Irish history. Members of the Galbraith Clan from all over the world have since this time been searching, 
2 CONC unsuccessfully to date, to discover who from amongst their number can prove themselves to be descended directly from Robert and thus claim to be the current Chief of the Clan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT James (June 22, 1608 - ?) 18th Chief of Clan Galbraith
2 CONT Robert (1615-1671)
2 CONT Harry (1610 - ?)
2 CONT Andrew
2 CONT Adam
2 CONT Patrick
2 CONT Rebecca
2 CONT Lettica
2 CONT John (1620-1671) married Susan Beckwith (1640-1671)
2 CONT William (1630 - 1686)
2 CONT James (1636 - 1718)
2 CONT
