1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR WILLIAM CUNINGHAM OF CUNINGHAMHEAD Baronet ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 July 1619: Antenuptial contract of marriage between William Conynghame of Conynghameheid with consents, and Elizabeth Nicolsone, daughter of Mr. Thomas Nicolsone, commissar of Aberdeen. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nr
2 CONC sonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH15%2f28%2f228&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=a&r=RH15%2f28&ro=m&df=1601&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotland, Cuningham of Cuninghamhead, reference RH15/28/228]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n343/mode/2up  Biographical Summary by the Complete Baronetage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Cunningham of Cuninghamhead n the parish of Dreghorn, co Ayr, son and heir of John Cuningham, of the same, by Mary, 1st daughter of Sir James Edmonstone of Duntreath, co Stirling, was born 24 November 1601; was heir gen
2 CONC eral of his Father, 24 October 1610; was created a Baronet [S] 4 sealed 26 July 1627, but not recorded in the Great Seal Register [S], with rem. to heirs male whatsoever, and with a grant of, presumably, 16,000 acres, called the B
2 CONC arony of Cuningham in Anti Costi, Nova Scotia, of which he had seizin July 1627. He was M.P. [S] for co Ayr, 1628-33 and 1639-40. He married firstly in 1619, Elizabeth, daughter of Thomas Nicolson, Commissary of Aberdeen. He marri
2 CONC ed secondly, Margaret, daughter of Hugh (Campbell), 1st Lord Campbell of Loudoun [S], by Elizabeth, daughter of William (Ruthven), 1st Earl of Gowrie [S]. He died June 1640. [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n343/mo
2 CONC de/2up Complete baronetage; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 325]'''
