1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ARCHIBALD EDMONSTONE OF DUNTREATH AND BRAIDEN ISLAND ==
2 CONT == ARCHIBALD EDMONSTONE OF DUNTREAT AND BRAIDEN ISLAND ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''" Archibald Edmondston, of Braiden-island, in the County of Antrim, Esq., eldest son of William Edmoudston, of Dontreath, in the parish of Streablin, in the Sheriffdome of Striveling, in the kingdom of Scotland, Esq., eldest so
2 CONC n of Sir James Edmondston, of Dontreath aforesaid, Knight, which Archibald married Jane, daughter of Archibald Hamilton, of Halcraige, in the Sheriffdome of Lanirke, in the said Kingdom of Scotland, Esq., second brother to James, 
2 CONC Lord Viscount Clandeboy now living, by whom he had issue, William, eldest sonne, deafe and dumme ; Archibald, second sonne, upon whom his father conferred his estate, both unmarried as yett ; Helen, eldest daughter ; Isabell, seco
2 CONC nd daughter, as yett unmarried ; and some other children who died young. The said first-mentioned Archibald Edmondston, departed this mortall life at Braiden-Isand aforesaid, the 25th of December, 1636 ; and was interred in the Pa
2 CONC rish Church of Templecoran, in the County of Antrim aforesaid, the — of January followinge. The truth of the premisses is testified by the subscription of James Edmondston, brother to the defunct, who hath, returned this certifica
2 CONC te into my office to be there recorded. Taken by me, Thomas Preston, Esq., Ulster King of Armes, this 10th of July, 1637."[https://archive.org/details/hamiltonmanuscri00belf/page/158/mode/1up Hamilton Manuscripts: 158, citing Fune
2 CONC ral Entries, vol. 7, p. 101.]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Archibald Edmonstone of Broadisland (Braiden Island) married Jane Hamilton, daughter of Archibald Hamilton of Halcraig and his second wife. [https://archive.org/details/agenealogicalan09burkgoog/page/n383/mode/1up Burke's Commo
2 CONC ners I: 349] [https://archive.org/details/b24877876_0002/page/1155/mode/1up Burke's Landed Gentry: 1155]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/hamiltonmanuscri00belf/page/n6/mode/1up The Hamilton Manuscripts : containing some account of the settlement of the territories of the upper Clandeboye, Great Ardes, and Dufferin, in the county of Do
2 CONC wn. Edited by T. K. Lowry, Esq. LL.D. (Archer & Sons, Belfast 1867), 166 pp. plus appendix and index]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/b24877876_0002/page/n10/mode/1up texts A Genealogical and Heraldic Dictionary of the Landed Gentry of Great Britain & Ireland for 1852 : comprising particulars of upwards of 100,000 individuals. Edit
2 CONC ed by J. Bernard Burke. Vol. II. P-Z. (Colburn and Company, London, 1852) 234 pp.]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/details/agenealogicalan09burkgoog/page/n15/mode/1up A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Commoners of Great Britain and Ireland enjoying territorial possessions or high official rank; but uninvested wi
2 CONC th heritable honours. By John Burke, Esq. Vol. I (Henry Colburn, London, MDCCCXXXVI), 726 pp. including index]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/n8/mode/1up Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet, Genealogical Account of the Family of Edmonstone of Duntreath (Printed Privately, Edinburgh, MDCCCLXXV.), 95 p
2 CONC p.]
