2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalacco00inedmo/page/46/mode/1up Duntreath: 46-7]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://landedfamilies.blogspot.com/2013/04/23-adair-of-ballymena-castle-and.html?m=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert Adair (d. 1655) of Ballymena and Kinhilt.  Elder son of William Adair (d.1626) and his first wife Rosina, daughter of Sir Thomas McClellan.  Made a denizen of Ireland, 1624.  MP for Wigtownshire 1639, 1648.  He raised a
2 CONC  troop for service in Ireland in the 1640s and was commissioned to serve as a Colonel of horse under General Monck in Ulster in 1648; he was knighted about that time.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Jean or Jane, daughter of William Edmondstone of Duntreath (Stirlingshire) and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT *(1) William Adair (d. 1661) (q.v.); 
2 CONT *(2) Archibald Adair of Litter (Leix) (d. 1692); married and had issue a son;
2 CONT *(3) Alexander Adair of Drumore; 
2 CONT *(4) Robert Adair; 
2 CONT *(5) Isabella Adair, m. Patrick or Robert MacDowal of Logan (Wigtownshire); 
2 CONT *(6) Anne Adair, m. Rev. Kennedy; 
2 CONT *(7) Joan Adair, m. Patrick (surname unknown).
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited the Ballymena and Kinhilt estates from his father in 1626, and built Ballymena Castle as a centre for his property in Antrim. He died 1 March 1655.
