1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Archibald Stirling of Garden, Knight (Lord Garden)</strong> - eldest surviving son of Sir John Stirling of Garden. He was educated at the University of Glasgow, where he matriculated in the spring of 1643. He studied 
2 CONC law, and entered early into public life...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...On the eve of the Restoration, Sir Archibald was summoned by General Monck to London, with Glencairn and several other Royalists; and on the 14th February 1661, he was nominated one of the Senators of the College of Justice, wh
2 CONC en he assumed the title of Lord Garden...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He married, first Elizabeth, eldest daughter of Sir Patrick Murray of Elibank, Knight-Baronet, and Dame Elizabeth Dundas, his second wife. Their contract of marriage is dated 24th June 1637, and the marriage was celebrated at E
2 CONC dinburgh on the 9th of July...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He married secondly Mause Murray, daughter of Sir James Murray of Kilbaberton by his wife Dame Katherine Weir, then Lady Elibank...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Sir Archibald enjoyed the estates of Keir only a short time, having died in April 1668."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://www26.us.archive.org/stream/stirlingsofkeirt00fras#page/62/mode/2up The Stirlings of Keir, and their family papers]; Fraser, William Sir; page 62-66
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=grI2AAAAIAAJ An Historical Account of the Senators of the College of Justice: From Its Institution in MDXXXII]; by George Brunton, David Haig; 1832; Page 358
