1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ALEXANDER CUNNINGHAM OF CORSEHILL===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Cuningham of Corsehill was the son of Alexander Cuningham of Corsehill. He predeceased his father, dying before 19 January 1646.[http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f
2 CONC 113&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=corsehill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD39/5/113]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 January 1647: 	Crown Precept of Sasine for infefting Alexander Cunninghame now of Corsehil as heir to deceased Alexander Cunynghame of Corsehill, his father, in the 6 merk lands of Cuttiswrey, 6 merk lands of Clerkland and H
2 CONC illhouse and mill thereof, 2 1/2 merk lands of Little Robertland, 6 merk lands of Two Corsehills, 10 merk lands of Blacklaw, 6 merk lands of Hairshaw, 10 merk lands of Dowrey and Potterton, in lordship of Stewarton, bailiary of Cu
2 CONC nninghame and sheriffdom of Ayr. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f113&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=corsehill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls o
2 CONC f Glencairn, reference GD39/5/113]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 June 1646: Tutory under the Quarter Seal in favour of Alexander Cunninghame of Corsehill, to be tutor dative to Alexander, pupil son of deceased Alexander Cunninghame, eldest lawful son of said Alexander Cunninghame of Corse
2 CONC hill. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f112&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=corsehill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39
2 CONC /5/112]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://laurenandtristan.net/9aug10update/p1852.htm#i56335 laurenandtristan: Cunningham of Corsehill]
2 CONT
