1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Patrick Houstoun of that Ilk, 1st Baronet</strong>, (d.1696) was created a Baronet of Nova Scotia on February 29, 1668, the elder son of Sir Ludovick (or Louis) Houstoun of that Ilk (d.1662) by his spouse Margaret, da
2 CONC ughter of Patrick Maxwell of Newark...
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.thepeerage.com/p13166.htm#i131658
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Sir Patrick Houston married Anne, daughter of John, Lord Bargany, and had issue, five sons and four daughters. Of the latter, three made very notable Scottish marriages:
2 CONT * Margaret, married Sir Humphery Colquhoun of Luss, Bt.
2 CONT * Anne, married thrice: (1) Sir John Inglis, 2nd Baronet of Cramond, (2) Sir William Hamilton of Whitelaw, (3) Adam Cockburn of Ormiston, Lord Justice Clerk.
2 CONT * Jean, married thrice, (1) Walter Dundas of that Ilk, (2) Richard Lockhart of Lee, (3) Ludovick Grant of that Ilk.
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Sir Patrick was succeeded by his eldest son and heir, Sir John Houstoun, 2nd Baronet of that Ilk."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'Sir Patrick Houstoun, 1st Baronet', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 28 July 2012, 23:58 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Sir_Patrick_Houstoun,_1st_Baronet&oldid=504669824
2 CONC > [accessed 16 November 2012]
