1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Gordon A. MacGregor writes: "James Schaw of Greenock, m. Margaret, daughter of Hugh Montgomery of Haselhead, and was father of John Schaw of Greenock, had a charter under the Great Seal for the lands of Wester Greenock-Schaw on 15
2 CONC  February, 1623, and m. Helen, daughter of Sir Ludovick Houston of that Ilk, (c/m 29 September, 1619 and Robert Schaw, acted as attorney for infefting his brother John Schaw in the lands of Greenock on 23 December, 1622."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I96573&tree=CC
2 CONT
2 CONT >Identified as "?? of Langshaw". The only Langshaw family so far in the database is that of a Sir Thomas Home of Langshaw b. c1470. This could possibly be a descendant of that family or have changed hands to another family so far 
2 CONC unidentified.-Ed.
2 CONT
2 CONT The land held by the Schaws .... 
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=LKIKAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA627&ots=4WJYF4dbnD&dq=Sir%20Ludovick%20Houston%20of%20that%20ilk&pg=PA627#v=onepage&q&f=true Page 627] of A Genealogical and Heraldic History of the Extinct and Dormant Ba
2 CONC ronetcies ... By John Burke, Sir Bernard Burke
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >Sir Ludovick Houstoun, of that Ilk, in the county of Renfrew, great-great-great grandson of Sir Peter Houstoun, of that Ilk, who was slain at Flodden, and the representative of a very ancient Northern family, d. in 1662, leaving 
2 CONC by Margaret, his wife, daughter of Patrick Maxwell, esq. of Newark, with several daughters, m. into the families of Orbiestoun, Langshain, Pearstoun, and Kilcroich, two sons, Patrick, his heir ....
