1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Archibald Napier, 2nd Lord Napier</strong> (c. 1625–1660) was a Scottish peer and the grandson of John Napier of Merchiston...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Archibald Napier was a member of the Napier family of Merchiston, Scotland, and was in fact the grandson of John Napier, the inventor of logarithms...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Around 1642 he married Lady Elizabeth Erskine (d. 1683), the eldest daughter of John Erskine, 19th (or 3rd) Earl of Mar. They had five children:
2 CONT * Archibald (d. 1683), who succeeded as 3rd Lord Napier.
2 CONT * John (d. 1672)
2 CONT * Jean, who married Sir Thomas Nicolson of Carnock, whose son, Thomas (1669–1686), became the fourth Lord Napier.
2 CONT * Margaret (d. 1706), who became Lady Napier, fifth holder of the title in her own right (whose grandson, Francis (1702–1773), became the sixth holder of the title as the sixth Lord Napier).
2 CONT * Mary, who died unmarried."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'Archibald Napier, 2nd Lord Napier', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 24 May 2012, 09:22 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Archibald_Napier,_2nd_Lord_Napier&oldid=494125751>
2 CONC  [accessed 27 November 2012]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/424/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VI, page 425-426
2 CONT * [http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Napier,_Archibald_(d.1658)_(DNB00) Dictionary of National Biography, 1885-1900], Volume 40
