1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===CORNELIUS CRAWFURD OF JORDANHILL===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 March 1669: Bond of Warrandice by Richard Cunninghame, eldest son of deceased William Cunninghame, Deputy Keeper of the Privy Seal, in favour of [ - ], obliging said Richard to disburden lands after mentioned of clause of war
2 CONC randice, as soon as said [ - ] shall find personal warrandice that Barony of Glengarnock shall be free from all peril at all hands, and narrating (1) that by decreet in apprising at the instance of Cornelius Crawford of Jordanhill
2 CONC  against Sir David Cunninghame of Robertland, Kt., deceased, dated 18 June 1649, the 2 1/2 merk land of Robertland, with manor place &c. thereof, 3 merk land of Overlochrig, 6 merk land of Castelltoune Over and Nether, with mill t
2 CONC hereof, 14/- land of Horsemure, 4/- land of Lochside and mill called Lochmill, 11 merk land of Lochrig, 4 merk land of Bradicland, 20/- land of Spittell, 3 merk 5s. 9d. land of Waterland Halket and Herselbanke with mill thereof, 6
2 CONC  merk land of Foullshaw with mill thereof, all in bailiary of Cunninghame and sheriffdom of Ayr, lands and barony of Glengarnock, with castle, mill and loch thereof called Lochtankert, comprehending lands of Burnes, Barrhill, Dalm
2 CONC ochland, Plewlands, Auchinhuiff, Unthank, Denholme, Bridgend, Lochrig, Stanieholm, Lochend alias Paddockholme, 1/2 merk land of Cross, kirk lands of Kilbirnie, 40/- land of Cherrielands, all in said bailiary of Cunninghame, united
2 CONC  in a free barony called barony of Glengarnock, were apprised to belong to said Cornelius Crawford, which lands were disposed on 2 Feb. 1666 by said Cornelius Crawford, with consent of Hugh Crawford, his son, to said Richard Cunni
2 CONC nghame in liferent and Richard Cunninghame, younger, his son, in fee; (2) that James Anderson of Stobcorse disposed on 26 Feb. 1669 to said Richard Cunninghame 1/7th of the 8 merk land of Waterland and Halkhead with mill and loch,
2 CONC  in parish of Dunlop and bailiary of Cunninghame, which lands were apprised from Gabriel Porterfield, eldest son of deceased Gabriel Porterfield, in favour of said James Anderson; and (3) that said Richard Cunninghame elder, as tu
2 CONC tor to his said son, disponed on 4 Mar. 1669 to [ ], the 2 1/2 merk land of Robertland, 11 merk land of Lochrig, 4 merk land of Braidieland, lands of Waterland, Halket and Herselbanke, Foullshaw, 1/7th part of 8 merk land of Water
2 CONC land and Halkhead, under declaration that barony of Glengarnock should belong to him and his said son, and with clause of warrandice that in case of eviction, said Richard Cunninghame and his said son should have access to as much
2 CONC  of the land disponed by them as corresponded to said eviction. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f139&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=cornelius+crawford&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y N
2 CONC ational Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/5/139]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Please read Crawford Genealogy, pages 6 and 7. Proof of her marriage, and her children as well as her father. These pages are in the media section. :	
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/143680959/cornelius-crawford
