1 TITL Colonel
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Crawford
2 CONT * Born: 1630, Jordan Hill, Ayrshire, Scotland
2 CONT * Died: 1700, Norfolk, Virginia
2 CONT * Parents:  Lawrance Crawford and Margaret 
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigrated to America from Lenarkshire, Ayshire, Scotland & Donegal, Ireland 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography:
2 CONT
2 CONT William Crawford is a Qualifying Ancestor of the Jamestowne Society.
2 CONT William Crawford was a Virginia colonist.
2 CONT William Crawford is estimated to have been born about 1630 in Ayrshire, Scotland. He is said to have died about 1700 in Norfolk County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Crawford was transported to Virginia Colony prior to December 1648 by Richard Lee. He appears to have settled in Lower Norfolk County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Lee, Gent., 1,250 acs., 21 Dec. 1648, p. 153. On the N. side of Yorke River,... Due sd. Lee for trans, of 24 pers.: Wm. Crawford
2 CONT William is said to have married Margaret Jordan about 1660 in Norfolk County, Virginia. They had one confirmed son, William Crawford born about 1662, and probably other children as well.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Crawford was elected Burgess from Lower Norfolk County, Virginia in 1688 and William Craford [Crawford] was elected from Norfolk County in 1696.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT He is said to be the son of Lawrence Crawford, he had only one son, Lawrence, who died young. Having no surving heirs, the estate of Lawrence went to his elder brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Crafford/Crawford, William - A1910; died 1700 Norfolk Co.; Lower Norfolk Co.: 1688 (Burgess), Norfolk Co.: 1695-1696 (Burgess). accessed 22 July 2021
2 CONT ↑ Nugent, Nell Marion, Abstracted and Indexed by. Cavaliers and Pioneers: Abstracts of Virginia Land Patents and Grants, 1623-1800. In Five Volumes. Richmond, VA.: Press of the Dietz Printing Co., 1935. Page 178
2 CONT ↑ Stanard, William G. and Mary Newton Stanard. The Colonial Virginia Register. Albany, N. Y.: Joel Munsell's Sons, Publishers. 1902. Pages 86, 90.
2 CONT ↑ Crawfurd, George, "A General Description of the Shire of Renfrew: Including an Account of the Noble and Ancient Families ... To which is Added, a Genealogical History of the Royal House of Stewart, and of the Several Noble and I
2 CONC llustrious Families of that Name, from the Year 1034 to the Year 1710", Paisley: J.Neilson , 1818, Hathitrust, p. 72
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/9JZB-3RW
2 CONT
