1 NAME James Chisholm, 6th of Cromlix
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "VI. <strong>James Chisholm of Cromlix</strong>, who appears to have been married to a daughter of Sir Ludovick Houston of that Ilk, and to have had issue one son ; for we find a petition to Parliament, on the 5th of August, 1641,
2 CONC  from " Ludowick Chisholme onlie lawful son and appearand aer of umquhile James Chisholme of Cromlix," who, being a captain of foot in Lord Drummond's regiment, died at Kelso ; and the prayer of the petition is, that ward and marr
2 CONC iage may be granted without composition in the name of Sir Ludovick Houston of that Ilk, his gud-sire, and tutor testamentar. Ludovick seems to have died almost immediately after the presenting of this petition, for on the 22nd of
2 CONC  September following we find John Chisholm, who describes himself as heir apparent of James, making a similar application. On the 30th of January, 1647, an Act of Parliament was passed, referred to as the "Act, Laird of Cromlix," 
2 CONC but we have not ascertained its purport. 
2 CONT
2 CONT James was succeeded by his brother."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofchishol00mackuoft#page/216/mode/2up History of the Chisholms, with genealogies of the principal families of the name]; Alexander Mackenzie; 1891; page 217
