2 CONT
2 CONT David Tosheoch of Monzievaird
2 CONT *1610, July 3: Listed as son and heir of his father in a charter issued by John Tosheoch of Pittenzie, who held the lands at the end of Edward's life.
2 CONT *1618, May 29: Granted letters of reversion for Monzievaird by John Tosheoch of Pittenzie
2 CONT *1618, June 20: Killed in Perth by Laurence Bruce of Cultmalundy, the Younger, Alexander Fleming of Moness, and several others.
2 CONT *married Agnes, daughter of George Graham, 2nd of Inchbraikie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of:
2 CONT *Andrew Tosheoch of Monzievaird
2 CONT *Duncan Tosheoch
2 CONT *Elizabeth Tosheoch
2 CONT *Margaret Tosheoch
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://tolharndor.org/ft/toshach.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT David Tosoch/Toscheach.[5,28] 6th Laird of Monzievaird.[3] Born before 1580 (he married in 1600). In 1607 David was a witness of a lease in Strathphilane, in which he was described as "apparent of Monivaird".[2,4] That is, he was 
2 CONC of age, probably in charge of the estate and his father was still alive.[3] Inherited title 1610.[7] Died 1668.[7] In 1615 he mortaged an estate called "The Vaird" in the parish of Methven (Perthshire) comprising a 'toft' (homeste
2 CONC ad), several houses and surrounding land for the sum of 250 marks.[7] (What connection, if any, this estate had with the 'Brewlands of Mekven' owned by David's ancestor, Andrew, in the 1450's, is unknown.) David married Annas Grae
2 CONC me of Inchbrakie, Perth,[3,28] 4/4/1600, Inchbrakie, Perthshire.[6,28]
2 CONT
2 CONT Facts gathered from the Red Book of Scotland:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://redbookofscotland.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/Tosheoch-of-Monzievaird.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT David Tosheoch of Monzievaird
2 CONT
2 CONT 1610, July 3: Listed as son and heir of his father in a charter issued by John Tosheoch of Pittenzie, who held the lands at the end of Edward's life. 1618, May 29: Granted letters of reversion for Monzievaird by John Tosheoch of P
2 CONC ittenzie 1618, June 20: Killed in Perth by Laurence Bruce of Cultmalundy, the Younger, Alexander Fleming of Moness, and several others. married Agnes, daughter of George Graham, 2nd of Inchbraikie.
