2 CONT '''6 July 1678: Disposition by Sir George Stirling of Glorat, kt, son and heir of deceased Sir Mungo Stirling of Glorat, in favour of James Macfarlane of Keithtown, of lands called the Allans, and dale called the Elbow Daill, [nea
2 CONC r Ballincleroch]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD61%2f63&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+stirling+of+glorat&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Macfarlane of 
2 CONC Ballancleroch, reference GD61/63]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 August 1678: Inhibition at instance of James Macfarlane of Keithton against Sir George Stirling of Glorat, son and heir of deceased Sir Mungo Stirling of Glorat, relating to disposition of lands of Ballencleroch. Attached: e
2 CONC xecutions dated 15 and 19 August, 1678. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD61%2f64&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+stirling+of+glorat&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Sc
2 CONC otland, Macfarlane of Ballancleroch, reference GD61/64]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
