2 CONT '''24 December 1633: Extract retour of the special service before Sir Samuel Johnstoun of Elphingstoun, knight baronet, sheriff principal and Mr James Cockburn, sheriff depute of Edinburgh, within the constabulary of Haddington sp
2 CONC ecially constituted by Sir George Cockburn of Ormistoun, knight, Sir John Hamilton of Prestoun, knight, Sir Arthur Douglas of Quhittinghame, knight, Sir Patrick Douglas of Kilspindie, knight, John Hepburn of Munraw, JOHN FAWSYDE O
2 CONC F THAT ILK, William Congeltoun of that ilk, Mr Patrick Levingstoun of Saltcottis, George Hepburn of Aulderstoun, John Hepburn of Craig, John Lawsoun of Humbie, Robert Dowglas of Blaikertoun, George Brown of Colstoun, George Brown 
2 CONC of Thorneydykis, and John Seton of Pittmedden of Robert Seton, son of Robert, Earl of Winton as nearest and lawful heir of his father in the port and burgh of barony of Cowkany, which had been in the hands of the King and in those
2 CONC  of his predecessors since the death of the said Earl in the month of March 1603 for the space of 30 years and 9 months then elapsed by reason of non entry. Duly retoured to chancery. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinec
2 CONC atalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f11%2f16%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+fawsyde&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/11/16/5]'''
