2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 July 1689: Disposition by William Mudie of Melsetter to Jean McKenzie, relict of John Kennedy, elder, of Carmucks, now his spouse of liferent annuity from 9d. land of Osmondwall, 6d. land of Kirbuster with a cow's worth of l
2 CONC and there, 3d. land of Wairds, 2 merk and a cow's worth of land in Fea, 3d. and a cow's worth of land in Aith, 4½d. land in Brimms, 15 merkland in Melsetter with 2 quoys called Meiklequoy and Dowisquoy, with another quoy called Ki
2 CONC rbyster, 9 merk and a cow's worth of land in Thurvo with quoy called Annaquoy, lands and room of Ryssay and milne, 7d., 3 merk king's land with quoy called Pultisquoy in Utterstromnes, 3½d. kirkland there, 7½d. udal land there, ½d
2 CONC . land in Stanneigar there with house and biggings of Done and 1/3 merkland under said house, 1/3 of a house in Liagar and two part of yard thereof, with house and biggings of Brecknes, with house of Lesia (? Lefea) called Gentle 
2 CONC John's house, 6 merkland in island of Gramsey and town of Sutherland, house of Gorne and house of Banks with mansion house of Brecknes, and milne multures thereof, 3 merkland in ? Antawork in island of Gramsey, all lying in island
2 CONC s of Waalls and Gramsey, parish of Stromnes, 4 meils mailing and 3 cow's worth of udal land in towns of Lynnes and Thurvo, in said island of Waalls, and parsonage teinds of said island [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonline
2 CONC catalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f19&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+mudie+of+melsetter&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/19]'''
