1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===COMMODORE JAMES MOODIE OF MELSETTER, RN===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Marquis of Ruvigny and Raineval identified Captain James Moodie of Melsetter, here treated, as the uncle and heir of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Moodie-of-Melsetter/6000000019856506852 [https://archive.org/details/moo
2 CONC diebookbeinga00ruvi/page/n90 The Moodie Book: 34] who was the son and heir of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Moodie-of-Melsetter/6000000019856179357?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1569674030434&through=60000000131054190 [https://ar
2 CONC chive.org/details/moodiebookbeinga00ruvi/page/n86 Ibidem: 32]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Laird of Melsetter===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 9 December 1698 "Captain James Mudie, brother of William Mudie of Melsetter" had a charter for the lands of Melsetter and others [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD150%2f1691B&st=
2 CONC 1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mudie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD150/1691B] and signature on the same date. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SIG1%2f110%2f51&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mud
2 CONC die&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: SIG1/110/51]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Incident at Walls in October 1725===
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://genealogy.northern-skies.net/genealogy.php?number=25 Northern Skies Genealogy]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Shooting of Captain James Moodie of Melsetter===
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://genealogy.northern-skies.net/genealogy.php?number=23 Northern Skies Genealogy]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Last Will and Testament===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Captain James Moodie is reported to have made his last will and testament on 30 October 1725. He left all his possessions to Benjamin Moodie, his only son, and expressed his wish to be buried in the “burial place in the Island 
2 CONC of Walls among my ancestors.” [http://genealogy.northern-skies.net/genealogy.php?number=23 Northern Skies Genealogy]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Captain James Moodie died as a result of gunshot wounds received on 26 October 1725. [http://genealogy.northern-skies.net/genealogy.php?number=24 Northern Skies Genealogy] He made his last will and testament on 30 October 1725,
2 CONC  and died shortly thereafter, probably early in the morning of 1 November 1725, [https://archive.org/details/moodiebookbeinga00ruvi/page/n108 The Moodie Book: 40] since that is the date reported in his testament testamentar. [Nati
2 CONC onal Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of umquhile Captain James Moodie Senr. of Melsetter, reference CC8/8/91] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000109819566996& Ima
2 CONC ge of Testament]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Testament Dative===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 29 January 1727 the Testament Dative and Inventory of Captain James Moody of Melsetter was given up by his widow, Christian Crawford, to whom confirmation was granted on 10 February 1727. [National Records of Scotland, Edinb
2 CONC urgh Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of umquhile Captain James Moodie Senr. of Melsetter, reference CC8/8/91]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000109819566996& Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000109819837881&  Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000109819256856& Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Captain James Moodie of Melsetter married Lady Douglas.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Captain James Moodie of Melsetter married Christian Crawford.'''
2 CONT
