1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ROBERT STEWART (aka ROBERT STUART OF CULBEG)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert Stewart is the fourth child and second son of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Stewart-of-Culbeg/6000000077015408050?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1521471839683&through=6000000077019111452  and his wife https://www.geni.com
2 CONC /people/Annabella-Erskine/6000000076863287266?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1522317092759&through=6000000077019111452 He was born before 29 May 1630, the date upon which his baptism was registered at Gargunnock in Stirlingshire, Scotla
2 CONC nd .His baptismal record reads as follows: "Bapt to Robert Stewart of Culbeg and Annabell Erskine a son called Robert witneses Alexander Leckie of Leckie Sir George Mushette." [National Records of Scotland, Gargunnock Baptisms, 16
2 CONC 15-1819, reference OPR.481/1] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000077180582847& Image of the Baptismal Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 November 1660: Assignation by Mr George Mushett in favour of Alexander Stuart, lawful son to the deceased Robert Stuart of Kilbeg, his son-in-law (and in part payment of 4000 merks resting owing to him as tocher with his dau
2 CONC ghter) of the sum of 2000 merks of the sum of 3000 merks contained in the bond GD220/1/B/8/9/3 and corroborated by the contract GD220/1/B/8/9/4, dated at Dunning, 15 Nov 1660, with an instrument of intimation on the reverse dated 
2 CONC at Duncrub, 30 Mar 1661. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f8%2f9%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mushett&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of 
2 CONC the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/B/8/9/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 December 1664: Discharge by Katharine Halyday, relict and executrix of deceased Mr George Mushet, and Beatrix and Isobell Mushets, his lawful daughters, and Alexander Stuart in favour of James, Lord Rollo of the sum of 1600 
2 CONC merks in part payment of 3600 merks contained in GD220/1/B/8/9/6 and of the annualrent of the remaining 2000 merks preceding Martinmas 1664, dated at Dunning. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?ref
2 CONC erence=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f8%2f9%2f9&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+mushet&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/B/8/9/9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 December 1667: Discharge and renunciation by Isobell and Beatrix Mushet, heirs portioners to their father, deceased George Mushet, and Katharine Haliday, their mother, with consent of Robert Stuart of Culbeg, husband to Beatr
2 CONC ix and John Miller, indweller in Dunning, husband to Isobell, in favour of James, Marquess of Montrose, of the wadset right on a quarter of the town and lands of Aberuthven containing a procuratory of resignation ad remanentiam, d
2 CONC ated at Dunning and Stirling, 2 and 6 Dec 1667 and registered at Perth, 24 Jan 1668. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fC%2f1%2f3%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=culbeg&ko=p&r=
2 CONC &ro=s&df=1500&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/C/1/3/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This transcript may be defective. It suggests that Beatrix Mushet may have married her brother-in-law, Robert Stewart, as her second husband, but there is good reason for supposing that she was still married to Alexander 
2 CONC Stewart on 25 December 1675, the date upon which the baptism of her son John Stewart was registered at Stirling. Possibly, therefore, the words "Katharine Haliday, their mother, with the consent of" should be followed by "Alexande
2 CONC r Stuart, lawful son to the deceased Robert Stuart of Kilbeg."
