1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ALEXANDER STEWART (aka ALEXANDER STUART) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sergeant in Stirling Castle: Afterwards Merchant in Stirling===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Stewart , here treated, is the fourth son and youngest child of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Stewart-of-Culbeg/6000000077015408050?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1522357984781&through=6000000076864499890 and his wife 
2 CONC https://www.geni.com/people/Annabella-Erskine/6000000076863287266?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1522357195976&through=6000000077101835072 He was born before 2 March 1635, the date upon which his baptism was registered at Gargunnock in 
2 CONC Stirlingshire, Scotland. His baptismal record reads as follows: "Bapt to Robert Stewart and Anabel Erskine a son called Alexander wit: Adam and Alexander Cunninghams". [National Records of Scotland, Gargunnock Baptisms, 1615-1819,
2 CONC  reference OPR.481/1] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000077297672368& Image of Baptismal Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Stewart, here treated, is noticed as a sergeant in Stirling Castle on 26 November 1672, in the baptismal records of his daughter Elizabeth  [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000077309320021& Image of Bap
2 CONC tismal Record] and again on 6 November 1674, in the baptismal record of his son Archibald. [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000077308815856& Image of Baptismal Record] He is also noticed as a merchant, on 28 August 
2 CONC 1677, in the baptismal record of his daughter Mary. [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000077308401821& Image of Baptismal Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Stewart, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Beatrix-Mushet/6000000077020005834?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1522399097793&through=6000000077101835072 She was the eldest daughter of the Reverend George Mushe
2 CONC tt, minister of the Gospel at Dunning, and his wife Katharine Haliday.  [https://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiu04scotuoft#page/n279/mode/1up Fasti of the Church of Scotland, IV. Synods of Argyll, and of Perth, p. 268] He is iden
2 CONC tified as: "Alexander Stuart, lawful son to the deceased Robert Stuart of Kilbeg" in a deed of assignation dated 15 November 1660. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f8%2f9
2 CONC %2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mushett&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD220/1/B/8/9/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-Stewart/6000000077290349511?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1522343400109&through=6000000077101835072
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Stewart/6000000077295438932?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1522343570486&through=6000000077101835072
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Archibald-Stewart/6000000077295259101?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1522343635995&through=6000000077101835072
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Stewart/6000000077295089931?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1522343864748&through=6000000077101835072
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stewart/6000000196281863838
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Stewart/6000000077294897004?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1522343990273&through=6000000077101835072
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 November 1660: Assignation by Mr George Mushett in favour of Alexander Stuart, lawful son to the deceased Robert Stuart of Kilbeg, his son-in-law (and in part payment of 4000 merks resting owing to him as tocher with his dau
2 CONC ghter) of the sum of 2000 merks of the sum of 3000 merks contained in the bond GD220/1/B/8/9/3 and corroborated by the contract GD220/1/B/8/9/4, dated at Dunning, 15 Nov 1660, with an instrument of intimation on the reverse dated 
2 CONC at Duncrub, 30 Mar 1661. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f8%2f9%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mushett&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of 
2 CONC the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/B/8/9/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 December 1664: Discharge by Katharine Halyday, relict and executrix of deceased Mr George Mushet, and Beatrix and Isobell Mushets, his lawful daughters, and Alexander Stuart in favour of James, Lord Rollo of the sum of 1600 
2 CONC merks in part payment of 3600 merks contained in GD220/1/B/8/9/6 and of the annualrent of the remaining 2000 merks preceding Martinmas 1664, dated at Dunning. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?ref
2 CONC erence=GD220%2f1%2fB%2f8%2f9%2f9&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+mushet&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/B/8/9/9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 December 1667: Discharge and renunciation by Isobell and Beatrix Mushet, heirs portioners to their father, deceased George Mushet, and Katharine Haliday, their mother, with consent of Robert Stuart of Culbeg, husband to Beatr
2 CONC ix and John Miller, indweller in Dunning, husband to Isobell, in favour of James, Marquess of Montrose, of the wadset right on a quarter of the town and lands of Aberuthven containing a procuratory of resignation ad remanentiam, d
2 CONC ated at Dunning and Stirling, 2 and 6 Dec 1667 and registered at Perth, 24 Jan 1668. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fC%2f1%2f3%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=culbeg&ko=p&r=
2 CONC &ro=s&df=1500&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/C/1/3/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This transcript may be defective. It suggests that Beatrix Mushet may have married her brother-in-law, Robert Stewart, as her second husband, but there is good reason for supposing that she was still married to Alexander 
2 CONC Stewart on 14 July 1680, the date upon which the baptism of her daughter Margaret was registered at Stirling. Possibly, therefore, in the deed mentioned here the words "Katharine Haliday, their mother, with the consent of" should 
2 CONC be followed by "Alexander Stuart, lawful son to the deceased Robert Stuart of Kilbeg."
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1701: Draft ante-nuptial contract of marriage between Charles Stewart, son of deceased Alexander Stewart, sometime bailiff of burgh of Stirling, and Jean Jameson [Jamieson], daughter of Mr Edward Jameson, minister at Monymeall 
2 CONC [Monimail]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD124%2f3%2f76&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1676&dt=1725&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Er
2 CONC skine Family, Earls of Mar and Kellie, reference GD124/3/76]'''
