1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===HARIE STEWART===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Merchant in Edinburgh===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Harie Stewart is the son of Mr. Walter Stewart of Massater. minister of the Gospel at South Ronaldsay and Burray in Orkney, and his first wife Helen Sinclair. A birth or baptismal record has not been identified for him but his 
2 CONC mother died on 16 April 1645 and he must have been born before this date.  [https://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc07scot#page/230/mode/1up Fasti: vii, pp. 230-31]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 November 1654: Discharge by Mr Johne Dishingtoune to George Smyth for two meils meal in payment of the board of Harie and Walter Stewart, sons of the deceased Mr Walter Stewart. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinec
2 CONC atalogue/browseDetails.aspx?reference=GD195/108&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=massater&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Stewart of Massater, Orkney, reference GD195/108]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 May 1657: Account of Mr John Dischingtone of expenses of education of Walter and Harie Stewart. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/browseDetails.aspx?reference=GD195/112&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=massate
2 CONC r&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Stewart of Massater, Orkney, reference GD195/112]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 May 1661: Receipt by Harie Stewart, lawful son to umq. Mr. Walter S., Minister, as principal, and William S., brother of said H., as cautioner, to Captain Robert Irwing, indweller in Kirkwall, for Bond for £1000 Scots granted
2 CONC  by James Earl of Murray to said Mr Walter dated 2nd July 1645, which was assigned to said Harie as his bairns part of gear on 8th January 1647 and which he received from said Robert I, as Custodier thereof, appointed by umq. Jame
2 CONC s Stewart of Mains, tutor to said Harie. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD106%2f30&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=harie+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1720&di=y National Records of Scotland,
2 CONC  James Brown Craven bequest relating to local and ecclesiastical history on Orkney, reference GD106/30]'''
2 CONT
