1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MAJOR ROBERT HAMILTON OF DECHMONT ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Reverend Herbert Reid has this to say about Major Robert Hamilton of Dechmont: "Major Robert Hamilton, of Kirktoun and Kirktounholme, inherited from his father, Archibald Hamilton, in 1656, 'the lands callit Kirktoun of Kil
2 CONC bryde, extending to ane 8 1/2 merk land within the parish of Kilbryde......When Major Robert succeeded to the lands of Dechmont, Linlithgowshire, taking thereafter the style of Hamilton of Dechmont" he became "the Chamberlin to th
2 CONC e Duke of Hamilton's estates in Borrowstouness (Bo'ness). He sold, in 1658, his lands of Kirktoun of Kilbryde to Capt. Wm. Govan, third husband of Anna Hamilton, who styled herself Lady Kirktounholme". [Reverend Herbert Reid, The 
2 CONC Reids of Kittochside, Part II," (Glasgow, 1945), page 19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 May 1647: Marriage-contract of 29 May 1647 for marriage of Margaret Maxwell, youngest daughter of said Alexander Maxwell, to Major Robert Hamilton of Kirktounholme, whereby she was to have 5000 merks Scots of tocher within 6
2 CONC  months after her father's death. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/overview.aspx?st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Archibald+Hamiltone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Innes fam
2 CONC ily of Stow, Peeblesshire, reference GD113/5/172g]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
