2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 February 1629: Letters of general charge, at instance of Sir John Seaton of Barnes, kt, to Thomas Craig to enter heir to his father Sir Lewis Craig of Ricartoun [Riccarton], kt. Endorsed: Execution dated 25 Jun 1629. [http:/
2 CONC /catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD18%2f2277&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lewis+craig&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of Clerk family of Penicuik, Midlothian, refe
2 CONC rence GD18/2277]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 July 1668: Dispostion by Thomas Craufurd [Crawford], merchant burgess of Edinburgh in favour of Mr John Hay of Haystoun, one of the clerks of Session, of the part of the lands of Glen called Spittellhope, which with other pa
2 CONC rts of Glen were disponed to the said Thomas Craufurd by disposition, dated 11 and 18 August 1657, by the deceased John, Earl of Traquair, liferenter, the deceased John, then Lord Lintoun [Linton], thereafter Earl of Traquair, fia
2 CONC r thereof, with consent of Dame Anna Seatoun [Seton], then Lady Lintoun, William, Lord Drumlanrig and Thomas Craig of Riccartoun [Riccarton]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD34%2f82&
2 CONC st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Riccartoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Hay of Haystoun, Peeblesshire, reference GD34/82]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 October 1669: Extract special retour of the service of Lewis Craig of Riccarton as heir to Thomas Craig of Riccarton, his father in the lands of Riccarton and other others therein described, lying in the shire of Edinburgh, 
2 CONC dated 14th October 1669. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=CS228%2fC%2f2%2f24&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lewis+craig&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Court of Sess
2 CONC ion: Unextracted processes, 1st arrangement, Adams-Dalrymple office, reference CS228/C/2/24]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 April 1681: Contract of Marriage between James Chancellor of Sheillhill, and Sarah Craig, youngest lawful daughter to the deceased Thomas Craig of Riccartoun; whereby they accept of each other as lawful spouses: in contempla
2 CONC tion whereof, he binds himself to infeft her, in liferent, in an annual rent of 900 merks furth of parts of the lands of Quothquen and Sheilhill: for which cause she assigns to him a Bond of Provision for 4,000 merks, granted to h
2 CONC er by the deceased Lewis Craig of Riccartoun, her brother. Dated at Edinburgh. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD118%2f217&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Sarah+Craig&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&d
2 CONC i=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Chancellor family of Shieldhill, Lanarkshire, reference GD118/217]'''
2 CONT
