2 CONC sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwjDjKjWmO7pAhVHJTQIHXRNCFQQ6AEwBHoECAcQAQ#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] “Sir Alexander, Lord Durie, purchased the lands of that name, anciently belonging to the family of Durie of that ilk, and had a charter of t
2 CONC he same in 1614. He married Margaret, daughter of Sir Thomas Craig of Riccarton, lord advocate of Scotland, and, with 3 daughters, had 3 sons, Alexander, 2d baronet, Sir John Gibson of Pentland, who carried on the line of the fami
2 CONC ly, and George, of Balhouffie. ...”
