2 CONC he same in 1614. He married Margaret, daughter of Sir Thomas Craig of Riccarton, lord advocate of Scotland, and, with 3 daughters, had 3 sons, Alexander, 2d baronet, Sir John Gibson of Pentland, who carried on the line of the fami
2 CONC ly, and George, of Balhouffie. ...”
2 CONT * https://en.m.wikisource.org/wiki/Gibson,_Alexander_(d.1693)_(DNB00)_  “GIBSON, Sir ALEXANDER (d. 1693), clerk of session, was eldest son of Sir John Gibson of Pentland and Addiston, co. Edinburgh (knighted circa 1647), by Jean, 
2 CONC daughter and heiress of Alexander Hay of Kennet, Clackmannanshire. Sir John was second son of Sir Alexander Gibson, the first lord Durie (d. 1644) [q. v.] Douglas states that Sir John was a distinguished royalist, and was created 
2 CONC a knight-banneret at the battle of Worcester, but there seems no other evidence than his assertion. ....”
