1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT John Johnstone, of Westerhall, created a baronet in 1700. He m. Rachel, eldest dau. of  <strong>James Johnstone, of Schiennes</strong>, brother of Sir Archibald Johnstone, Lord Wariston, by Anna Hamilton, dau. of Sir John Hamilton
2 CONC , lord register of Scotland, brother of Thomas, 1st Earl of Hadington. By her he had issue, a dau. Philadelphia, wife of Douglas, of Dornock. Sir John Johnstone d. in 1711, without male issue, and was s. by his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Burke, Bernard, Sir. [http://www.archive.org/stream/agenealogicalhi00burkgoog#page/n320/mode/2up A genealogical history of the dormant, abeyant, forfeited, and extinct peerages of the British empire]. London: Harrison, 59
2 CONC  Pall Mall; 1866; page 302
