2 CONT '''1616: Procuratory of resignation by John Logan in Restalrig, [owner of the 4 oxgates of lands of town and lands of Restalrig which were of old set by deceased Robert Logan of Restalrig to deceased Marion Skowgall, relict of Mic
2 CONC hael Logan in Restalrig, in liferent, and to deceased William Logan, his son, heritably, and thereafter sold by said deceased William to deceased Gilbert Logan, brother of said deceased William, and son and heir to deceased Michae
2 CONC l Logan, in barony of Restalrig and sheriffdom of Edinburgh,] and Elizabeth Quhippo. his spouse, and with consent of John Arnot of Wodmylne, oy and heir of deceased Sir John Arnot of Barswick, kt., to [blank] to resign said 4 oxga
2 CONC tes in hands of John, lord Balmerino, baron of barony of Restalrig, as in hands of immediate superior, in favour of James Nisbet, merchant, burgess of Edinburgh, and Marion Arnot, his spouse,, in liferent, and to Henry Nisbet, the
2 CONC ir son in fee. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD237%2f1%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=henry+nisbet&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Records of Messrs Tods 
2 CONC Murray and Jamieson WS, lawyers, Edinburgh, Nisbet of Dean, reference GD237/1/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 November 1619: Sheriffdom of Midlothian: Instrument of sasine in favour of Henry Nisbet, son of James Nisbet, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, of twelve oxgates of land in Restalrig. [PRS Edinburgh, 19 December 1619]. [http://
2 CONC catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f943&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=henry+nisbet&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Brooke Family of Biel, reference GD6
2 CONC /943]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 August 1622: Sheriffdom of Midlothian: Contract whereby Marion Arnot, relict of James Nisbet, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, dispones to Henry Nisbet, her son, her right of conjunct fee or liferent in four oxgates of land in
2 CONC  Restalrig. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f944&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=henry+nisbet&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Brooke Family of
2 CONC  Biel, reference GD6/944]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 January 1637: Letters of four forms at the instance of Henry Nisbett, portioner of Rastelrig, against Earl of Mar, to infeft said Henry in the Kirklandis of Lentrethane, Landrik and Pettinane with teinds of the half kirk of L
2 CONC andrik called the out kirk of Landrik and of the kirks of Lentrethane and Pettinane apprised by said Henry from James, Earl of Buchan. 5 January 1637. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=G
2 CONC D16%2f41%2f317&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=henry+nisbit&ko=a&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Airlie, Legal Papers: General Legal Letters & Papers, reference GD16/41/317]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 March 1639: [Extract] Decreet in action at the instance of said Henry Nisbit against James, Lord Ogiluie, James, Master of Ogiluie, John Ogiluie of Innerkeillour and others for payment of duties furth of the kirklands of Len
2 CONC trathen and teinds of parish kirk thereof and of the kirklands of Lanerk and Pettinane with the teinds. 31 March 1639. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD16%2f41%2f317&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn
