2 CONC rgh, 1908), 770 pp.]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/brucesofairththe00arms/page/n224/mode/1up The Bruces of Airth and their Cadets: 93]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ij/johnstone04.php Stirnet: Johnstone 04]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://tompaterson.co.uk/bruce/BruceStenhouse.htm Bruce of Stenhouse]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Rachael_Johnstone_%281%29 werelate]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT WILLIAM BRUCE, obtained Stenhouse from his grandfather in 1611 and was created a baronet of Nova Scotia Sept. 29, 1628. Married 1st the daughter of General Middleton of Letham and 2nd to Rachel widow of John Jackson. He built [htt
2 CONC ps://tompaterson.co.uk/places/AMS200sten.htm Stenhouse] in about 1622. They had William Bruce, b abt 1682 and Charles Bruce.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bruce-754
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel Johnston was born 1588 in Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland, daughter of Archibald Johnston and Rachel Arnot. She was the sister of Joseph Johnston, James Johnston and Janet (Johnston) Inglis.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel married Johnne Jaksoune on January 11, 1604 in the parish of Edinburgh, Midlothian.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel and John had at least one child baptised in Edinburgh:
2 CONT *Elizabeth Jacksone (bap 10 Apr 1614)[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William Bruce in 1621 (to 1630) in Stafford England.  William Bruce obtained Stenhouse from his grandfather in 1611 and was created a baronet of Nova Scotia Sept. 29, 1628. Married 1st the daughter of General Middleton
2 CONC  of Letham and 2nd to Rachel widow of John Jackson. He built Stenhouse in about 1622.
2 CONT
2 CONT William and his first wife had at least one child:
2 CONT *Jonet Bruce who married a Michael Nasmyth in 1661[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William had at least six children with Rachel Johnstone, all baptised in Edinburgh:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Williame Bruce (bap 19 Aug 1621)[2]
2 CONT # Jeane Bruce (bap 22 Sep 1622)[3]
2 CONT # Rachel Bruce (bap 1 Feb 1625) [4]
2 CONT # James Bruce (bap 23 Jan 1628)[5]
2 CONT # Jonet Bruce (bap 6 May 1629)[6]
2 CONT # Archebald Bruce (bap 9 Jul 1630)[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Bruce died in February 1630 and his will was confirmed in Stirling Commissary Court on 9 June 1630.[8][9]
2 CONT
