2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04paul/page/34/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 34]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Ogilvie of Inchmartine, younger, here treated, predeceased his father and died intestate on 21 November 1592. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Testament Dative and Inventory ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 23 November 1596. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Patrik Ogilwie, younger, apparent of Inchemartene, sheriffdom of Perth, reference CC
2 CONC 8/8/28]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Ogilvy of Inchmartine, younger, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Halyburton/6000000034913984968?through=6000000015193766694 She is noticed as his wife in an antinuptial contract of marriage dat
2 CONC ed 11 August 1581. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD181%2f35&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1560&di=n NRS: GD181/35]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 August 1581: Antenuptial contract of marriage between Margaret Halibirtoun, daughter of Sir George Haliburtoun of Petcur, kt, and Patrick Ogilvy, son and apparent heir of Patrick Ogilvy of Inchemertyne. [https://catalogue.nr
2 CONC scotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD181%2f35&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+ogilvy&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1550&dt=1560&di=n National Records of Scotland, Aboyne Muniments, reference GD181/35]'''
2 CONT
