1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Robert Colvill of Cleish</strong>, who, as eldest son of his father, had a Crown charter of the barony on 1 February 1635, and was served heir to his father 12 September 1643. A warrant to dub him knight was granted by Ki
2 CONC ng Charles I, on 2 May 1632. He was created a Peer by King Charles II. when in exile, 4 January 1651, as <strong>LORD COLVILL OF OCHILTREE</strong>, with remainder to his heirs-male whatsoever. He died at Crombie on Monday 25 Augu
2 CONC st 1662, and was buried there that very night. He married, first, Janet, second daughter of Sir John Wemyss by his second wife Mary, daughter of Sir James Stewart of Doun, and sister of John, first Earl of Wemyss. She died at Clei
2 CONC sh in April 1655, without issue. He married, secondly, Euphan, daughter of Sir Thomas Myrton of Cambo by a daughter of Halket of Pitfirrane. She had a charter as Lady Colvill 23 December 1656. She survived him and married, secondl
2 CONC y, James, brother of Sir David Carmichael of Balmedie. She died 8 November 1708, and was buried in the Chapel of Crombie. Her testament was given up at St. Andrews, and confirmed on 5 October 1709, by Cecilia Carmichael, Lady Barn
2 CONC s, her daughter."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft#page/572/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. II, page 573
