1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MAJOR FRANCIS SINCLAIR===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Major Francis Sinclair is the son of James Sinclair of Murkle. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02paul/page/340 The Scots Peerage II: 340] His father gave him a bond for two thousand merks Scots on 10 May 1620. [htt
2 CONC p://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD139%2f538&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Francis+Sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1670&di=n NRS: GD139/538]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It has been suggested that he is the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Francis-Sinclair/6000000020054796149?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1576265039765&through=6000000114795121288 but this seems unlikely.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Major Francis Sinclair married Janet Sutherland, daughter of Alexander Sutherland of Forss. The marriage contract is dated 19 July 1621. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun02paul/page/340 The Scots Peerage II: 340] On
2 CONC  10 October 1629 Major Francis acknowledged receipt of four thousand merks Scots from his father-in-law in respect of his wife's "tocherguid". [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD139%2f5
2 CONC 39&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Francis+Sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1670&di=n NRS: GD139/539]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 May 1620: Bond of James Sinclair of Murkle to Francis Sinclair, his son, for 2,000 merks Scots. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD139%2f538&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Francis+Sin
2 CONC clair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Sutherland family of Forse, Sutherland, reference GD139/538]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 October 1629: Extract discharge by Francis Sinclair in Murkle, son of James Sinclair of Murkle, to Alexander Sutherland of Forse, his father in law, for 4000 merks Scots as tocherguid. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrs
2 CONC onlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD139%2f539&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Francis+Sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Sutherland family of Forse, Sutherland, reference GD139/539]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 June 1633: Signet letters of horning raised at the instance of Alexander Sutherland of Fors against Sir James Sinclair of Murkle for failing to pay to Alexander 4000 merks assigned (25 July 1629) to him by Francis Sinclair; w
2 CONC hich sum of money was due to Francis by the late James Sinclair of Murkle, his father, and the above Sir James, his brother, under the marriage contract (19 July 1621, registered Register of Deeds, 22 June 1632) between Francis on
2 CONC  the one part and Jonnett Sinclair [sic], daughter of the above Alexander Sutherland, on the other part. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD139%2f133&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Francis+
2 CONC Sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Sutherland family of Forse, Sutherland, reference GD139/133]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 October 1635: Signet letters of loosing of arrestment raised at the instance of Alexander Sutherland of Forss, Major Francis Sinclair having caused fence and arrest 600 merks, owing to him by Sir James Sinclair of Murkle his
2 CONC  brother, "... upoun meir malice .... [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD139%2f134&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sutherland+of+forss&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1650&di=n National Records of Scotl
2 CONC and, Papers of the Sutherland family of Forse, Sutherland, reference GD139/134]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
