1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Ogilvy,_2nd_Lord_Banff
2 CONT
2 CONT George Ogilvy, 2nd Lord Banff From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to navigationJump to search
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms of the Lords of Banff as shown in Brown's The Peerage of Scotland, 1834 George Ogilvy, 2nd Lord Banff (died March 1668) was member of the old Scottish Parliament, a feudal baron, and a Cavalier.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents 1	Family 2	Career 3	Marriage 4	References Family The son of Sir George Ogilvy, 1st Lord Banff, and 1st Baronet (1627), by his spouse Janet, daughter of William Sutherland, Lord Duffus. George, 2nd Lord Banff, was, on 29 O
2 CONC ctober 1663, served heir to his father in the baronies of Inchdrewer and Mountbray, and on 24 September 1664, in lands in the parish of Gamrie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Career Prior to succeeding his father in the honours, he represented Nairnshire in the Parliament held in Edinburgh on 4 June 1644. Like his father, "conspicuous at the King's side", he was an adherent of King Charles I and his so
2 CONC n, Charles II. He fought for the latter at the battle of Worcester, from which he escaped.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage The second Lord Banff married Agnes, daughter of Sir Alexander Falconer, 1st Lord Falconer of Halkerstoun. They had issue, ten children: eight daughters and two sons, of whom:
2 CONT
2 CONT # George Ogilvy, 3rd Lord Banff (1649–1713) with issue.
2 CONT # Sir Alexander Ogilvy, 1st Baronet of Forglen, M.P. (1651–1727) with issue.
2 CONT # Agnes (b.1651) married Francis Gordon of Craig of Auchindoir.
2 CONT # Helen (c1656 - 1714), who married Sir Robert Lauder of Beilmouth, Knt.
2 CONT # Mary (b.c1657), married in 1680 John Forbes of Balflugg .
2 CONT References Balfour Paul, Sir James, The Scots Peerage, Edinburgh, 1905, volume 2, p. 14, under 'Banff'. Peerage of Scotland Preceded by George Ogilvy	Lord Banff 1663–1668	Succeeded by George Ogilvy _____________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p7530.htm#i75296
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir George Ogilvy, 2nd Lord Banff1  M, #75296, d. March 1668 Last Edited=4 Sep 2016
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir George Ogilvy, 2nd Lord Banff was the son of Sir George Ogilvy, 1st Lord Banff and Janet Sutherland.1 A contract for the marriage of Sir George Ogilvy, 2nd Lord Banff and Agnes Falconer was signed on 12 August 1648.2 He died i
2 CONC n March 1668.1
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Nairn in 1644.1 He fought in the Battle of Worcester, for King Charles II.1 He succeeded as the 2nd Lord Banff [S., 1642] on 11 August 1663.1 He succeeded as the 2nd Baronet Og
2 CONC ilvie [S., 1627] on 11 August 1663.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sir George Ogilvy, 2nd Lord Banff and Agnes Falconer
2 CONT #Janet Ogilvy+3
2 CONT #Hon. Marjorie Ogilvy+4
2 CONT #Hon. Sir Alexander Ogilvy, Lord Forglen+5 b. a 1649, d. 30 Mar 1727
2 CONT #Sir George Ogilvy, 3rd Lord Banff+1 b. 9 Sep 1649, d. Nov 1713
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT * [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinc
2 CONC t or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 410. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *[S2] Peter W. Hammond, editor, The Complete Peerage or a History of the House of Lords and All its Members From the Earliest Times, Volume XIV: Addenda & Corrigenda (Stroud, Gloucestershire, U.K.: Sutton Publishing, 1998), page 6
2 CONC 3. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage, Volume XIV.
