1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alexander of Kinminitie, son of James Sutherland, of Kinminitie, had, on 25 August 1675, from George, Lord Strathnaver, a gift of the ward duties of Skelbo, married Jean, daughter of Thomas Forbes of Waterton,[4] a
2 CONC nd had two sons, Alexander and Thomas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The latter married in 1686 Violet, daughter of Michael Strachan of Auchnagat, afterwards wife of George Gordon, younger, of Glastyrim.[5] They had a son James, born about September 1688. Thomas died 17 April 1692.[6] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander, the elder son, was apparently twice married, his second wife being Marie Ogilvy,[7] daughter of the first Lord Banff. He died 11 November 1710, leaving two sons, Alexander, and Mr. James, the latter of whom, an advocate
2 CONC , had the lands of Croftcroy, on 30 July 1694, from the town of Elgin,[8] and died s.p. The eldest, Alexander, succeeded to Kinminitie and other lands in Banffshire, and died in July 1725.[9] He married Elizabeth Edwards, afterwar
2 CONC ds, in 1726, wife of Sir Kenneth McKenzie of Grandvale.[10] He had issue with other children, a son, Alexander, who succeeded him, but died before 1726, and a daughter, Mary, married to Alexander Sutherland of Clyne.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www26.us.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/12/mode/2up Page12 No. 66
2 CONT
2 CONT (66) Alexander Sutherland of Kinminitie. Married Jean, daughter of Thomas Forbes of Waterton, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 66(a) Alexander (No. 67 below).
2 CONT * 66(b) Thomas Sutherland, died 17th April 1692. He married, 1686, Violet, daughter of Michael Strachan of Auchnagat
