1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ELIZABETH MACINTOSH===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/fastiecclesiaesc06scot/page/365/mode/1up Fasti of the Church of Scotland VI: 365]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                      1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''13 February 1649: Retour of the special service of Elizabeth McIntosche [McIntosh], spouse of Mr. Lachlan Grant, minister of the Word of God at the church of Moy, as heir of the deceased Lady Elizabeth Sinclair, her grandmother
2 CONC , in the lands of Dundelchaig [Duntelchaig] with pertinents lying in the Castlelands of Inverness, which are held in chief of William McIntosche [McIntosh] of Torcastell [Torcastle], son and heir of the deceased Sir Lachlan McInto
2 CONC sche [McIntosh] of Torcastell, in free blench, and which have been in the superior's hands for twenty-seven years since the death of the said Elizabeth Sinclair, which took place in July 1622.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The retour was exped in the court-house of Inverness on 13th February 1649, before Thomas Schives [Shivas] of Muirtoun [Muirton], sheriff-depute of Inverness, and the following jury--Alexander Baillie of Dunzeane [Dunain], Alex
2 CONC ander Fraser of Erchet [Erchite], John Robertsone [Robertson] of Inches [Inshes], Robert Baillie, Alexander Dumbar [Dunbar], David Cuthbert, Mr. Walter Ross, Alexander McPhersone [McPherson], George Dunbar, William Cuthbert, James
2 CONC  Dumbar [Dunbar], Robert Monro [Munro], John Munro, Alexander Duff, and Alexander Grant, burgesses of Inverness. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD176%2f401&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=
2 CONC lachlan+grant&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Family of Mackintosh of Mackintosh, reference GD176/401]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 January 1650: Letters of Suspension of Horning raised against William McIntosche [McIntosh] of Torcastle by Elizabeth McIntosche [McIntosh], who claims to be granddaughter and heir of the deceased Elizabeth Sinclair, Lady Mc
2 CONC Ky [McKay], & legal documents following thereon. In the lands of Dundalschak [Duntelchaig], Lachlan McIntosche [McIntosh] of Eschieghe [Essich] having become cautioner for him; dated 17th January 1650. [http://catalogue.nrscotland
2 CONC .gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD176%2f403&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Elizabeth+Sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y Papers of the Family of Mackintosh of Mackintosh, reference GD176/403]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 February 1650: Decreet of Declarator of the redemption of these lands by William McIntoische [McIntosh] of Torcastle, son and heir of the deceased Sir Lachlan McIntoische [McIntosh] of Torcastle, against the foresaid Elizabe
2 CONC th McIntoische, lawful daughter of the deceased John McIntoisch [McIntosh] in Dundelchak by Christian McKy [McKay], his spouse, and heir retoured to Dame Elizabeth Sinclair, her grandmother, and against Mr. Lachlan Grant, minister
2 CONC  at Kingousie [Kingussie], her spouse; dated 28th February 1650. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD176%2f403&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Elizabeth+Sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&
2 CONC di=y Papers of the Family of Mackintosh of Mackintosh, reference GD176/403]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 March 1650: Precept of Clare Constat by William Mackintoshe [McIntosh] of Torcastell [Torcastle] in favour of the said Elizabeth McIntoshe in the lands of Dundelchack; dated at Inverness, 5th March 1650; likewise
2 CONT (4) Instrument of Sasine following thereupon, dated 26th April 1650. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD176%2f403&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Elizabeth+Sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1
2 CONC 700&di=y Papers of the Family of Mackintosh of Mackintosh, reference GD176/403]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 June 1650: Deed of Resignation of the foresaid lands as wadset on 5th June 1620, by the said Elizabeth McIntosche in favour of William McIntosche of Torcastle, dated at Moy, 10th June 1650; witnesses, William McIntosche [McI
2 CONC ntosh] of Correbruch [Corribrough], Robert McIntoshe [McIntosh] of Loynvuilge [Lynwilg], Mr. Donald Fraser, clerk to the Presbytery of Inverness, and Angus McQueen, lawful son of Angus McQueen of Ravogbeig. [http://catalogue.nrsco
2 CONC tland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD176%2f403&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Elizabeth+Sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y Papers of the Family of Mackintosh of Mackintosh, reference GD176/403]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 June 1650: Renunciation by Duncan Grant, sometime in Gartlay [Gartlie] and now in Dundelchag, and Katherine Macdonald [McDonald], his spouse, in favour of the said Mr. Lachlan Grant and his spouse, who have paid him £1000, of
2 CONC  his tack of the lands of Dundelchag; dated 5th June 1650. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD176%2f403&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Elizabeth+Sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y P
2 CONC apers of the Family of Mackintosh of Mackintosh, reference GD176/403]'''
