1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir John Moncreiffe the twelfth Laird and chief of Clan Moncreiffe was made Baronet of Nova Scotia in April 1626.[2] However John was unable to support the king and signed the National Covenant in 1638.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John Moncreiff, of Moncreiff</strong>, co Perth, 2nd but 1st surviving son and heir of William Moncreiff of the same (who sat as a minor Baron [S] 1579), by Anne, daughter of Robert Murray, of Abercairnie, sat (as 'Laird 
2 CONC of Easter Moncreiff') as a minor Baron [S] 1605, and was created a Baronet [S] as 'of Moncreiff', 22 April, sealed 22 June 1626, with rem. to heirs male whatsoever, and with grant of, presumably, 16,000 acres in Nova Scotia, entit
2 CONC led the Barony of Moncreiff, of which he had seizin in the same month of June; was M.P. [S] for Perthshire, 1639-41. He married firstly Anne, daughter of David Beaton, of Creich. He married secondly, in or before 1635, Mary, daugh
2 CONC ter of William (Murray), 2nd Earl of Tullibardine [S], by his 2nd wife Dorothea, daughter of John (Stewart), 5th Earl of Atholl [S]. She died December 1650 'att Moncreiffe at Stratherne', and he died shortly afterwards."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n329/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 310
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations 
