1 NOTE {geni:about_me}   John Grant, 6th of Freuchie is the son of John Grant, 5th of Freuchie and Lady Lilias Murray.1 He married Mary Ogilvy, daughter of Walter Ogilvy, 1st Lord Ogilvy of Deskford.1 He died in 1637.1
2 CONT
2 CONT      John Grant, 6th of Freuchie lived at Multen, Scotland.1 He lived at Freuchie, Scotland.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Grant, 6th of Freuchie and Mary Ogilvy
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Mary Grant+2 d. a 25 Dec 1707
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Patrick Grant1
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Major George Grant1
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Mungo Grant1
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Robert Grant1
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Thomas Grant1
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Alexander Grant1
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Anne Grant1
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Lilias Grant1
2 CONT
2 CONT     * James Grant, 7th of Freuchie+1 b. 24 Jun 1616, d. Sep 1663
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p273.htm#i2721
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Earl Sir John Grant II, Knight  Born 	17 Aug 1596  	of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland  Died 	1 Apr 1637  Buried 	Holyrood Abbey, Canongate, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland   Person ID 	I613927  	Stewart Genealogy Last Modifi
2 CONC ed 	5 Jun 2013 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father   John Grant, laird of Freuchie,   b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland   d. 20 Sep 1622  Mother 	Lilias Murray,   b. Abt 1576, Tullibardine, Blackford, Perthshire, Scotland  d. Abt 1643  (Age ~ 67 years)  Married 	15
2 CONC  Apr 1591  Family ID 	F318176  	Group Sheet  |  Family Chart
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 	Ancestors Mary Ogilvy,   d. Aft 1646  [Expand] Married 	Abt 11 Dec 1613  Children  	 +	1. Lieutenant-Colonel Patrick Grant,   b. of, Cluniemore   d. Aft 30 Jun 1672 +	2. Alexander Grant,   b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray,
2 CONC  Scotland    d. Aft 1665 +	3. Robert Grant,   b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland    d. Bef 22 Aug 1653 Married: 2x	4. Mungo Grant,   b. of, Kinchirdie   d. Aft 28 Dec 1679 Married: 1x	5. Anne Grant,   b. of, Freuchie, Crom
2 CONC dale, Moray, Scotland  Married: 1x	6. Lilias Grant,   b. of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland  +	7. James Grant, laird of Freuchie,   b. 24 Jun 1616, of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland   d. 1663, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Sco
2 CONC tland   (Age 46 years) +	8. Mary Grant,   b. Abt 1624, of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland   d. Aft 25 Dec 1707  (Age ~ 83 years)
2 CONT  	9. Captain George Grant,   b. Abt 1631, of, Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland  +	10. Thomas Grant,   b. 1637, of, Balmacaan, Urquhart, Inverness-shire, Scotland Family ID 	F318191  	Group Sheet  |  Family Chart
2 CONT
2 CONT         KINSHIP: Son and heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT         HONORS: Knighted, 1617.
2 CONT
2 CONT         PROPERTY: Laird of Freuchie {Freuchie, Cromdale, Moray, Scotland}.
2 CONT         PROPERTY: On the resignation of his father, he and his wife had a royal charter erecting the lands of Mulben with its castle, Mekle Ballinbreiche, with fishings, etc., the lands of Cardeny, Auldcash and Forgie, into the fr
2 CONC ee barony of Mulben 1616.
2 CONT         PROPERTY: Retoured heir to his father in the lands of Lethen 1623.
2 CONT         PROPERTY: Twice exchanged the jointure lands of his wife, first 1627 the lands of Lethen and others 1627, afterwards,when Lethen was sold, for the lands in the lordship of Urquhart and others 1634.
2 CONT
2 CONT         PROBATE: Will dated 31 May 1637.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Sources  	
