1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == FREDERICK LYON OF BRIGTOUN ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Frederick Lyon of Brigtoun married Jean Stewart, the daughter of Sir James Stewart of Eday and his wife Margaret Lyon. [https://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft#page/574/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 574]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Frederick Lyon of Brigtoun is reported to have died in 1660. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ll/lyon02.php Stirnet Lyon 02]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence Published by the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 June 1628: Antenuptial contract of marriage between Frederick Lyone of Brigtoune and Margaret Ogilvie daughter of Sir Patrick Ogilvie of Inchmartine and dame Anna Campbell, his spouse. [Note: This Margaret Ogilvie not in Sco
2 CONC ts Peerage]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD248%2f577%2f8&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+ogilvie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1600&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Ogilv
2 CONC y family, Earls of Seafield (Seafield Papers), reference GD248/577/8]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 January 1654: Bond by Frederick Lyon of Brigtoun and Patrick Lyon, fiar thereof, his eldest son, the said Frederick being tutor to Patrick, Earl of Kingorne, to appoint factors and chamberlains to manage the estate of the sa
2 CONC id Earl by the advice and consent of Patrick, Earl of Panmure, grandfather to the said Earl, and George, Lord Brechin, his son [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f2855&st=1&tc=
2 CONC y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=lyon+of+brigtoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Maule Family, Earls of Dalhousie, reference GD45/16/2855]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 February 1666: Charge to the enter heir at the instance of James, Lord Ogilvie, against [David] Erskine of Dune, eldest son and apparent heir of Sir Alexander Erskine of Dun, and [Patrick] Lyon, eldest son and apparent heir 
2 CONC of [blank] Lyon of Brigtoun. 22 February 1666. With relevant papers. (5 items). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/overview.aspx?st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD16%2f41%2f464&ro=m&df=&dt=1700&di=y National
2 CONC  Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Airlie, reference GD16/41/464]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
