1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sir John Haldane, eleventh Laird of Gleneagles was a professional soldier who fought for Henry, Prince of Orange, along with his brother, James Haldane in the Netherlands<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Sir John Haldane, 11th of Gleneagles''' 
2 CONT * Son of Sir James Haldane, 10th of Gleneagles and Lady Margaret Murray.
2 CONT * Married by contract, '''firstly''', Catherine Wemyss, daughter of Sir John Wemyss of Wemyss and Mary Stewart, on 18 August 1624.
2 CONT * Married by contract, '''secondly''', Margaret Fraser, daughter of Simon Fraser, 6th Lord (Fraser of) Lovat and Jean Stewart, on 22 December 1634.
2 CONT * Died on 3 September 1650, killed in action, although there is a family tradition that he was taken prisoner instead.
2 CONT
2 CONT With his brother James, he joined the forces which were fighting in Netherlands against Imperial troops under Frederic Henry, Prince of Orange.
2 CONT * Lived at Gleneagles, Scotland.
2 CONT * Before 1624 he returned to Scotland.
2 CONT * Held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Perthshire in 1630.1
2 CONT * Appointed Knight in 1633.
2 CONT * Colonel of the forces raised in the sheriffdom of Perth.
2 CONT * Held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Perthshire between 1643 and 1645.
2 CONT * Fought in the Battle of Dunbar on 3 September 1650. '''Children of Sir John Haldane, 11th of Gleneagles and Catherine Wemyss'''
2 CONT * John Haldane, 12th of Gleneagles d. a 1660
2 CONT * Jean Haldane
2 CONT * Marie Haldane
2 CONT * Isabel Haldane
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of Sir John Haldane, 11th of Gleneagles and Margaret Fraser'''
2 CONT * Mungo Haldane, 13th of Gleneagles d. May 1685
2 CONT * Patrick Haldane, 1st of Lanrick b. c 1637, d. May 1686<br/>
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p1678.htm#i16773<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
