1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/36258974/mary-clifton
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, first, on Feb 2,1626/7 at Halifax, Yorkshire, Henry Butterworth.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, second, shortly after Jan 28,1640/1, Thomas Clifton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children(by first marriage): John Butterworth, Abraham Butterworth, Mary Butterworth Mason, Samuel Butterworth, and Henry Butterworth. NOTE: Older information names a daughter Sarah, born c1623, who married Pardon Tillinghast. How
2 CONC ever, she was born four years before the marriage of Henry and Mary, so she may not even be of the Butterworth family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children(by second marriage): Patience Clifton Beere/Berry Allen and Hope Clifton Holder. Some sources say the Mary Clifton Bowen was a daughter of hers, but Mary was born in 1628 (well before the marriage of Thomas Clifton and Ma
2 CONC ry), and she may have been a daughter of Thomas Clifton by a prior wife.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''The genealogical dictionary of Rhode Island: comprising three generations of ... By John Osborne Austin, George Andrews Moriarty
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=LA7ntaS11ocC&pg=PA102&lpg=PA102&dq=Thomas+Clifton+1681&source=bl&ots=Zr9wpswrPf&sig=WfM6k9uuvr1pBWqCeV3IBqrR-6M&hl=en&ei=K812TrCyD4fKiALa7L35AQ&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=4&ved=0CCwQ6AE
2 CONC wAzgU#v=onepage&q=Clifton&f=false/ The genealogical dictionary of Rhode Island: comprising three generations of ... By John Osborne Austin, George Andrews Moriarty]
2 CONT *Pg. 48
2 CONT *''''''THOMAS CLIFTON. b. 1606 d. 1681, Jul. 9, mar. 1641 MARY BUTTERWORTH b. 1600 d. 1687, Jan. 26. ch'''''': I. Hope d. 1681 Jan 16 mar. 1665 Dec. 30 Christopher Holder, II. Patience b. 1646, Jul 2. d. 1692, Oct. 16, 1mar. 1664,
2 CONC  Sep. 4. John Beere, 2mar. 1677, May 16. William Allen.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *''''''New England marriages prior to 1700 By Clarence Almon Torrey, Elizabeth Petty Bentley
2 CONT *[http://books.google.com/books?id=mOgK8dM9qqUC&pg=PA162&lpg=PA162&dq=Thomas+Clifton+1681&source=bl&ots=ZgBobbMGNf&sig=SYyqHuvBmAATsiQcnydhoRmqRLU&hl=en&ei=H8x2TtOXMdHPiALBhfyzAg&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=7&ved=0CDwQ6AE
2 CONC wBjgU#v=onepage&q=Thomas%20Clifton%201681&f=false/ New England marriages prior to 1700 By Clarence Almon Torrey, Elizabeth Petty Bentley]
2 CONT *Pg. 162
2 CONT *''''''CLIFTON, Thomas (1606-1681) & Mary [BUTTERWORTH] (1600, 1606-1681, 1687), w Henry; aft 18 Jan 1640/1; Rehoboth/Newport
2 CONT
2 CONT http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~sam/butterworth/henry.html
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The Butterworth Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Butterworth was born ca 1598-1600, possibly in Rochdale, Lacastershire, England. While still in England, in married Mary (____) ca 1620. Henry died ca 1640 in Weymouth, Norfolk County, Massachusetts. It is not known when or 
2 CONC how he came to America, but his brother, Samuel is also to be found in Weymouth and Rehoboth town records.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, Mary, remarried in 1641 to Thomas Clifton, a Quaker, by whom she had two daughters, Hope and Patience. They moved to Newport, Rhode Island where Mary died on January 26, 1687/8.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Lanbotham
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Sex: F
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Born: 1600
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Died: 26 JAN 1687 in Newport,Newport,RI
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Reference: 1675
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1: Henry Butterworth, b. 1598/1600 in Rochdale,Lancaster,England
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Married: FEB 1626 in Halifax,York,England
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Mary Butterworth
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Abraham Butterworth
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. John Butterworth, b. ABT 1630 in Rochdale,Lancaster,England
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Sarah Butterworth, b. ABT 1640 in MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 2: Thomas Clifton
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Married: 1641 in Weymouth,MA
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Hope Clifton
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Patience Clifton, b. 2 JUL 1646
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Mary and Henry were married on 2 February 1626/27 in the St. John the Baptist Church, Halifax, Yorkshire, England.
2 CONT * After Henry's death in about 1636, Mary married Thomas Clifton after 28 January 1641, in Rehoboth, Plymouth Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
