1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir John Colquhoun, Baronet [S 1625] of Luss</strong>, 1st son and heir, born about 1622; succeeded to the family estates in 1647 (which had been preserved to the family by his uncle Sir Humphrey Colquhoun, of Balvie, who
2 CONC  was M.P. [S], for Dumbartonshire, 1643-49); succeeded to the Baronetcy about 1650. He purchased the estate of Balloch in 1652, and acquired that of Lochend, co Haddington (which, however, he sold in 1678) by marriage; was M.P. [S
2 CONC ] for Dumbartonshire 1650, 1661-63, 1665, 1667, and 1669-74. He married (contract 17 February 1636) Margaret, daughter and heir of Sir Gideon Baillie, Baronet [S 1636], by Magdalen, daughter and coheir of David Carnegie, style Lor
2 CONC d Carnegie. He died 11 April 1676. His widow married 1 April 1677, Archibald Stirling of Garden, and died 20 July 1679."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n313/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 294
