1 NAME Lilias /Colquhoun/
2 GIVN Lilias
2 SURN Colquhoun
2 _MARNM Colquhoun
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1630
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lilias Colquhoun is the daughter of Sir John Colquhoun of Luss, 1st Bt. and Lady Lilias Graham.2 She married John Napier of Kilmahew, younger, son of John Napier of Kilmahew and Lady Susannah Cuninghame, in 1649.1
2 CONT
2 CONT From  http://www.ebooksread.com/authors-eng/william-fraser/the-chiefs-of-colquhoun-and-their-country-volume-1-sar/page-27-the-chiefs-of-colquhoun-and-their-country-volume-1-sar.shtml
2 CONT
2 CONT * She married John Napier, eldest son and apparent heir of Robert Napier of Kilmahew, in the county of Dumbarton. Their marriage-contract is dated at the place of Kilmahew and of Rossdhu, 10th and 12th February respectively, 1649.
2 CONC  In the contract, in which Lilias is designated second sister of John Colquhoun, they engaged to solemnize and complete the band of matrimony betwixt them in face of God's holy kirk and congregation.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Lilias Colquhoun and John Napier of Kilmahew, younger
2 CONT # Margaret Napier 
2 CONT # Katherine Napier
2 CONT
