1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ARCHIBALD CAMPBELL OF KNOCKMELLIE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/cc4aq/campbell11.php Stirnet: Campbell 11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Commentary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Archibald is the half-brother of the 3rd Baronet of Auchinbreck who died childless, so Archibald's son Duncan became the 4th Baronet of Auchinbreck.
2 CONT
2 CONT There has been a lot of confusion regarding this particular line of descent from Rev. Dugald Campbell of Letterkenny, with ambiguous documents presented by a number of parties to support conflicting theories.  While there are clea
2 CONC r inaccuracies with all of them, I believe that research can ultimately reconcile them in a manner that is most consistent with the descent portrayed in the entry for the Auchinbreck baronets within the 1914 edition of Burke's Pee
2 CONC rage.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000053900663830&
2 CONT
2 CONT For a more complete consideration of the merits of the conflicting theories, see the linked blogpost entries, along with updates, by Jack Mason.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://lostodonnells.blogspot.com/2015/09/maria-daughter-of-dugald-campbell.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://lostodonnells.blogspot.com/2015/09/reconciling-traditions.html
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-379451941-1-502858/sir-archibald-campbell-of-knockme-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-31f8e3175fc5f7cc006548be968b6323&mrid=9e726ae1a5281a612fda628fbbb8
2 CONC eed7 MyHeritage Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 8 2023, 23:15:09 UTC''
