1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Drummond, 1st Viscount Strathallan was born in 1617/18.1 He was the son of John Drummond, 2nd Lord Maderty and Margaret Leslie.2 He married Elizabeth Johnston, daughter of Sir Archibald Johnston, on 28 Febr
2 CONC uary 1667/68.1 He died on 23 March 1687/88.2
2 CONT      He was educated at St. Andrews University, St. Andrews, Fife, Scotland.1 He fought in the English Civil War, as a Royalist.1 He fought in the Battle of Worcester in 1651, where he was captured by the Parliamentarians and impr
2 CONC isoned.1 He gained the rank of Lieutenant-General between 1655 and 1665 in the Russian Army, against the Poles and Tartars.1 He gained the rank of General from 1666 to 1667 in the Scottish forces.2 He was appointed Privy Counsello
2 CONC r (P.C.) [ Scotland] in January 1665/66.1 He was appointed Privy Counsellor (P.C.) [Scotland] from 1666/67 to May 1674.1 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Perthshire between 1669 and 1674.2 He held the office o
2 CONC f Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Perthshire in 1678.2 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Perthshire from 1681 to 1682.2 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Perthshire from 1685 to 1686.2 He he
2 CONC ld the office of Commissioner of the Treasury [Scotland] in March 1685/86.2 He was created 1st Lord Drummond of Cromlix [ Scotland] on 16 August 1686, with special remainder to heirs male whatsoever.1 He was created 1st Viscount S
2 CONC trathallan [ Scotland] on 16 August 1686, with special remainder to heirs male whatsoever.1 He held the office of Commissioner of the Treasury [ Scotland] in 1687.2
2 CONT Children of William Drummond, 1st Viscount Strathallan and Elizabeth Johnston
2 CONT Hon. Margaret Drummond+2 d. 21 Mar 1695/96
2 CONT William Drummond, 2nd Viscount Strathallan+1 b. 8 Aug 1670, d. 7 Jul 1702
