2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 March 1621: Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that he has given certain lands in the barony of Cambusnethan to John Somerville, junior of Cambusnethan, the son and apparent heir of James Somerville, senior o
2 CONC f Cambusnethan, his father, to be held by him in liferent following the death of his father: “in vitali redditu post decessum dicti Jac”. The charter reserved the  liferent interest in these lands that was held by James Somerville
2 CONC  junior, also the son of John Somerville, junior of Cambusnethen: “reservando Jacobo Somervell, juniori, filio dicti Jo.,heredibus ejus”, who also had a grant of the lands and barony of Cambusnethan, which land and barony had been
2 CONC  resigned in his favour by his grandfather, James Somerville, senior of Cambusnethan. His grandfather also reserved his own liferent interest in the barony, as well as that of his son and apparent heir, John Somerville, junior of 
2 CONC Cambusnethan, and John junior’s wife Marie Hamilton. The King also subscribed anew to incorporate these lands in the free barony of Cambusnethan, which lands and barony was to be held by James Somerville, junior, and his lawful ma
2 CONC le heirs, whom failing by his brother THOMAS SOMERVILLE and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by his brother Patrick Somerville and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by the nearest male heirs whomever of James Somerville, juni
2 CONC or, who bear the name and arms of Somerville. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/48/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, 1620-33, charter number 148]'''
1 FAMC @F6000000181345145870@
1 RFN geni:6000000181115296821
1 SUBM @S6000000008879398364@
