1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == PATRICK SOMERVILLE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Somerville, here treated, is the youngest son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Somerville-junior-of-Cambusnethan/6000000019459772315?through=6000000181086502842  [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogu
2 CONC e/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1485&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=somervall&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD109/1485] and the younger brother of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Somerville-of-Cambusnethan/6000000023678173866?thro
2 CONC ugh=6000000181086502842 [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1488&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+james+somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=&di=n NRS: GD109/1488]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Father's Testament Dative and Inventory ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The testament dative and inventory of John Somerville of Cambusnethan, here treated, was given up by: "Patrick Somervell youngest lawfull son to the defunct as lawll creditor to him in suo far as the defunct was justlie adebted
2 CONC  & awand to him the sowm of 2000 mks Scots mony prinll sown 500 lbs mony foirsd of liquidat expenss with the @rent of the said prinll sowm frme the terme of Whitsunday 1634 yeirs extending now to the sowm of 265 lbs mony foirsd co
2 CONC nteinit in and band & obligatioune mad & granted be the defund to the said Patrick Somervell of the dait the [ blank ] day of Junij 1634 yeirs".'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''At the time of his death, John Somerville of Cambusnethan was owed £400 Scots money, with £10 of liquidate expenses, by Sir John Hamiltoun of Bargany, knight, Sir John Hamiltoun of Carridden, knight, Sir John Hamiltoun of Broom
2 CONC hill, knight, and Gavin Hamilton of Raploch. [Note] William Hendersoun, merchant burgess of Glasgow, acted himself as cautioner for Patrick Somerville, and confirmation was granted to him on 2 February 1672. [National Records of S
2 CONC cotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The Testament Dative of John Sommervell of Cambusnethan, reference CC9/7/39]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000181317449028 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000181331996835 Image of Testament]
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000181317224997 Image of Testament]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: The bond for £400 mentioned here was subsequently assigned by Patrick Somervill, here treated, who is identified in the assignation as the brother of the deceased Sir James Somerville of Cambusnethan. [https://catalogue.n
2 CONC rscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1488&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+james+somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=&di=n NRS: GD109/1488]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 March 1621: Charter by which James VI, King of Scots, confirms that he has given certain lands in the barony of Cambusnethan to John Somerville, junior of Cambusnethan, the son and apparent heir of James Somerville, senior o
2 CONC f Cambusnethan, his father, to be held by him in liferent following the death of his father: “in vitali redditu post decessum dicti Jac”. The charter reserved the  liferent interest in these lands that was held by James Somerville
2 CONC  junior, also the son of John Somerville, junior of Cambusnethen: “reservando JACOBO  SOMERVELL, juniori, filio dicti Jo.,heredibus ejus”, who also had a grant of the lands and barony of Cambusnethan, which land and barony had bee
2 CONC n resigned in his favour by his grandfather, James Somerville, senior of Cambusnethan. His grandfather also reserved his own liferent interest in the barony, as well as that of his son and apparent heir, John Somerville, junior of
2 CONC  Cambusnethan, and John junior’s wife Marie Hamilton. The King also subscribed anew to incorporate these lands in the free barony of Cambusnethan, which lands and barony was to be held by James Somerville, junior, and his lawful m
2 CONC ale heirs, whom failing by his brother Thomas Somerville and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by his brother Patrick Somerville and his lawful male heirs, whom failing by the nearest male heirs whomever of James Somerville, jun
2 CONC ior, who bear the name and arms of Somerville. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/48/mode/1up Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, 1620-33, charter number 148]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 June 1634: Bond by John Somervall of Cambusnethene to Patrick Somervall, his youngest son, for 200 merks scots. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD109%2f1485&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&
2 CONC tp=n&k=somervall&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/1485]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 February 1637 and 12 December 1672: Bond by Sir John Hamiltoun of Bargany, kt., Sir John Hamiltoun of Carridden, kt., Sir John Hamiltoun of Brumhill, kt., and Gavin Hamiltoun of Ropploche, to John Somervell of Cambusnethen, 
2 CONC for £400 scots, with assignation thereof by Patrick Somervell, brother of deceased Sir James Somervell of Cambusnethen, son of said John, to [blank]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=G
2 CONC D109%2f1488&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+james+somervell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Dalrymple-Hamilton of Bargany, Ayrshire, reference GD109/1488]'''
