2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 May 1674: Commission by John, Lord Belhaven, and Margaret Hamilton, Lady Belhaven, his spouse, to William Broun, their servant, to require Robert Hamilton, clerk of Session, to repair with John Hamilton, his eldest son, to t
2 CONC heir house of Beill "wher Margaret Hamilton, our grandchyld, whoum the sayd Jhon Hamilton is to marie, remaynes, to the effect that hee maye have conference with her and that with consent of hise saed father and of use, Ser Robert
2 CONC  Hamilton of Sellvertonhill, father to the saed Margaret, and other frends, to agrie upon the conjunctfee and leyffrent to be provyded to her and upon other lawfull condetions of the sayd mariage". [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov
2 CONC .uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f2206&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+hamilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Brooke Family of Biel, reference GD6/2206]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 March 1686: Precept by James Hamilton, WS to Lady Belhaven, dowager following in a heritable bond granted by Robert Hamilton of Presmennan. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f
2 CONC 14%2f2%2f3%2f22&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Belhaven&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers Relating to Hamilton of Presmennan and Whittinghame, reference GD3/14/2/3/22]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 May 1688: Margaret Hamilton, Lady Belhaven, Beill, to [her niece Anne, duchess of Hamilton], sending walnuts, some julep and eleackticarie to help relieve the duke [of Hamilton's] illness. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/
2 CONC nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD406%2f1%2f3477&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+hamilton&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Douglas Hamilton Family, Dukes of Hamilton and Brand
2 CONC on, reference GD406/1/3477]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 August 1695: [James Hamilton of Pencaitland], Edinburgh, to the earl of Arran, referring to the serious illness of old Lady Belhaven [a natural daughter of the earl's great-grandfather], and sending him an account or money re
2 CONC ceived by his order. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD406%2f1%2f6653&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Belhaven&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Doug
2 CONC las Hamilton Family, Dukes of Hamilton and Brandon, reference GD406/1/6653]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 September 1695: [James Hamilton of Pencaitland], Edinburgh, to the earl of Arran, discussing the purchase of guineas, mentioning that an order has come for the release of the earl of Breadalbane, and giving news of the death
2 CONC  of old Lady Belhaven. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD406%2f1%2f6824&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Belhaven&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Do
2 CONC uglas Hamilton Family, Dukes of Hamilton and Brandon, reference GD406/1/6824]'''
