1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JAMES DUNLOP OF GARNKIRK ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''University Graduate; Solicitor in Glasgow; Member of the Faculty of Procurators of Glasgow; Merchant in Glasgow; Burgess and Guild Brother of Glasgow'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Dunlop of Garnkirk, here treated, is the only son of John Dunlop of Garnkirk and his wife Bessie Dunlop. He was born before 10 December 1633, the date upon which his baptism was registered at Glasgow in Lanarkshire, Scotl
2 CONC and. His baptismal record reads as follows: "Mr Jon Dunlap and Bessy Dunlap ane l. sone James Godfthrs James Dunlap and James Stewart elder." [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Baptisms, 1662-1743, reference 626/1/3] [https://
2 CONC www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000069312769086 Image of Baptismal Record]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Dunlop of Garnkirk, here treated, was served as heir to his deceased father on 28 September 1672. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5
2 CONC Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=snippet&q=dunlop&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam: 5574]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Education ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Dunlop of Garnkirk, here treated, was a graduate of the University of Glasgow. [https://archive.org/details/munimentaalmeuni03mait/page/n25/mode/1up Glasgow University Records. Volume I, p. xvi]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Burgess and Guild Brother of Glasgow ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Dunlop of Garnkirk was enrolled as a burgess and guild brother of the burgh of Glasgow on 28 February 1670. He was admitted in right of him being the only son of his deceased father, Mr. John Dunlop of Garnkirk, merchant 
2 CONC in Glasgow, burgess and guild brother of Glasgow. [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso43scotuoft#page/187/mode/1up James R. Anderson, The Burgesses & Guild Brethren of Glasgow, 1573-1750 (Printed for the Scottish Record So
2 CONC ciety by J. Skinner & Company Ltd., Edinburgh, 1925), page187]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Dunlop of Garnkirk, here treated, is reported to have died in 1695. [Newsletter of the Glasgow and West of Scotland Family History Society, No. 47 Autumn 1996, p. 11] He certainly died before 1 September 1687, when his so
2 CONC n James was served as his heir in the lands of Garnkirk and Casnockhill.  [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved
2 CONC =0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=snippet&q=garnkirk&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc. II]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Dunlop of Garnkirk, here treated, married https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Roberton/6000000001499815711?through=6000000001499754914 The marriage contract is dated 5 April 1654. [Newsletter of the Glasgow and West of 
2 CONC Scotland Family History Society, No. 47 Autumn 1996, pp. 11-16 for the first part of Donald Whyte's scholarly account of the family of Dunlop of Garnkirk]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
