2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 November 1669: Renunciation by James Dunlop, now of Garnkirk, only son and heir to the late Mr John Dunlop of Garnkirk, to William, Earl of Kilmarnock, of an annual rent corresponding to the principal sum of 5,000 marks. [ht
2 CONC tp://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD8%2f854&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=garnkirk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Boyd Papers, Burgh of Kilmarnock, reference GD8/8
2 CONC 54]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
