1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JAMES DUNLOP OF HOUSEHILL===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 August 1670: Precept under the testimony of the Great Seal of Charles II narrating that John, Earl of Glencairne, had presented a supplication to the Lords of Council and Session setting forth that he was about to obtain a b
2 CONC rieve from Chancery for serving himself as nearest and lawful heir to Alexander, Earl of Glencairne, his brother, who died last vest and seised as of fee at the faith and peace of the King in certain lands, baronies and annualrent
2 CONC s lying within the sheriffdoms of Renfrew, Stirling and Air and the bailiary of Cunynghame, and that he could not conveniently be served before the different judges without trouble and great expense: The King, therefore, by delive
2 CONC rance of the said Lords, constitutes and ordains James Dunlop of Houshill and Mr. Hugh Montgomerie of Silverwood his sheriffs in that part of said sheriffdoms and his bailies of said bailiary, giving and granting to them full powe
2 CONC r to sit within the tolbooths of the burghs of Edinburgh and Renfrew for serving said brieve, to receive, proclaim and serve the same, to hold courts and to appoint officers etc. At Edinburgh 10 August 1670 a.r.22. In dorso:- Oath
2 CONC  de fideli administratione taken by the said James Dunlop in presence of Sir Johne Lockhart of Castelhill, knight, one of the Senators of the College of Justice. At Edinburgh 19 Augt. 1670. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrso
2 CONC nlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD86%2f678&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Dunlop+of+houshill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Sir William Fraser Charters, reference GD86/678]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 October 1670: Discharge by William Blair of that ilk to James Dunlop of Houshill, chamberlain of estates formerly belonging to Robert Ker of Kersland and John Cunningham of Bedland, parish of Dalry [Ayrshire] for sums paid in
2 CONC  accordance with treasury act of 1668 Dec 19. Endorsed: 'That the laird mynd Kelb[urn] his ingadgment not only for the bond of the bridg but to bear proportionally of the remainder thereof'. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrs
2 CONC onlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=E20%2f49&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Dunlop+of+houshill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Exchequer miscellanea, reference E20/49]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 July 1672: Signature of the lands of Houshill etc granted to James Dunlop. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SIG1%2f39%2f11&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+dunlop&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=
2 CONC &dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register of Signatures, boxed series, reference SIG1/39/11]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 January 1673: Extract registered bond by Ludovick Stewart to James Dunlop of Houshill for 220lib Scots. Dated at Glasgow and registered in the register there, 2nd August 1679. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecata
2 CONC logue/details.aspx?reference=GD3%2f1%2f10%2f48%2f20&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Dunlop+of+houshill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Montgomerie Family, Earls of Eglinton, reference GD3/1/10/
2 CONC 48/20]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 March 1678: The earls of Linlithgow, Strathmore and Caithness, Glasgow, to James Dunlop of Howsill, bailie depute of the regality of Glasgow, requiring him to attend the meeting of their committee on the following day in ord
2 CONC er to give an account of his diligence in the king's service. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD406%2f1%2f8894&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+dunlop&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n Nat
2 CONC ional Records of Scotland, Papers of the Douglas Hamilton Family, Dukes of Hamilton and Brandon, reference GD406/1/8894]'''
