1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===GEORGE BUCHANAN OF SOUND===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Published by the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT 21 September 1652: Disposition by Sir William Dick of Braid, Kt., with consent of Sir Andrew Dick of Craighouse, Kt., and Mr. Alexander Dick, his sons, to '''Thomas Buchanan of Sound and Margaret Smith, his spouse, in liferent and
2 CONC  to their heirs in fee,''' of land and Isle of Northronaldsay comprehending the 18½ penny land in Soulnes and Sand with a tow maill there called Lynie, the 29¾ penny land in Nese, Bouster and Sand with two towmaills there called N
2 CONC owst and Holland, the 18 penny land in Linklet called an Vrisland with the skerrie called Selchskerrie and the 3 penny udal land in Howar and Harga, with the teind sheaves, all lying in sheriffdom of Orkney. [http://catalogue.nrsc
2 CONC otland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD41%2f423&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+buchanan+of+sound&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Dick-Lauder family of Fountainhall, refer
2 CONC ence 	GD41/423]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT 24 December 1652: Tack by the Provost Magistrates and Council of Edinburgh to '''George Buchanan, lawful son of Thomas Buchanan of Sound in Orkney''' and James Baikie of Tankerness in Orkney, of the lands rents profits and duties 
2 CONC and others which belonged to the late Bishop of Orkney, and that for the space of five years and crops from 1652, dated 24 Dec 1652. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=CS230%2fM%2f1%2f52&
2 CONC st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+buchanan+of+sound&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Court of Session: Unextracted processes, 1st arrangement, Currie-Dalrymple office, reference CS230/M/1/52]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 February 1656: Decreet in action at instance of '''Mr. George Buchanan of Sound, eldest son and executor dative of aforesaid Thomas Buchanan, now deceased,''' against David Mclelland of Woodwick, chamberlain of Orknay, represen
2 CONC tative for said Sir Andrew Dick, as heir to his father, of rents and duties furth of foresaid lands for 1653-55. Kirkwall. Three Discharges by said '''George Buchanan''' to said David Mclelland for rents for years 1655, 1656 and 1
2 CONC 658. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD41%2f423&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+buchanan+of+sound&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Dick-Lauder fa
2 CONC mily of Fountainhall, reference 	GD41/423]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 November 1663: Charter by '''Arthur Buchannan of Sound, in favour of Margaret Buxtoun, his spouse,''' of the liferent of the 36d. land of Sound, manor place and teinds thereof, the 8d. land called Elwick, with the mill thereof 
2 CONC called the mill of Shapinsha and the holm called Elginhome, and teinds thereof, the 1½d. land called How between the Hills, and teinds thereof, the 1½d. land called Horraldisgarth, whereof 1d. land is udal land and ½d. land someti
2 CONC me pertained to St. Katharine's prebendary and thereafter to the bishopric of Orkney, the 8d. land of Weyland and the quoy called Laverock, the 3¼d. and half farthing land called the Kingisland of Nes with the quoy called Liaquoy,
2 CONC  and the 5¾d. land in Holland, all in island of Shapinsha, the 6d. land called Grind and the 1d. land called Foirland, in parish of St. Ola, the 3 merk udal land in Grimbuster, in parish of Firth, the lodging and tenement of house
2 CONC s on both sides of the close presently possessed by Mathew McCaill, apothecary, and Andrew Young, indweller in Kirkwall and said '''Arthur Buchannan,''' lying in the Midtoun of Kirkwall and built into one great lodging by the dece
2 CONC ased Sir John Buchanan of Scottiscraig, kt., and Dame Margaret Hartsyde, his spouse; which thereafter belonged to the deceased '''Thomas Buchanan of Sound, father of said Arthur, thereafter to the deceased George Buchannan, eldest
2 CONC  son of said deceased Thomas Buchannan, who disponed the same to said Arthur,''' the yard opposite said great lodging, tenement of land formerly pertaining to the deceased Hugh Halcro of Aickers and the tenement of land now posses
2 CONC sed by William Linkletter, merchant, and Andrew Corner, notary public, lying in the Laverick in Kirkwall [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f78&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+buc
2 CONC hanan+of+sound&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/78]
