1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ARTHUR BUCHANAN OF SOUND===
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthurd Buchanan of Sound is the second son of Thomas Buchanan of Sound. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=CS230%2fM%2f1%2f52&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+buchanan+of+sound&ko=p&r=&
2 CONC ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Court of Session: Unextracted processes, 1st arrangement, Currie-Dalrymple office, reference CS230/M/1/52] His mother seems likely to be Margaret Smith. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.
2 CONC gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD41%2f423&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=thomas+buchanan+of+sound&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Dick-Lauder family of Fountainhall, reference 	G
2 CONC D41/423]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur Buchanan of Sound was alive in 1675 [http://www.buchanan-heraldry.net.nz/body/sound.html Buchanan Heraldry: Arthur Buchanan of Sound] but he appears to have died in about 1676. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=bbRKAQAAI
2 CONC AAJ&pg=PA774&lpg=PA774&dq=Thomas+Buchanan+of+Sound&source=bl&ots=iJtaCVnVvK&sig=gBBRbRzQNyUTZPDq4ST1-gipR7E&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiitPiNz5nSAhWCIsAKHW_mCFUQ6AEISTAI#v=onepage&q=Thomas%20Buchanan%20of%20Sound&f=false The decisions 
2 CONC of the Court of Session: from its first institution to the present time : digested under proper heads, in the form of a dictionary, Volume 13, number 71]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Published by the National Records of Scotland===
