2 CONT 1664: Rentals: Rental of the lands pertaining to '''Arthur Buchanan of Sound,''' formerly possessed by David McLellane of Woodwick [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f525&st=1&tc=y&
2 CONC tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=arthur+buchanan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/525]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT 25 November 1670: Instrument of sasine following on charter, 25 Nov. 1670, by '''Arthur Buchanan of Sound''' to William Monteith, eldest son of William Monteith, residenter in Kirkwall, and Marie Monteith, his spouse, second daugh
2 CONC ter of deceased Patrick Monteith of Egilshay, of 4½d. king's land called Towquoy, 4d. land of Howan in North Towne and Howatoft, 1d. land in Howatoft, 12¾d. king's land in Towquoy, ¾d. land and quoy called Meikil Quoy of said land
2 CONC s of Towquoy, 1¼d. land of Skaill, with manor place of Towquoy, all in island of Wostray, with lands and isle of Eday, with manor place of Greintoft, holmes of Eday, in special warrandice, reserving holme called Calff of Eday with
2 CONC  salt pans thereof, sea port thereof called Calff Sound, and north end of island of Eday until stone called the Salteris stone and cornland comprehended therein [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?r
2 CONC eference=GD217%2f421&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=arthur+buchanan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/421]
