2 CONT 11 April 1671: Contract of Tack between '''John Buchanan of Sandsyd, curator to Robert Stewart, eldest son and heir of the deceased Colonel John Stewart of Newwark,''' with consent of '''Arthur Buchanan of Sound, another curator,'
2 CONC '' on the one part, and Jerome Dunnisone in Warsitter for himself and for Janet Fea, his spouse, on the other part, whereby the said John lets to the said Jerome and Janet the lands of Warsitter, presently possessed by them, in th
2 CONC e island of Sanday for 9 years Witnessed, inter alios, by William Cochrane, minister in Sanday [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f95&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=arthur+buchanan&ko=p
