2 CONT 15 November 1672: Instrument of Sasine in favour of '''Arthur Buchanan of Sound,''' of a tenement of land in Kirkwall presently possessed by Katharine Grahame, relict of John Murray, sometime Commissar of Orkney, and extending fro
2 CONC m the west gable of the house presently possessed by Patrick Blair of Litle Blair towards the close of the Grammar School of Kirkwall; on charter, dated 6 November 1672, by Andrew, lord bishop of Orkney, with consent of the provos
2 CONC t and chapter of the cathedral kirk of Orkney [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD31%2f100&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=arthur+buchanan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotla
2 CONC nd, Papers of the family of Fea of Clestrain, Orkney, reference GD31/100]
