1 NAME Sir George Oliphant of Newtoun, 3rd Baronet
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1691
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir George Oliphant, Baronet [S 1628] of Newtoun</strong>, brother and heir, succeeded to the Baronetcy in 1659, on the death of his brother, to whom he was served heir in 1674. He, in 1691, sold the estate of Newtoun. He
2 CONC  married firstly Margaret, daughter of (--) Drummond of Invermay. He married secondly Margaret, 1st daughter of James (Rollo), 1st Lord Rollo [S], by his 2nd wife, Mary, daughter of Archibald (Campbell), 7th Earl of Argyll [S]. He
2 CONC  died s.p. probably not long after 1691, when the Baronetcy became dormant."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n387/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 368
