1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===KATHERINE GRAHAM===
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine Graham is the daughter of John Graham of Breckness and his wife Barbara Stewart. [James M. Irvine, The Breckness Estate: A History of its Lairds, Tenants and Farms, and Skaill House (James M. Irvine, 2009), pp. 41] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine Graham died on 19 November 1688. [http://archive.org/stream/moodiebookbeing00ruvi#page/25/mode/1up The Moodie Book, p. 25]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine Graham married John Murray of Pennyland, Commissary of Orkney and Shetland. [James M. Irvine, The Breckness Estate: A History of its Lairds, Tenants and Farms, and Skaill House (James M. Irvine, 2009), p. 41] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine Graham married Harie Mudie of Elsetter. [http://archive.org/stream/moodiebookbeing00ruvi#page/24/mode/1up The Moodie Book, p.24] The marriage was booked on 25 June 1672, at Kirkwall in Oorkney, Scotland [https://familyse
2 CONC arch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:XYSL-8ZX Scottish Marriages]
2 CONT
