2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-Graham/6000000051135907852?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1550740503197&through=6000000017932524203
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James Grahame, fifth son of James G. of Breckness; min. of Evie and Rendall in 1673; trans. and inst. 26th Feb. 1688; conformed to Presbyterianism and was received by the General Assembly 4th Jan. 1696; died 8th Jan. 1721
2 CONC . He marr. 15th Sept. 1673, Elizabeth, daugh. of Patrick Craigie, Provost of Kirkwall, and had issue (she survived her husband, and was latterly in reduced circumstances) - Thomas, died at Kirkwall 1716; George; Andrew, min. of Fi
2 CONC rth and Stenness; Margaret; Francisca; Mungo; Geillis; Elizabeth (marr. George Clerk, litster, Stromness)"</strong>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 May 1720: Disposition and Settlement dated at Esquoy in the parish of Holme 25 May 1720 by Mr James Grahame, minister of the Gospel at Holme [Holm], in favour of Mungo Graham, his youngest lawful son begotten between him and
2 CONC  Elizabeth Craigie, his spouse. Conveying his 2 1/2d udal land in the town of Girsness in that part called Upatoune in parish of Rendall and stewarty of Orkney presently tenanted by Alexr. and Patrick Sclaitters [Slater], and his 
2 CONC 2nd land of Nistahow in the same parish, as for the principal, and the 5 merk udal land in Skarth sometime possessed by the deceased Henry Linklater and his sub-tenants in the parish of Firth, in warrandice, reserving his and his 
2 CONC wife's liferent and with the burden and provision of the payment of 760 merks by the said Mungo as follows viz:- to George Graham the granter's eldest lawful son 100 merks, Mr Andrew Graham his second lawful son 60 merks, Marjory 
2 CONC Graham, spouse to Andrew Sinclair, shipmaster in Zetland 100 merks, Margaret Graham, the granter's second lawful daughter 200 merks, Fransisca Graham his fourth lawful daughter 200 merks and Geils Graham his fifth lawful daughter 
2 CONC 100 merks (his daughter Elizabeth Graham, spouse to George Clerk, litster in the parish of Stromness, being already sufficiently provided) and that after the lapse of three terms after the decease of the survivor of himself and hi
2 CONC s spouse. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f192%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elizabeth+graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1820&di=n National Records of Scotland, Miscellaneous small coll
2 CONC ections of family, business and other papers, Orkney Documents, reference GD1/192/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 May 1720: Latter Will and Testament, dated as above, by Mr James Grahame, minister of the Gospel at Holme, desiring to be buried in the Church of Holme, and nominating his youngest surviving son Mungo as Executor with provis
2 CONC o that he carry out the provisions of the Disposition and Settlement of this date. He also bequeathes to Mr Andrew Graham his second surviving son all his books and MSS. conform to inventory to be made up by him. [http://catalogue
2 CONC .nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f192%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=andrew+graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1746&di=y National Records of Scotland, Miscellaneous small collections of family, business an
2 CONC d other papers, Orkney Documents, reference GD1/192/2]'''
2 CONT
