1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MARGARET GRAHAM ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margaret Graham, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Graham-of-Breckness/6000000017930306713?through=6000000032772704854 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Barbara-Stewart/6000000032771323006
2 CONC ?through=6000000032772704854 [James M. Irvine, The Breckness Estate: A History of its Lairds, Tenants and Farms, and Skaill House (James M. Irvine, 2009), pp. 32-46]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 April 1677: Extract discharge by Mr. Robert Honyman, only son of deceased Andrew, bishop of Orknay, with consent of Margaret Grahame, his spouse, to Harry Grahame of Brecknes, of all bairn's part due to said Margaret by dece
2 CONC ase of John Grahame of Brecknes, her father, or of Barbara Stewart, her mother. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f488&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=barbara+stewart&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&
2 CONC dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/488]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 December 1680: Factory by Margaret Graham, relict of Mr. Robert Honyman, son of late bishop of Orkney and Zetland, with consent of tutors of Robert, Harry, Euphame and Margaret Honyman, her children, appointing Thomas Stewart
2 CONC , writer in Kirkwall, to receive money due to said deceased Robert. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f856&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=margaret+graham&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=
2 CONC n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breckness, Orkney, reference GD217/856]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 May 1684: Receipt by Margaret Grahame relict of Mr. Robert Honyman, son of deceased Andrew, bishop of Orknay, to Thomas Prestoune, tailor, burgess of Edinburgh, in name of Harry Grahame of Brecknes, for £138. 17s. 4d. scots.
2 CONC  [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD217%2f495&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+honyman&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scarth Family of Breck
2 CONC ness, Orkney, reference GD217/495]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
