1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>George Drummond</strong>, the fifth laird, was born at Blair in Stormount, Novemher 29, 1638. In 1682, he sold Blair. In 1684, he bought the lands of Kincardine in Mopteith from James third earl of Perth, the lord high ch
2 CONC ancellor of Scotland. On these lands he built a house, to which he gave the name of Blair Drummond, and this afterwards became the designation of the family and the estate. He married Elizabeth, daughter to Sir Gilbert Ramsay of B
2 CONC anff, Bart. and dying June 24th 1717, left issue, seven sons and one daughter."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=hTEwAAAAYAAJ Genealogical memoir of the most noble and ancient house of Drummond], G. Maxwell, 1808, page 46
