1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == WILLIAM FRASER OF FAICHFIELD ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Fraser of Faichfield is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Andrew-Fraser-1st-Lord-Fraser/6000000017331867285?through=6000000214922929821 and his wife  https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Douglas/600000001955208534
2 CONC 1?through=6000000214922929821. He and his two elder brothers were all admitted burgesses of Aberdeen 21 April 1627. He had a charter of Faichfield and other lands on 15 September 1629. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun
2 CONC 04pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/113/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 113]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Fraser of Faichfield married Jean Barclay, second daughter of Patrick Barclay, fiar of Towie, who, as his future wife, grants him a charter of Drumquhendill 30 September 1630. He left a son William, who had a precept of
2 CONC  clare constat as his father's heir 11 October 1667, and who, in the same year, disponed Faichfield to Mr. William Thomson, Preacher of the Word of God. He married Christian Garioch. William Fraser, sometime of Faichfield, and Chr
2 CONC istian Garioch his wife, had a charter of Invernorth in January 1668. He (the younger William) had a son William, baptized 29 March 1665, and a daughter Elizabeth, baptized 20 September 1666. This branch seems to have died out, or
2 CONC  left Aberdeenshire before 1696, as they are not found in the List of Pollable Persons of that year. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/113/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 113-4]
2 CONC '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
