1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>Robert Douglas</strong>, son of Robert D. of Nether Kilmonth (son of James D. of Glenbervie), and Margaret Sibbald ; educated at King's College, Aberdeen ; M.A. (1647) ; adm. min. of Laurencekirk before Jan. 1657 ; trans, 
2 CONC to Bothwell before 20th Sept. 1665 ; trans, to Renfrew 15th March 1669; trans, to Hamilton and Deanery of Glasgow in 1675 ; consecrated Bishop of Brechin in 1682 ; trans, and installed 10th Aug. 1684 ; signed an address to James V
2 CONC II. 3rd Nov. 1688 ; deprived at the abolition of Episcopacy 11th April 1689 ; had a yearly pension of £1200 ; died at Dundee 22nd April 1716. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He marr. (1) a daugh. of Irvine of Drum, and had issue — 
2 CONT * Robert, min. of Bothwell
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) cont. 9th July 1661, Elizabeth, daugh. of Sylvester Lammy, min. of Glamis, and had issue - 
2 CONT * Sylvester of Whiteriggs in Mearns; 
2 CONT * William, Provost of Forfar, born 1666, died 1746; 
2 CONT * George ; 
2 CONT * James ; 
2 CONT * Katherine (marr., cont. 17th July 1713, George Reid, physician, Dundee); 
2 CONT * Susanna (marr. Charles White, merchant, Dundee); 
2 CONT * a daugh. (marr. Provost Dean of Forfar); 
2 CONT * Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc00scot#page/338/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. VII, page 338
