1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from http://archive.org/stream/thanageoffermart00byutemp#page/427/mode/1up
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. William Uldeny of Uldeny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1548 his name occurs in an assize of the Lords and Barons of Aberdeenshire for making an assessment. The laird of Oudny's proportion of the tax is £\o. In 1565 he granted a charter of the lands of the Mains of Oudny with the to
2 CONC wer and fortalice thereof, mill, and mill lands to his brother, Andrew Udny of Tillery. In 1575 the said Andrew signed a bond of reversion to his nephew, William Udny. William Udny, married a daughter of Duncan Forbes of Monymusk,
2 CONC  and had issue, three sons : — 
2 CONT
2 CONT I. William, his successor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Robert, of Crabadona. 
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Hercules. On 24 April, 1865, William Udny signed a precept of sasme in favour of his son, Hercules, of the feu lands of Balnakettle.' 
2 CONT
2 CONT This William Udny died in 1573 or 1574, and was succeeded by his son, the fourth of the name,  VIII. William Udny of Udny. 
