1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lord Donald was thrice  married. His first wife was Barbara, whom he married in 1610, eldest daughter of Kenneth, 1st Lord Kintail, and sister of Colin and George, 1st and 2nd Earls of Seaforth. She bore him four s
2 CONC ons and two daughters
2 CONT
2 CONT * i. lye, died 1617.
2 CONT * ii. John, succeeded as 2nd Lord Reay, and of whom follows.
2 CONT * iii. Hew, died unmarried before 1642.
2 CONT * iv. Lieut -Col. Angus, progenitor of the Melness Mackays, of whom see in their genealogy afterwards.
2 CONT * v. Jane, married Wm. Mackay III. of Bighouse, and had issue as given in the genealogy of that family.
2 CONT * vi. Mary, married Sir Roderick Macleod of Talisker, second son of Macleod of Macleod. pg. 123
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT THE BOOK OF MACKAY BY ANGUS MACKAY, M.A. (St. Andrews University) Minister at Westerdale, Caithness EDINBURGH : NORMAN MACLEOD, -25 GEORGE IV. BRIDGE CANADA : EDWARD MACKAY, ST. PETER'S MANSE, MADOC, ONT. M DCCCC VI
2 CONT
2 CONT ===================
2 CONT Barbara Mackenzie1
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #231584
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=20 Aug 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Barbara Mackenzie is the daughter of Kenneth Mackenzie, 1st Lord Mackenzie of Kintail and Anne Ross.1 She married Donald Mackay, 1st Lord Reay, son of Hugh 'Du' Mackay and Lady Jane Gordon, in August 1610.1,2 From August 1610, her
2 CONC  married name became Mackay.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Barbara Mackenzie and Donald Mackay, 1st Lord Reay
2 CONT * 1.Lt.-Col. Angus Mackay of Melness3 d. bt 1699 - 1703
2 CONT * 2.Mary Mackay2
2 CONT * 3.Hugh Mackay of Strathnaver2 d. b 1652
2 CONT * 4.Jane Mackay2
2 CONT * 5.Iye Mackay of Strathnaver2 b. c 1611, d. 1617
2 CONT * 6.John Mackay, 2nd Lord Reay+3 b. c 1612, d. a 1680
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S37] Volume 2, page 2413. See link for full details for this source. Hereinafter cited as. [S37]
2 CONT * 2.[S3268] Hans Harmsen, "re: Chester Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 21 August 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Chester Family."
2 CONT * 3.[S37] See. [S37]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p23159.htm#i231584
2 CONT
2 CONT ===================
2 CONT
2 CONT " In February 1649," says Gordon, lC Donald Mackay, Lord Reay, having retired to Denmark, died in that kingdom... He had five wives; 1st, Lady Barbara Mackenzie, Lord Seaforth's daughter ; issue by her, four sons, Iye, 
2 CONT * John his successor,  
2 CONT * Hugh, and  
2 CONT * Colonel Angus of Melness; and two daughters,  
2 CONT * Jane and  
2 CONT * Mary 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Iye and Hugh died young; Jane married the second William Mackay of Bighouse, and Mary married Sir Robert mcLeod of Talisker in Sky.   pg. 328-329
2 CONT
2 CONT ============================
2 CONT
2 CONT  GENI  list her as Daughter of Sir Roderick Mackenzie of Coieach, tutor of Kintail and Anne Ross
2 CONT
2 CONT and  [http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/content/reay1628.htm Cracroft's Peerage] lists her as:
2 CONT
2 CONT Aug 1610 Hon Barbara Mackenzie (d. aft. 9 Jan 1617), sister of Colin [Mackenzie], 1st Earl of Seaforth, and 1st dau. of Kenneth [Mackenzie], 1st Lord Mackenzie of Kintail, by his first wife Anne Ross, dau. of George Ross of Balnag
2 CONC owan
2 CONT
