1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Colin, second Lord Mackenzie of Kintail</strong>, succeeded to the Peerage in 1611, his minority being dispensed with by royal precept. He was served heir-male to his father 23 May 1615, and to his grandfather 15 June 161
2 CONC 9...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...on 3 December (1623) was created <strong>Earl of Seaforth</strong> by patent, with remainder to his heirs-male whomsoever...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...He died at Chanonry 15 April, and was buried in the church there 28 May 1633. He married, in Holyrood Abbey Church, 5 June 1614, Margaret Seton, fourth daughter of Alexander, first Earl of Dunfermline, and by her (who died 20 F
2 CONC ebruary, and was buried at Dalgety 8 March 1630) he had issue."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft#page/506/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VII, page 506-507
2 CONT
