1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Thomas Ross of Nether Pitkerrie</strong>, born about 1614, son of George R. of Nether Pitkerrie ; adm. before 28th Aug. 1655; deprived by Act of Parliament and Decreet of Privy Council 1st Oct. 1662, and went to Tain, whe
2 CONC re he made himself useful in the work of the Gospel. He was in Moray in 1669 where he was accused of keeping conventicles, and was imprisoned in 1675 in the Tolbooth of Nairn. In 1076 he was removed to the prison of Tain and confi
2 CONC ned till 9th Oct. 1677, when he was liberated on finding caution for 2000 merks to appear when called upon. He died in his own house in Tain 13th Jan. 1679. James Fraser of Brea dedicated his Memoirs to him as a "singularly pious 
2 CONC minister." He marr. Lilias Dunbar, and had issue — Alexander of Nether Pitkerrie, min. of Fearn ; George, min. of this parish."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc00scot#page/60/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. VII, page 60
