1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>James, second Viscount of Kilsyth</strong>, was served heir to his father and grandfather 11 May 1664 and 3 May 1665. On 23 July 1680 the King confirmed a charter of resignation by the Viscount in favour of his brother, M
2 CONC r. William, on condition of being allowed 4000 merks yearly for his aliment and sustentation, together with the use of the mansion-house of Colzium for his lifetime. By this charter the remainder was altered, and it was provided t
2 CONC hat in the event of an heir-female succeeding, she was to be obliged to marry a gentleman of the surname of Livingston, or who, and his heirs-male succeeding, should assume and bear the surname and title and dignity of Viscount of
2 CONC  Kilsyth, and bear his arms. The Viscount died unmarried in 1706."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft#page/192/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. V, page 192
