2 CONT
2 CONT Migrated from Europe to Albany, New York where he became wealthy in the fur trade, and then obtained a patent to 160,000 acres that would become Livingston Manor in Columbia and Dutchess County.  He was first lord of Livingston Ma
2 CONC nor.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as Secretary for Indian Affairs from 1695 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was referred to in a biography as "the most important person to live in colonial Albany."
