1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN PORTERFIELD OF THAT ILK ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Porterfield of that Ilk, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Porterfield-of-that-Ilk/4863709371240010417?through=6000000005583766418 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Blair/4863709
2 CONC 385690010423?through=6000000005583766418 [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/pp/porterfield1.php Stirnet: Porterfield 1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Portfield of that Ilk, here treated, died intestate in May 1690. [NRS: CC9/7/48]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Testament Dative and Inventory ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 30 December 1690. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of John Porterfield of that Ilk, reference CC9/7/48]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # 
2 CONT # 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 August 1676: Precept of sasine by John, Earl of Glencairn in favour of John Porterfield of that ilk. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD514%2f1%2f28%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k
2 CONC =john+porterfield+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Legal Records, reference GD514/1/28/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 January 1680: Heritable Bond of Corroboration by John, Earl of Glencairn, in favour of John Porterfield of that Ilk, of (1) Bond, dated 3 September 1658, by deceased William, Earl of Glencairn, in favour of deceased Alexander
2 CONC  Porterfield of that Ilk for 3000 merks, and in security whereof he disponed an annual rent of £120 furth of lands and barony of Finlayston, in parish of Kilmacolm and sheriffdom of Renfrew; (2) bond, dated 4 Oct. 1669, by decease
2 CONC d Alexander, Earl of Glencairn, brother german to said John, Earl of Glencairn, in favour of John Porterfield of that Ilk, for 2300 merks, and in security thereof he disponed an annual rent of £92 furth of the lands of Denniston, 
2 CONC then possessed by James Holme in Rowantreehill, Alexander Laird, and John Halltrigg in Parsmuire, part of barony of Finlayston, and (3) bond, dated 17 Feb. 1674, by John, Earl of Glencairn, in favour of said John Porterfield for £
2 CONC 800 Scots. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f154&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+porterfield+of+that+ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glen
2 CONC cairn, reference GD39/5/154]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 May 1691: Instrument of Sasine in favour of Alexander Porterfield now of that Ilk, of annual rents furth of lands and barony of Finlayston, in parish of Kilmacolm and sheriffdom of Renfrew; on precept of clare constat, dated
2 CONC  22 May 1691, by John, Earl of Glencairn, in favour of said Alexander Porterfield, as heir to deceased John Porterfield of that Ilk, his grandfather. Recorded P.R.S. Renfrew 29 May 1691. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonli
2 CONC necatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f165&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+Porterfield+of+that+Ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/5/165]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 April 1692: Disposition by Alexander Porterfield of that Ilk, as heir to deceased John Porterfield of that Ilk, his grandfather, with consent of John, Earl of Glencairn, and them both, with consent of Sir John Maxwell of Net
2 CONC herpollock, Kt., Bart., Sir Archibald Stewart of Blackhall, Kt., Bart., Archibald Crawfurd of Auchenanes, James Hamilton of Aikenhead, James Stewart of Lumloch, Alexander Porterfield of Fullwood, Alexander Porterfield, indweller i
2 CONC n Paisley, Annabel Stewart, relict of  William Porterfield of that Ilk, curators to said Alexander Porterfield, in favour of Mr John Cochrane of Ferguslie, of annual rent of £260 furth of lands and barony of Finlayston, formerly w
2 CONC adset by the deceased William, Earl of Glencairn. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f167&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=William+Porterfield+of+that+Ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y Na
2 CONC tional Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/5/167]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
