2 CONT '''17 April 1712: Porterfield. Alexander, chyrurgeon being already burgess, as serving appr. with dec. John Robison, apothecary chyrurgeon,  B. and G.B., is now made G.B., same  right  (see  20  May 1690) [https://archive.org/deta
