1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JAMES HAMILTON OF AIKENHEAD ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Merchant in Glasgow: Burgess and Guild Brother of Glasgow===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Hamilton of Aikenhead is the son of Robert Hamilton of Aikenhead and his wife Mary Porterfield. [https://archive.org/stream/historicalgeneal00ande#page/304/mode/1up Hamilton Memoirs]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Bonds for One Thousand Merks and Five Hundred Merks ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Hamilton of Aikenhead borrowed fifteen hundred merks from Jean Porterfield. She mentions this fact in her last will and testament which was made at Glasgow on 28 December 1658: "Item thr being adebtd & awand to me be Jame
2 CONC s Hamilton of Aiknheid the soume of ane thousand merks conform to his band grantit to me thranent of the dait the sexteint day of November Jajvjc & fifty seven yeirs of the qlk soum I heirby leive in legacy to Elisabeth & Mary Por
2 CONC terfield dochts laull to umqle Gabriell Porterfield of Hapland the sumn of sex hundreth merks mony eqlly betwext them vix three hundreth merks to each of them Item ane hundreth merks of the forsd thousand merks I heirby leive in l
2 CONC egacy to Jeane Wallace dochter to umqle Wm Wallace sometyme of Johnstoun Iem ane uther hundreth merks throf I leive in legact to Jeane Fergushill dochter to the lait Laird of Fergushill Item thr being anu uthr ffyve hundreth merks
2 CONC  in the hands of the sd James Hamiltoun for the qch he hes given band to Margaret & Agnes Hamiltouns his sisters at my desyre I heirby declair that they sall have each of them the eqll half throf Item as for the rest of the forsd 
2 CONC soume of ane thousand merks money eftir my debts ar payed & the charges of my funeral defrayed I leive the haill remenant throf to Mr George Wallace son to the sd umqle Wm Wallace". [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Record
2 CONC s of Glasgow, reference CC9/7/32]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence Published by the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1719-1825: Bundle of legal documents, sasine extracts and dispositions regarding land of Duchall and the Porterfield family. Held in safe keeping by the family lawyer, the bundle includes a disposition of the lands of Aikenhead
2 CONC , the owner, being James Hamilton of Aikenhead whose first wife was Anne, daughter of John Porterfield of Porterfield. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD514%2f1%2f55&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=
2 CONC n&tp=n&k=hamilton+of+aikenhead&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Legal Records, reference GD514/1/55]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
