2 CONT
2 CONT Book of Mackay p 354 states: "Patrick of Larg, m. in 1550...and ...had issue: Alexr.,...; Duncan of Palgown; and Patrick."
2 CONT
2 CONT Kirkcudbright Sheriff Court Record P 72 1578 "Anent the caus persewit be Alexander Carlell aganis Robert McCulloch as cautionar for Doncan McKe in the terme assignit to answer..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Privy Council Register 1577, pg 645 states: "Patrik McKe of Larg, souirtie (surety) for Duncane McKe burges of Quhitherne..." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Duncan M'Kie of Larg also obtained a wadset on the farm of Lessons, which was continued to Patrick and then Fergus M'Kie on wadset charters. 
