2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT Sir Robert GRAHAM of Morphie, son of John GRAHAM of Morphie and Unknown was born about 1575 and died before 30 July 1662 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married Euphame (Margaret?) CARNEGIE, daughter of David CARNEGIE of Colluthie, then 7th of Kinnaird and Euphame WEMYSS, 20 October 1599(contract).  Euphame (Margaret?) CARNEGIE was born about 1578 and died before 21 April 1
2 CONC 627 
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Euphame married (contract 15, 16, and 20 October 1599) to Robert Graham, younger of Morphie, a grandson of Sir Henry Graham of Morphie." - from Scots Peerage (vol 8)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 
2 CONT # Robert Graham of Morphie+  Married Mary Irvine.  
2 CONT #John Graham of Craigie+  Married Rachel Bruce.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT “During the reighn of King James VI, according to ''Criminal Trials in Scotland'', Sir Robert Grahame of Morphie was one of the pursuers, as a near kinsman, along with James Graham, brother of the dead man, for justice against Rob
2 CONC ert Symmer, who, it was claimed, had been responsible for the "crewall Slauchter" of David Graham, the son of "James Grahame of Leuchland".”
2 CONT
2 CONT see Criminal Trials in Scotland 1609-1624
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir Robert Graham of Morphie ..... was one of the tutors of his kinsman the great marquis of Montrose, and in 1638 he accompanied him on his first visit to Aberdeen at the head of the army of the Covenant. He continued to adhere 
2 CONC to him during the whole of the wars in which he was engaged in Scotland, previous to his departure for the Continent in 1646, nearly to the ruin of his estate. In 1661, when Montrose's head was taken down from the pinnacle of the 
2 CONC Tolbooth of Edinburgh, Graham of Morphie was one of the five personal friends of the great marquis present to receive it."
2 CONT
2 CONT from Electric Scotland website
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
