1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MAGDALENE DALYELL Lady of Binns ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Magdalene Dalyell, here treated, is the eldest child of https://www.geni.com/people/Sir-Thomas-Dalyell-1st-Baronet-of-the-Binns/6000000008947218574?through=6000000008947306814 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Katha
2 CONC rine-Drummond-Lady-of-Binns/6000000008948330907. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/77/mode/1up The Binns Papers I: 386] She was born before 7 November 1673, the date upon which h
2 CONC er baptism was registered at Abercorn in West Lothian, Scotland. [National Records of Scotland, Abercorn Baptisms, reference OPR.661/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dame Magdalen Dalyell, died in December 1732. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/119/mode/1up The Binns Papers II: 578]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 January 1683: Bond of Provision by General Thomas Dalyell [Dalziel] of Binns, to William Dalyell for 10,000 merks, Magdalen Dalyell for 8000 merks and to Janet Dalyell for 6000 merks, all children of Captain Thomas Dalyell, 
2 CONC eldest son of the said General Thomas Dalyel. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD30%2f794&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=magdalen+dalyell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1750&di=y National Records of 
2 CONC Scotland, Papers of the Shairp family of Houston, West Lothian, reference GD30/794]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1719: Letters to Thomas Shairp of Houstoun from Thomas Shairp [Sharp], his nephew, and vice versa; also to said nephew Thomas from Elizabeth Shairp, his cousin, daughter of said Shairp of Houstoun; all relating to the conduct o
2 CONC f nephew Thomas's affairs on his attaining his majority, and especially regarding his interests as possible heir to his deceased uncle, Sir Thomas Dalyell [Dalziel] of the Binns [who died 4 May, 1719] in competition with the claim
2 CONC  of his "Aunt Auldcathie" [Magdalen Dalyell, said Sir Thomas's sister]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD30%2f1558&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=magdalen+dalyell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=175
2 CONC 0&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Shairp family of Houston, West Lothian, reference GD30/1558]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 March 1720: Contract of Agreement between Magdalane Dalyell [Dalziel], daughter of the deceased Sir Thomas Dalyell [Dalziel] of Binns, baronet, with consent of James Monteith of Auldcathy [Auldcathie], her husband, and James 
2 CONC Monteith, their eldest son, on the one part, Thomas Shairp [Sharp] of Blans [Blance] and Janet Dalyel, second daughter of the deceased Sir Thomas Dalyell [Dalziel], on the second part, and Thomas Dalyell [Dalziel] of Neuck, only s
2 CONC on of the deceased Lieutenant Colonel John Dalyell [Dalziel] of Muiravonside, with consent of Alexander Crawfurd [Crawford], younger, of Manuclmiln [Mannock Mill?], his brother-in-law, and also his cautioner, on the third part, co
2 CONC ncerning provisions under disposition and tailzie, dated 3 August, 1682, by the deceased General Thomas Dalyell [Dalziel] of Binns and also disposition and tailzie, dated 11 July, 1717, by the said deceased Sir Thomas Dalyell [Dal
2 CONC ziel], relating to the lands of Binns, in the shire of Linlithgow. (Cancelled) [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD30%2f370&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=auldcathie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=175
2 CONC 0&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Shairp family of Houston, West Lothian, reference GD30/370]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 May 1721: Ratification and Obligement by Thomas Dallyell [Dalziel] of Newck [Newark], only son of the deceased Lieutenant Colonel John Dallyell of Mureavanside [Muiravonside], on reaching his majority, of Contract of Agreeme
2 CONC nt dated 8 March 1720 between Magdalene Dallyell, daughter of the deceased Sir Thomas Dallyell of Binns, baronet, with consent of James Monteith of Auldcathie, her husband, and James Monteith, their eldest son, on the one part, Th
2 CONC omas Sharp of Blans [Blance], on the other part, and the said Thomas Dalyell of Newck, as principal, and Alexander Craufurd [Crawford], younger of Manwelmilne [Manuel Mill], his brother-in-law, as cautioner, on the third part. [ht
2 CONC tps://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD30%2f2221&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=auldcathie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1750&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Shairp family of Houston, West
2 CONC  Lothian, reference GD30/2221]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 April 1723 and 3 May 1723: Contract between Thomas Sharp of Blanse [Blance], on the one part, and Alexander Guthrie, WS, with consent of James Dallyell [Dalziel], elder, now of Binns, formerly James Monteith of Auldcathie, o
2 CONC n the other part, concerning the debts due by the deceased Sir Thomas Dalyell [Dalziel] of Binns and an ajudication at the instance of the said Alexander Guthrie against Magdalen Dallyell, Lady Binns, as heir of the said deceased 
2 CONC Sir Thomas Dallyell, her brother, and the said James Dalyell [Dalziel], her spouse; and list of debts due by the said deceased Sir Thomas Dalyell [Dalziel]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refe
2 CONC rence=GD30%2f561&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=auldcathie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1750&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Shairp family of Houston, West Lothian, reference GD30/561]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 December 1732: Contract between Sir James Dalyell of Binns, bt., on one part, and Christian, Janet, Jean and Katherine Monteith, children of deceased James Monteith, alias Dalyell of Binns, and deceased Magdalen Dalyell, lad
2 CONC y Binns, on other part, whereby said Sir James discharges said Christian, Janet, Jean and Katherine of all claims he might have made against them and they bind themselves to pay said Sir James £220 scots if they fail to obtain pay
2 CONC ment of bond for £800 scots by deceased Thomas Cornwall of Bonheid to deceased Sir Thomas Dalyell of Binns. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD75%2f370&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=magda
2 CONC len+dalyell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1750&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Dundas Family of Dundas, West Lothian, reference GD75/370]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Binns Papers ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 January 1683: Copy of Bond of Provision by General Thomas Dalyell of Binns, supplementing the provisions of Bond of Provision in No. 385 by bequeathing these portions : To William Dalyell 10,000 merks, to Magdalen Dalyell 80
2 CONC 00 merks, and to Janet Dalyell 6coo merks, all children of the marriage of Captain Thomas Dalyell, eldest son of the General, and the late Katherine Drummond. Dated at Canongate, II January 1683. Witnesses, John Cant, servant of t
2 CONC he said General, and James Hay, W.S. (Written by Robert Gumming, servitor of the said James Hay.) [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/77/mode/1up The Binns Papers I: 386]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 June 1688: Inventory of the Writs of Auldcathie with the patronage of the kirk thereof and teinds lying formerly in the paiish of Auldcathie and now by annexation in the parish of Dalmenie, and of the Kirklands of the kirk of
2 CONC  Auldcathie. extending to 2 acres, sold by James Monteith of Auldcathie with consent of Magdalen Dalyell, his wife, and James Monteith, his son, to Charles. Earl of Hopetoun, conform to disposition dated 13 December 1721  . . . . 
2 CONC . [42] Contract of Marriage between the said James Monteith, younger, and Mistress Magdalen Dalyell, eldest daughter of Sir Thomas Dalyell of Binns : 9 June 1688. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishreco
2 CONC rds54scotuoft/page/110/mode/1up The Binns Papers II: 545]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 March 1701: By his Disposition and Bond of Taillie of the same date General Dalyell disponed all his estates to his said grandson, and the heirs male of his body ; whom failing to the heirs female of his body ; whom failing 
2 CONC to his grandson William Dalyell, the second son born of the said marriage, and his heirs male and female ; whom failing to any person hereafter nominated by the General ; failing which nomination to his grand-daughter, Magdalen Da
2 CONC lyell, the eldest daughter born of the said marriage, and heirs male and female ; whom failing to his grand-daughter, Janet Dalyell, the youngest daughter born of the said marriage, and her heirs male and female : whom failing suc
2 CONC cessively to his second son, Thomas Dalyell, to his third son, John Dalyell, to his fourth son, Charles Dalyell, to his eldest daughter, Mary Dalyell, to his daughter, Anna Dalyell, and to his daughter, Margaret Dalyell, daughter 
2 CONC of Marion Abercrombie, and their heirs male and female. Place and witnesses as above. Registered in the Books of Council and Session, 24 March 1701.  [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft
2 CONC /page/76/mode/1up The Binns Papers I: 385]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 July 1719: Claim by Magdalen Dalyell, wife of James Monteith of Auldcathie, for service as heir of tailyie to her brother, the late Sir Thomas Dalyell of Binns, who died on 4 May 1719, in the lands of Binns, etc., as in No. 9
2 CONC 4, 615 acres of Abercorn Moor, as in No. 273, Blackness lands, as in No. 125, and Cauldcoats, as in No. 40; presented before the sheriff of Linlithgow. An Advocation of the said service by the Lords of Council and Session from the
2 CONC  said sheriff to their Lordships, dated 19 and signeted 20 June 1719, at the instance of Thomas Shairp of Blanse, was admitted by the sheriff substitute, 3 July 1719. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottish
2 CONC records54scotuoft/page/107/mode/1up The Binns Papers II: 522]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 November 1734: Letter from Thomas Monteith to his brother Sir James Dalyell, dated at Rapahannock, Virginia, 17 November 1734. It is therein narrated that their mother, Magdalen Dalyell, died in December 1732, and that their
2 CONC  brother John and their sisters Betty and Magdalen were dead; and that the writer of the letter married in June 1734. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/119/mode/1up The Binns Pap
2 CONC ers II: 578]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
