1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR THOMAS DALYELL OF THE BINNS Baronet ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Binns Papers ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 November 1685:  Patent of Baronetcy in favour of Captain Thomas Dalyell of Binns 7 November 1685 In Latin : Translation) James, by the Grace of God King of Great Britain, France and Ireland, Defender of the Faith, to all hone
2 CONC st men to whom our present letters shall come, Greetings. . . . . We give, grant and confer, on the said Captain Thomas Dalyell and after his death on Thomas Dalyell, his eldest son and his heirs male and of tailyie following him 
2 CONC in hereditary right to the estate and family of Binns, the Title, rank, degree and honour of Knight Baronet, and by these presents We make, constitute and appoint them Knights Baronets for all time . . . . . In witness whereof We 
2 CONC have ordered Our Great .Seal to be appended to these presents. Given at Our Court of Whythall, 7 November 1685 and of our reign the 1st year. Sealed at Edinburgh the seventh day of December 1685. [https://archive.org/details/scott
2 CONC ishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/80/mode/1up The Binns Papers I: 396]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/n2/mode/1up The Binns Papers 1320-1864. Part I. 1320-1685( Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh, 1936), pp. pp. 1-80]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/n86/mode/1up The Binns Papers 1320-1864. Part II. 1686-1864. (Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh, 1936), pp. 81-146]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Thomas Dalziell, or Dalyell, Baronet [s. 1685], of the Binns aforesaid, only s. and h. ; suc. to the Baronetcy on his father's 1719. death. He d. unm. 4 May 1719 when the Baronetcy, apparently, became extinct." [https://arc
2 CONC hive.org/details/cu31924092524408/page/n353/mode/1up Complete Baronetage; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 334'''
