2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 July 1686: Postnuptial Marriage Contract between John Moubray in Manerstoune, eldest son of James Moubray in Scotstoun, on the one part, and Mary Daiyell, natural daughter of Sir Thomas Daiyell of Binns, on the other part, w
2 CONC hereby the said John declares that he is "presently worth in plenishing, pennie and pennie worth " the sum of 3000 merks Scots, which sum he binds him to make forthcoming to the said Mary Daiyell, his wife ; and the said Sir Thoma
2 CONC s binds him to pay to the said John 500 merks in name of tocher. Dated at Linlithgow, 24 July 1686, and written by Henry Keir, servitor of Andrew Craufurd, sheriff clerk of Linlithgow. Witnesses, the said Andrew Craufurd and Henry
2 CONC  Keir. (Signed) "John Moubray, Thomas Dalyell," and the witnesses. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/81/mode/1up The Binns Papers II: 400]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 December 1691: Discharge by the said John Mowbray in favour of Sir Thomas Dalyell on payment of the said 500 merks of tocher. Dated at Binnes, 21 December 1691. Witnesses, James Ker, tenant in Binnes, John Duffes, servant to
2 CONC  the said Sir Thomas, and Andrew Craufurd, sheriff clerk of Linlithgow. (Signed) "John Mowbray," and the witnesses. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecords54scotuoft/scottishrecords54scotuoft/page/81/mode/1up The Binns Papers
2 CONC  II: 400]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
