1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Sometime after the death of the said Coll. Dalyell I intermarried with the said Christian by whom I have had several children and particularly one son called Charles now about Eighteen years old, and after our I
2 CONC ntermarriage, John the second son upon the death of his brother Thomas who died without Issue, being Intitled to the said Estate and being then a Minor I was obliged to become his Guardian and he having died without issue, the Est
2 CONC ate came to James, the third son, to whom one William Watt was appointed Guardian by the Lord Chancellor. This James during his Life was a very easy, supine, Indolent Man, subject to many Extravagancies, and led a Course of Life m
2 CONC uch beneath the Dignity of the Worthy Family he descended from. And particularly for some time kept company with one Jane Doyle a woman of a very Infamous Character and Daughter to one Henry Doyle who was a tenant on the Estate an
2 CONC d a man of a very base Character.
2 CONT
2 CONT (under 18 when his father died before 1710)
