1 NAME John /Barrington/
2 GIVN John
2 _MARNM Barrington
1 NAME Sir John Barrington, 4th Baronet Barrington
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 16 OCT 1670
1 BURI
2 DATE 1691
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hatfield Broadoak
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1691
2 ADDR
3 CITY St. Clement Dane's Church, The Strand, London
3 CTRY England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.thepeerage.com/p13404.htm#i134040
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Barrington, 4th Bt. was born on 16 October 1670.1 He was the son of Thomas Barrington and Lady Anne Rich.1 He died on 26 November 1691 at age 21 at St. Clement Danes Church, The Strand, London, England, from smallpox, unm
2 CONC arried.1 He was buried at Hatfield Broadoak, Essex, England.1 He died intestate and his estate was administered on 18 December 1691, and again 16 November 1693.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Barrington, 4th Bt. succeeded to the title of 4th Baronet Barrington, of Barrington Hall [in Hatfield Broadoak], co. Essex [E., 1611] on 24 March 1682/83.1
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Citations''
2 CONT * [S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume I, page 28. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
1 FAMC @F6000000010964578283@
1 RFN geni:6000000006582100611
1 SUBM @S6000000003703300491@
1 CHAN
2 DATE 26 APR 2022
3 TIME 22:43:56
0 @I6000000006582402202@ INDI
1 NAME Charles /Barrington/
2 GIVN Charles
2 _MARNM Barrington
1 NAME Sir Charles Barrington 5th Baronet Barrington
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1670
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 29 JAN 1715
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.thepeerage.com/p13405.htm#i134041
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Charles Barrington, 5th Bt. was born after 1670.1 He was the son of Thomas Barrington and Lady Anne Rich.1 He married, firstly, Bridget Monson, daughter of Sir John Monson and Judith Pelham, on 20 April 1693 at St. Bride's, Fl
2 CONC eet Street, London, England.1 He and Anna Marie FitzWilliam obtained a marriage license on 23 May 1700.1 He died on 29 January 1714/15, without issue.1 He was buried at Hatfield Broadoak, Essex, England.1 His will (dated 2 July 17
2 CONC 14) was probated in December 1715.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Charles Barrington, 5th Bt. succeeded to the title of 5th Baronet Barrington, of Barrington Hall [in Hatfield Broadoak], co. Essex [E., 1611] on 26 November 1691.1 He held the office of Member of Parliament (M.P.) for Essex be
2 CONC tween February 1694 and 1715.1 He held the office of Vice-Admiral of Essex.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wotton's Baronetage recrds that he was "a fast friend of the Church and Monarchy, and a courteous affable gentleman, as much esteemed as any in the county he lived in, and died generally lamented by all his friends."1
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Citation''s ''[S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume I, page 29. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.accessgenealogy.com/baronets/barrington.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Sir CHARLES, who was several times elected knt. of the shire for Essex, and was made, by Queen Anne, vice-admiral of that co.; m. 1st, Bridget, sole da. of sir John Monson, bart. (by Judith, da. of sir Thomas Pelham, bart., gre
2 CONC at-grandfather to Thomas, duke of Newcastle), and after her decease he m. 2dly, Anna-Maria, da. of William, Earl Fitzwilliam, but neither of them had any issue. The greatest part of his estate he left by will to his sister, Shales
2 CONC  {http://www.geni.com/people/Anne-Barrington-Shales/6000000006582486102] , and after her decease to his nephew, Riche-Shales Barrington, esq., her eldest son, who dying unm., it came to his youngest brother John-Shales Barrington,
2 CONC  esq., of Hatfield Broad Oak, in Essex. He d. 29 Jan. 1'715, when the title devolved on his first cousin, John Barrington.
