2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redcastle
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT II. <strong>Murdoch Mackenzie, second of Redcastle</strong>, who has a sasine as heir to his father in 1615. He married Margaret, daughter of William Rose, XI. of Kilravock (marriage contract 13th of June 1 599; tocher 4500 merks)
2 CONC , with issue — 
2 CONT * Kenneth, who died young. 
2 CONT * Roderick, his father's heir and successor. 
2 CONT * Alexander, who married a daughter of William Paterson, with issue — Roderick, who married, a daughter of Mackenzie of Fairburn ; William ; John ; Murdo ; Colin ; and two daughters, the elder of whom married Roderick, son of Murd
2 CONC och Mackenzie, V. of Hilton, with issue — Colin, who died without issue in 1682. 
2 CONT * The Rev. John, who after he was ordained, was schoolmaster at Chanonry, and died in 1640, unmarried. 
2 CONT * William, M.D. at the Court of Spain, where he died, without issue. 
2 CONT * Margaret, who married Angus Chishoim, XVIII. of Chisholm, without issue. 
2 CONT * Finguala, who married Roderick Mackenzie, I. of Applecross, with issue. 
2 CONT * Catharine, who married Donald Mackenzie, III. of Loggie, without issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Four other daughters married respectively, Alexander Fraser of Reelig ; the Rev. William Mackenzie, minister of Tarbat ; Alexander MacRae, Chamberlain of Kintail ; Fraser, son of Fraser of Foyers, and secondly, Hugh, brother of Fr
2 CONC aser of Culduthel. He had also a natural daughter, who married John Mor Mackenzie, natural son of William Mackenzie of Shieldaig, Gairloch. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Murdoch was succeeded by his eldest surviving son."
2 CONT
