1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "III. <strong>Robert Munro, first of Inveran</strong>, who was a member pf the Assize held at Inverness on the 4th of June, 1616, when John, eighteenth Earl of Sutherland, was served heir to his father, Earl John. He was also a me
2 CONC mber of an Assize held in the Tolbooth, Inverness, in 1630, when the same Earl John was declared lawful heir to the three previous Earls of Sutherland. He married Margaret, only child of Robert Munro, sixteenth Baron of Fowlis. On
2 CONC  the 31st of March, 163 1, there is a sasine—" Margaret Munro, spouse to Robert Munro of Assin, in favour of Andrew Munro in Culcraggie, and Farquhar Munro of Teanord, in part of Fyreis." By her he had issue — 
2 CONT * Hugh, his heir and successor. 
2 CONT * George, who witnesses a contract of Reversion of the lands of Teaninich passed between Farquhar Munro, III. of Teanoird, and Hugh Munro, III. of Teaninich, dated at Culcraggie on the 27th of November, 1641. 
2 CONT * Colin, who entered upon a military career, and rose to the rank of Lieutenant-Colonel in the army of Charles I. He was for some time Governor of Penrith Castle, and died unmarried. 
2 CONT * John, I. of Achany, parish of Lairg, of whom presently. 
2 CONT * Elizabeth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert was succeeded by his eldest son."
2 CONT
