2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT William Mackay, third son of Donald of Scowry, was Lieutenant-colonel in the service of Gustavus Adolphus, and was killed at the battle of Lutzen in 1632, '''unmarried'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Source: THE SCOWRY BRANCH OF MACKAYS (1829) page 563. < [https://archive.org/details/historyofhousecl00mackuoft/page/562/mode/2up Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William, Captain in the 1st Lord Reay's Scots regiment serving in the Thirty Years War. He afterwards became Lieut. -Col. of a Swedish regiment, and fell at Lutzen, near Leipzig, in 1632, where also fell King Gustavus Adolphus, un
2 CONC der whose banner he fought.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # Mackay, Robert, 1766-1847.  History of the house and clan of Mackay, containing for connection and elucidation, besides accounts of many other Scottish families, a variety of historical notices, more particularly of those relati
2 CONC ng to the northern division of Scotland during the most critical and interesting periods; with a genealogical table of the clan (1829) < [https://archive.org/details/historyofhousecl00mackuoft/page/562/mode/2up Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT #THE BOOK OF MACKAY BY ANGUS MACKAY, M.A. (St. Andrews University) Minister at Westerdale, Caithness EDINBURGH : NORMAN MACLEOD,  -25 GEORGE IV. BRIDGE CANADA : EDWARD MACKAY, ST. PETER'S MANSE,  MADOC, ONT. M DCCCC VI. pg. 288 < 
2 CONC [https://archive.org/details/bookofmackay00mack/page/288/mode/2up Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT # https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mackay_of_Scoury
2 CONT # https://www.st-andrews.ac.uk/history/ssne/item.php?id=471 MACKAY, WILLIAM [SSNE 471] William Mackay was a son of Donald Mackay of Scourie. He served in Danish service from 15/10/1627, and was reformed in 1629. Mackay was appoint
2 CONC ed to the rank of lieutenant after Andrew Morton in the winter of 1628-9. He later transferred to Sweden with the rank of captain and became a lieutenant colonel soon after. He was killed in action at Lutzen in 1632.
