1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Mentioned 27 March 1642 in Aberdeen. (Records of Old Aberdeen MCLVII-MCMIII, page 15.)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Mentioned 22 August 1662 as 'Dr. George Middleton, brother-german to Mr. Alexander Middleton.' - Reg. of Deeds (Durie), 21 July 1664.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Physician to James II in France. ([http://www.archive.org/details/historyfetterca00camegoog The History of Fettercairn: A Parish in the County of Kincardine (1899)]) This seems to be '''incorrect'''. The physician is too young.
2 CONT
2 CONT * The couple is mentioned in [http://www.scribd.com/doc/74346000/Jacobite-Extracts-Parish-Register-Saint-Germain-Vol-II-1910 Jacobite Extracts Parish Register Saint-Germain Vol II 1910] (page 100): "Georges Middleton, 1er apothica
2 CONC ire du Roi d'Angl., et de Marie Chaplain, femme de Georges Middleton.". The same page lists his death date and age at death, which puts his birth year to cirka 1660. His supposed father Robert (according to The History of Fetterca
2 CONC irn) died in 1645, so something must be incorrect!
2 CONT
2 CONT * James II's physician can '''not''' have been the George Middleton who was brother to principal Alexander.
2 CONT
2 CONT * There was a [https://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.1.1/XY6G-ZSW George Middleton], born 25/01/1660 in Aberdeen, son of George Middleton and Helen Middleton. Were both father and son doctors, explaining why they're confused?
