1 OCCU Master of the Mint in Scotland, Master of the mint in the reign of Charles the Second
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} FALCONER, John of Balmakellie, Advocate and Master of the Mint, Sir
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: about 1600 Marriage (1): OGILVY, Sibil Marriage (2): BRIOT, Esther in 1637 Died: November 1682 1
2 CONT    Other names for John were FALCONER, Johne, Sir, FALCONER, Johnne, FALCONER, Johnne, Sir and FFALCONER, John of Balmekellir.2
2 CONT
2 CONT   General Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sir John Falconer, of Balmakellie, third son of Sir Alexander Falconer of Halkertoun and his wife Agnes, and younger brother of the first Lord Falconer of Halkertoun, was master of the mint in the reign of Charles the Second. He 
2 CONC had a son, Robert, a merchant in London, James, the fourth son, was designed of Coatfield in the county of Elgin."
2 CONT
2 CONT from The Scottish Nation: Falconer
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Falconer was a witness to the baptism in 1679 in Edinburgh of the eldest daughter, Elizabeth, of Captain John Strauchan and Elizabeth Hamilton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: some published genealogical databases show Sir John Falconer to have died in 1670, based on a memorial in Greyfriars. The date of the baptism noted above shows clearly that 1670 is erroneous as his year of death, as do other
2 CONC  texts eg Proceedings Against the Earl of Lauderdale in volume 11 of the Complete Collection of State Trials. 2 3
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Sibil OGILVY. (Sibil OGILVY was born about 1600 and died on 4 December 1634.)
2 CONT
2 CONT John next married Esther BRIOT, daughter of Nicolas BRIOT Graver of the Mint to King Louis XIII and Unknown, in 1637. (Esther BRIOT was born about 1620.)
2 CONT --------------------
