2 SURN Falconar
2 _MARNM Falconar
1 NAME Rev. William Falconer, Minister. of Dyke,Moray
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1647
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1712
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>William Falconar</strong>, born about 1647, eldest son of Colin F., Bishop of Moray ; educated at King's College, Aberdeen ; M.A. (2nd July 1667) ; schoolmaster of Dyke, 1668-70; ord. in England by Henry, Bishop of Oxford
2 CONC  ; pres. by Alexander, Earl of Dunfermline, coll. 16th, and adm. 23rd Sept. 1674; deprived by decreet of Privy Council, 10th Oct. 1689, for neither reading the Proclamation of the Estates, nor praying for King William and Queen Ma
2 CONC ry. He retired to Forres and was alive in 1712. He marr. 29th April 1675, Elizabeth, eldest daugh. of Alexander Tulloch of Tannachie, and had issue — Alexander, merchant, Elgin [father of Bishop William Falconar]."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc06scot#page/416/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. VI, page 416
