1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == RODERICK MACKENZIE OF REDCASTLE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/historyofmackenz00mack/page/537/mode/1up Mackenzie History: 537-8]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Roderick Mackenzie of Redcastle, here treated, is reported to have died in 1650. [https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/mac/mackenzie12.php Stirnet: Mackenzie 12]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "III. <strong>Roderick Mackenzie, third of Redcastle</strong>. He has a sasine in 1629 and in 1638. He was fined £200O for taking part in the wars of Montrose against the Covenanters, and was for some time imprisoned in Edinburgh 
2 CONC along with Thomas Mackenzie of Pluscardine. During his imprisonment General Carr besieged his castle, the only stronghold which still held out for the King ; killed the commander, who exposed himself on the ramparts set fire to th
2 CONC e castle, and razed its walls to the ground. He was liberated on the intercession of his maternal uncle on payment of 7000 merks Scots. In 1690 he excambed with Kenneth Mackenzie, I. of Dundonnel, formerly of Glenmarkassie, the la
2 CONC nds of Acha-ta-Donill, Blachlach, etc., belonging to Redcastle, for the davoch of Meikle Scatvvell, of old possessed by Allan and Alexander Mackenzie. He married Isobel, daughter of Alexander Mackenzie, I. of Kilcoy, with issue — 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Colin, his heir and successor. 
2 CONT * Alexander, an Advocate, who died unmarried. 
2 CONT * Charles, of whom nothing is known, 
2 CONT * Anne, who married John Mackenzie, II. of Scatwell, with issue — an only daughter, Lilias, who in 1679 married Colin Mackenzie, III. of Kincraig, with issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his eldest son."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmackenz00mack#page/536/mode/2up History of the Mackenzies, with genealogies of the principal families of the name]; Alexander Mackenzie; 1894; page 537
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Family:Roderick_McKENZIE_and_Isabella_McKENZIE_%281%29
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redcastle
