1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "I. <strong>John Munro</strong>, fourth son of Robert Munro, III. of Assynt and I. of Inveran and Achness, was the first of the Munros of Achany, county of Sutherland. He has a sasine, dated the 21st of March, 1657, in favour of "
2 CONC John Munro, son of Robert Munro of Achness." He married, first, Janet, daughter of John Corbet of Rhynie, with issue — 
2 CONT * Hugh, his heir and successor. 
2 CONT * John of Invernauld, who married a daughter of William Mackay, Gruids, Lairg, with issue — John ; Mary, who married Angus Sutherland, Scourie ; and another daughter, who married Robert Mackay, Lairg. 
2 CONT * Hector, who married, with issue — a son Hugh, who married Marion Munro, with issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Margaret, daughter of William, IV. of Teanoird, with issue — 
2 CONT * William of Linside, who married Margaret, daughter of Robert Munro, IV. of Pittonachy and Achnagart, with issue, among others, Kenneth, a "Littster" in Culcairn, who married Janet, daughter of William Mackenzie, miller, Contin, 
2 CONC with issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John was succeeded by his eldest son."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmunroso00mack#page/474/mode/2up History of the Munros of Fowlis: with genealogies of the principal families of the name to which are added those of Lexington and New England]; Alexander
2 CONC  Mackenzie; 1898; page 474
