1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Wikipedia biographical summary==
2 CONT "<strong>Alexander Burnett of Leys</strong> (died 5 July 1619) was the Laird of Crathes Castle in the late 16th and early 17th century, being credited for the completion of Crathes in 1596 He acquired Muchalls Castle circa 1600 an
2 CONC d commenced its early 17th century reconstruction. Having died in 1619, the completion of the Muchalls Castle work was carried out by Alexander Burnett's son, Sir Thomas Burnett, 1st Baronet. Alexander Burnett's daughter Helen was
2 CONC  married to John, Laird of Allardice on 3 September 1617."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'Alexander Burnett of Leys', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 8 July 2012, 17:02 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Alexander_Burnett_of_Leys&oldid=501266749> [accessed 17 No
2 CONC vember 2012]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT 12th Laird 1578 - 1619.
2 CONT
2 CONT Became the Laird of Crathes Castle which he completed in 1596 (minus a few finishing touches which took a few more years).
2 CONT
2 CONT Member of Parliament for Kincardine.
2 CONT
