2 CONT Robert was called the second son of James, married to Elizabeth Simson from ye Culies.  He had two sons and two daughters: Stephen, Robert, Janet and Katherine, his age not 50 (meaning he died before age 50 years), from Deaf Rober
2 CONC t Cochran's manuscript.  Marriage date from WFT Vol. 23 #604.[Monroe2001.FTW]6. Robert14 Cochran (James13, John12, John11, John10, Robert9, Alan8, John7, Robert6, William5, Gosiline4, John3, William2, Waldeve ? Walddemar1 de Cochr
2 CONC ane) was born July 01, 1596 in County Donegal, Ireland, and died in Calies, Ulster, Ireland. He married Elizabeth Simson June 15, 1625 in Ro Water, Ulster, Ireland, daughter of Unknown Simson. She was born July 01, 1603 in Culies,
2 CONC  Ireland, and died in Ro Water, Ulster, Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Robert Cochran:
2 CONT Robert was called the second son of James, married to Elizabeth Simson from ye Culies. He had two sons and two daughters: Stephen, Robert, Janet and Katherine, his age not 50 (meaning he died before
2 CONT age 50 years), from Deaf Robert Cochran's manuscript. Marriage date from WFT Vol. 23 #604. Children of Robert Cochran and Elizabeth Simson are:
2 CONT i.   STEPHEN15 COCHRAN, b. July 01, 1630, Rosnalong, Ulster, Ireland; d. Rosnalong, Ulster, Ireland.
2 CONT ii.   JANET COCHRAN, b. Abt. 1636, Ireland.
2 CONT iii.   CATHERINE COCHRAN, b. Abt. 1638, Ireland.
2 CONT iv.   JAMES COCHRAN, b. Abt. 1642, Ireland; m. ISABEL COCHRAN; b. Abt. 1645, Ireland.
2 CONT v.   ROBERT COCHRAN, b. Abt. 1643, Mayboy, Londonderry, Ireland; d. Mayboy, Londonderry, Ireland.
