1 NOTE [Knox.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT TEXT Date of Import: Oct 13, 2001In the Old Cochran Manuscript by Deaf Robert Cochran, James is called the third son to ye first James and was married to Eleinor Stinson from Culies, sister to
2 CONT Robert's wife. His age not forty (meaning he died before his 40th birthday).
2 CONT During the 1680s, the following men were High Sheriff of Londonderry, Ireland:
2 CONT 1682 James STRONG and Henry COCHRAN
2 CONT 1683 William HEMSWORTH and James SYMPSON
2 CONT Derry, Londonderry - National Censuses/Substitutes
2 CONT 1659: Pender's 'Census', NL Ir 31041 c 4
2 CONT 1663: Hearth Money Roll. NL MS. 9584 & PRONI T.307
2 CONT Civil Survey of Ireland - http://www.rootsweb.com/~fianna/county/derry/ldy-1.html
2 CONT Sir William Petty's Civil Survey of Ireland, compiled between 1655 & 1667, contains lists of the principal landlords of each townlands as well as their predecessor before the Cromwellian confisctions
2 CONT of 1641. It contains a great deal of topographical information arranged by county, barony, parish and townland. Unfortunately very little of this survey remains, although County Londonderry and
2 CONT County Tyrone are available. PRONI T.371
2 CONT THE SCOTCH-IRISH OR THE SCOT IN NORTH BRITAIN, NORTH IRELAND, AND NORTH AMERICA
2 CONT CHAPTER XII WHO ARE THE SCOTCH-IRISH? page 160: ...Examining the details of the census of 1881 the clearest traces of the Scottish emigration are to be found. Down has only 38% of Presbyterians, but
2 CONT that is because the south of the county was never colonized, and is still Roman Catholic. The old Scottish colony in Upper Clan-naboye and the Great Ards is still nearly as Presbyterian as in 1630.
2 CONT James Hamilton, immediately after settling there in 1606, raised churches and placed "learned and pious ministers from Scotland" in the six parishes of his, estate--Bangor, Killinchy, Holywood,
2 CONT Ballyhalbert, Dundonald, and Killyleagh. These parishes have gone on flourishing, so that when the census collector did his rounds through Hamilton's old estate in 1881, he found that it contained
2 CONT 29,678 inhabitants; and that although it was situated in what has been called the most Catholic country in Europe, only 3444 Roman Catholics were there to be found, as against 17,205
2 CONT Presbyterians....and an interesting fact is that intermarriages between the natives and the Scotch settlers of the 17th century, and their descendants in Ulster, have been so rare and uncommon as to
2 CONT be practically anomalous, and in consequence can hardly be said to enter into the general question of race origin....
2 CONT
