1 NAME Bryce /Cochrane/
2 GIVN Bryce
2 SURN Cochrane
2 _MARNM Cochrane
2 NICK Bruce Cochran
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1620
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1661
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Northern Ireland
1 OCCU
1 TITL Colonel Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT http://wiki.bcw-project.org/commonwealth/foot-regiments/sir-bryce-cochrane
2 CONT
2 CONT “Sir Bryce Cochrane was a Scot, previously serving the Covenanters in Glencairn’s regiment in Ulster, he betrayed Carrickfergus to Monck’s Parliamentarians. In 1650 he fought for Charles II and was captured at Musselburgh. He may 
2 CONC have seen Dutch service as well. Cashiered in 1660, he went to Ireland.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT 31 May 1659 William Adair married Anna Helena Scott and he died 30 November 1661. Anna Helena Scott remarried Sir Bryce (Brice) Cochrane.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://www.ancestry.com/boards/surnames.adair/723.1.1.1.1.4/mb.ashx
2 CONT *5/20 19 April 1688 Declaration by PATRICK ADAIR, Belfast, Ireland, concerning a sum paid by LEUES STEWART, Elderstown, Scotland, as part of the marriage portion of ANNA HELENA SCOTT, wife of WILLIAM ADAIR, now deceased (d.1661), 
2 CONC to SIR BRUCE (BRICE / BRYCE) COCHRANE, as the request of Anna Helena Adair (nee Scott), for the use of her infant son, Robert Adair, and placed by SIR BRUCE (BRICE / BRYCE) COCHRANE (whom she remarried) in the hands of his brother
2 CONC , the EARL OF DUNDONALD. (Were they known as BRICE ?)
2 CONT *Would Colonel William Brice and his wife, Matilda MacLelland Cochran, of Duplin County, North Carolina, be connected to Sir Robert Adair's mother, Anna Helena nee Scott ? Did she marry Sir Bryce (Brice) Cochrane, bro. of Dundonal
2 CONC d, after she married Mr. Edmonstone ?
2 CONT *Paul, James Balfour. The Scots peerage: founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's ‘Peerage of Scotland’ containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobility of that kingdom, with armorial illustrations. (Edin
2 CONC burgh: D. Douglas, 1904-1914), Vol. 3, Pages 334 to 368. Cochran of Dundonald.  “ Alexandre Cochrane de evderft (sp)dated anno 1618. He was a man of fingular virtue and probity, and greatly improved the eftate of the family. By th
2 CONC e faid Elizabeth Cochrane, he left iffue of feven fons and two daughters 1. Sir John his heir. 2. Sir William of Cowdon, who fucceeded his brother. 3. Alexander, a great loyalft, and a colonel in the army of King Charles I, whofe 
2 CONC grandfon was larid of Manfhiel. 4. Hugh, anceftor of the Cochranes of Fernguflee, alfo a great loyalist, who firft fervid in the wars abroad under the great general Guftavus Adolphus, was afterwards a colonel in king Charles I, hi
2 CONC s army, and was particularly excepted from pardon by the parlament, anno 1648. 5.''' Sir Bryce Cochrane, who was likewife a colonel in the royal army, from the beginning of the civil war, till he loft his life in the king’s fervic
2 CONC e, anno 1650.''' [SIC - apparently not ... ] 6. Arthur, alfo a captain in the royal army. 7. Captain Gavin, anceftor to the Cochranes of Craigmuir. 1ft daugher, Elizabeth married to John Lennox of Woodhead, Efq. 2. Grizel, married
2 CONC  to Thomas Dunlop of Houfe-hill. He was fucceeded by his eldeft fon ...”
2 CONT * “History of the County of Ayr: With a Genealogical Account of the ...,” Volume 2.  By James Paterson.  Page 508.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=BIXSAAAAMAAJ&lpg=PA508&ots=PFUmufT57P&dq=Col.%20Sir%20Bryce%20Cochrane&pg=PA508
2 CONC #v=onepage&q=Col.%20Sir%20Bryce%20Cochrane&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * https://www.ancestry.ca/boards/thread.aspx?mv=flat&m=1405&p=surnames.adair “There was an Edward Brice of "Kilroot" just south of Edmonstone's "Red Hall". William Adair, (Secretary of Virginia) had a dau. who may have married int
2 CONC o the Brice family. The Brice family were related to the Maxwell family, as were Adair (refer Dr. John Adair's will AD1794), and Dobbs (see "Dobbsland" & other townlands on map attached).”
