1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===DAME MARGARET CARNEGIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft/page/66/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 66]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===First Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Magdalene Carnegie married Sir Gideon Baillie of Lochend. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD29%2f1304&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=gideon+baillie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1650&di=y N
2 CONC RS: GD29/1304]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Crawford of Kilbirnie married Lady Magdalene Carnegy. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08paul/page/66/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 66]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children of the Second Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Ann-Crawfurd/6000000019005187686?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1603819695055&through=6000000012105557585
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Crawford-heretrix-of-Kilbirnie/6000000014166266587
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 November 1642: Extract discharge by Dame Magdalene Carnegie, Lady Lochend, relict of Sir Gideon Baillie of Lochend, kt, to William, Earl of Mortoun [Morton], and Robert, Lord Dalkeith, of outstanding annualrents under a cont
2 CONC ract dated 10 and 11 August 1630. Registered B of C and S, 14 December 1643. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD29%2f1304&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=gideon+baillie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&
2 CONC dt=1650&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Bruce family of Kinross (Kinross House Papers), reference GD29/1304]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 May 1643: Pre nuptial contract of marriage between Sir John Crawfurde of Kilburnie, kt, and Dame Magdalene Carnegy, relict of Sir Gideon Baillie of Lochend, bt, with consents. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecat
2 CONC alogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f684&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=gideon+baillie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1650&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/684]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 June 1643: Instrument of resignation by Sir John Crawfurde of Kilbirnie, kt, in the hands of commissioners of James, Duke of Lennox, of the twenty pound lands of Drumry in favour of himself and Lady Magdalene Carnegy, relict 
2 CONC of Sir Gideon Baillie of Lochend bt, his affianced spouse, in terms of no 684. (With charter of resignation and novodamus of the same date). [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD20%2f1%2f
2 CONC 685&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=gideon+baillie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1650&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/685]'''
