1 NAME Sir David Carnegie, 1st Bt.
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1641
2 PLAC Pittarrow, Kincardineshire, Scotland
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE NOV 1708
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>David Carnegie, fiar of Pittarrow</strong>, co. Kincardine 1st s. and h. ap. of the Hon. Sir Alexander Carnegie, of the same (d. March 1681/2), by Margaret, sister of Robert, 1st Viscount Arbuthnott [S.], da. of Sir Rober
2 CONC t Arbuthnott, of Arbuthnott, co. Kincardine, which Alexander was 4th s. of David (Carnegie), 1st Earl of Southesk [S.] (so cr. 22 June 1633), was, on account of services rendered by him and his father to the Crown, cr. a Baronet [
2 CONC S.], 20 Feb. 1662/3, the patent being sealed 27 May 1663, 'provydit to aires male'). He was M.P. [S.] for Kincardineshire, 1667 and 1669-74. He m. firstly (contract 29 Oct. 1673), Catherine, sister of the half-blood to Archibald, 
2 CONC 1st Earl of Rosebery [S.], being 2d da. of Sir Archibald Primrose, 1st Baronet [S. 1651], by his 1st wife, Mary, da. of John (Fleming), 6th Earl of Wigtoun [S.]. She d. Oct. 1677. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. secondly (contract 29 Oct. 1684), Catharine, Dowager Viscountess Arbuthnott [S.], da. of Robert Gordon, of Pitlurg and Straloch. She d. 23 April 1693. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. thirdly, Jean, da. of James Burnett, of Lagaron and Kair, by whom he had six children, having had in all nine sons and eight daughters. He d. Nov. 1708, His widow d. May 1740."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524390#page/n355/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1903; Vol. III; page 337
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-205600841-1-503681/david-carnegie-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-4f19ecb19c40d0691757948503b226bc&mrid=51b17b06b582949027f7020cd54e298d MyHeritage Fam
2 CONC ily Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 27 2020, 20:17:43 UTC''
