2 DATE ABT 1704
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir John, of Drumcairn</strong>, sometime Tutor of Stormont, was nominated an Ordinary Lord of Session in 1681; elected a commissioner for the county of Perth to the Parliaments of 1685 and 1686; nominated a Lord of Artic
2 CONC les same year, and a Lord of Justiciary 1687. The heirs-portioners of Binn disponed that barony to him in 1667, and he was seised of the barony of Cumnock in Ayrshire 1679. He was patron of the Kirk of Strathmiglo. Sir John died a
2 CONC bout 1704, having married, at Edinburgh,1 January 1673, his first cousin Katherine, daughter of William Murray of Drumcairn."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun08pauluoft#page/202/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. VIII, page 202
