1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY JEAN GRAHAM ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Jean Graham, here treated, is the only daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/James-Graham-1st-Marquess-of-Montrose/6000000008630911984?through=6000000112682720902 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Magdelena-Carneg
2 CONC ie/6000000008640681003?through=6000000112682720902 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/254/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 254-5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Jean Graham, here treated, is identified as 'Lady Jane Grahame, only lawful daughter procreat betwixt umquhile James, Marquess of Montrose, and umquhile Lady Magdalen Carnegy his spouse' in an assignation which she granted
2 CONC  on  2 July 1686. According to the late William C. Bishop: "Her childish fortunes were linked with those of her brother Robert. Along with him she joined their brother the second Marquess at Mugdock, and lived there in family with
2 CONC  him till his death. She then removed with the widowed Marchioness to Glasgow, and was intrusted with the management of the household on a journey she took to London. In her will the Marchioness, who died in December 1672, recomme
2 CONC nds the care of her children ' while at the schools ' to their aunt Lady Jean. In her later years Lady Jean Graham resided at Nether Liff, near Dundee. In a letter to the widow of her nephew, the third Marquess of Montrose, dated 
2 CONC 30 June 1686, she mentions the present indisposition I am in,' l and she died at Liff soon after." [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/254/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 254-5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Jean Graham, here treated, died intestate in September 1686. [NRS: CC20/4/15] She probably died at Nether Liff in the parish of Liff, Forfarshire, Scotland. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/255/
2 CONC mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: 255]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Her Testament Dative and Inventory ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The testament dative and inventory of "umqle Lady Jean Grahame lawfull daughter to ane Noble & potent Marquyse James Marquys of Montose wtin the parochine of Liff and Screfdome of fforfar" was given up by her creditors, John Gr
2 CONC ay, younger of Crichie, and James Kinloch of Kilrie, who were recognised as her executors dative by the Commissary Court of St. Andrews. Alexander Gray, brother german to John Gtay of Crichie, acted himself as cautioner for the ex
2 CONC ecutors and confirmation was granted to them on 14 July 1688. [National Records of Scotland, St. Andrews Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Lady Jean Grahame, lawful daughter to James Marquis of Montrose, pari
2 CONC sh of Liff, reference CC20/4/15]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000197158111902 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000197158732821 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/n6/mode/1up The Scots Peerage : founded on Wood's edition of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland; containing an historical and genealogical account of the nobili
2 CONC ty of that kingdom. Edited by Sir James Balfour Paul, Lord Lyon King of Arms. Volume VI. (David Douglas, Edinburgh, 1909), 601 pp.]'''
