1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Sandilands,_1st_Lord_Abercrombie James Sandilands, 1st Lord Abercrombie] (bef. 1627 – aft. 1667) was a Scottish nobleman, the son of Sir James Sandilands and Agnes Carnegie, daughter of David Ca
2 CONC rnegie, 1st Earl of Southesk.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Jean Lichtoun after 1643 and had two children:
2 CONT *James Sandilands, 2nd Lord Abercrombie (1645–1681)
2 CONT *Anna Sandilands A wastrel and riotous liver, he rapidly ran into debt after his father's death in 1644. He was created Lord Abercrombie on 12 December 1647, but in 1649, he was forced to dispose of his property to settle his debt
2 CONC s. The castle of Newark or St Monans and his other properties in Fife were sold to David Leslie, the Covenanter general. He lived abroad on the continent from 1650 to 1658. He divorced his wife on 13 March 1663 and, late that year
2 CONC , married Christian Fletcher. She has been identified as one of those who hid the Scottish regalia before the fall of Dunnottar Castle. Abercrombie died after February 1667.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'James Sandilands, 1st Lord Abercrombie', Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia, 16 April 2013, 18:33 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=James_Sandilands,_1st_Lord_Abercrombie&oldid=5506812
2 CONC 94> [accessed 15 November 2013]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
