1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Charles Erskine, of Cambo</strong>, co. Fife, 3d s. of Alexander Erskine, styled Viscount Fentoun (s. and h. ap. of Thomas, 1st Earl of Kellie [S.], but d. v.p. Feb. 1633), by Anne, da. of Alexander (Seton), 1st Earl of D
2 CONC unfermline [S.], was b. probably about 1620; joined the Royalist troops and was taken prisoner, Nov. 1654, in the Braes of Angus ; was installed Lyon King of Arms, 25 Nov. 1663, and was cr. a Baronet [S.], as above, 20 Aug. 1666, 
2 CONC with rem. to heirs male of the body. He had a, charter of the Barony of Cambo (which he had purchased), 27 Oct. 1669. He m. in or before 1665, Penelope, da. of Arthur Barclay, of Colhill, Gentleman of the King's Chamber. He d. Feb
2 CONC . 1677."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n273/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 255
2 CONT
