1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Ben M. Angel notes: The existence of "A Memoir of Lady Anna Mackenzie" indicates that she was known by her maiden name after the death of her second husband, Archibald Campbell, 9th Earl of Argyll, in 1685.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Lady Anne Mackenzie:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p2045.htm#i20446
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Anne Mackenzie [1]
2 CONT *F, #20446, 
2 CONT *d. 2 May 1707
2 CONT *Last Edited=19 Feb 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.17%
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Anne Mackenzie married, firstly, Alexander Lindsay, 1st Earl of Balcarres, son of Sir David Lindsay, 1st Lord Lindsay of Balcarres and Lady Sophia Seton, in April 1640.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Archibald Campbell, 9th Earl of Argyll, son of Archibald Campbell, 1st Marquess of Argyll and Lady Margaret Douglas, on 28 June 1670.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 2 May 1707.[2] She was buried on 29 May 1707 at Balcarres, Fife, Scotland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Colin Mackenzie, 1st Earl of Seaforth and Lady Margaret Seton.[1] 
2 CONT *From April 1640, her married name became Lindsay. As a result of her marriage, Lady Anne Mackenzie was styled as Baroness Lindsay of Balcarres in March 1641. As a result of her marriage, Lady Anne Mackenzie was styled as Countess
2 CONC  of Balcarres on 9 January 1651. As a result of her marriage, Lady Anne Mackenzie was styled as Dowager Countess of Balcarres on 30 August 1659.[1] 
2 CONT *From 28 June 1670, her married name became Campbell. As a result of her marriage, Lady Anne Mackenzie was styled as Countess of Argyll on 28 June 1670. 
2 CONT *On 30 June 1685 at Edinburgh Castle, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland, she was a prisoner on rumours of her husband's invasion.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Anne Mackenzie and Alexander Lindsay, 1st Earl of Balcarres
2 CONT *1. Lady Henrietta Lindsay+[3]
2 CONT *2. Anne Lindsay [4]
2 CONT *3. Lady Sophia Lindsay d. 1698
2 CONT *4. Charles Lindsay, 2nd Earl of Balcarres [2] b. 7 Feb 1651, d. 15 Oct 1662
2 CONT *5. Colin Lindsay, 3rd Earl of Balcarres+[2] b. 23 Aug 1652, d. 1722
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
