1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===LADY ANNA ELPHINSTONE===
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Spurious Pedigree'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It has been suggested that Lady Anna Elphinstone, here treated, is the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Elphinstone/6000000084691764249, the second wife of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Lockhart-Merchant-in-
2 CONC Edinburgh/6000000084596702072?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1544997828799&through=6000000084691764249 [https://www.ourfamtree.org/browse.php/Margaret-Burnet/p34321 our Family Tree] but this is wrong. Robert Lockhart married Anna Elphin
2 CONC ston, daughter of Harry Elphinstone of Calderhall and his wife Elizabeth Henderson [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalheral02burk/page/371 Commoners: 371-72]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===The Question of Identity===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Anna Elphinstone is the daughter of Alexander, sixth Lord Elphinstone, and his wife, Lady Lilias Elphinstone. She was born before 22 June 1648, the date upon which her baptism was registered at Airth in Stirlingshire, Scot
2 CONC land. She married Walter Sandilands, Lord Torphichen. The marriage contract was dated 7 April 1671. [https://archive.org/details/cu31924092516206/page/n565 The Scots Peerage etc., Vol. III., p. 542]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Possible Portrait of Lady Torphichen===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Portrait of Anne, daughter of Lord Elphinstone (later Lady Torphichen) by Henry Tilson. Description: 17th century oil on canvas in Victorian gilt frame. The sitter depicted in a feigned oval.The portrait bears a 19th c. inscrip
2 CONC tion wrongly identifying the sitter as Anna, daughter of John, 11th Lord Elphinstone; on stylistic grounds (clothes, style of painting etc) this is clearly incorrect. It seems likely that the sitter is Anne, daughter of Alexander,
2 CONC  6th Lord Elphinstone. Anne married Walter Sandilands, 6th Lord Torphichen on 11 April 1671. [https://www.sellingantiques.co.uk/15857/soldportrait-of-anne-daughter-of-lord-elphinstone-later-lady-torphichen-circle-of-henry-tilson/ 
2 CONC Selling Antiques]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===ANNA ELPHINSTONE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Anna Elphinstone here treated is not the same person as https://www.geni.com/people/Anna-Elphinstone/6000000084586824888
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Robert Lockhart: Information from Rootsweb, #1888, Daniel_lockhart, (daniel_lockhart@msn.com)
2 CONT
2 CONT [Douglas's Peerage, Baronage of Scotland]
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, a merchant, and one of the Baillies of Edinburgh. His son, Sir William Lockhart, was created Solicitor General for Scotland by king William (reign: 1689 - 1702).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Abbrev: Douglas' Baronage, Peerage of Scotland Title: Douglas' Baronage, Peerage of Scotland 2. Abbrev: Lanark - Register of Sasines, 1618-1720, Index Title: Lanark - Register of Sasines, 1618-1720, Index
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Robert Lockhart and Anna Elphinstoune: Marriage: Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert Lockhart and Anna Elphinstoune are: +James Lockhart, b. 1647, Scotland, d. 1710, Richmond County, VA. William Lockhart, d. date unknown. John Lockhart, d. date unknown.
