1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===LADY SOPHIA LINDSAY===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Sophia Lindsay is the daughter of Alexander Lindsay, Earl of Balcarres, and his wife Lady Anna Mackenzie. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/548/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 520] She was born bef
2 CONC ore 9 October 1649, the date upon which her baptism was registered at Kilconquhar in Fife, Scotland. [National Records of Scotland, Kilconquhar Baptisms, 1637-1709, reference OPR.436/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 December 1681: Copy letter, unsigned, to Mr John Campbell, son to the earl of Breadabane. Expresses pleasure that recipient has found the country peaceable; weather bad; Earl Argyle found guilty by the assize and an express 
2 CONC despatched to court; return was that sentence was to be passed upon him, but the execution to be delayed until the king should signify his further pleasure; sentence being death and forefeiture, on the 20th inst., the earl, in the
2 CONC  habit of a footboy attending Lady Sophia Lindsay, [his step daughter,] made his escape out of the castle; uproar followed but search made in vain; urges caution in letter and suggests making a cipher, an alphabet of private chara
2 CONC cters. Damaged. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f39%2f133%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Sophia+Lindsay&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cam
2 CONC pbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), Correspondence, reference GD112/39/133/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun01pauluoft/page/548/mode/1up The Scots Peerage I: 520]
