2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://thepeerage.com/p2045.htm#i20448 Biographical Summary by Darryl Lundy's Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Lindsay, 2nd Earl of Balcarres [1]
2 CONT *M, #20448, 
2 CONT *b. 7 February 1651, 
2 CONT *d. 15 October 1662
2 CONT *Last Edited=19 Feb 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=6.83%
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Lindsay, 2nd Earl of Balcarres was baptised on 7 February 1651 at Dundee, Angus, Scotland.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 15 October 1662 at age 11 at Balcarres, Fife, Scotland, from a 'large stone being found in his heart', unmarried.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried on 21 October 1662 at Balcarres, Fife, Scotland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Alexander Lindsay, 1st Earl of Balcarres and Lady Anne Mackenzie.[1] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 3rd Lord Lindsay of Balcarres [S., 1633] on 30 August 1659.[1] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 2nd Earl of Balcarres [S., 1651] on 30 August 1659.[1] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 2nd Lord Lindsay and Balneil [S., 1651] on 30 August 1659.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
