1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Robert Lindsay
2 CONT *Son of Bernard Lindsay Lt Colonel and Rachel Lindsay
2 CONT *Brother of James Lindsay
2 CONT *Husband of Susanna (Opie) Lindsay — married about 1659 in Virginia Colony
2 CONT *Father of Opie Lindsay
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Opie's father was Col. Robert Lindsay of the Mount, Falls Church Va. He was born in Northumberland Co. Va. and migrated to Fairfax Co. and built the Mount on 1200 acres in the Falls Church area. It was his grandfather Robert Linds
2 CONC ay of Leith Scotland who was the immigrant in 1652, brought to Va. as an 11 yr. old. by his half uncle, Rev. David Lindsay. That is the Robert who was the 1st son of Lt. Col Bernard Lindsay of Kingswerk, grandson of Thomas Lindsay
2 CONC , Snowden Herald, and Rachel Lindsay, daughter of Sir Jerome Lindsay Lord Lyon. These parents died in an epidemic in Leith. This needs to be corrected !!!! Joseph W. Lindsay Haley III Esq. ATP FSA Scot. Steward of Carrifran. Past 
2 CONC Historian of the USA Clan Lindsay Member of the Clan Lindsay Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT PS The Rev. David's tomb at Cherry Point had two slabs, as his grandson Capt. Thomas Opie is buried in the same tomb. The first slates he is the first son of Sir Heirome (Jerome) Lindsay Lord Lyon. d. 1667 It was broken when Capt.
2 CONC  Opie's slab was placed under the original. The two broken pieces were taken to the Smithsonian and recorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. Robert's wife's surname is unknown as per records, despite the oft copied and pasted maiden name of Opie, which is based on a speculation of a sibling connection to Capt. Thomas Opie. All that it is known from records that he
2 CONC r first name was Susanna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clan Lindsay has the most searched records of this family, and only use what is recorded by historical record, and not what is donated by the Mormons.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was not married to Robert Lindsay of Scotland, but to Col Robert Lindsay of the Mount Falls Church VA. He was the grandson of Robt of Scotland 1641. These Lindsays arrived in Virginia in 1652. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
