2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 June 1668: Extract Disposition by Robert Bruce of Kennets, to Alexander Bruce, his second lawful son, whom failing, to David Bruce of Shanbody, his eldest son and heir; of the lands of Garlett, with the teinds thereof, 3 acr
2 CONC es of Carse land adjacent thereto, with the pasturage of four soumes, in Shanbody, under the reservation of his own liferent of said lands. Witnesses Mr James Kennoway Writer to the Signet, John Kennoway his son, and David Kippen,
2 CONC  servant of the said Mr Robert Bruce, - Dated at Easter Kennet. This is an Extract from the Records. Registered B. of C. and S., 20 Oct. 1731. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD11%2f17
2 CONC 3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Bruce Family of Kennet, Clackmannanshire. reference GD11/173]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 August 1674: Discharge by Thomas Cadie, Tailor in Carnock, to Mr Alexander Bruce, brother of the deceased David Bruce of Kennet; of a years annualrent, of the sum of 350 merks money of Scotland, in Bond by the said David Bruc
2 CONC e, to the said Thomas Cadie, dated 2d Decemb. 1672, and that in name and behalf of David Bruce of Kennet, son and heir of the said deceased David Bruce of Kennet. Witnesses Mr James Hutton Schoolmaster of Culross writer of the Dis
2 CONC charge, and William Burn, Merchant burgess of Culross- Dated at Culross. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD11%2f189&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1
2 CONC 700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Bruce Family of Kennet, Clackmannanshire. reference GD11/189]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 December 1674: Charter by David Bruce of Clackmannan, to Robert Scotland, Litster in Clackmannan, and Margaret Reid his spouse, of the Eastmost half of a Tenement of houses and yard, together with a croft or 2 riggs of land l
2 CONC ying contiguous to the same, on the north side of the high street of his town of Clackmannan, with a proportional part of the Muir of Pilmuir, all lying in the barony and County of Clackmannan; To be holder of the said Robert Bruc
2 CONC e and his heirs; for payment yearly of 6 shillings 8 pence, money of Scotland, at the usual terms, and service of Court. Witnesses Mr Alexander Bruce of Garlet, Mr John Buchanan bailie of Clackmannan, and William Morrison, Sheriff
2 CONC  Clerk of Clackmannan - Dated at Clackmannan. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD11%2f191&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=n National Records o
2 CONC f Scotland, Papers of the Bruce Family of Kennet, Clackmannanshire. reference GD11/191]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 June 1687: Assignation Disposition and Retrocession, by Alexander Bruce of Garland, to Thomas Burn second son of the deceased Andrew Burn in Easter Gellet of assignation GD11/201 - (vide GD11/160.), and that in terms of Back 
2 CONC Bond, by the said Alexander Bruce to him, dated 18th May 1678.-and reconveying to him the lands and barony of Shanbody and others in security as therein mentioned. Witnesses William Morrison Sheriff Clerk of Clackmannan, and Alexa
2 CONC nder and Henry Morrison, Writers in Alloa - Dated at Alloa. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD11%2f217&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=nNatio
2 CONC nal Records of Scotland, Papers of the Bruce Family of Kennet, Clackmannanshire. reference GD11/217]'''
