1 NAME Janet /Alexander/ Heiress of Gartmore
2 GIVN Janet
2 SURN Alexander
2 NSFX Heiress of Gartmore
2 NICK note: only daughter
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1636
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} About 1633/1634, John Alexander married Agnes, the only daughter of Robert Graham of Gartmore, Perthshire. Agnes was married to John when her father died in 1634 and was described in estate documents as "lawful doc
2 CONC hter of . . . Robert Graham of Gartmoir, and with consent of John Alexander, lawful son to ane noble and potent erle, William, Erle of Stirling, Lord Alexander, her spouse." Agnes Graham Alexander died some time prior to 23 Januar
2 CONC y 1636, when her husband, John Alexander, was "invested in that portion of the lands of Gartmore which had passed to her at her father's death."
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Graham Alexander had a brother Gilbert Graham who also inherited a portion of Gartmore, on the death of their father Robert Graham. Gilbert died in 1641 without children or siblings to inherit. As a result, his niece''' "Jan
2 CONC et Alexander, only daughter of John Alexander and the deceased Agnes Graham"''' received her uncle's share in the lands of Gartmore (Sheriff Court Book, Stirling). If John and Agnes Graham Alexander had other children, they were d
2 CONC ead by 1641, otherwise they would have inherited from their Uncle Gilbert along with Janet Alexander.
