1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Erskine of Pittodrie, founder of the Hospital (p. 147), appears, in 1675 ; he took the oaths of allegiance to William and Mary in 1689. By his wife, Mary, daughter of Patrick Grant of Ballindalloch, he had,
2 CONC  besides his heir, a daughter, Jean, married to James Moir of Stoneywood, the Jacobite Colonel of 1745. – (John Davidson 1878, Inverurie and the Earldom of the Garioch)
2 CONT
2 CONT Admissi  in  2  da  classe,  1661… Gulielmus  Erskin,  Pitodrie. – admission role of 1661 in 'Fasti Academiae Mariscallanae aberdonensis'. vol 2 : Alumni and Graduates in Arts
