1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Evidence needed to support as mother of https://www.geni.com/people/Frances-Hamilton/6000000000734550893
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hamilton-632
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith Hamilton was the daughter of Rev James Hamilton and Catherine Leslie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith was the sister of Rev Andrew Hamilton.
2 CONT
2 CONT He graduated from Trinity College, Dublin in 1686 and Rev Alexander Colquhuon graduated in 1684.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev Andrew Hamilton suceeded his father as Archdeacon of Raphoe and Rector of Taghboyne. He petitioned in 1690 to hold both parishes together and succeed his father as he was resident in Taghboine and that both parishes, formerly 
2 CONC of considerable value, were not now, by reason of the calamities of the present war. It was referred to the Bishop of Raphoe that the petitioner's father died at the beginning of the present troubles left a large numerous family, 
2 CONC which in great measure was dependent on the petitioner for their support and maintence and that the petitioner was believed to be a person of good learning and piety. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the reference (copy attached) Alexander and Judith had four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Child: William Calhoun
2 CONT # Child: Alexander Calhoun
2 CONT # Child: Audley Calhoun
2 CONT # Child: James Calhoun (reference states James other information suggests James Patrick Colquhoun, no evidence for middle name
2 CONT
2 CONT Here are their details:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Major William Colquhoun, of Cross and Straband County Tyrone m. Patience, dau of Oliver McCausland, High Sheriff of County Tyrone in 1730 and in 1739.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Alexander Colquhoun of Rush-hill in the Townland of Ballyhallachoun b. 1705 m Margaret Hazlitt. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Audley Colquhoun (there is a potential problem here it shows he married Judith Hamilton? Is she a cousin perhaps otherwise it appears he married his mother!)[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) James Colquhoun, m Catherine Montgomery. It is not clear from the reference if it was him or his son James Colqhoun who was killed by the Indians in 1760. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disproved Lineage 
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted From [https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/PgROOegO2OU Colquhoun-Hamilton-- royal heritage or hoax?] Mar 10, 1998
2 CONT
2 CONT > According to Orval Calhoun, who wrote 4 vols. on American Calhouns (and variations of the name), both Alexander Colhoun and Judith Hamilton descended from Princess Mary of Scotland, b. 1452, granddaughter of James I and Joan Bea
2 CONC ufort, and thus a descendant of Edward III and Philippa of Hainault. The descents he gives are as follows: …
2 CONT
2 CONT Extracted From reply by William Addams Reitwiesner [https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/PgROOegO2OU GoogleBooks] 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >Claude Hamilton, b. 1536 m. Lady Margaret Douglas
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the fourth son of his parents, and was created 1st Lord Paisley.
2 CONT His oldest son was created 1st Earl of Abercorn.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >George Hamilton, b. @1600 m. ?
2 CONT
2 CONT See SP I:43 for him. Sir George was the fourth son, and his estates were
2 CONT Greenlaw in co. Tyrone and Roscrea in co. Tipperary. I don't know about
2 CONT him being born in or around 1600, as in 1611 he and his wife and family
2 CONT were living in Derriewoone in a house 62 feet long by 30 feet wide he
2 CONT himself had built. His only surviving child was a son by his (second?)
2 CONT wife Lady Mary Butler, and that son was named James.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >James Hamilton b. ? m. Catherine Leslie
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately this wasn't him, as James Hamilton, the only surviving son of Sir George Hamilton, died unmarried some time before his (James's) will was proved, which was on 2 Feb. 1658/9. SP I:43.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT >Judith Hamilton, b. 1662 m. Alexander Colhoun
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Genealogy 
2 CONT
