2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hamilton-2293
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew was born in 1669. He was the son of Rev James Hamilton and Catherine Leslie. Catherine was the daughter of Col James Leslie and Isabella Conyngham.
2 CONT
2 CONT He suceeded his father as Archdeacon of Raphoe and Rector of Taghboyne. He petitioned in 1690 to hold both parishes together and succeed his father as he was resident in Taghboine and that both parishes, formerly of considerable v
2 CONC alue, were not now by reason of the calamities of the present war. It was referred to the Bishop of Raphoe that the petitioner's father died at the beginning of the present troubles left a large numerous family, which in great mea
2 CONC sure was dependent on the petitioner for their support and maintence and that the petitioner was believed to be a person of good learning and piety.
2 CONT
2 CONT Archdeacon Andrew Hamilton, matriculated at Trinity college, Dublin as Pensioner 17 june 1682, aged 13, son of James H of co. Donegall. Educated by Mr Sympson. His College Tutor was Samuel Foley (afterwards Bishop of Down and Conn
2 CONC or). He graduated B,A, Vern. 1686 and B. and D.D. 1704. he was perhaps a Scholar. Dr Hamilton was Vicar-General of the Diocese and dying 22 September 1753, in his 84th year, was buried at St Ann's Dublin
2 CONT
2 CONT He was archdeacon of Raphoe from 1690 (or perhaps 1698) until his death. Also Rector of Taghboyne.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was Sarah, daughter of Henry Conynghame, who ran away from boarding school at the age of 12 to marry him, before 1703. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew died in 1753 without a will. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
