2 CONT * Identified as "probably connected with the Hamiltons of Binning Easter" was ... John Hamilton in Priestfield in Blantyre (d before 02.06.1597)
2 CONT **3.	'''Hew Hamilton of Loughenas''', later of Lisdevin in co. Tyrone (d 1637) 	m. '''Marion Gibbs''' (sister of James Gibbs).   	'HamiltonHistory' (p717) shows that Hew & Marion were parents of George, Hugh, Frederick, John, Will
2 CONC iam & Robert with Hugh, shown as 'of Lisdevin & Tullodowy', identified as father, by Agnes (dau of Lt. Col. James Galbraith), of James (Archdeacon of Raphoe), John, Margaret & Elizabeth. However, on p1017, that James is identified
2 CONC  as eldest son of Andrew (prebendary of Kilskerry) by Rebecca, dau of Lt. Col. James Galbraith. On p995 is shown a different James as son of Hugh of Tullydowey by Agnes Galbraith. We suspect that the confusion has been caused by b
2 CONC rothers (Hamiltons, could be cousins?) marrying sisters (Galbraiths). We speculate that (a) Andrew was another son of Hew & Marion; (b) Archdeacon James was son of Andrew & Rebecca; and (c) the James who was son of Hugh & Agnes wa
2 CONC s not the Archdeacon (of Mountgavelin') but was 'of Lisdevin'.
2 CONT ***C.	'''Andrew Hamilton''' (prebendary of Kilskerry) The following comes from 'HamiltonHistory' ('Mountgavelin', p1017+) with input/support from TCB (vol 5, 'Hamilton of Manor Cuningham', p382). 	m. Rebecca Galbraith (dau of Lt. 
2 CONC Col. James Galbraith of Mountgavelin)
2 CONT **** 	i.	'''James Hamilton of Mountgavelin''' (b 1638, d 1690, Donagheady & Taghboyne, Archdeacon of Raphoe) 	m. '''Catherine''' '''Leslie''' (dau of James Leslie by Catherine, dau of Alexander Conyngham, Dean of Raphoe)
2 CONT ***** 	a.	'''Andrew Hamilton''' (b 1669, d 22.09.1753, rector of Donagheady & Taghboyne, Archdeacon of Raphoe) 	Andrew's wife is named Anne by 'HamiltonHistory' but Sarah by TCB. m. (before 1703) Anne or Sarah Conynghame (dau/heir
2 CONC  of Henry (not Sir William) Conynghame of Castle Conynghame). “ His wife was Sarah, daughter of Henry Conynghame, who ran away from boarding school at the age of 12 to marry him, before 1703.”
2 CONT ***** 	b.	'''William''' Hamilton (d 1729, Archdeacon of Armagh) 	m. (1701) Catherine Leslie (b 1682, d 1740, dau of Henry Leslie, Archdeacon of Down ('grandson (not son) of Henry, Bishop of Meath'))
2 CONT *****c.	'''Judith''' Hamilton 	m. (c1700) '''Alexander Colhoun''' (rector of Templecarne)
2 CONT ***** 	d.+	other issue including '''James''' (b 1765, a 1693), '''Ezekeal''' (b 1680, a 1703)
