2 CONT ===Mary (Fobes) Southworth (abt. 1689 - 1712)===
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Southworth formerly Fobes
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1689 in Little Compton, Newport County, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of William Fobes and Martha (Pabodie) Fobes
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Phebe (Fobes) Seabury [half], Joseph Seabury [half], Martha (Seabury) Sawyer [half], Elizabeth (Forbes) Briggs, Constant (Fobes) Little and Mercy Fobes
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Edward Southworth — married 17 Mar 1708 (to 29 Feb 1712) in Little Compton, Newport, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Rebecca (Southworth) Seabury and Fobes Southworth
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 29 Feb 1712 in Little Compton, Newport County, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (Fobes) Southworth was related to a passenger on the Mayflower.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Should not be confused with her younger sister, Mercy/Marcy (1694-1712).[1]
