1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From profile of brother William:
2 CONT
2 CONT ''William arrived in America in 1734 with wife Jane Gaffney, Brother James & wife Janey, Niece Jenny, Nephew William, and son William age 22 & his wife Mary Caldwell age 19.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Source-Citations include WLA Book, added after the history was written in 1901.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Source-Chron-368, Margaret Armstrong of Mason Texas; NSSAR 93, Price.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Source-From the Rutledge Files. The family settled in Augusta Co., Va.and resided there a few years, then William moved with his wife, to South Carolina and resided in Honea Path, Anderson Co., S.C. until his death in1775.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Source-De Wolfe Miller manuscript states that Jany/Jenny is sister to William.
2 CONT Compiled by W.L.A.(AZ.)
2 CONT
2 CONT As for James's life after arriving in the future United States, it is possible he first went to Paxtang, Dauphin County, and later removed to Franklin County, Pennsylvania.  He could thus have been one of the "Paxtang Armstrongs",
2 CONC  with parentage misattributed to a cousin.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Note===
2 CONT
2 CONT The wife who accompanied the James Armstrong who died in Franklin County was called "Janey".  The similarity to the immigration account above cannot be overlooked, although the fate of children William and Jennet would need to be 
2 CONC accounted for if this indeed was the case.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note also that "Jenny" and "William" would have been underage in 1734, and they would have been James's last children.  His earlier children either died young, married and stayed in Ireland, or emigrated separately.  I assume a ro
2 CONC ugh marriage date of 1710.  A marriage date of 1704 can be found in web trees but it is unrealistic because it has his wife being just 16 at the time of marriage, and that was quite unusual in Ireland at this time.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Likely name of Thomas's father based on children's names.
