1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://bedminsterpa.com/township-government/history/ This reference] describes Joseph as one of the founders of the town of Bedminster, Bucks County.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Note===
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joseph married children of other immigrant Irish Armstrongs, so that hints that Joseph was likely from Ireland as well, and it localizes him to the family of John of Brookeborough in fact.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Immigrated in 1731, according to 'VIRKUS, FREDERICK A., editor. Immigrants to America before 1750. An Alphabetical List of Immigrants to the Colonies, before 1750, Compiled from Official and Other Records'.
2 CONT
2 CONT A key question is whether Joseph arrived already married or not.  His eldest son is presumed to be Ephraim, but he was said to have been born in 1730.  That may be approximate, however, so it's not a definitive answer.  
2 CONT
