1 NOTE {geni:about_me} We know Jeanette existed because of the strongly-followed Irish naming conventions of the family of John Armstrong of Brookeborough.  But only recently has DNA evidence come to light that indicates Jeanette may hav
2 CONC e married.  If she did marry, it was to a Simpson, likely named "Robert".
2 CONT
2 CONT The DNA evidence at this time allows for Robert to have married either an Armstrong, or a Johnson, or a McKee, or a Robertson.  Further analysis of DNA matches should clarify who he married, but the odds are quite good of him marr
2 CONC ying an Armstrong just by sheer numbers in that part of Ireland.
