1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DNA ties a descendent of https://www.geni.com/people/John-McClure/6000000018767122324 (B.C.) to a descendant of the Armstrong clan of County Fermanagh.  It is therefore likely that John's parents married in the vic
2 CONC inity of Clogher, County Tyrone, and he was born there.
2 CONT
2 CONT We don't know the name of this Armstrong daughter but we do know she must have existed.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/DNA-Data/6000000203271618840 This private profile] summarizes the evidence in detail.  The gist of the argument involves two distinct chunks of DNA.  The first chunk is shared among at least 7 individu
2 CONC als, of which 3 are provable descendants of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Armstrong/6000000032389303254?through=6000000185654529921.  Four are plausible descendants of the same individual.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the first DNA overlap region, several individuals are proven descendants of https://www.geni.com/people/John-McClure/6000000018767122324 .  I know only details of one of those individuals, due to privacy restrictions.  But the 
2 CONC obvious conclusion is that this McClure line is descended from the Brookeborough Armstrongs.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a second group of six individuals who are provably descended as well from this McClure line.  This group includes two individuals from the first group, but the rest only overlap in the second section of DNA, and only one 
2 CONC of these two is a provable Armstrong descendant.  Thus, this second DNA overlap may or may not be Armstrong DNA.
