2 CONT
2 CONT http://landedfamilies.blogspot.co.za/2015/09/182-armstrong-and-heaton-armstrong-of.html
2 CONT
2 CONT William Armstrong (c.1635-90?) was also a soldier, but is of particular interest here as the man who laid the foundations of the family's Irish estates, through a series of grants from the Crown in the 1660s (recognising their los
2 CONC ses and service during the Civil War and Commonwealth), and purchases in the 1670s. He made his home at Farney Castle near Thurles (Tipperary), and when he died he left a life interest in it to the widow of his executed brother. S
2 CONC he died in 1693 and '''the estate passed to William's son, John Armstrong (d. 1707). John's heir was his eldest son, Col. William Armstrong (d. 1767)'''
