1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 2. James, who died .in Juniata County, Pennsylvania c. 1774, was a private in the militia company captained by James Patterson in 1758. Indians captured his wife and two children on 27 January 1756, but she was rel
2 CONC eased a year later at Fort Augusta.5 After his death by drowning, letters of administration were issued 23 April 1774. The younger of the ten surviving children went under the guardianship of their uncle, John Lyon.
