2 CONT John Armstrong, 'The Pedigree of the family of Armstrong', continued by the Rev. W. A. Armstrong (no imprint, 1813) states: "Robert, the third brother of Martin married and had several children, viz. Martin, Lancelot, and others, 
2 CONC and died in 1744 aged 65. Alexander the second son of Robert the Cornet married Grisel the second daughter of Andrew Armstrong of Ballycumber." This is clumsily worded and it is unlikely that Robert the Cornet should have been bor
2 CONC n about 1679 since two siblings are said to have been born in 1647 and 1668, and Robert was Cornet to his brother Martin in 1689. It seems more likely that there was a younger Robert, a son of the Cornet, who died in 1744, as in t
2 CONC he above reference in antonymaitland.com, and that Martin and Lancelot were sons of the younger Robert. This is also the story in another version of John Armstrong's manuscript, that produced by Liz Yeats from a manuscript of the 
2 CONC Rev. J. N. R. Abbott (National Library of Ireland Ms. 5216), and in 'Registered Pedigrees' (National Library of Ireland GO MS 171). 
