1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://bolesbooksblog.wordpress.com/2015/01/23/4-dugal-mcqueen-scottish-rebel-and-gateway-ancestor-to-royalty/
2 CONT
2 CONT Dugal, it was clear, was the son of John Macqueen by Anne, daughter of William Mackintosh, the 18th chief, and his wife Margaret Graham.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT According to genealogist and researcher Dr. David Boles, Anne McQueen should be the mother of Dugal. I have personally corresponded with Dr. Boles over the parentage of Dugal McQueen.
2 CONT
2 CONT  THE OMNIBUS ANCESTRY: 589 DOCUMENTED AMERICAN AND EUROPEAN LINES 
2 CONT
2 CONT      by David B. Boles 
2 CONT
2 CONT A Publication of Bolesbooks 
2 CONT  David B. Boles 5541 Woodberry Lane Tuscaloosa, AL  35405 
2 CONT
2 CONT Copyright 2016   David B. Boles 
2 CONT
2 CONT P. 197
2 CONT
2 CONT John McQueen, b. ca 1640?, d. p 1719  in co. Inverness, Scotland  m. ca 1665? to Anne Mackintosh, see Mackintosh Line .  John was of Pollochaig (Pollochak), co. Inverness .  In 1671 he was called "John mcquein of pollochak" when t
2 CONC he Valuation Roll showed he held an estate worth £50 "including the Earle of Murrayes few Duties" .
2 CONT
2 CONT Antiquarian Notes, Historical, Genealogical,and Social (Second Series): Inverness-shire Parish by Parish. Inverness: A. & W.Mackenzie.
