1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MASTER JOHN HAMILON OF HALCRAIG ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Honorary Burgess of Glasgow===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Master John Hamilton of Halcraig, here treated, was the son of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Hamilton-of-Halcraig-Senator-of-the-College-of-Justice/6000000017552481415?through=6000000212795729825. [NRS:  CC8/8/83] The name o
2 CONC f his mother is not certainly known. However, he was probably aged twenty-one years or more when he was enrolled as a burgess of Glasgow on 29 June 1704, and this suggests that he may have been the son of https://www.geni.com/peop
2 CONC le/Ursula-Ralston/6000000023942470532?through=6000000212795729825. '''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Master John Hamilton of Halcraig. here treated, died intestate in October 1706. It appear that at the time of his death he was unmarried. [NRS: CC8/8/83]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Burgess Records of Glasgow ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 June 1704: Hamilton, Mr. John, of Hallcraig, younger, B. and G.B. gratis. [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso43scotuoft/scottishrecordso43scotuoft/page/258/mode/1up Glasgow Burgesses: 258]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Testament Dative and Inventory (Joint: With his Father) ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 March 1707: Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig died intestate in March 1706. His only lawful son, John Hamilton of Halcraig, also died intestate in October 1706. Their joint testament dative and inventory was given up on 29 March
2 CONC  1707, in name and behalf of Sir John's daughters, Miss Anna Hamilton, and Miss Elizabeth Hamilton, who were: "decerned as nearest in kin to their said deceased father and brother." The testament dative and inventory was given up 
2 CONC by James Dunlop, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, William Muir, advocate, and John Rusell of Breedshaw, all three of whom had been appointed as curators to the before mentioned daughters by an act of curatory dated 10 January 1707. 
2 CONC Confirmation was granted to the executors dative on 11 April 1707. Three months or so later, because certain amounts of money owed to the deceased had been omitted from the principal testament dative and inventory, an addition was
2 CONC  made. Mr. Gavin Muir, student of Divinity, acted himself as cautioner for the executors dative and confirmation was granted to them on 21 April 1708. Twenty-three years or so later a second addition was made for the same reason. 
2 CONC The executors dative, who had married during the intervening years, were described as follows: "Mrs Anna Hamilton relict of the deceast Mr Wm Law of Elvinstoun" and Mrs Elizt Hamilton relict of Mr Daniel Weir of Stonbyres." Mr Cha
2 CONC rles Gordon, son of Sir William Gordon of Invergordon, Baronet, acted himself as cautioners for the executors dative and confirmation was granted to them on 8 December 1732. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Cour
2 CONC t, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Sir John Hamiltoune of Halcraig, and Mr. John Hamiltoune of Halcraig, his only lawful son; includes 2 Eiks dated 21/04/1708 and 08/12/1732, reference CC8/8/83]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000213374978825 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000213374915838 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000213374825839 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000213374881821 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000213374746841 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000213374530851 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Sasine Registers ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 July 1709 x 31 July 1719: Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig. John Hamilton of Halcraig, son of Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig. Isobel Hamilton, daughter of Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig, and spouse of Sir William Gordon of Dalpho
2 CONC llie. Anne Hamilton, daughter of Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig. Elizabeth Hamilton, daughter of Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig. [Particular Register of Sasines for the Sheriffdom of Lanark, reference RS42/XII/226]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 July 1709 x 31 July 1719: Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig. John Hamilton of Halcraig, son of Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig. Isobel Hamilton, daughter of Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig, and spouse of Sir William Gordon of Dalpho
2 CONC llie. Anne Hamilton, daughter of Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig. Elizabeth Hamilton, daughter of Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig. [Particular Register of Sasines for the Sheriffdom of Lanark, reference RS42/XII/227]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                      3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 January 1761 x 28 June 1766: Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig. John Hamilton of Halcraig, son of Sir John Hamilton of Halcraig. Charles Hamilton Gordon of Newhall. William Gordon. [Particular Register of Sasines for the Sheriffd
2 CONC om of Lanark, reference RS42/XVII/189]'''
2 CONT
