1 NAME Hugh /Wallace of Elderslie/
2 GIVN Hugh
2 SURN Wallace of Elderslie
2 _MARNM Wallace of Elderslie
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1678
1 OCCU Succeeded grandfather at Elderslie in 1637; died without heirs and Elderslie was sold to Sir Thomas Wallace of Craigie
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===HUGH WALLACE OF ELDERSLIE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to Charles Rogers, Hugh Wallace of Elderslie is the son of William Wallace of Elderslie. He says that he was served heir to his deceased father in certain rents from the lands of Helington in the Kyle-Stewart division
2 CONC  of North Ayrshire, in May 1637. [https://archive.org/stream/bookofwallace01roge#page/n86/mode/1up The Book of Wallace, i, p. 29] He was served heir to his grandfather on 28 March 1637. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAA
2 CONC AcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=onepage&q=ellerslie&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retorn
2 CONC atarum, etc., II Inquisitiones Speciales. Renfrew]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''(100) Mar. 28. 1637. Hugo Wallace, haeres Willelmi Wallace de Ellerslie, avi, - in 20 solidatis terrarum antiqui extentus de Windiehill, alias Butismealing, Muirheid et Clippingis nunc vocatis, in dominio, baronia, et regalitat
2 CONC e de Paisley. - E. 26s. 8d. xv. 184. [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots=qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AE
2 CONC IRDAG#v=onepage&q=ellerslie&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc., II Inquisitiones Speciales. Renfrew]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 July 1640: Contract of wadset between John Crawfurd at Kilbirnie and Hew Wallace of Elderslie for 504 merks. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH15%2f112%2f2%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=
2 CONC n&tp=n&k=wallace+of+elderslie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Sir William Wallace of Craigie: Legal Documents, reference RH15/112/2/4]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 February 1655: Extract decree of the sheriff court of Renfrew at the instance of Sir John Crawfuird of Kilbirnie, kt, as wadsetter, against Hugh Wallace of Elderslie and tenants of the twenty shilling lands of Cartisyid in t
2 CONC he parish of Paisley declaring a back-tack to the said Hugh of the said lands to be expired and decerning the tenants to pay rents and duties to the pursuer. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refe
2 CONC rence=GD20%2f1%2f467&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=wallace+of+elderslie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Earls of Glasgow (Crawford Priory), reference GD20/1/467]'''
2 CONT
