2 CONT XIII. JOHN BUCHANAN of Buchanan had gift of the ward and non-entry of all his estates since the death of his father, Sir George, dated, Perth, 28th March 1599. On 26th October 1602 he is retoured heir of his father Sir George Buch
2 CONC anan in Buchanan, and other lands, and in the same year he had a thirty-eight years' tack of the whole teinds of Kilmaronock from his father-in-law, Adam, Commendator of Cambuskenneth, to him and his wife Annabel Erskine. By Annab
2 CONC el Erskine he had at least two sons: (1) George; and (2) Walter, who was at Glasgow College 7th March 1620.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''XIV. GEORGE BUCHANAN of Buchanan married Elizabeth Preston, only daughter of Sir George Preston of Craigmillar, Knt. He had an infeftment as heir-apparent of his father. Sir John Buchanan, in the estate of Buchanan, to him and 
2 CONC his wife, Elizabeth Preston, 10th July 1629. He and his father were dead before 1653. He left issue: one son John, and three daughters: (1) Helen, who became second wife of Sir John Rollo of Bannockburn;2 (2) Agnes, who married Ja
2 CONC mes Stewart of Rosyth3 (marriage contract dated 7th July 1649);4 and (3) Jean or Janet,5 who married, 5th December 1661, John Leckie of that Ilk.6'''
