2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''x 11 Deceember 1649: Draft declaration by Agnes Scott that a translation dated 11 December 1649 made to her by Mr. Henry Chaip of Ormestoune, advocate, of a third of the sum contained in a bond by deceased William, Earl of Mort
2 CONC on, to Lieut-Gen David Leslie dated 10 and 11 July 1644 was procured by Sir Robert Douglas of Blaikerstoune, kt, for purposes of her apprising against the Earl of Morton. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/det
2 CONC ails.aspx?reference=GD29%2f1352&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=robert+douglas&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Bruce family of Kinross (Kinross House Papers), reference GD29/1352]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 February 1655: Obligation by Sir Robert Douglas of Blakerstoune to infeft Mr. Robert Sinclair of Longformacus and his spouse, Elizabeth Douglas, daughter of the granter, in the lands of Hairhead and others in sheriffdom of B
2 CONC ervick in terms of their marriage contract, 10 December 1647, etc. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH9%2f17%2f67&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=blakerstoune&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y Nati
2 CONC onal Records of Scotland, Miscellaneous Documents, reference RH9/17/67]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 November 1660: Commissions to Commissioners to Parliament - Berwick. John Home of Plandergaist; Sir Robert Dowglas of Blaikerstoun. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=PA7%2f25%2f6&
2 CONC st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=blaikerstoun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Supplementary Warrants and Parliamentary Papers, reference PA7/25/6]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 December 1667: Remission in favour of William, Master of Ramsay, of any complicity in killing of Sir James Home of Eccles, following declaration by William Douglas, son of deceased Sir Robert Douglas of Blackerstoun, Kt., sh
2 CONC ortly before his death that said Master of Ramsay, although in company, had no concern therein. [Not in R.M.S.; fragment of seal on tag.] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f65%2f7&
