1 TITL V
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN BUCHANAN OF AUCHMAR ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 March 1663: Contract between John Buchanan of that ilk and Patrick Buchanan of Auchmar and John Buchanan, fiar thereof, whereby both parties grant liberty and privilege to one another, their heirs and successors, to win and 
2 CONC carry away limestone out of any of their lands under certain provisions mentioned. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fE%2f2%2f5%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Patrick+Buchana
2 CONC n+of+Auchmar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/E/2/5/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 June 1678: Feu contract by Mungo Haldane of Gleneagles, with consent of John Haldane, his eldest son, in favour of John Buchanan of Auchmar, his heirs and assignees, of the 20 shilling lands of Calleden lying in the parish o
2 CONC f Inchcailloch, barony of Haldane and sheriffdom of Stirling and by annexation in the sheriffdom of Perth to be held of Mungo Haldane for payment of 5 merks scots feu duty yearly. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecata
2 CONC logue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f2%2f3%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=a&r=GD220%2f1%2fF%2f2%2f3%2f2&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments
2 CONC ), reference GD220/1/F/2/3/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 November 1682: Charter of resignation by James, Marquess of Montrose in favour of John Buchanan in liferent and William Buchanan in fee of the town and lands of Achingyle, to be held feu for payment of 10 merks feu duty year
2 CONC ly, but reserving the Croman Meadow with the pasturage belonging to the pendicles of Ballomaha [Balmaha] and Gartcay, and free ish and entry to the tenants of Gartfairn for watering their cattle in Loch Lomond as is the custom. [h
2 CONC ttps://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fL%2f2%2f1%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+buchanan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1680&dt=1750&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graha
2 CONC m Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/L/2/1/3]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 November 1682: Obligation by James, Marquess of Montrose to dispone in favour of John and William Buchanan, their heirs etc. all right he had or should acquire to the teinds of the lands of Achingyle, to be possessed by them
2 CONC  in the same manner and as freely as he should obtain them. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fL%2f2%2f1%2f5&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+buchanan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1680&
2 CONC dt=1750&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/L/2/1/5]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 November 1692: Instrument of resignation by John Buchanan in the hands of James, Marquess of Montrose as superior thereof in favour of John Buchanan himself in liferent and William Buchanan, his son, in fee, of the town and 
2 CONC lands of Achingyle, teinds and pertinents of the same. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fL%2f2%2f1%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+buchanan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1680&dt=17
2 CONC 50&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/L/2/1/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 January - 9 February 1693: Instrument of sasine following on precept contained in charter of resignation by James, Marquess of Montrose in favour of John Buchanan in liferent and William Buchanan in fee of the town and lands
2 CONC  of Achingyle (GD220/1/L/2/1/3). Dated 29 Jan and registered at Stirling, 9 Feb 1693. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fL%2f2%2f1%2f4&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+buch
2 CONC anan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1680&dt=1750&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/L/2/1/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''21 January 1697: Extract submission and decreet arbitral between James, Marquess of Montrose and John Buchanan of Auchmar whereby they submit their differences to the decision of Mr William Cochrane of Kilmaronock, mutual arbit
2 CONC er. He decerns John Buchanan of Auchmar and William Buchanan, his son, to pay the Marquess 10 merks yearly feu duty for his lands of Auchingyle for previous years unpaid and in time coming. He finds that neither Auchmar nor his te
2 CONC nants have any right to the Muir of Buchanan above the head dyke as belonging to the lands of Auchingyle. He finds the land on the west of Auchmar, between Auchmar and Arrochymore (bounds particularly described), to be held in com
2 CONC mon between the possessors of Auchmar and Arrochymore. He finds that the tenants of Gartincaber, Gartfarn and Gartbane have been in possession of the muir on the east side of Auchmar called Calleden as part of the common muir of B
2 CONC uchanan and that neither John Buchanan nor his son have any right to it, and should denude themselves of any right they have, or pretend to have, to the lands of Calleden, in favour of the Marquess. The submission is dated 21 and 
2 CONC 23 Jan, the decreet arbitral is dated 11 Oct 1697. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fH%2f6%2f4%2f2&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Buchanan+of+Auchmar&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&d
2 CONC i=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/H/6/4/2]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 May 1697: Contract and agreement between John and William Buchanan elder and younger of Auchmar on the one part, and John Buchanan of Arnprior and Mr Robert Buchanan, advocate, his son, on the other part, that the tenants an
2 CONC d possessors of Bollomaha [Balmaha] belonging to Arnprior shall have eight soums grass upon the lands of Auchengyle belonging to Auchmar, four younger ones to be pastured with the milk cows of Auchengyle upon the infield grass and
2 CONC  the rest to be pastured in the common muir. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD220%2f1%2fK%2f2%2f4%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+buchanan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1680&dt=1750&di=n Na
2 CONC tional Records of Scotland, Papers of the Graham Family, Dukes of Montrose (Montrose Muniments), reference GD220/1/K/2/4/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/historicalgeneal1820buch/page/135/mode/1up Essay upon the Family and Surname of Buchanan. By William Buchanan of Auchmar. (First published in the year 1723) (Glasgow, Printed for J. Wylie & Co., 1
2 CONC 820), 276 pp.] [https://archive.org/details/historicalgeneal1820buch/page/184/mode/1up For the family of Buchanan of Auchmar see pp. 184-92]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/stream/strathendrickits00smit#page/n12/mode/1up Strathendrick and Its Inhabitants from Early Times: An Account of the Parishes of Fintry, Balfron, Killearn, Drymen, Buchanan, and Kilmaronock. By John Guth
2 CONC rie Smith, FSA. Scot. (J. Maclehose and sons, Glasgow, 1896) 410 pages including index] [https://archive.org/details/strathendrickits00smit/page/373/mode/1up For Buchanan of Auchmar see pp. 373-6]'''
