2 CONT Family 2	Margaret McAlester [MacAlister],   d. Feb 1692  Married	Y  [1, 4]  Children 	 +	1. Hector MacNeil, of Lossit,   d. Yes, date unknown +	2. Mary MacNeil,   d. Yes, date unknown +	3. Isabel MacNeil,   d. Yes, date unknown +	
2 CONC 4. Neil Oig McNeill, of Macrihanish and Aros,   d. Aft 1728 +	5. Margaret MacNeil,   d. Yes, date unknown +	6. Annabelle McNeil [MacNeil],   d. Yes, date unknown +	7. Malcolm McNeill, of Ballymascanlon,   b. 1668,   d. 28 Jun 1731
2 CONC   (Age 63 years) Last Modified	24 Aug 2015 14:03:00  Family ID	F15046 	Group Sheet  |  Family Chart
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes 	 1 - Lauchlan McNeill Buidhe of Tirfergus, founder of the families of Ugadale and Lossit Hector MacNeill, 1746— 1818, poet and author distinguished by an entry in the Dictionary of Rational Biography, is one of at least eig
2 CONC ht MacNeills in that August company who were descended from Lachlan MacBeill Buidhe of Tirfergus.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 - He sleeps in the ancient Kirkyard of Kilkivan four miles west of Campbeltown close to the lands of Tirfergus and Losset which he acquired and bequeathed respectively to John his oldest son by his first marriage and Hector the 
2 CONC oldest son by his second marriage. Kilkivan dominates the fertile plain of the Laggan and beyond it can be seen the Island of Gigha all former holdings of his ancestors. [ http://www.kintyremag.co.uk/1998/22/page4.html ]
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 - Lachlan McNeill m (1) Mary McNeill of Colonsay. He m. (2) Margaret McAllister and had 8 sons and three daus. It is said that at least four of his sons settled in Northern Ireland. [ http://genforum.genealogy.com/macaulay/messa
2 CONC ges/820.html ]
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 - Lachlan Macneill Buie of Tirfergus (1611-1695) an elder of the Highland Church must have been a very remarkable man. He was the son, presumably, of Neil Buie McNeill . Lachlan seems to have escaped completely unscathed from th
2 CONC e dynastic and religious wars which devastated Kintyre during most of his life. By his first marriage with Mary McNeill of Carskiey. [http://generation13.net/Kintyremull/Annabelle/AnnabellaEdinburgh.htm]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 	 [S6] Stirnet Genealogy, Peter Barns-Graham, MacNeil02.
