2 CONT '''7 April 1640: Charter by Donald McLauchlane, captain of Insedonnell, and Colin McLauchlane, his lawful first born son and heir apparent, in implement of their part in a contract of marriage made 3 March last between them and  S
2 CONC ir Dugald Campbell of Auchinbreck, knight, bart., for himself and Moir Campbell, his natural daughter, giving said Moir Campbell in liferent the 20 shilling land of Couldconnell, the 16 shilling and 8 penny land of Dupenni alias B
2 CONC allegowne, the 3 merk land of Ereden, and 2½ merk land of Camismachgawine, in barony of Lochawe in sheriffdom of Argyll, in full satisfaction of all her third part as relict spouse of said Colin after his decease, with precept of 
2 CONC sasine directed to John Campbell of Orgaig, baillie in that part to said Donald and Colin. Written by Donald Camerone, servitor to George Campbell, sheriff clerk of Argyll At Inversary Witnesses:- George Campbell and Donald Camero
2 CONC ne, Alexander Campbell and Patrick Denneistoune, also servitors to said George Campbell. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD437%2f148&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=moir+campbell&ko=p&r=&ro
2 CONC =s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, MacNeill of Taynish and Campbell of Danna Titles, reference GD437/148]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 June 1666: Extract Registered Disposition by Archibald, Earl of Argyll in favor of Colin McLauchlane, Captain of Innischonnel in liferent and Lachlan MacLachlan, his son in fee. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlineca
2 CONC talogue/details.aspx?reference=GD43%2f33%2f34&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Colin+McLauchlane&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Title deeds of Malcolm Family of Poltalloch, reference GD43/33/34]'''
