1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  
2 CONT
2 CONT Hector Roy MacLean received a charter in 1642 for the lands of Coll, Rum, Muck, and two-thirds of Ouinish. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A supporter of the royalist cause during the civil wars, he fought at the Battle of Inverlochy and may also have been present at the Battle of Inverkeithing. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Financial difficulties later led to legal action, and in 1655 a court at Inveraray found that George Campbell of Kinnochtrie held a substantial claim against him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1656 Oliver Cromwell granted the Coll lands to the Campbell Clan in settlement of the debt, although the property was later restored to the MacLean family after the Restoration under Charles II. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marion MacLean, eldest daughter of Hector MacLean of Killean (later second of Torloisk), their marriage contract being dated 22 January 1641 at Tiree. They had six children.
2 CONT
2 CONT #Lachlan MacLean who succeeded to Coll in 1661.
2 CONT #Catherine MacLean
2 CONT #Janet MacLean
2 CONT #Margaret MacLean
2 CONT #Una MacLean
2 CONT #Donald MacLean born in 1656 on the Isle of Coll.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hector Roy died in 1676, predeceasing his father, John Garbh MacLean.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
