2 CONT "<strong>Sir Dugald Campbell, Baronet [S 1628] of Auchinbreck</strong>, son and heir by second wife; succeeded to the Baronetcy in 1645, as also to the command of his father's regiment in Ireland, receiving 10,000 merks in recogni
2 CONC tion of his late father's service. He, however, resigned his command and declared for the King. He was M.P. [S] for Argyllshire, 1649. He died unmarried soon after the Restoration."
2 CONT
