1 NAME George /Maxwell of Newark/
2 GIVN George
2 SURN Maxwell of Newark
2 _MARNM Maxwell of Newark
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE MAY 1683
1 OCCU
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR GEORGE MAXWELL OF NEWARK ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir George Maxwell of Newark, here treated, is the eldest son of https://www.geni.com/people/Patrick-Maxwell-of-Newark/6000000002116164996?through=6000000054014173909. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgo
2 CONC w, Testament Dative of Sir Patrick Maxwell of Newark, reference CC9/7/43 page 262]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Burgess of Glasgow ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir George Maxwell, the laird of Newark, younger, was enrolled as a burgess and guild brother of the burgh of Glasgow, on 1 April 1668. The town council admitted him "gratis for good reasons known to the magistrates and Dean of
2 CONC  Guild." [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso43scotuoft#page/181/mode/1up Burgesses and Guild Brethren of Glasgow,, 1573-1750, p. 181]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Death of his Father ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Patrick Maxwell of Newark died intestate in June 1678. Sir George Maxwell of Newark, his eldest son, gave up his father's testament dative and the inventory of his goods and gear. Among the debts owed by Sir Patrick was one
2 CONC  thousand, six hundred and sixty-six pounds, thirteen shillings and four pence, owed to his daughters Margaret and Jean. Confirmation was granted to Sir George Maxwell of Newark on 17 January 1679.  [National Records of Scotland, 
2 CONC Commissary Records of Glasgow, Testament Dative of Sir Patrick Maxwell of Newark, reference CC9/7/43 f.262]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir George Maxwell of Newark died in May 1683. [National Records of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, Testament Dative of Sir George Maxwell of Newark, reference CC9/7/46 ff. 159-61]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                    1
2 CONT
2 CONT 21 June 1660: Letter from  George Maxwell, Paris, to his father, the laird of Newark.  [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD190%2f3%2f81&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=george+maxwell&ko=p&r=&
2 CONC ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Smythe Family of Methven, Perthshire, reference GD190/3/81]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 February - 4 March [1665]: Extract obligation by '''Sir George Maxwell fiar of Newark,''' Adam Muschet, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, John Smollet, dean of guild of Dumbarton, and others to Alexander, Earl of Glencairne, son a
2 CONC nd heir of deceased William, Earl of Glencairne, for 37,000 merks in consideration of assignation of gift under the Great Seal, 17 August 1661, for prosecution of usurers, etc. (R.M.S. 1660-1668, no.118). Registered B.C.S., 9 Janu
2 CONC ary 1667 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f462%2f3&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=newark&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Title Deeds of the Earl of Glencairn, r
2 CONC eference GD1/462/3]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 January 1668: Letters of horning Alexander Earl of Glencairn against '''Sir George Maxwell fiar of Newark,''' George Muschet of Craighead, Nicol Bontin of Ardoch, Francis Sempill of Beltrees, Mr James Cunningham sheriff depute o
2 CONC f Ayr, William Cunningham Writer in Edinburgh and John Smollett dean of guild of Dumbarton for not payment making of their respective proportions of 37,000 merks due by them to the Earl at Whitsunday 1666 each of them according to
2 CONC  the division therein mentioned all contained in and due by their obligation to the Earl dated the 10 and 11 February 16[ ]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f311&st=1&tc=y&tl
2 CONC =n&tn=n&tp=n&k=newark&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/311]
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT 27 February 1672: Bill of suspension for John Smollett bailie of Dumbarton of letters of horning against him at the instance of John Earl of Glencairn for not making payment to the Earl of £14,306.1.4 contained in and due by a dec
2 CONC reet obtained by the Earl agt. the said John Smollet, '''Sir George Maxwell fiar of Newark'''  Mr James Cunningham sheriff depute of Ayr, George Muschet of Craighead, James Stirling at the Mill of Keir, Francis Freeland of that Il
2 CONC k, Mr William Cunningham Writer in Edinburgh and James Lockhart one of His Majesty's heralds. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f1%2f320&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=newark&ko=p&r=&r
2 CONC o=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/1/320]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Accounts===
2 CONT
