2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19-23 October 1648: Contract of marriage between David Kennedy, elder of Kirkemichell, Thomas Kennedy, his eldest son, and John Kennedy, eldest son of Thomas on the one part, and Sir Patrick Maxwell of Newwark and Isobel Maxwel
2 CONC l, his daughter, on the other part, for the marriage of the said John and Isobel; David and Thomas to infeft John and Isobel in the £20 lands of Knokdolian in the parish of Calmonell, and the said John in the £10 lands of Kirkemic
2 CONC hell and others in the parishes of Kirkmichell, Calmonell, etc. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD180%2f199&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Sir+Patrick+Maxwell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y Nat
2 CONC ional Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cathcart Family of Genoch and Knockdolian, reference GD180/199]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 December 1649: Ratification by David Kennedy of Kirkmichael to John Kennedy, his eye, of the provisions in No. 199, despite the death of Isobel Maxwell and non-payment of her tocher. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrson
2 CONC linecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD180%2f200&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=isobel+maxwell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cathcart Family of Genoch and Knockdolian, reference GD180/200]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 April 1651: Contract between Thomas Kennedy of Kirkmichell and John Kennedy, younger of Kirkmichell, his son, by which the said Thomas ratifies the infeftment by umquhile David Kennedy of Kirkmichell, his father, and him to 
2 CONC the said John in the contract of marriage between the said John and umquhile Isabel Maxwell, daughter of Sir Patrick Maxwell of Newwark, (she having died within a year and a day of the marriage) of the £20 lands of Knokdolian with
2 CONC  the salmon fishing in the water of Stinhiar in the parish of Colmonell, the £10 lands of Kirkmichell in the parish thereof, 5 mark lands of Barbour, 20/- lands of Kirkland of Kirkmichell, 5 mark lands of Altiquine in the parish o
2 CONC f Mayboll, £4 lands of Carrikmoore in parish of Colmonell, 10 mark lands of Schallochen, 50/- lands of Clashlochen and Ballirasie in the parish of Kirkcubrycht Innertig, superiority of 40/- lands of Auchinflour, 6 1/2 mark lands o
2 CONC f Schalloch, in the same parish, superiority of 40/- lands of Knokbreks in the parish of Colmonell, superiority of £5 lands of Glenmuk in the parish of Girvan, and superiority of the mark land of Litle Schallochen in the parish of
2 CONC  Kirkcudbrycht; the said John making certain financial provisions to the said Thomas, and to Thomas and Janet Kennedie, other children of the said Thomas. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?referen
2 CONC ce=GD180%2f42&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Sir+Patrick+Maxwell&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cathcart Family of Genoch and Knockdolian, reference GD180/42]'''
