1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===MARGARET MAXWELL===
2 CONT
2 CONT Margret Maxwell is the daughter of Sir Patrick Maxwell of Newark. She is not mentioned in the Clan MacFarlane account of the family [http://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I2536&tree=CC
2 CONC  Clan MacFarlane and associated clans genealogy]  At the time of his death in June 1678, her father owed Margaret and her sister Jean one thousand, six hundred and sixty-six pounds, thirteen shillings and four pence. [[National Re
2 CONC cords of Scotland, Commissary Records of Glasgow, Testament Dative of Sir Patrick Maxwell of Newark, reference CC9/7/43 page 262]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Death of her Father ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Patrick Maxwell of Newark died intestate in June 1678. Sir George Maxwell of Newark, his eldest son, gave up his father's testament dative and the inventory of his goods and gear. Among the debts owed by Sir Patrick was one
2 CONC  thousand, six hundred and sixty-six pounds, thirteen shillings and four pence, owed to his daughters Margaret and Jean. Confirmation was granted to Sir George Maxwell of Newark on 17 January 1679. [[National Records of Scotland, 
2 CONC Commissary Records of Glasgow, Testament Dative of Sir Patrick Maxwell of Newark, reference CC9/7/43 page 262]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Maxwell married Archibald Campbell, brother of Campbell of Arkinglass. A sasine in her name was registered on 26 August 1702. [https://archive.org/stream/indexes300scotuoft#page/578/mode/1up Index to the General Register 
2 CONC of Sasines, 1701-1720 (HMSO, Edinburgh, 1917), p. 578]
