2 CONC re, Scotland. [https://archive.org/stream/scottishrecordso41scotuoft#page/73/mode/1up Index to the Register of Marriages and Baptisms in the Parish of Kilbarchan, 1649-1772 (Scottish Record Society, Edinburgh, 1912), p. 73]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Death of his Father ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir Patrick Maxwell of Newark died intestate in June 1678. Sir George Maxwell of Newark, his eldest son, gave up his father's testament dative and the inventory of his goods and gear. Among the debts owed by Sir Patrick was one
2 CONC  thousand, six hundred and sixty-six pounds, thirteen shillings and four pence, owed to his daughters Margaret and Jean. Confirmation was granted to Sir George Maxwell of Newark on 17 January 1679.  [National Records of Scotland, 
2 CONC Commissary Records of Glasgow, Testament Dative of Sir Patrick Maxwell of Newark, reference CC9/7/43 f.262]'''
