2 CONT 19:52: Brian Bond added John (Campbell) Campbell IVth of Lochnell (abt.1592-1645) as father of Archibald Campbell (abt.1633-bef.1675). [Thank Brian for this]
2 CONT This page has been accessed 1,795 times.
2 CONT Preceded by
2 CONT Alexander Campbell 	4th of Lochnell
2 CONT 1635 - 1645 	Succeeded by
2 CONT Colin Campbell
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Roll of Honor
2 CONT John (Campbell) Campbell IVth of Lochnell was killed in Action during Wars of the Three Kingdoms at the Battle of Inverlochy.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was the son of Alexander Campbell, 3rd (laird) of Lochnell and Isabel MacDougall[1] and the 4th of Lochnell.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was Anne Campbell, daughter of Sir Dugald Campbell, 1st Baronet of Auchinbreck and Isabel Boyd.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Among their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT     Colin Campbell, 5th of Lochnell
2 CONT     Donald Campbell of Ardintallen (possible other maternity)
2 CONT     Margaret Campbell: : Donald, the fifth Invernahyle, was married to Margaret Campbell, daughter to the Laird of Lochness, and had issue fours sons and two daughters... [4] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT     "John Campbell, laird of Lochnell (1592 - 1645)." British Isles. Peerage, Baronetage, and Landed Gentry Families with Extended Lineage - FamilySearch PID I237727 - unable to locate - broken link is removed. 
2 CONT
