1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>John Stewart of Grandtully</strong>, the only son of Sir Thomas, held the family estates nearly thirty-two years. Never having been knighted like his ancestors, he was, when advanced in life, familiarly known as <em>Old G
2 CONC randtully</em>. The precise date of his birth has not been ascertained. But as his parents were married in the year 1627, and as he had entered as a student at the University of St. Andrews in the year 1663, it  may be assumed tha
2 CONC t he was born about the year 1643."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/redbookofgrandtu01fras#page/n149/mode/2up Red Book of Grandtully], William Fraser, 1868, page cxxviii
2 CONT
2 CONT "After enjoying the family estates from the death of his father in 1668, for a period of nearly thirty-two years, this laird of Grandtully died in February 1720, aged about seventy-seven years. He died in his mansion in Dundee."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/redbookofgrandtu01fras#page/n181/mode/2up Red Book of Grandtully], William Fraser, 1868, page clx
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT There is some discrepancy between materials as to whether to consider [http://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-Stewart/6000000017528262021 Alexander] first or second of Grandtully.  e.g. William Fraser identifies Alexander as second 
2 CONC of Grandtully ([http://archive.org/stream/redbookofgrandtu01fras#page/236/mode/2up Red Book of Grandtully]), while [http://www.redbookofscotland.com/Stewart%20of%20Grantully.html Red Book of Scotland - Stewart of Grantully] identi
2 CONC fies him as the first. For this purpose, have aligned to <em>Pedigree of the Family of Stewart of Grandtully</em> outlined in the above mentioned <em>Red Book of Grandtully</em>.
