1 TITL Lady
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lady Jean Alexander (b. 1606 - d. 1670), married first in 1623, Hugh Montgomery, the 2nd Viscount of the Ards (d. 1642) and second, Maj-Gen. Robert Munro, son of Obsdale Munro of Foulis; Jean, married, 3 August 162
2 CONC 3, in Kensington Church, to Hugh, afterwards second Viscount Montgomery of the Ards, Ireland. He died at Newtown, Ireland, 15 November 1642, and she married, secondly, as his second wife, Major-General Robert Munro, second son of 
2 CONC George Munro of Obsdale, and grandson of Robert Munro, fifteenth of Fowlis. He had a distinguished military career, and is supposed, together with Sir James Turner, to have afforded Scott a model for Dugald Dalgetty in the Legend 
2 CONC of Montrose. His wife died in 1670, but he survived for ten years or more, as he is mentioned as alive in 1680 in the will of Major William Buchanan of the Botown, Ireland. He had no issue by his second wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Hugh 1st Earl Mt Alexander Montgomery (1623 – 1663)
2 CONT # James Montgomery (1627 – 1689)
2 CONT # Elizabeth Montgomery (1634 – 1677) married William Montgomery of Rosemount
2 CONT # Henry DY Montgomery (1636 – 1638)
2 CONT # James Montgomery (1639 – 1689)
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional children seen without supporting evidence:
2 CONT # John Montgomery (1640 – 1689)
2 CONT # Joseph Montgomery (1645 – )
2 CONT # Samuel MONTGOMERY (1657 – 1703)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''MERGE CAUTION - from CLE - note: This Is the Correct Parentage and Marriage placement for this woman'''- Lady Jean Alexander, based on the source placed in her profile: parents: Sir William Alexander Lady Janet Erskine, Countes
2 CONC s of Stirling, of Balgownie
2 CONT
2 CONT No birth date has surfaced as of 12/18/2013, but we know she was the eldest daughter of Sir William and Lady Janet
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT *Chapter on Alexander Family from The Scots Peerage  Founded on Wood's ed. of Sir Robert Douglas's Peerage of Scotland, 1911 p165-185. ALEXANDER, EARL OF STIRLING page 165
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexanders_of_Menstrie “ Lady Jean Alexander, eldest daughter of the first Earl of Stirling, also settled in Ireland, and in 1623 married Hugh Montgomery, 2nd Viscount Montgomery. Their son, the 3rd
2 CONC  viscount, was created Earl of Mount Alexander in the Irish Peerage, in honour of his mother's family.”.
2 CONT * http://landedfamilies.blogspot.ca/2013/10/80-alexander-of-menstrie-earls-of.html
2 CONT * https://archive.org/stream/memorialsofearlo01rogeuoft#page/249/mode/1up
