1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LIEUTENANT-COLONEL JAMES ALEXANDER ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Lieutenant-Colonel in His Majesty's Foot Guards===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Bogus Genealogy'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08paul/page/180/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 180]
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://landedfamilies.blogspot.ca/2013/10/80-alexander-of-menstrie-earls-of.html The Landed Familes of Britain and Ireland]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == The Question of Identity ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lieutenant-Colonel James Alexander is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Alexander-1st-Earl-of-Stirling-7th-Baron-of-Menstrie/6000000007924997912?through=6000000010010080671 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/
2 CONC Janet-Erskine-Countess-of-Stirling/6000000007925106215?through=6000000010010080671 [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08paul/page/180/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 180]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death and Burial ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lieutenant-Colonel James Alexander died before 9 December 1671, the date upon which his body was interred in Greyfriars Burying-Ground in Edinburgh, Midlothiam, Scotland. [https://archive.org/details/registerinterme00socigoog/p
2 CONC age/n30/mode/1up Register of Interments in Greyfriars Burying-Ground, Edinburgh: 13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08paul/page/180/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 180]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun08paul/page/180/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VIII: 180]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Child of the Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Alexander/6000000024017789222?through=6000000010010080671
2 CONT
