1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ~ James Stewart ~
2 CONT
2 CONT James (3rd Earl of Moray) Stewart
2 CONT Birth: 1581 in Elgin, Dyke Darnaway, Moray, Scotland
2 CONT Death: 06 Aug 1638 _ in Darnaway Castle, Morayshire, Scotland
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~*
2 CONT PARENTS:
2 CONT
2 CONT Father:
2 CONT James Stewart (2nd Earl of Moray) "The Bonny Earl"
2 CONT Birth: 1565 in Islands, Orkney, , Scotland
2 CONT Death: 7 Feb 1592 in Avon, Gloucestershire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother:
2 CONT Elizabeth Stewart (2nd Countess of Moray)
2 CONT Birth: Aug 1565 in Edinburgh, Mid, Lothian, Scotland
2 CONT Death: 18 Nov 1591 in Scotland
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~*
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT Lady Anne Gordon Countess Hunt
2 CONT Birth: 1590 in Huntly, Aberdeenshire, Scotland
2 CONT Death: 1674 in Dyke, Moray, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~*
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN:
2 CONT
2 CONT James Stuart, 4th Earl of Moray Stewart
2 CONT Birth: 25 June 1608 in Dyke, Earldom of Moray Aberdeenshire, Scotland.
2 CONT Death: 4 March 1653 in Dyke, Earldom of Moray, Aberdeenshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~*
2 CONT
2 CONT James Stuart, 3rd Earl of Moray (1581 / 6 August 1638) was the son of James Stewart, 2nd Earl of Moray and Elizabeth Stuart, 2nd Countess of Moray.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lady Anne Gordon, daughter of George Gordon, 1st Marquess of Huntly and Lady Henrietta Stuart, on 2 October 1607 (contract). He inherited the title Earl of Moray when his father was murdered by his future father-in-law 
2 CONC in 1592. He was responsible for completing Castle Stuart on the banks of the Moray Firth.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1638 and his title passed to his son, James.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT James (Stewart) Third Earl of Moray is a member of Clan Stewart.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stewart-36060
2 CONT
2 CONT James Stewart was said to be born in 1582, although in July 1597 he was given as aged 10 years.[1] He was the son of James Stewart, 2nd Earl of Moray and his wife, Elizabeth Stuart, 2nd Countess of Moray.[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited his mother's title Earl of Moray when his father, the jure uxoris Earl of Moray was murdered by his future father-in-law in 1592. He was responsible for completing Castle Stuart on the banks of the Moray Firth.
2 CONT
2 CONT While still a minor he ignored a summons to attend the Privy Council and was denounced a rebel on March 16, 1601. On August 11, 1607 Parliament ratified various charters that had been granted to his grandfather, James Stewart, 1st
2 CONC  of Moray.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Anne Gorden. They had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT # James, 4th Earl of Moray.[5]. married Lady Margaret Home, 
2 CONT # George, died unmarried.[5]
2 CONT # Margaret, married James Grant of Freuchie.[5] AKA Mary. The Fraser/Grant database shows her as daughter of the 2nd Earl rather than the 3rd.
2 CONT
2 CONT James died on 16 Aug 1638 at Darnaway Castle, Moray, Scotland[5][6] and his title passed to his son, James. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His daughter Lady Henrietta Stuart married in 1662 Sir Hugh Campbell of Cawdor, elder (? - 11 March 1716), Knighted in 1660, and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
