1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 49.	Thomas Ross 1, 2, 3 (Mary Goodnow , Thomas Goodenow Goodnow , Thomas A , John ) was born 4 on 29 Sep 1660 in Sudbury, Middlesex, MA. He died 5 in 1718 in Lancaster, Worcester, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married 10, 11, 12 Anna Ann Rice 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9 before 1705. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * +	127	M	i	 Thomas Ross Jr was born about 1704. He died in 1786.
2 CONT * 128	F	ii	Hannah Ross was born 1 about 1706 in Sudbury, Middlesex, MA. Hannah married Josiah Bennett.
2 CONT * +	129	M	iii	 James Ross was born on 23 Oct 1711.
2 CONT * 130	F	iv	Lidiah Lydia Ross 1 was born 2, 3 on 12 Jul 1710 in Sudbury, Middlesex, MA. Lidiah married 2 Reuben Rugg 1 on 10 Mar 1730 in Lancaster, Worcester, MA.
2 CONT *+	131	M	v	 Timothy Ross was born on 20 Aug 1714.
2 CONT *+	132	F	vi	 Anna Ross was born on 23 Nov 1716. She died on 5 May 1746.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.goodenowfamily.org/pafn05.htm#8
2 CONT
2 CONT >In the Company from Sudbury in the Canada Expedition in 1690. Also Queen Anne's War; his house was burnt during the Indian attack on Lancaster in 1704. One of 99 Lancaster men who bought of the Indians that territory later known 
2 CONC as Sterling. From Ann B. Wohleber, 2003: With his brother, James, he took part in Sir William Phips' Expedition against Quebec in 1690. On 31 Jul 1704 his home at Lancaster, Worcester, MA was burned during an Indian raid.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.goodenowfamily.org/pafg05.htm#8
