1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JEAN KENNEDY===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A daughter of Major Thomas Kennedy of Baltersan married Hugh Kennedy of Ardmillan. Her name is not mentioned but her husband is noticed as Major Thomas's son-in-law on 17 February 1701. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrson
2 CONC linecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f8%2f1004&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=kennedy+of+ardmillan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1701&dt=&di=n NRS: GD25/8/1004]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 August 1687: Charter by Hugh Kennedy of Baltersan to Jean K., his spouse, following on contract. Glenluy, alias Glenluigh, bailiary of Crosregall in Carrick, sheriffdom of Ayr. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecat
2 CONC alogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f7%2f59&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hugh+kennedy+of+baltersan&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), r
2 CONC eference GD25/7/59]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: Ratification of the same on 23 August 1687 by Robert D., Bishop of Dunblane, commendator of the Abbacy of Crocereguall, superior.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 June 1699: Instrument of Sasine by Hugh Kennedy of Baltersan in favour of Jean K., his spouse, following on charter of 23 July 1687. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f7%2f68&
2 CONC st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hugh+kennedy+of+baltersan&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1600&dt=1700&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/7/68]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: (Regd. G.R.S., 58.195: 1688, August 1). Easter Dunevens and Mochrumhill, parish of Croseregall, sheriffdom of Ayr.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 February 1701: Case for Sir John Kennedy of Cullean as against Hugh Arburthnot, gentleman, and as examined by Robert Raymond, Lincoln's Inn, re title to certain lands, following upon grant of the same by Sir Alexander Kenned
2 CONC ay of Cullean to Major K., his second son, citing disposition of 17 February 1701 by Hew Kennedy of Ardmillan and Baltersan, son-in-law of the said Major, to John, his son, whom failing, to the above Sir John, and narrating subseq
2 CONC uent claim of the said Hew Arburthnot [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD25%2f8%2f1004&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=kennedy+of+ardmillan&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1701&dt=&di=n National Records of 
2 CONC Scotland, Papers of the Kennedy Family, Earls of Cassillis (Ailsa Muniments), reference GD25/8/1004]'''
2 CONT
