1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From:  My Southern Family, by Hiram Kennedy Douglass, available at: http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~lelandva/kenneintro.html
2 CONT
2 CONT This book follows the family in Scotland back to Duncan de Carrick, born circa 1200.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~lelandva/kenne017.htm#id4045
2 CONT
2 CONT 24. Alexander17 Kennedy (Alexander16, Alexander15, Thomas14, Gilbert13, Gilbert12, David11, John10, Gilbert9, James8, Gilbert7, John6, Gilbert5de Carrick, Gilbert4, Roland3, Nicol,2, Duncan1) was born circa 1687 Scotland.110 
2 CONT
2 CONT "This brings us to our ancestor who left Scotland for Ireland.  David Kennedy (1768-1837) wrote in his Bible which has come down to me a short sketch of his family, starting with his great grandfather, Alexander who left Scotland,
2 CONC  so the next five generations are from his Bible. Here is what he wrote: 
2 CONT
2 CONT " David Kennedy's small sketch of the history of the family he sprang from, with that of his wife, Joanna: my great grandfather was from Scotland by the name of Alexander. He fled from that country in the time of the great rebelli
2 CONC on (that would be the rebellion of 1715 in protest over bringing George I to the throne rather than the Stuart Pretender) to Ireland.  There John Kennedy, my grandfather was raised and married and had three sons and four daughters
2 CONC ; the daughters names are forgotten but the sons were Robert, John and Alexander.  Robert was drowned at sea.  John died near Philadelphia and left a son by the name John.  Alexander, my father was married in Philadelphia, where h
2 CONC is wife died; he then married my mother, Mary Thomas in Maryland.  She was born and raised in London and married John Thomas and had two children, Thomas and Jane all of whom died.  Her maiden name was Tanday.  My father had by he
2 CONC r Nancy, John, David, Mary and Alexander.  She died when I was small.  My father then married the Widow Lavin and by her had George, Annie, Joseph, Robert, Nathan and Esther.  The family of my wife Joanna, as follows:  Her father'
2 CONC s name was Edward Moore of Welsh descent; her mother's name was Martha Thomson, both raised in the Jerseys.  Their children were as follows: Susan, Salley, Mary, William, Elizabeth, John, Thomas, Martha, Joanna and Edward."
2 CONT
2 CONT This short sketch of my great grandfather and the data on births, marriages and deaths which follow have been a great help to me in establishing my Kennedy lineage. My "supreme court" in this country, Dr. Arthur Adams and John Kev
2 CONC an mcDowall of Glasgow both agree that the connection seems to them proper; that Alexander kennedy, son of Alexander of Craigoch and Kilhenzie was the Alexander who left Scotland, great grandfather of David. The genealogical autho
2 CONC rities in Edinburgh know nothing about what happened to Alexander Kennedy; but in Scotland they lose interest in a man when he departs for Ireland !111 He emigrated in 1715 from Ireland; left with his family when Bonnie Prince Cha
2 CONC rlie attempted with French aid to restore the Stuarts to the throne of Britain.112
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Alexander17 Kennedy and an unknown spouse were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT •	27. i. John18, b. circa 1710 Scotland.
