3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Teller V. A. Van Ness  by  Stefan Bielinski
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Teller was the daughter of New Netherland pioneers Willem and Margaret Donchasen Teller. She probably was born during the 1640s.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her first husband was Beverwyck and Albany trader Pieter Van Allen. The marriage produced several children before his death in 1674. In 1676, she was a widow and was called "Maria Lookermans." At that time, she was petitioning the
2 CONC  Albany court to prosecute her late husband's debtors on her behalf.
2 CONT
2 CONT In February 1677, she married (maybe for the third time) Gerrit Van Ness after signing a pre-nuptual agreement protecting her widow's holdings. Over the next decade, she appears to have given birth to a number of Van Ness children
2 CONC  who were baptized in the Albany Dutch church where she was a member. These Van Nesses were Albany residents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Teller Van Allen Loockermans Van Ness was dead by March 1715 when Gerrit Van Ness filed his will. That instrument superceded a joint will probabaly filed after 1708 - when she still would have been alive. Her son, Willem Van
2 CONC  Allen, was a prominent Albany resident.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.nysm.nysed.gov/albany/bios/t/mateller6616.html
2 CONT
