1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun07pauluoft/page/387/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VII: 387]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir William Cuninghame, Baronet [S 1627] of Cuninghamhead</strong>, only son and heir by 1st wife; succeeded to the Baronetcy June 1640, and had the gift, <em>gratis</em>, of his own ward and marriage, on account of his f
2 CONC aher's death in service of the State. On 12 May 1642, he had special service to his father; was Colonel and a member of the Committee of Estates, 1649. He was M.P. [S] for Ayrshire, 1648-49 and 1650; was a great Anti-Episcopalian,
2 CONC  and in 1661 was fined £4,800; committed to prison in September 1662, and was not finally discharged till 1669. He married in August 1661, Ann, 1st daughter of Thomas (Ruthven), 1st Lord Ruthven of Freeland [S], by Isabel, daughte
2 CONC r of Robert (Balfour, formerly Arnot), 2nd Lord Balfour of Burleigh [S]. He died 1670. His widow married William Cuninghame of Craigends, and died about 1669, when her son was served her heir."
2 CONT
