1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===HELEN EDMONSTONE===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Helen Edmonstone is the daughter of Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath and his wife Dame Jean Hamlton.[https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/48/mode/1up Edmonstone of Duntreath, p. 48]''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Helen Edmonstone married Thomas Niven of Monkredding. [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/48/mode/1up Edmonstone of Duntreath, p. 48]''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Nevin-of-Monkredding/6000000075117047821?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1517341836944&through=6000000074994448876
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/William-Nevin-of-Monkredding/6000000075048955285?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1517342022919&through=6000000074994448876
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogical Account===
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/n8/mode/1up Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet, Genealogical Account of the Family of Edmonstone of Duntreath (Printed Privately, Edinburgh, MDCCCLXXV.), 9
2 CONC 5 pp.]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/stream/historycountyay00pategoog#page/n8/mode/1up James Paterson History of the County of Ayr with a Genealogical Account of the Families of Ayrshire, Vol. II. (Thomas George Stevenson, Edinburgh, M.DCCC.
2 CONC LII.), 525 pp See pp. 253-55 for the family of Nevin of Monkredding]'''
