1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Ballymena Castle, Antrim
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1626 William Adair acquired newly-settled lands at Ballymena in exchange for part of his patrimony in Wigtownshire, and his son, Sir Robert, built the castle as a centre for the new estate.  The original building burned down in
2 CONC  1740 and was at best patched up afterwards. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://landedfamilies.blogspot.com/2013/04/23-adair-of-ballymena-castle-and.html?m=1
2 CONT
2 CONT William Adair (d. 1661) of Ballymena and Kinhilt.  Eldest son of Sir Robert Adair (d. 1655) and his wife Jane, daughter of William Edmondstone of Duntreath (Stirlingshire).  He married c.1658 Anne Helena (who married second, Archi
2 CONC bald Edmondstone of Braid Island (Antrim) and d. c.1710), daughter of Col. Walter Scott of Hartwoodburn, and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Col. Sir Robert Adair (1659-1745), kt. (q.v.).
2 CONT
2 CONT He inherited the Ballymena and Kinhilt estates from his father in 1655.
2 CONT He died 30 November 1661.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Andrew Agnew, The Agnews of Lochnaw: A History of the Hereditary Sheriffs of Galloway (Edinburgh: Adam and Charles Black, 1864), p. 617, digital images, [https://books.google.com/books?id=zF4BAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA617 GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT >10. William Adair, succeeded 1655, married, first, Jean, daughter of Sir William Cunningham of Cunninghamhead; married, second, Anne, daughter of Colonel Walter Scott; by her he had
2 CONT
2 CONT >11. Sir Robert Adair of Kilhilt and Ballymena, a knight banneret, sold the baronies of Kilhilt and Drumore to the Earl of Stair; married, 1st, Penelope, daughter of Sir Robert Colvile; married, 2d, Martha—died August 1705; marrie
2 CONC d, 3d, October 1705, Ann M'Aulay; married, 4th, Arabella Rickets; left by his third wife ...
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * “Genealogical account of the family of Edmonstone of Duntreath”. Author: Edmonstone, Archibald, Sir, 1795-1871. cn. Page 52.  [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/52/mode/1up Archive.Org]:  “Archibald Edmons
2 CONC tone of Duntreath married Anna Helena Scott, daughter of Col. Walter Scott of Harwood, and widow of Sir William Adair of Kilshilt, by whom he had four sons and five daughters ...”
2 CONT * “Burke's Genealogical and Heraldic History of Peerage, Baronetage and Knightage.” (1914) Page 68.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=RVggAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA68&ots=2Dfx0yscvJ&dq=Col.%20Walter%20Scott%2C%20of%20Hartwoodburn&pg=PA68#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=Col.%20Walter%20Scott,%20of%20Hartwoodburn&f=true GoogleBooks] “Adair.”
2 CONT * https://landedfamilies.blogspot.com/2013/04/23-adair-of-ballymena-castle-and.html?m=1
2 CONT * https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I50135&tree=CC
2 CONT * https://www.ancestry.com/boards/surnames.adair/723.2.1.1.1.1/mb.ashx CALENDAR OF STATE PAPERS relating to Ireland AD1660-1662. page 482. “30 December 1661. at Whitehall, London, England. The King to the (Master of the Wards) for
2 CONC  Francis GODOLPHIN. Directing that he have wardship of Robert Adare (Adair), son and heir of the late William Adare of Ballymanagh (Ballymena), county Antrim, Ireland. P.1/4. State Papers, Domestic. Signet Office V. p.102.”
