2 DATE 1675
2 ADDR
3 CITY Belfast
3 CTRY Northern Ireland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Share some things about....................
2 CONT
2 CONT Joan Adair is your 10th great grandmother.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Patrick Adair (1625?–1694) was an Irish presbyterian minister, notable for his part in negotiations with government for religious liberty and settlement through his career.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married:
2 CONT
2 CONT * first, in 1650, if not slightly earlier, to Margaret, daughter of the Rev. Robert Cunningham of Holywood
2 CONT *second, his cousin Jean (died 1675), second daughter of Sir Robert Adair of Ballymena;
2 CONT *third, a widow, Elizabeth Anderson (née Martin)
2 CONT
2 CONT He left four sons:
2 CONT *William (ordained at Ballyeaston 1681, removed to Antrim 1690, and died 1698),  (son of his first wife)
2 CONT *Archibald, 
2 CONT *Alexander, and 
2 CONT *Patrick (minister at Carrickfergus, died June 1717
2 CONT
2 CONT and a daughter 
2 CONT *Helen
2 CONT
2 CONT By which wife Patrick Adair had his second, third and fourth sons, and his only daughter, we do not know. Possibly they were all born at Cairncastle, for Adair was fifty years of age when he relinquished his charge there.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT From “ William Adair (d.1626) m. Catherine Kirchart”
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/boards/thread.aspx?mv=flat&m=723&p=surnames.adair
2 CONT
2 CONT In a book on the County of Suffolk, England, vol. 1 by Suckling 1846 there appears a chart for the family of Adair (which may or may not be correct)
2 CONT
2 CONT William Adair married Catherine KIRCHART. William and Catherine Kirchart had children :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sir Robert Adair was made a denizen of Ireland with his father 1624, served heir to his father and grandfather in the Scottish Estates, Feb. 19 1629. Was made Knight c 1648. Had livery of his Irish estates Dec. 2 1628, made his
2 CONC  will Feb 15 1655. Died March 1, 1625. Married Jane, dau. of Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Robert and Jane had children :
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. William Adair d. Nov. 30, 1661 m. Anna Helena Scott.
2 CONT * 2. Archibald Adair of Litter, Queen's co. had son William of Litter, Queens co, Ireland.
2 CONT * 3. Alexander Adair, 3rd son.
2 CONT * 4. Robert Adair, 4th son
2 CONT * 5. Isabella, wife of Robert Macdowall of Logan in the shire of Wigton in Scotland
2 CONT * 6. Joan, wife of (Rev.) Patrick Adair
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_Adair
2 CONT * https://antrimhistory.net/patrick-adair-of-cairncastle/
