1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===WILLIAM EDMONSTONE OF BROICH===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Edmonstone of Broich is the son of John Edmonstone of Broich. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f1067%2f10&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmonstone+of+broich&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df
2 CONC =&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD1/1067/10]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1664 William Edmonstone, the son of William Edmonstone of Broich, here treated, complained to the Privy Council of Scotland about the behaviour of Archibald Edmonstone of Harlehaven and his son James Edmonstone, who had brok
2 CONC en into his father's house of Broich, and carried away some of his property. The Privy Council found in favour of William, and, by an act dated 14 July 1664 ordered Archibald and James Edmonstone to quit the house and restore the 
2 CONC property belonging to William Edmonstone, elder. [https://archive.org/details/parishofstrathbl00smit/page/96/mode/1up Strathblane: 96]''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It is by no means certain but it is possible that he is the man of the same name who acquired certain lands in the County of Antrim in Ireland in 1625. [https://archive.org/details/calendarpatenta00offigoog/page/n85/mode/1up Ir
2 CONC eland: 77]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===An Account of the Edmonstone Family===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''‘The seventh Laird of Duntreth called, William Edmonston, married Issobel Hadden, Daughter to the Laird of Glennegies, and had by her five Sons and two Daughters, . . . . . . . . . . John Edmonston third Son to said William Edm
2 CONC onston of Duntreth, married Eliz. Edmonston, Daughter to John Edmonston of Broich, and got with her both the Lands of Broich in Scotland, and the Lands of Bellibantro in Ireland; and had by her four Sons and five Daughters; Willia
2 CONC m his Eldest Son, James his second Son, Robert his third Son, and [blank space] Edmonston his fourth Son: His eldest Daughter called Issobel, married to Crawfurd of Walston, and had issue; his second Daughter called, Jean; his thi
2 CONC rd; his fourth Helen; and his fifth Agnes, married to Andrew Adair, and had issue. Secondly the said John Edmonston married Catherine Cunningham, of the family of Glengarnock, and had by her five Sons and two Daughters: The Eldest
2 CONC  Son called Archibald; the second John; the third Son James; the fourth son Robert; the fifth Son Alexander: His Eldest Daughter called, Katherine, and Anna his second Daughter. William Edmonston Eldest Son of the said John Edmons
2 CONC ton by his first Wife, married Jean Buchanan, of the Family of Buchanan, and had by her six Sons and four Daughters; William, John, Archibald, Robert, James; his Daughters, Eliz. Mary Jean & Anna-Helena: James Edmonston the third 
2 CONC Son of the said John Edmonston by his second Wife, married Margaret Lindsay, Daughter to the Laird of Dow-hill in Fife, and had by her two Sons and five Daughters; John and Robert, Katherine, Anna-Helena, Margaret, Eliz, and Letti
2 CONC ce’ [https://drive.google.com/file/d/1n8MLsVdxL72BKPF67Ed_FBAwP0AyuReU/view Duntreth: pp. 13-4] Link supplied by Tamás Flinn Caldwell-Gilbert'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Patent and Close Rolls in Chancery in Ireland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 December 1625: Licence to Sir Faithful Fortescue to alienate certain lands in the county of Antrim to Willam Adare, William Edmonston, and William Houston : To hold one moiety thereof to the said William Adare, one-fourth pa
2 CONC rt to William Edmonston, and another fourth part to William Houston.  [https://archive.org/details/calendarpatenta00offigoog/page/n85/mode/1up Ireland: 77]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the Index to the Register of Deeds===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''16 June 1663: Dalrymple 8/796. Bond. William Edonstoune son of John E. of Broich. Granter. Archibald E. of Harlhevine. Grantee. [Scottish Record Office Index, Vol, III] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=60000001383886
2 CONC 07822& Image of Index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 December 1663: Mack 8/932. Bond and Assig. John Edmonstoune of Broich. Granter. William E, his son.  Granter.  Archibald E. of Harlhevine. Granter. Archibald E. his son. Granter. [Scottish Record Office Index, Vol, III] [htt
2 CONC ps://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138388607822& Image of Index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 December 1663: Mackenzie 9/933. Bond. William Edmonstoune son of John E. of Broich. Granter. Archibald E. of Harlhevine. Granter. [Scottish Record Office Index, Vol, III] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=600000013
2 CONC 8388607822& Image of Index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 December 1663: Mack 8/935. Bond and Assig. John Edmonstonue of Broich. Granter. William E. his son. Granter. Archibald E. of Harlhevine. Granter. Archibald E. his son. Granter. Scottish Record Office Index, Vol, III] [https:
2 CONC //www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138388607822& Image of Index]'''             
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''14 December 1663: Mack 8/948. Contract of Wadset. John Edmonstoune of Broich. Granter. William E. his son. Granter. Archibald E. of Harlhevine Granter. Archibald E. his son. Granter.Scottish Record Office Index, Vol, III] [http
2 CONC s://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138388607822& Image of Index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 December 1664: Dalrymple 12/901. Bond. William Edmonstone son of John E. of Broch. Grantee. [Scottish Record Office Index, Vol, III] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138544907823& Image of Index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 December 1665: Mackenzie 14/984. Bond. William Edmonstone son of John E. of Broch. Grantee. James E. son of Archibald E. of Ballewin. Granter. [Scottish Record Office Index, Vol, III] [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc
2 CONC _id=6000000138544495827& Image of Index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 October 1666: Mackenzie 17/120. Bond. William Edmonstoune son of John E. of Broych. Granter. James E. don of Archibald E. laird of Duntreath. Grantee. [Scottish Record Office Index, Vol, III] [https://www.geni.com/documents/v
2 CONC iew?doc_id=6000000138544045002& Image of Index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 December 1666: Mackenzie 17/503. Sub. And Dec. Arb. William Edmonstoune son of John E. of Broych. Principal Party. James E. son of Archibald E. laird of Duntreath. Grantee. [Scottish Record Office Index, Vol, III] [https://ww
2 CONC w.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138544045002& Image of Index]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 August 1668: Translation by Alexander Leckie of May to William Edmonstone of Broich, son of John Edmonstone of Broich, of a bond and assignation dated 1654, Aug 2 and 3, by the said John Edmonstone with James Leckie of May an
2 CONC d Archibald Edmonstone of Arlehaven as cautioners, to Row Gibb and John Hendrie, former treasurers and box masters for the poor of the burgh of Stirling, for 500 merks, assigned to said Alexander Leckie by John Christisen, merchan
2 CONC t and John Andersone, baxter burgess in Stirling, then treasurers and box masters for the poor of said burgh, by assignation dated 1656 Oct 29. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f10
2 CONC 67%2f10&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=edmonstone+of+broich&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Edmonstone of Broich, reference GD1/1067/10]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Printed Evidence===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/details/calendarpatenta00offigoog/page/n7/mode/1up Calendar of the Patent and Close Rolls of Chancery in Ireland, of the Reign of Charles the First. First to Eighth Year, Inclusive. By James Morrin, Clerk of E
2 CONC nrolments in Chancery. (HMSO., Dublin and London, 1863), 700 pp. including index]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/genealogicalacco00inedmo#page/n6/mode/1up Sir Archibald Edmonstone of Duntreath, Baronet, Genealogical Acoount of the Family of Edmonstone of Duntreath]
2 CONT # [https://archive.org/stream/parishofstrathbl00smit#page/n8/mode/1up John Guthrie Smith, FSA (Scot).,The Parish of Strathblane and its Inhabitants from Early Times : A Chapter of Lennox History (Glasgow : James Maclehose and Sons
2 CONC , 1886), 394 pp. including index. See pp.pp. 95-100 for Edmonstine of Ballewan and Spittal] 
