2 CONC heriffdom of Stirling, resigned by Walter Forester of Culmoir, the former owner : To be held - the said land, with mill, etc., - of the granter and his heirs, for the service of ward, relief, and marriage. Precept of Sasine direct
2 CONC ed to John Lenox of Blairinschogill, as bailie. Dated at Fintrie, 26th June 1627. Signed by the granter, Mr. Henry Livingstone, minister of Kippen, James Dog of Dunrobin, the said John Lenox, Thomas Buchanan of Wester Polder, and 
2 CONC George Buchanan, notary public. [2588, Box 66.] [https://archive.org/details/calendaroflaing00edin/page/478/mode/1up Laing Charters: 1993]'''
