2 CONT ===Her Father's Testament Dative===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The Testament Dative and Inventory of Mr. John Edmonstoun, sometime of Broiche, afterwards of Bailliebentrone in County Antrim, Ireland, was given up by his daughter Katherine Edmonstoun on 16 March 1721. At the time of his dea
2 CONC th, John Edmonstoun of Bailliebrentone was owed one thousand merks Scots money by his nephew, Archibald Edmonton of Duntreath.The Commissary Court of Edinburgh recognised Katherine as the only executor dative and nearest of kin to
2 CONC  her deceased father. Thereafter, John Edmonstoun, writer in Edinburgh, who identified himself as the eldest son of Mr. James Edmonstoun of Baillie Bentrione, acted himself as cautioner for Katherine Edmonstoun, and confirmation w
2 CONC as granted to her on 14 February 1721. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Mr. John Edmonstoun, sometime of Broich, thereafter of Bailliebentrone, Co. Antrim, Ireland, r
2 CONC eference CC8/8/87]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000138105855839& Image of Testament]'''
