1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ANNABEL STEWART===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Annabel Stewart is the daughter of Jogn Stewart of Blackhall, younger. [https://archive.org/stream/topographicaldes00robe#page/278/mode/1up Topographical Description of Ayrshire, p. 278]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Annabel Stewart married William Porterfield of that Ilk. [https://archive.org/stream/topographicaldes00robe#page/278/mode/1up Topographical Description of Ayrshire, p. 278] She is noticed as his widow on 25 April 1692. [http://
2 CONC catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f167&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=William+Porterfield+of+that+Ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD39/5/167]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence Published by the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 April 1692: Disposition by Alexander Porterfield of that Ilk, as heir to deceased John Porterfield of that Ilk, his grandfather, with consent of John, Earl of Glencairn, and them both, with consent of Sir John Maxwell of Net
2 CONC herpollock, Kt., Bart., Sir Archibald Stewart of Blackhall, Kt., Bart., Archibald Crawfurd of Auchenanes, James Hamilton of Aikenhead, James Stewart of Lumloch, Alexander Porterfield of Fullwood, Alexander Porterfield, indweller i
2 CONC n Paisley, Annabel Stewart, relict of William Porterfield of that Ilk, curators to said Alexander Porterfield, in favour of Mr John Cochrane of Ferguslie, of annual rent of £260 furth of lands and barony of Finlayston, formerly wa
2 CONC dset by the deceased William, Earl of Glencairn. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f167&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=William+Porterfield+of+that+Ilk&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y Nat
2 CONC ional Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/5/167]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Account of the Families of Birnie and Hamilton of Broomhill''.  By John Birnie.  Page 35-36.  < [https://books.google.com/books?id=4chrAAAAMAAJ&vq=porterfield&pg=PA35#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir James Hamilton his second daughter, JEAN, married John Porterfield of that Ilk, or of Duchal, to whom she had ''William'' and Alexander, Ann, Margaret, and Joan. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William married Annabella, daughter to Sir Archibald Stewart of Blackhall; had issue ,-Alexander, now of Duchall, who married Lady Katherin Boyd, daughter to William Earle of Kilmarnock, and has issue,-William, who married Julian,
2 CONC  only child of Mr William Steill, Presbyterian minister at Lochmaben.
2 CONT
2 CONT The above  William Porterfield of Duchal has another son, John, a merchant in Philadelphia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean, William's eldest daughter, married Gavin Ralston of that Ilk, whose eldest son William, now of Ralston, married Marion, only daughter to Mr David Ewen, Presbyterian minister at Calder.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ann, William of Duchal's other daughter, married James Ferquhar of Gilmilscroft; also with issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander, now of Duchal, who married the aboue Lady Kathren Boyd, has ishue, besides their aboue eldest son William, Jean, married to her cussen, James Corbet, younger of Towcrosse.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
