1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR ALEXANDER CUNNINGHAM OF CORSEHILL Baronet===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Cuninghame of Corsehill, Baronet. He was the son of Alexander Cuninghame and Anne Crawford. [http://thepeerage.com/p32655.htm#i326549 Darryl Lundy's Peerage] He was still a pupil when his father died, and his grandfat
2 CONC her had a brieve of tutory under the quarter seal on 19 January 1646. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f112&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=corsehill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n 
2 CONC NRS: GD39/5/112]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Alexander Cunningham of Corsehill married Mary Stewart, daughter of John Stewart, circa 1665. He died before March 1685. In 1663 his grandfather settled the family estate of Corsehill on him and his affianced wife, reserving to
2 CONC  himself the life rent. He was ruined by guaranteeing the credit of his cousin, Sir David Cuningham of Robertland, 4th Bt. He was created 1st Baronet Cuninghame, of Corsehill, co. Ayr. [Nova Scotia] on 26 February 1671/72. [http:/
2 CONC /thepeerage.com/p32655.htm#i326549 Darryl Lundy's Peerage]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 June 1646: Tutory under the Quarter Seal in favour of Alexander Cunninghame of Corsehill, to be tutor dative to Alexander, pupil son of deceased Alexander Cunninghame, eldest lawful son of said Alexander Cunninghame of Corse
2 CONC hill. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f112&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=corsehill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39
2 CONC /5/112]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''19 January 1647: Crown Precept of Sasine for infefting Alexander Cunninghame now of Corsehil as heir to deceased Alexander Cunynghame of Corsehill, his father, in the 6 merk lands of Cuttiswrey, 6 merk lands of Clerkland and Hi
2 CONC llhouse and mill thereof, 2 1/2 merk lands of Little Robertland, 6 merk lands of Two Corsehills, 10 merk lands of Blacklaw, 6 merk lands of Hairshaw, 10 merk lands of Dowrey and Potterton, in lordship of Stewarton, bailiary of Cun
2 CONC ninghame and sheriffdom of Ayr. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f113&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=corsehill&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls of
2 CONC  Glencairn, reference GD39/5/113]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 February 1672: Diploma of Knight Baronetcy in favour of Alexander Cunningham of Corsehill. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD39%2f5%2f141&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=corsehill&ko=
2 CONC p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Earls of Glencairn, reference GD39/5/141]'''
2 CONT
