2 CONT '''20 October 1687: Assignation by Isobell Bontein [Bunting], daughter of Nicoll Bontein [Bunting] of Ardoch and Robert Grahame [Graham] of Callangad [Gallangad], her spouse, in favour of [blank], of the following bonds: By Alexan
2 CONC der Dunlop of Dunlop, with Sir James Montgomery of Skelmorly [Skelmorlie] as cautioner, of the sum of 1000 merks Scots, dated 27 February 1685. By Sir James Montgomery of Skelmorly, of the sum of £116 3s 4d Scots, dated 27 March 1
2 CONC 685. By Sir Robert Barclay of Perstoune [Perceton], kt, with Robert Barclay, younger of Perstoune, his son, as cautioner, of the sum of 2000 merks Scots, dated 19 April 1682. By Arthour Hameltoune [Hamilton] of Auchengramont [Auch
2 CONC ingramont], advocate, of the sum of 600 merks Scots, dated 29 January 1677, in favour of Robert Barclay, late provost of Irvine, grandfather of Issobell, who succeeded to the Bond as his heir. By Archibald Muir, merchant burgess o
2 CONC f Edinburgh, with Alexander Dunlop, fiar of that ilk, as cautioner, of the sum of 1400 merks Scots, dated 3 March 1681. By Nicoll Bontein [Bunting] of Ardoch, father of Issobell, of the sum of 500 merks Scots, dated 14 August 1686
2 CONC . On the back of the Assignation is the judicial attestation by Issobell Bontein [Bunting], dated 31 October 1687, at Dumbarton. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD22%2f1%2f103&st=1&tc
2 CONC =y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=alexander+dunlop&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1601&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Cunninghame Graham Family of Ardoch, Dunbartonshire, reference GD22/1/103]'''
