1 NAME Andrew /Tosheoch of Monzievaird/
2 GIVN Andrew
2 SURN Tosheoch of Monzievaird
2 _MARNM Tosheoch of Monzievaird
2 NICK Toshack
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1620
2 ADDR
3 CITY Aberdeen
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE JAN 1665
2 ADDR
3 STAE Scotland
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Facts gathered from the Red Book of Scotland:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://redbookofscotland.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/Tosheoch-of-Monzievaird.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT *1618, June 20: Was a child at the time his father, David, was murdered in Perth.
2 CONT *1618, December: Received the instrument of sasine (property transfer) for Monzievaird from his deceased father.
2 CONT *1637, Nov. 4: Retoured as heir to his father. Soon after, became a Royalist in the cause of Charles I. Eventually, his estate is sequestered by Parliament.
2 CONT *1641, Mar. 9: Received  at Kenmore charter of marriage with Katherine, daughter of Sir Robert Campbell, 3rd Baronet of Glenorchy.
2 CONT *1660: Following restoration of King Charles II, he is appointed Commissioner for the Peace within Strathearn.
2 CONT *1665, January: Died, according to Dunblane Testaments.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of:
2 CONT *David Tosheoch of Monzievaird
2 CONT *Margaret Tosheoch, who executed her father's will and testament in 1665.
2 CONT *Isabel Tosheoch
2 CONT *Barbara Tosheoch
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Andrew Toshoch,[28] born between 1600-1620.[14] Died 1665.[22] {Note that Andrew died before his father (1668[7]), hence the successor to his father was Andrew's son, David, not Andrew himself}. Married Catherine Campbell,[7,9] 16
2 CONC 41.[28] Catherine was born 1619/1620, Kenmore or Merchiston and is probably of the Lawers/Glenorchy Campbell's.[3,28]
2 CONT
2 CONT child of Andrew Toshoch and Catherine Campbell:
2 CONT      i. David Toshoch.{8}
2 CONT     ii. Margaret Toschoch.[32] Emigrated to America with her
2 CONT         husband.[31] Was still alive 23/11/1710 when she filed a
2 CONT         petition for the return of her husband's land grant.[31] The
2 CONT         petition was finally approved in 1720, by which time Patrick
2 CONT         Jr was listed as the heir.[31] Had Margaret died by then?
2 CONT         Married Patrick MacGregorie.[3,29] Patrick was a soldier of
2 CONT         fortune, serving in the English army in France under Charles I,
2 CONT         achieving the rank of captain.[31] Upon returning to Scotland
2 CONT         he became involved in the religious controversy of 1681-1682
2 CONT         and partly as the result of this emigrated to America with his
2 CONT         brother-in-law, David,[31] 7th Laird of Monzievaird. {See also
2 CONT         entry for David}. Was killed, 3/1691.
2 CONT               Children: Hugh, John (1687), Patrick Jr.,
2 CONT                         Catherine and Jane.[31,32]
