1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lady Margaret Campbell1
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #72537, d. December 1665
2 CONT
2 CONT      Lady Margaret Campbell was the daughter of John Campbell, 1st Earl of Loudoun and Margaret Campbell, 2nd Baroness Campbell of Loudoun.1 She married John Elphinstone, 3rd Lord Balmerinoch, son of John Elphinstone, 2nd Lord Bal
2 CONC merinoch and Ann Kerr, on 30 October 1649 at Holyrood House Chapel, Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland.1 She died in December 1665.1 She was buried at Restalrig, Midlothian, Scotland.1
2 CONT       From 30 October 1649, her married name became Elphinstone.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Lady Margaret Campbell and John Elphinstone, 3rd Lord Balmerinoch
2 CONT  1.John Elphinstone, 4th Lord Balmerinoch+1 b. 26 Dec 1652, d. 13 May 1736
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT  1.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extin
2 CONC ct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 390. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
