1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===DONALD CAMPBELL OF GLENCARRADALE===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''30 January 1712: The Procurator Fiscal agt Donald Campbell of Carradale (Saddell) John Campbell of Saddell (Saddell ) James Campbell of Ormsary, John dow Campbell in Lephinbeag (Saddell) and 19 others in Kintyre. Accused of Imp
2 CONC orting and selling 20 bolls of victual and 20 head of cattle from Ireland in contravention of various Acts of Parliament; fishing at the forbidden time, killing deer and river and moor fowl . 8 found guilty in so far as they refus
2 CONC ed to depone; nothing proved against the others. Donald Campbell of Glencarradale fined £100 sterling and to remain in ward until the fine was paid. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SC5
2 CONC 4%2f17%2f2%2f37%2f1&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=glencarradale&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1630&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Inveraray Sheriff Court, reference 30/01/1712]'''
