1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MUNGO STIRLING OF CRAIGBERNARD ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 February 1701: Extract feu contract between Mungo Stirling of Craigbarnet, with consent of Mary Stirling, his mother, on one part, and William Lapsley, indweller in Clachane of Campsie, on other part, whereby said Mungo gran
2 CONC ts to said William houses in Clachan of Campsie, and Croft Angrie, part of lands of Ballincleroch. (Registered in Court Books of sheriffdom of Stirling, 10 June, 1706.) [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/detai
2 CONC ls.aspx?reference=GD61%2f78&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=mary+stirling&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=1720&di=n National Records of Scotland, Macfarlane of Ballancleroch, reference GD61/78]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Mungo Stirling married Marjory Stirling and had two sons - James, who succeeded, and another son, whose name  has not been ascertained, but he's noticed under the designation of Glorat's 'sister's son,' as being recently dead, in 
2 CONC a letter from James Stirling the Venetian, 24th. June 1712; and a daughter, Mary, married to George Graham in Shannonchill, great grandfather of the present <<<<major Graham Stirling of Craigbarnet. Mary Stirling died in 1759, age
2 CONC d  ninety years and upwards. Her husband, George Graham, predeceased her in 1736, as in a letter from Captain John Stirling of Auchyll to Sir Henry Striling of Ardoch, dated 14th. June 1736, he mentions the death of 'George Graham
2 CONC  in Shannonchyle.' Mungo Stirling of Craigbarnet died of "a cold and sthma,' on 7th. January 1733, aged seventy-three years.  (Campsie Parish records) 'Marjory Stirling, Lady Craigbarnet' also died of 'a cold and asthma', on 18th 
2 CONC January 1733, aged sixty-three years. (Craigbarnet Writs). Mungo was succeeded by his only surviving son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: THE STIRLINGS OF KEIR and their family papers. by William Fraser - Edinburgh (Privately printed) MDCCCLVIII.
