1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JEAN BRUCE Lady Airth ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jean Bruce married Richard Elphinston of Calderhall, younger. The marriage was booked on 14 December 1674, at Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland. The marriage record reads as follows: "Richard Elphingstoun younger of Calderhall.
2 CONC  Jean Bruce. married be Mr John Paterson Dean of Edinburgh." [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Marriage Records, reference OPR.685/1 440 155]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 February 1678: Signature of the lands of Airth etc granted to Richard Elphinstone and Jean Bruce (Bruice), his wife. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SIG1%2f51%2f60&st=1&tc=y&tl=
2 CONC n&tn=n&tp=n&k=richard+Elphinstone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register of Signatures, boxed series, reference SIG1/51/60]'''
2 CONT
