1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on John Henderson:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p43749.htm#i437482
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Henderson of Fordell, 1st Bt.[1]
2 CONT *M, #437482, 
2 CONT *d. 26 January 1683
2 CONT *Last Edited=2 Mar 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Henderson of Fordell, 1st Bt. was the son of Sir John Henderson, 5th of Fordell and Margaret Menteith.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret Hamilton, daughter of Sir John Hamilton of Orbiston and Bethia Henderson, in October 1657.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 26 January 1683.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created 1st Baronet Henderson, of Fordell [Nova Scotia] on 15 July 1664.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Sir John Henderson of Fordell, 1st Bt. and Margaret Hamilton
2 CONT *1. Sir William Henderson, 2nd Bt.+3 d. 1709
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1865. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume III, page 347. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT also married Margaret Hamilton
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The Henderson Baronetcy, of Fordell (agnatic primogeniture) in the County of Fife, was created in the Baronetage of Nova Scotia on 15 July 1664 for John Henderson. The fifth Baronet sat as Member of Parliament for Fife, Kirkcaldy 
2 CONC Burghs, Seaford and Stirling Burghs. The title became extinct on the death of the sixth Baronet in 1833.(The pretenders to the baronetcy would logically be the descendants of Capt. James Henderson (1618-1644), uncle of the 1st Bar
2 CONC onet. But no one in his descendants seems to have claimed the title officially.) 
