1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =William Henderson=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Sir John Henderson, Kt., 5th of Fordell and Margaret Menteith of Raniford
2 CONT * Birth:	June 26, 1626 in Fordell Castle, Dunfermline, Fife, Scotland
2 CONT * Death:	July 22, 1676 (48) in Dalgety Bay, Fife, Scotland
2 CONT * [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/148693269/william-henderson '''William Henderson Find A Grave Memorial''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[http://www.thepeerage.com/p27461.htm#i274605 '''The Peerage''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Henderson, 5th of Fordell1 
2 CONT
2 CONT M, #274605, b. circa 1599/0, d. 11 March 1650
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=2 Dec 2017Dictionaries & Encyclopedias
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir John Henderson, 5th of Fordell was born circa 1599/0.2 He was the son of Sir John Henderson, 4th of Fordell and Agnes Balfour.3 He married Margaret Menteith, daughter of William Menteith of Randiford and Jean Bruce, on 7 Febru
2 CONC ary 1625.3 He died on 11 March 1650.3. He was a distinguished soldier, taken prisoner when commanding at the African Coast, ransomed, and later served in Civil War.3 He was appointed Knight by King Charles I.3
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children of Sir John Henderson, 5th of Fordell and Margaret Menteith=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Jean Henderson'' '+1
2 CONT * '''Francis Henderson''' 3
2 CONT * '''George Henderson''' 3 d. 1659
2 CONT * '''Margaret Henderson''' 3
2 CONT * '''Elizabeth Henderson''' 3
2 CONT * '''Bethia Henderson''' +3
2 CONT * '''Anna Henderson''' +3
2 CONT * '''Sir John Henderson of Fordell,''' 1st Bt.+3 b. 1626, d. 26 Jan 1683
2 CONT * '''William Henderson''' 3 b. c 1628, d. 21 Jul 1676
2 CONT * '''James Henderson''' +3 b. c 1630, d. 2 May 1675
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Erica-Howton/363677820350011581 Erica Howton] writes: William Henderson was born Bet Aug 1627 and Jun 1628 in , Fife, Scotland, and died 22 Jul 1676. He was buried in St. Theriot's Chapel, Fordell Cast
2 CONC le, Fifeshire, Scotland. He was the son of John Henderson and Margaret Menteith. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Marioun Shipart 27 Jul 1654 in Ferry Port On Craig, Fife, Scotland, daughter of Thomas Shipart and Janet Putie. She was born 14 Mar 1637 in Ferry Port On Craig, Fife, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also [http://www.thepeerage.com/p43749.htm#i437485 The Peerage] entry, which quotes ''Burke's Peerage''. That site doesn't mention his wife nor his children. (This paragraph by [https://www.geni.com/people/Jim-Henderson/600000
2 CONC 0021010310497 Jim Henderson])
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT * ”I have found the Christening of William at Dunfermline on April 27, 1676, the illegitimate son of John Henderson and Magdaline Lundie. I also have found in the Scottish records a John Henderson born 1655 with father William. I 
2 CONC think this may be the William, second son to John Henderson and Margaret Menteith, but have no definitive proof. It does fit, however, very well. With this info, I and others think Sir John's son William to be the most likely fath
2 CONC er for John 1655, father to William 1676. If not it seems almost certain that there is a tie somewhere to the Fordell Hendersons. See my article in Fall 2001 edition of An Canach for details (is included in my Henderson Book.”
2 CONT * This seems the most probable link to our ancestors in America. There is a lot of evidence to support this assertion. From the Miller Book we see the solid information that the William Henderson(wife Margaret Bruce) was the fathe
2 CONC r of James,our first ancestor in America, and the son of Gentleman John Henderson. Miller gives good reasons for William being from Fordell and that his father was born around 1650 to the son of one of the sons of Sir John Henders
2 CONC on and Margaret Menteith.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://archive.org/details/hendersonchronic00mccu/page/6/mode/2up?q=James
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
