1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == REVEREND MR. JAMES BRUCE MA ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Minister of the Gospel at Killyleagh in County Down, Ireland; Formerly Minister of the Gospel at Trinity-Gask in Perthshire, Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Bruce, M.A. (Edinburgh); admitted as minister  the Gospel at Trinity-Gask in Perthshire. after 11 October 1661. He was still minister there on 17 September 1673. [https://archive.org/details/fastiecclesiu04scotuoft/page/n
2 CONC 298/mode/1up Fasti IV: 274]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Bruce, M.A. (Edinburgh), was minister of the Gospel at Killyleagh in 1685. He removed to Scotland at the Revolution, but returned to Ireland in 1691. He died 17 February 1730. His son Patrick succeeded him at Killyleagh i
2 CONC n 1730. [https://archive.org/details/fastiecclesiaesc00scot/page/527/mode/1up Fasti VII: 527]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy and Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/fastiecclesiu04scotuoft/page/n6/mode/1up Fasti Ecclesiæ Scoticanæ. The Succession of Ministers in the Church of Scotland from the Reformation. By Hew Scott, DD. New Edition. Volume IV. Synods of A
2 CONC rgyll, and of Perth and Stirling (Oliver and Boyd, Edinburgh, 1923), 414 pp. including indices]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/fastiecclesiaesc00scot/page/n6/mode/1up Fasti Ecclesiae Scoticanae. The Succession of Ministers in the Church of Scotland from the Reformation. By Hew Scott, D.D. New Edition. Volume VII. Synods o
2 CONC f Ross, Sutherland and Caithness, Glenelg, Orkney and of Shetland. The Church in England, Ireland and Overseas (Oliver and Boyd, Edinburgh, 1928), 800 pp. including indices]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/bb4fz/bruce09.php Stirnet: Bruce 09]'''
