1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MICHAEL ELPHINSTONE OF QUARREL ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Michael Elphinstone of Quarrel, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Elphinstone-of-Quarrel/6000000199480101822?through=6000000199480445821 [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/detai
2 CONC ls.aspx?reference=GD65%2f97&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=michael+elphinstone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: 97] and the grandson of https://www.geni.com/people/Michael-Elphinstone-of-Quarrel/6000000199295422825 [https://catalogue.nr
2 CONC scotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD65%2f91&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=michael+elphinstone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD65/91]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 July 1681: Signature of the lands of Skaithmure etc granted to Michael Elphinstone and Sir Robert Elphinstone (Elphingstone, Elphinston). [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=SIG1%2f
2 CONC 51%2f66&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Robert+Elphinstone&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register of Signatures, boxed series, reference SIG1/51/66]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 January 1683: Precept of Clare Constat by John, Lord Elphinstone, in favour of Michael Elphinstone, now of Quarrel, as grandson and heir of the deceased Michael Elphinstone of Quarrel, in the lands as in GD65/31 [Note 1] and
2 CONC  GD65/36. [Note 2] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD65%2f91&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=michael+elphinstone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Dundas of Fingask, 
2 CONC reference GD65/91]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note 1: The 8 oxingait of land of the lands of Bothkynner [Bothkennar] and the kirklands mansion and glebe pertaining to the vicarage of Bothkynner.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note 2:  Three and one half oxingangs and an odd part of the lands of Dulungrie of Westertoun of Bothkenner [Bothkennar].'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 August 1684: (1) Disposition by Michael Elphingstone of Quarrel [Elphinstone of Quarrel] and Rachel Bruice [Bruce], his spouse in favour of James Hunter of Foster-saltcoats and Henry Hunter, his youngest son, of the other ha
2 CONC lf of the subjects as in GD65/93. In dorso Judicial Ratification thereof by said Rachel dated 24 July 1685. (2) Instrument of Resignation following thereon. Dated 27 February 1685. (3) Charter under Great Seal following thereon. D
2 CONC ated 18 March 1685. [Tag, seal gone]. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD65%2f94&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elphinstone+of+quarrel&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotlan
2 CONC d, Dundas of Fingask, reference GD65/94]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 January 1685: (1) Precept of Clare Constat by Robert Milne of Barntoune [Barnton] and Henry Elphinstone, collector at Aberdeen, as tutors for Charles Elphinstone of Airth, in favour of Michael Elphinstone, now of Quarrell [Q
2 CONC uarrel], as son and heir of the deceased Sir Robert Elphinstone, in the lands of Quarrell and Easter Skeathmure. (2) Sasine following thereon. Dated 27 February 1685. Registered P.R.S. Stirling, 15 April 1685, vii, 5-6. [https://c
2 CONC atalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD65%2f97&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=michael+elphinstone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Dundas of Fingask, reference GD65/97]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 November 1687: 1) Instrument of Resignation by Michael Elphinstoune of Quarrell [Elphinstone of Quarrel] of the lands of Quarrell and Easter Skaithmurie, reserving his liferent thereof, in favour of Robert Elphinstone, his e
2 CONC ldest son, following on marriage
2 CONT contract between said Robert and Michael on the one part and Anna Campbell and Mr Adam Campbell of Gargunnock on the other, dated 24 November 1687. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD6
2 CONC 5%2f104&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Robert+Elphinstone&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Dundas of Fingask, reference GD65/104]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''31 January 1693: (1) Instrument of Resignation by Michael Elphinstoune of Quarrell [Elphinstone of Quarrel] of the lands of Quarrell and Easter Skaithmurie, reserving his liferent thereof, in favour of Robert Elphinstone, his e
2 CONC ldest son, following on marriage contract between said Robert and Michael on the one part and Anna Campbell and Mr Adam Campbell of Gargunnock on the other, dated 24 November 1687. (2) Charter by Sir Robert Milne of Blackburne [Bl
2 CONC ackburn] and Henry Elphinstone of Melgoline as tutors for Charles Elphinstone of Airth,  following on the above. Dated 31 January 1693. (3) Sasine following thereon. Dated 18 August 1703. Registered P.R.S. Stirling, 1 October 1703
2 CONC , xi, 269-70. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD65%2f104&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elphinstone+of+quarrel&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Dundas of Fingask, r
2 CONC eference GD65/104]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 July 1694: Signature of the lands of Sketmure [Skaithmure] etc granted to Michael Elphinstone and Robert Elphinstone (Elphingstone, Elphinston). [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=
2 CONC SIG1%2f52%2f9&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Robert+Elphinstone&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Register of Signatures, boxed series, reference SIG1/52/9]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1711: Titles to lands in parish of Bothkenner, Sheriffdom of Stirling: Special retour of Robert Elphinstone, Younger of Quarrell, as heir to his father, Michael Elphinstone of Quarrell, in lands of Howkerse, Fiendyaird and part
2 CONC  of Bothkenner, with precept and instrument of sasine following thereon. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f1041%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=michael+elphinstone&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=
2 CONC &dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Dundas of Fingask Charters; Halket of Pitfirrane Papers reference GD1/1041/7]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     9
2 CONT
2 CONT '''9 August 1725: Disposition by Robert Elphingstone of Quarrell [Elphinstone of Quarrel], with consent of his interdictors, Anna Campbell, his spouse, and Michael Elphingstone, his eldest son, in favour of Mr John Drummond, merch
2 CONC ant of London, brother german of James Drummond of Blair-Drummond, and Agatha Vanderbent, his spouse, of the lands of Quarrell and Easter Skeathmuire with the teinds thereof, on payment by the said John Drummond of the sum of £37,
2 CONC 631 16s Scots. Also Judicial Ratification thereof by the said Anna. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD65%2f172&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elphinstone+of+quarrel&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&d
2 CONC i=n National Records of Scotland, Dundas of Fingask, reference GD65/172]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                    10
2 CONT
2 CONT '''11 July 1729: Special Retour in favour of William Hunter, now of Kirktoun, as brother and heir of the deceased Henry Hunter of Kirktoun, in 8 oxengates of land of Bothkennar, Kirklands of Bothkennar, 4 and one part oxengates of
2 CONC  the lands of Dallungry, with the teindsheaves thereof, reserving to the heirs of the deceased Michael Elphingston of Quarrell [Elphinstone of Quarrel], the road from the coal-heughs of Quarrell to the coal house in so far as it p
2 CONC assed on the said lands, and the superiority of the piece of ground called Nunyeard. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD65%2f178&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=elphinstone+of+quarrel&ko=p&
2 CONC r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Dundas of Fingask, reference GD65/178]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
