1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://myallredfamily.com/front-page/what-states/north-carolina/john-1792/samuel-finley/
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Finley was the Father of John Allred
2 CONT by: Linda Allred Cooper
2 CONT Time Line of Samuel Finley Estate
2 CONT Our AFO DNA Project Manager, John Allred, wrote two compelling articles published in newsletter #88 and newsletter #104 that will help you understand how DNA helped confirm who John Allred's parents were.   DNA results proved a gr
2 CONC owing group of Allreds, who traced their roots back to Randolph County, NC, had Y Chromosome DNA that matched each other but did not match the majority of Allreds. What does this mean?
2 CONT As you know, land and court records proved John Allred, Thomas Allred, 2 men named Solomon Allred (one older, one younger) and 2 men named William Allred (one older, one younger) arrived in North Carolina in the mid 1700’s. Everyo
2 CONC ne thought these men were related. At one time everyone thought they were brothers but additional information proved they were a combination of uncles, cousins and brothers.
2 CONT (See link for more.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/171511041/samuel-finley<br/>
2 CONT It is suggested that Samuel FINLEY's wife died in 1707 at the birth of their daughter Mary FINLEY in West Nottingham Township, Chester County, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on YDNA testing we believe that the widower Samuel FINELY became acquainted with Elizabeth ALLRED daughter of Solomon ALLRED I and Ann YORK. Samuel FINLEY became the father of John "Johnny" ALLRED born 1728 out of wedlock wi
2 CONC th Elizabeth ALLRED. This is well documented by Allred researcher Darnell Hatton Griffin, pp 105-113 in the excellent book "From England to America Our Allred Family"
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Per FAG, he is buried in Prince George Co MD
2 CONT Samuel Finley
2 CONT BIRTH 18 Mar 1684 Ireland
2 CONT DEATH 16 Oct 1736 (aged 52) Prince George's Co MD
2 CONT BURIAL Fort Lincoln Cemetery Brentwood, Prince George's Co MD
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID 171511041 ·
