1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Emigrated with his brother, Michael and their families, on chartered ship Eagle Wing arriving first at Newcastle, Delaware, Then Philadelphia, Pennslyvania on Sept. 28, 1734, In 1736, Archibald along with brothers-
2 CONC in-law Archibald, Thomas, and Henry Kelso, contracted with George Fritzwater for 500 acres of land in New Britian Township, Bucks County Pennsylvania, lying along the NW side of the present Upper State Road. However, Fritzwater di
2 CONC ed before any payments were made and his executors were authorized to convey the land upon payment to his estate. By mutual agreement, the land was partitioned among the parties and Archibald Finley was allotted 151 acres and 53 p
2 CONC erches. He died in a house erected on this property on March 11, 1750 and the deed was then conveyed by the executors of Fitzwater to Margaret Finley, his widow, and John and Henry Finley, his two eldest sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alt. Born January 08, 1685/86
2 CONT
