1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == MASTER JOHN DICK OF BRAID ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1 July - 30 July 1633: Extract contract between Sir John Hoome of Northberwick, kt., with consent of Sir George Hoome, his eldest son, Mr. Patrick Hoome, also his son, and Alexander Hoome of Rowanstoune, on one part, and Willia
2 CONC m Dick of Braid, merchant, burgess of Edinburgh, and John Dick of Braid, his eldest son, on other part, whereby said Sir John dispones to said William lands and barony of Northberuick, (specified), under reversion, for payment of 
2 CONC debts of said Sir John (specified). Reg. b. of c. & s., 5 April 1639. With a transcript. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD110%2f49&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Dick+of+Braid&ko=p&
2 CONC r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Hamilton-Dalrymple Family of North Berwick, reference GD110/49]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 September 1637: Charters de me and a me by Hew Dowglas of Lewchie, with consent of Margaret Home, his spouse, to Mr. John Dick, fiar of Braid, and lady Nicolas Bruce, his spouse, in fulfillment of contract, 29 September 1637
2 CONC , of lands of Lewchie, to be held of Sir John Johnstoun of Elphinstoun, kt., bt. In dorso: ratification thereof by said Sir John, 27 January 1638. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD11
2 CONC 0%2f300&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=nicolas+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Hamilton-Dalrymple Family of North Berwick, reference GD110/300]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 May 1639: Charter de me by Mr. John Dick, fiar of Braid, with consent of lady Nicolas Bruce, his spouse, to John Bannantyne, son of Sir James Bannatyne of Newhall, kt., and Marion Marioribanks, his spouse, of lands of Lewchi
2 CONC e. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD110%2f302&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=nicolas+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Hamilton-Dalrymple Family
2 CONC  of North Berwick, reference GD110/302]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 August 1673: Mr. John Dick, son of deceased Mr John Dick of Braid and Agnes Dick, daughter of deceased William Dick of Grainge. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=RH9%2f7%2f234&st=1
2 CONC &tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Dick+of+Braid&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Marriage Contracts, RH9/7/234]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''26 April 1686: Extract Bond by Sir William Nicolsone [Nicholson] of that ilk to Agnes Dick, relict of Mr. John Dick, son of deceased Mr. John Dick of Braid, and Mr. Robert Craufoord [Crawford], doctor of medicine, now her spous
2 CONC e, of 2,400 merks, being bygones of annuity of 12,000 merks contained in bond of corroboration, dated 30 Jun 1677, by Captain Andrew Dick, brother german and heir of said John, and deceased Sir John Nicolsone of that ilk, brother 
2 CONC of said Sir William of marriage contract, dated 7 Aug 1673, between said John and Agnes. Sir William, in corroboration of his bond, binds himself to infeft said Agnes and her spouse in annualrent of said principal sum of 2,400 mer
2 CONC ks from lands and barony of Lausued [Lasswade]. Registered in B. of C. and S., 3 Dec 1686. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD18%2f1517&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=John+Dick+of+Braid&ko
2 CONC =p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of Clerk family of Penicuik, Midlothian, reference GD18/1517]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: 1. Sasine following thereon, 27 Apr 1686. 2. Decreet of poinding at instance of said Robert Craufurd [Crawford] and Agnes Dick, his spouse, for payment of annualrent, 15 Dec 1686.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
