1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == WILLIAM DICK OF GRANGE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Merchant Burgess of Edinburgh===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''The Question of Identity'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''William Dick of Grange, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/William-Dick-of-Braid/6000000022699640870?through=6000000194211789852 and his wife https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Morrison/60000
2 CONC 00019064671638?through=6000000194211789852 He was born before 20 January 1614, the date upon which his baptism was registered at Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Baptisms, reference OPR.6
2 CONC 85/1/2]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''William Dick of Grange, here treated, is not noticed as the Laird of Grange until after his death on 14 May 1647, although he made his last will and testament at Nether Grange. Thereafter, his widow https://www.geni
2 CONC .com/people/Janet-McMath/6000000204916685899?through=6000000194211789852 is occasionally referred to as as "Lady Grange, relict of  William Dick of Grange." [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refe
2 CONC rence=GD41%2f19&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+dick&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1650&dt=1700&di=y NRS: GD41/19] He is noticed as William Dick, third son of William Dick of Braid on 28 August 1639, the date upon which he was enrolled as a 
2 CONC burgess and guild brother of Edinburgh, [https://archive.org/details/scottishrecordso46scotuoft/scottishrecordso46scotuoft/page/n157/mode/1up EBR: 148] and as William Dick, younger, merchant in Edinburgh, brother of Lewes Dick, me
2 CONC rchant there, on 31 August 1639. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD41%2f17&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=william+dick&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1639&dt=1639&di=y NRS: GD41/17]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Dick of Grange made his last will and testament at Nether Grange near Edinburgh on 8 April 1647. The following witnesses were present, viz. Mr. John McMath, writer in Edinburgh, Thomas Young, servant to the foresaid Wil
2 CONC liam Dick, and Alexander Dick, writer. He nominated and appointed his wife Janet McMath to be his only executrix and universal intromitter. She was given power to make and give up an inventory of his belongings, including any mone
2 CONC y owed to him, or by him. She was to do this with the advice and consent of any four of the following individuals, viz. "my most loving faither" Sir William Dick of Braid, Sir Lues Stewart of Kirkhill, Sir William Nisbet of the De
2 CONC an, John Nicholsone of Poltoun, Mr. Andro Alexander, Lues Dick, brother of the foresaid William Dick of Grange, George Lawson, James Loch of Drylaw, and Robert Davidson, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, providing always that Sir Wil
2 CONC liam Dick of Braid and Sir Lues Stewart of Kirkhill were part of the four people meeting for this purpose. He also nominated and appointed his wife Jonet McMath to be the sole curator, guardian and governor, to their four children
2 CONC , viz. William Dick, Jonet Dick, Bessie Dick, and Margaret Dick, an office she was to exercise with the help and advice of his father Sir William Dick of Braid and Sir Lues Stewart of Kirkhill, and any four of the people previousl
2 CONC y mentioned. Robert Davidson, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, acted himself as cautioner for Jonet McMath and confirmation was granted to her on 1 June 1648. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament 
2 CONC Testamentar and Inventory of Williame Dick, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, reference CC8/8/63]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000205032705834 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000205032725832 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000205032697824 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000205032336850 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000205032340860 Image of Testament]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Dick of Grange, here treated, died on 14 May 1647. He probably died at Nether Grange in St. Cuthbert's parish, near Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland, where he made his last will and testament on 8 April 1647. [NRS: CC8
2 CONC /8/63]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Dick of Grange, here treated married https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-McMath/6000000204916685899?through=6000000194211789852 A date and place for the marriage has not been identified, However, the marriage must have ta
2 CONC ken place before 29 November 1637, the date upon which the baptism of their daughter Bessie Dick was registered at Edinburgh in Midlothian, Scotland. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Baptisms, reference OPR.685/1/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
