1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===COLONEL JAMES MOODIE OF MELSETTER (aka THE YOUNG LAIRD)===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Colonel James Moodie of Melsetter is the son of William Moodie of Melsetter and his wife Barbara Stewart. [http://archive.org/stream/moodiebookbeing00ruvi#page/32/mode/1up The Moodie Book, pp. 32-4] His date of birth is not kno
2 CONC wn but his parents were married on or after 23 November 1670, and it seems likely that he was born after this date.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Member of the Scottish Parliament===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Colonel James Moodie of Melsetter was one of the Commissioners of Supply for Orkney in the the Parliament of 19 June 1702; and, as Captain  James Moodie of Melsetter he was a Commissioner for Orkney and Shetland in the Parliame
2 CONC nt which met 6 July 1704.  He was also a member of the last Scottish Parliament and appears to have voted for the Union with England. [http://archive.org/stream/moodiebookbeing00ruvi#page/32/mode/1up The Moodie Book, pp. 32-4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Soldier of Fortune===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Colonel James Moodie of Melsetter entered the service of Spain and rose to the rank of Colonel.  He afterwards entered the service of the Venetian Government and became Commander-in-Chief of their forces. [http://archive.org/st
2 CONC ream/moodiebookbeing00ruvi#page/32/mode/1up The Moodie Book, pp. 32-4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Colonel James Moodie of Melsetter is reported to have died unmarried. He is also reported to have had at least three children who were born out of wedlock. [http://archive.org/stream/moodiebookbeing00ruvi#page/32/mode/1up The M
2 CONC oodie Book, pp. 32-4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Bastard Bairns===
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/N-N/6000000048694648867?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1477585201268&through=6000000019856506852
