2 CONT '''17 March 1711: Complaint of presbytery of Kirkwall, especially Thomas Baikie, minister at Kirkwall, and James Sands, minister at Birsay and Harray, against Captain James Moodie, who has called ministers giddie-headed gospel-mon
2 CONC gers and is guilty of  hellish malice' towards them, also complaining of episcopal intruders, especially James Lyon. Including a letter from Lord Morton date at London 17 March 1711. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlineca
2 CONC talogue/details.aspx?reference=CH1%2f2%2f31&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=james+moodie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1660&dt=1760&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the General Assembly of the Church of Scotland, Main Series, reference C
2 CONC H1/2/31]'''
