1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JAMES MOODIE OF MELSETTER younger MP===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Member of Parliament for Orkney and Shetland 1715-22===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Moodie of Melsetter, younger, is the son of Captain James Moodie of Melsetter, RN. [https://archive.org/details/moodiebookbeinga00ruvi/page/n106 The Moodie Book: 39-40]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''According to J. M. Simpson. Sir James Moodie of Melsetter's mother was a daughter of James Douglas, eleventh Earl of Morton, notwithstanding the fact that the eleventh earl was named Robert Douglas. [http://www.historyofparliam
2 CONC entonline.org/volume/1715-1754/member/moodie-james-1724 The History of Parliament: James Moodie].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''On 2 March 1715 James Moodie of Melsetter, younger, was elected to serve as member of parliament for Orkney and Shetland. [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1715-1754/constituencies/orkney-and-shetland History of 
2 CONC Parliament: Orkney and Shetland] He lost his seat in 1722. [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1715-1754/member/moodie-james-1724 The History of Parliament: James Moodie]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James Moodie of Melsetter, younger, died during his father's lifetime, on 4 February 1724. [http://www.historyofparliamentonline.org/volume/1715-1754/member/moodie-james-1724 The History of Parliament: James Moodie]'''
