1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===CAPTAIN BENJIMAN MOODIE OF MELSETTER===
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Captain in the 47th Regiment of Foot, formerly Lieutenant in the 46th Regiment of Foots===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Captain Benjiman Moodie of Melsetter is the son of Captain James Moodie of Melsetter, RN., and his wife Christian Crawford. He is reported to have been born on 17 February 1723, at Aikerness in the Orkney parish of Evie, Scotla
2 CONC nd.  [http://archive.org/stream/moodiebookbeing00ruvi#page/55/mode/1up The Moodie Book, pp. 45-52]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Military Career===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Captain Benjiman Moodie of Melsetter was appointed Lieutenant in the 46th (Colonel Murray's) Regiment on 5 April 1745. He afterwards transferred to the 47th Regiment with the rank of Captain and served at the Battle of Culloden
2 CONC  on 16 April 1746. Thereafter he asked and obtained permission from the Duke of Cumberland to proceed against the Orkney Jacobites (who had looted Melsetter in 1745). He captured Sir James Stewart, and his brother Alexander, and s
2 CONC ent them to the Tower of London to await trial for murder.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Captain Benjamin Moodie of Melsetter died shortly before the birth of his youngest child on 19 September 1769. [http://archive.org/stream/moodiebookbeing00ruvi#page/52/mode/1up The Moodie Book, p. 52]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Captain Benjiman Moodie of Melsetter married Henrietta Sinclair. [http://archive.org/stream/moodiebookbeing00ruvi#page/49/mode/1up The Moodie Book, p. 49]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Children===
