2 CONT ===Evidence from Peterkin's Rentals===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Compt made with the Vassalls and Tennents of the Bishoprick of Orkney, Cropt 1739. . . . . . Bemjamin Moodie of Melsetter, and Christian Crawfoord, Lady Melsetter, Factorix upon that estate, compt and showld pay for the lands u
2 CONC nderwrittem, viz. Imp. For 3d. land of Melsetter, 3 lp. oyle, 18d. scat sr. . . . . . [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=hvd.hxjui2&view=1up&seq=459 Peterkin's Rentals, Donald Groat's Bishoprick Compt Boook cropt 1739, p. 11]
2 CONC '''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Genealogy===
2 CONT
2 CONT # [http://archive.org/stream/moodiebookbeing00ruvi#page/55/mode/1up The Moodie Book, pp. 45-52]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Observation===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The story of the Moodies is an astonishing saga of feud, adventure and fighting, the decay of the family's fortunes having started at least two decades before the Rising of 1745, during which Melsetter House was sacked by Jacob
2 CONC ites. The eighth Laird, Benjamin, was serving on the mainland as an officer in the Hanoverian Army at the time and, for years after his return to Orkney, he spent most of his energies in wreaking a terrible revenge on surviving Or
2 CONC kney Jacobites, although he did conserve enough to enable him to father 13 children in subsequent years. [https://www.geni.com/projects/South-Africa-History-and-Families-of-Witsand-White-Sands-and-Port-Beaufort/12050 A concise his
2 CONC tory of Port Beaufort & White Sands (also known as Witsand) including Family Trees White Sands & Port Beaufort' written by John McGregor]'''
