1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "(283) <strong>Sir John Murray of Philiphaugh</strong>, died 1676. He was served heir to his father 10th February 1648, and succeeded his grandfather. He was M.P. for Selkirkshire 1661. He married, first, Anne, daughter of Sir Arc
2 CONC hibald Douglas of Cavers, and had issue: -
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sir James (No. 284 below).
2 CONT * John Murray of Bowhill, died about 1714. He was M.P. for Selkirkshire 1689- 1707, and was a Senator of the College of Justice. He had a son: -
2 CONT ** John of Bowhill, died August 1718.
2 CONT * Colonel William Murray.
2 CONT * Archibald Murray, died young.
2 CONT * Thomas Murray, died young.
2 CONT * Lewis Murray.
2 CONT * Walter Murray, apprenticed to an Edinburgh merchant 9th August 1648 (Apprentice Roll).
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, second, Margaret, daughter of Sir John Scott of Scotstarvet, and had a daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT ARMS recorded in Lyon Office, 1672-77. - Argent, a hunting horn sable, garnished gules; on a chief azure three mullets of the field. CREST: A demi man winding a horn proper. MOTTO : "Hinc usque superna venabor." [Plate V., fig. 6.
2 CONC ]"
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/68/mode/2up The heraldry of the Murrays: with notes on all the males of the family, descriptions of the arms, plates and pedigrees], by G. Harvey Johnston, 1910, 
2 CONC page 69, paragraph 283
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sir John Murray of Philiphaugh. He was served heir to his father 10th February 1648,
2 CONT and succeeded his grandfather. He was M.P. for Selkirkshire 1661.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == SIR JOHN MURRAY OF PHILIPHAUGH ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
