1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JANET BROADIE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/gg/grant02.php Stirnet: Grant 02]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Janet Brodie
2 CONT *Birth abt 1656, Of Lethen, Scotland
2 CONT *Death 1697 Age: 41
2 CONT *Father Aleaxander Brodie, M (~1626-1688)
2 CONT *Mother Elizabeth Craig, F (~1628-1683) Spouses:
2 CONT *1 1st Laird of Grant Ludovic Grant 8th Laird of Freuchie, M Birth 1652, Of Grant Death 19 Nov 1716, Edinburgh, Scotalnd Age: 64 Father James Grant 7th Earl of Freuchie, M (1616-1663)Mother Mary Stewart, F (~1605-1662) Marriage 20
2 CONC  Dec 1671, Freuchie, Perth, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT *John (Died as Child), M (~1675-1682)
2 CONT *Alexander, M (~1674-1719)
2 CONT *James, M (1679-1746)
2 CONT *George, M (~1682-1755)
2 CONT *Lewis "Lodovick", M (~1683-1742)
2 CONT *Elizabeth, F (1685-)
2 CONT *Anne, F (1687-)
2 CONT *Janet, F (1687-1761)
2 CONT *Margaret, F (1689-1729)
2 CONT *Marjory (Died as Infant), F (1691-1691)
2 CONT *David, M (1693-)
2 CONT
2 CONT Comment:
2 CONT
2 CONT A slightly different child list here: http://thepeerage.com/p18876.htm#i188756
2 CONT
2 CONT #Anne Grant+6
2 CONT #Major George Grant6 d. Dec 1755
2 CONT #Colonel Lewis Grant+6 d. 11 Mar 1742
2 CONT #Janet Grant+6 d. 10 Feb 1761
2 CONT #Margaret Grant+2 d. 1729
2 CONT #Elizabeth Grant+2 d. 1714
2 CONT #Brig.-Gen. Alexander Grant, 2nd of Grant6 b. 1672, d. 14 Aug 1719
2 CONT #Sir James Grant of Grant, 6th Bt.+6 b. 28 Jul 1679, d. 16 Jan 1747
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes for Ludovic (Spouse 1)
2 CONT He was fined by King James II's Commissioners the sum of £42,500 Scots, for non-conformity with Episcopacy, 11 February 1685. On his petitioning against the sentence, the King fully exonerated and discharged him of the fine 9 Janu
2 CONC ary 1686. His remission was owing to the promptitude he displayed in raising his clan at the time of Argyll's invasion. He was a member of the Convention of Estates called together by the Prince of Orange, which began its sittings
2 CONC  on 14 March 1689, and was one of the framers of that resolution of the Estates which declared that King James had forfeited the right to the crown, and that the throne had become vacant. On 19 April 1689 the Laird oi Freuchie vol
2 CONC unteered to raise and equip six hundred men, and three days afterwards he was appointed colonel of his own regiment. On 24 April he was appointed Sheriff Principal of Inverness in room of the Earl of Moray. He was member for Inver
2 CONC ness in Parliament until the Union in 1707. He made considerable additions to, and consolidated his estate, having acquired, about 1670, the lands of Achmonie from Gillies Mackay, Pitcherrell and Auchatemrach in 1674 from John Gra
2 CONC nt of Corriemony, in exchange for Carnoch and others, Abriochan from Alexander Fraser of Kinneras in 1695, and Culnakirk and Clunemore from John Grant of Glenmoriston in 1696. On 28 February 1694 he received irom William and Mary 
2 CONC a charter erecting his whole lands of Freuchie and others into a regality, to be called the regality of Grant, and ordaining the castle and manor place of Freuchie to be called in all time coming the Castle of Grant; also the town
2 CONC  formerly called Castletown of Freuchie, to be called the town and burgh of Grant. From this date the Laird of Freuchie changed his former designation and became the Laird of Grant. Lodovick Grant, the eighth Laird of Freuchie, wa
2 CONC s called "the Highland king". He supported the government of Mary and William. Doing this, got Mary and William to appoint him a colonel and Sherrif of Inverness, and raise the barony of Freuchie to regality status which was later
2 CONC  abolished after the failure of the Jacobite rising of 1745. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://thepeerage.com/p18876.htm#i188756
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Brodie-101
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/LT8P-J9N
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/152073607/janet_"joannett"-grant
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: 1697, Moray House, Canongate, Edinburgh, Scotland
