2 CONT == Critical Commentary ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''It is claimed that James Craig and Margaret Peters had a son named John Craig whose baptism was registered at Inveresk in Midlothian on 20 April 1612. It should be noticed, however, that the name of John Craig's mother is not m
2 CONC entioned in his baptismal record. Moreover, the marriage and baptismal records of Inveresk and Musselburgh do not mention Margaret Peters.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A marriage record for James Craig and Margaret Peters appears not to have survived. However, James Craig and Margaret Peter (Not Peters) had a son named John Craig whose baptism was registered at Glasgow in Lanarkshire on 18 Ap
2 CONC ril 1613. [National Records of Scotland, Glasgow Baptisms, reference OPR.644/1/1] John Craig is the only known child of this couple. They have no known connection with Inveresk and Musselburgh in Midlothian, or Dunfermline in Fife
2 CONC .'''
