1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Thomas Gibson, of Keirhill</strong>, co Edinburgh, 4th and yst. b. of Sir John Gibson, of Pentland and Alderston in that county, being only s. by his 3d wife Elizabeth, da. of Sir Thomas Thomson, 1st Baronet [S. 1636] of 
2 CONC Duddingston, was, 14 Feb. 1685, served heir of provision gen. of his father's said third marriage ; bought the estate of King's Cramond, co. Edinburgh, in 1694, but sold it in 1697, and having bought that of Keirhill, was cr. a Ba
2 CONC ronet [S.], as above, 31 Dec. 1702, with rem. to heirs male in perpetuum. He m. 11 June 1701, at Kirkliston, co. Edinburgh, Jean, da. of Edward Marjoribanks, of Hallyards, in Kirkliston, merchant and burgess of Edinburgh, by his 1
2 CONC st wife Agnes, da. of Robert Murray, of Melgund. He d. in or before 1713. His widow, who was bap. 30 April 1686, to. 22 June 1718, at Edinburgh, Rev. George Arbuthnot, Rector of the High School, Edinburgh, and d. 13 Feb. 1724."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n423/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 404
