1 NAME John Murray of Touchadame and Polmaise
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1690
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===JOHN MURRAY OF TOUCHADAME===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Murray of Touchadame is the son of William Murray of Touchadame. He was served heir to his decease father on 13 May 1643. . [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=PiVDAAAAcAAJ&pg=PR17&lpg=PR17&dq=Nether+Carmyle&source=bl&ots
2 CONC =qkxdEQg71e&sig=HyjCNPSI5Zn-R82Uv3MfsmcM1os&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwivnPu529DTAhWlKsAKHeowAM0Q6AEIRDAG#v=snippet&q=polmais&f=false Inquisitionum Ad Capellam Domini Regis Retornatarum, etc. II: Inquisitiones Speciales. Stirling]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "(237) <strong>John Murray of Touchadam and Polmaise</strong>. Will recorded 10th January 1690 (Stirling). Served heir to his father 13th May 1643. M.P., Stirlingshire, 1645-46, 1648, 1661-63. He married Janet, daughter of Sir Wil
2 CONC liam Nisbet of Dean, Provost of Edinburgh, and had issue:-
2 CONT * Major William Murray, baptised 2nd October 1648. Will recorded 27th April 1677 (Stirling). His daughter, Janet, served heir to him 12th February 1691.
2 CONT * John (No. 238 below).
2 CONT * Charles Murray, born 29th May 1660."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://www.archive.org/stream/heraldryofmurray00john#page/56/mode/2up The heraldry of the Murrays: with notes on all the males of the family, descriptions of the arms, plates and pedigrees], by G. Harvey Johnston, 1910, 
2 CONC page 56, paragraph 237
2 CONT
2 CONT "<strong>John Murray, of Polmais and Touchadam</strong>, served heir to his father in January, 1655. He <em>m.</em> Janet, daughter of Sir John Nisbit, of Dean, lord provost of Edinburgh, and was <em>s.</em> by his son."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/genealogicalhera03burk#page/68/mode/2up A genealogical and heraldic history of the commoners of Great Britain and Ireland, enjoying territorial possessions or high official rank; but univested w
2 CONC ith heritable honours]; Vol. III; page 68
