1 NAME Patrick /Nisbet of Craigintinny/ Baronet
2 GIVN Patrick
2 SURN Nisbet of Craigintinny
2 NSFX Baronet
2 _MARNM Nisbet of Craigintinny
2 NICK Sir Patrick Nisbet of Dean
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1682
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == SIR PATRICK NISBET OF CRAIGINTINNY Baronet ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''22 February 1609: Sheriffdom of Midlothian: Instrument of sasine in favour of Patrick Nisbet of Craigintinnie, as heir to Sir Henry Nisbet of Craigintinnie, his father, in subjects in Restalrig. [PRS Edinburgh, 11 March 1669]. 
2 CONC [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f955&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+nisbet&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Brooke Family of Biel, ref
2 CONC erence GD6/955]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [https://archive.org/details/cu31924092524408/page/n293/mode/2up?view=theater&q=Nisbet Biographical Summary] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Patrick Nisbet, of Craigintinny, 1st son and heir of Sir Henry Nisbet, of the same, by Isabella Nicholson, daughter of Thomas Nicholson, of Cockburnspath, was created a Baronet [S.], as above, 2 December 1669, with rem. to heir
2 CONC s male of the body. He, in 1672, exchanged his paternal estate with his 2nd cousin, Alexander Nisbet, of Dean, for the Barony of Dean, county Midlothian. He married Agnes Brown, daughter of James Brown, of Stevenston. He died 1682
2 CONC , when he is said to have been in his 100th year." [https://archive.org/details/cu31924092524408/page/n293/mode/2up?view=theater&q=Nisbet Complete Baronetage 1665 to 1707 by George Edward Cokayne Volume 4 Published 1904 Page 275]'
2 CONC ''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [http://www.stravaiging.com/history/castle/craigentinny-castle Craigentinny Castle Edinburgh - Stravaiging around Scotland]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT James Nisbet was the eldest son of Henry Nisbet, a former Provost of Edinburgh. Later Craigentinny passed to one of James’ grandsons, Sir Patrick Nisbet, who in 1672 exchanged it with his cousin, Alexander Nisbet, for the estate o
2 CONC f Dean. The castle remained in the Nisbet family for the following 90 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.scotlandspeople.gov.uk/search-records/church-registers/church-births-baptisms#form&record_type=opr_births&church_type=Old%20Parish%20Registers&surname=Nisbet&surname_so=soundex&forename_so=soundex&from_year=16
2 CONC 50&to_year=1690&parent_names=Patrick&parent_names_so=exact&parent_name_two=Agnes&parent_name_two_so=exact&sort=asc&order=Date&field=year Scotland's People: Old Parish Registers: Births and Baptisms] NOTE: can't find a David'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Possible list of 12 children of Patrick Nisbet and Agnes Broun from first: 12 April 1657 Marion Nisbet to last: 8 April 1680 Jean Nisbet
2 CONT
2 CONT * 12 April 1657 birth or baptism of Marion Nisbet, daughter of Patrick Nisbet and Agnes Broun [child 1], in the parish of Canongate
2 CONT * 26 June 1659 birth or baptism of Henry Neisbit, son of Patrick Neisbit and Agnes Broune [child 2], in the parish of Leith South
2 CONT * 21 August 1663 birth or baptism of Issobell Neisbit, daughter of Patrick Neisbit and Agnes Broune [child 3], in the parish of Leith South
2 CONT * 23 July 1665 birth or baptism of Agnes Nisbet, daughter of Patrick Nisbet, Baronet, and Agnes Brown [child 4], in the parish of Edinburgh
2 CONT * 9 October 1666 birth or baptism of John Nisbet, son of Patrick Nisbet, Baronet, and Agnes Brown [child 5], in the parish of Edinburgh
2 CONT * 5 November 1667 birth or baptism of Patrick Neisbit, son of Patrick Neisbit and Agnes Broun [child 6], in the parish of Leith South
2 CONT * 9 April 1669 birth or baptism of Catharen Neisbit, daughter of Patrick Neisbit and Agnes Broune [child 7], in the parish of Leith South
2 CONT * 14 January 1673 birth or baptism of James Nisbet, son of Patrick Nisbet, Baronet, and Agnes Brown [child 8], in the parish of Edinburgh
2 CONT * 27 February 1675 birth or baptism of Jonet Nisbet, (U) [son or daughter] of Patrick Nisbet, Baronet, and Agnes Brown [child 9], in the parish of Edinburgh
2 CONT * 20 April 1676 birth or baptism of William Nisbet, son of Patrick Nisbet, Baronet, and Agnes Brown [child 10], in the parish of Edinburgh
2 CONT * 23 June 1678 birth or baptism of Alexander Nisbet, son of Patrick Nisbet, Baronet, and Agnes Brown [child 11], in the parish of Edinburgh
2 CONT * 8 April 1680 birth or baptism of Jean Nisbet, daughter of Patrick Nisbet, Baronet, and Agnes Brown [child 12], in the parish of Edinburgh
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD6%2f956&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Craigintinnie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 22 June 1672 - 6 July 1672: Sheriffdom of Midlothian: Extract bond of warrandice by Alexander Nisbet of Dean to Sir Patrick Nisbet of Craigintinnie, granting the said Sir Patrick an annualrent of 3600 merks furth of twelve oxgates
2 CONC  of land in Restalrig, in real warrandice of the lands and barony of Dean; with instrument of sasine following thereon. [PRS Edinburgh, 10 August 1672].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD237%2f1%2f7&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Craigintinnie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 1672: Bonds, discharges, accounts and related papers
2 CONT
2 CONT Including (1) 22 June 1672: Inventory of writs of lands and barony of Dean disponed by Alexander Nisbet of Dean to Sir Patrick Nisbet of Craigintinnie. Begins with charter of Robert, King of Scots, to Sir William Mure, Knight, dat
2 CONC ed at Breadsheill, 13 January ar 11.[?]
