2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the Register of Interments in Greyfriars Burying-ground ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 November 1665: Jackson. Janet, widow of Patrick Bruce of Newton (above head of Blackfriars Wynd). [https://archive.org/details/registerinterme00socigoog/page/338/mode/1up Greyfriars Interments: p. 338]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''5 July 1627: Charter issued under the Great Seal of Scotland by which Charles I, King of Scotland, confirms to Patrick Bruce, feudatory of Newtoun, and Jonet Jacksoun, his future spouse, possession of various parts of the land 
2 CONC called Newtoun, in the barony of Bothkenner and Sheriffdom of Stirling. The lands in question had previously been resigned by Patrick Bruce in order to obtain a new grant in favour of himself and his future spouse. His resignation
2 CONC  was made with the consent of Jean Flemyng, who retained her own liferent interest. Patrick Bruce and Jonet Jacksoun were to hold this land in conjunct fee and liferent. The land in question was destined to pass to their lawful ma
2 CONC le heirs, whom failing to the lawful heirs of William Bruce of Stenhous. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/387/mode/1up RMS 1620-33: charter number 1101]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''27 May 1630: Instrument of Sasine in favour of Rachel, Janet, Helen and Elizabeth Jackson, [daughters of the said John Jackson,] sisters and heirs portioners of Mr. John Jackson, [portioner of Broughton,] of subjects contained 
2 CONC in GD90/5/1 hereof. [Note] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD90%2f5%2f12&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=john+jackson&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Yule Colle
2 CONC ction, reference GD90/5/12]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: Tenement of land formerly belonging to deceased William Currour, within the tenement of deceased Nicolas Spathie on the north side of the High Street of Edinburgh and two lower fore booths and two annualrents therefrom.''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 December 1630: (Extract) Disposition (registered in the Burgh Court Books of Edinburgh, 7 Jan. 1631), by said Rachel, Janet, Helen and Elizabeth Jackson, with consent of Mr. Harie Foulis, Advocate, spouse of said Rachel, and
2 CONC  of Patrick Bruce of Newtoun, spouse of said Janet, to William Baillie, merchant burgess of Edinburgh, and Margaret Jackson, his spouse, of subjects contained in GD90/5/1 hereof. [Note] [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonli
2 CONC necatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD90%2f5%2f13&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+bruce&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Yule Collection, reference GD90/5/13]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: Tenement of land formerly belonging to deceased William Currour, within the tenement of deceased Nicolas Spathie on the north side of the High Street of Edinburgh and two lower fore booths and two annualrents therefrom.''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registerinterme00socigoog/page/n10/mode/1up Register of Interments in the Greyfriars Burying-ground, Edinburgh, 1658-1700. Edited by Henry Paton, MA., Searcher of Records. (Scottish Record Society, 
2 CONC 1902), 722 pp. including index, notanda and glossary]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
