1 NAME Hillebrand Gilbert /Andersen/
2 GIVN Hillebrand Gilbert
2 _MARNM Andersen
2 NICK Gilbert Andrews Mortimer
2 NICK Skotte
1 NAME Hillebrand /Andersen Martemer/
2 GIVN Hillebrand
2 SURN Andersen Martemer
2 NICK Mortemer
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1583
2 ADDR
3 CITY Montrose
3 STAE Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1629
2 PLAC Stubbekøbing
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 Stubbekøbing Sogn, Falsters Nørre Herred
3 STAE Falster
3 CTRY Denmark
1 OCCU Købmand (Merchant) i Stubbekøbing, Danmark
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/GEN-MEDIEVAL/1999-07/0932588573
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert Andrews Mortimer, or Hillebrand Andersen Skotte, had grandchildren with the name spelled Mortemer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a merchant of Stubbekøbing, perhaps with a branch in Aberdeen, his grandfather's and uncle's city. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hillebrand lived 1607 in Stubbekøbing in Denmark, where he probably already was a merchant as mentioned above, in 1618 he bought a garden in Stubbekøbing, which had formerly belongued to the mayor of the city. In 1618 and 1624 Mor
2 CONC timer was in a fistfight, with some native people. They had to pay him for the pain, so perhaps they had only been after him because of his being a Scotsman.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1628 he might have been the Hillebrand Andersen "of Aberdeen", who sailed from Scotland with soldiers for the danish king Christian IV. The same year he sailed through Elsinore (Helsingør) on the Island of (Seeland) Sjælland in
2 CONC  Denmark. He had then been in Copenhagen to deliver the Soldiers, and was now heading back to Aberdeen, shortly after he must have been back in Denmark, where he died in 1629 and was buried inside the citychurch. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hewas married to Gundel Carstensdatter, a dane, and they had three children Hillebrand Hillebrandsen, Carsten Hillebrandsen and Thomes Hillebrandsen Mortemer. 
