1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Agnes Gray:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p3069.htm#i30681
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Gray [1]
2 CONT *F, #30681
2 CONT *Last Edited=19 Aug 2012
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.07%
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Gray is the daughter of Patrick Gray, 6th Lord Gray and Lady Mary Stewart.[1],[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married William Graham, 7th Earl of Menteith, son of John Graham, 6th Earl of Menteith and Maria Campbell, after 30 March 1612.[2] As a result of her marriage, Agnes Gray was styled as Countess of Menteith after 30 March 1612.
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT From after 30 March 1612, her married name became Graham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Agnes Gray and William Graham, 7th Earl of Menteith
2 CONT *1. Lady Mary Graham+[1] d. 28 Jan 1653
2 CONT *2. Lady Margaret Graham+[3]
2 CONT *3. John Graham, Lord Graham of Kinpont+[4] b. c 1613, d. 6 Sep 1644
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S15] George Edward Cokayne, editor, The Complete Baronetage, 5 volumes (no date (c. 1900); reprint, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 1983), volume II, page 283. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Baronetage.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1642. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *3. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume III, page 519. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *4. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 2, page 2752.
