1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Major-General Gordon was the eldest son of Alexander Gordon of Achintoul, one of the senators of the college of justice, in the reign of King James VII. by his wife, Isobel Gray, daughter to Gray of Braik, brother
2 CONC  to Lord Gray; and was born the 17th of December 1669."
2 CONT
2 CONT from History of Peter the Great
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "Lord Auchintoul married Isobel Gray, 'daughter of Gray of Braik and niece of Lord Gray' (Life, prefixed to Major-Gen. Gordon's Peter the Great}, "with whom he begat three sons and daughters" (Balb. MS., P- 52)."
2 CONT
2 CONT from Coclarachie
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT His (George Gordon's) Son George Gordon fiar of Cockclearichie married Grizell Setton the Laird of Pittmeddens daughter, with whom he begat sons and daughters, George, Alexander and James Gordons. George dyed young. Alexander marr
2 CONC ied Issabel Gray daughter of with whom he begat three sons and daughters, viz, his eldest son Alexander Gordon made Major General in the Muscovite Service..."
2 CONT
2 CONT from Balbithan MS
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.patrickspeople.scot/our%20family/7947.htm
2 CONT
