1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This individual must be Mary Bruce of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muness_Castle Muness].
2 CONT
2 CONT Not ''Bruis''.
2 CONT
2 CONT The time frame here suggests that [https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurence_Bruce Laurence Bruce] is most likely to be her grandfather, in which case Mary's father would be Laurence"s son Andrew Bruce of Muness who inherited the c
2 CONC astle. Hence the name Mary Bruce of Muness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Time frame also supports this because building of the Muness Castle begun, or was finished, so late in 1598.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary probably followed Andrew to Sweden. If she did not, Andrew went to Sweden in 1635, probably at relatively young age.
2 CONT
2 CONT There were two daughters to Andrew Bruce in Geni whose names were "Marjorie". 
2 CONT
2 CONT The first Marjorie was born earlier than the other, and had a family. Therefore the other "Marjorie" is probably a misnomer because the other Marjorie did not die as child, and that makes the other Marjorie likely to be the Mary i
2 CONC n this profile. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The other Marjorie, does not have husband, and the date of his death is not known. The other Marjorie, therefore, has to be the Mary here.
2 CONT
2 CONT I'll add Andrew as his father. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In Laurence's Wikipedia page, a number of relatives and in-laws has been mentioned, and are likely of help in verification / connecting this profile to the rest of the tree.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brock_(adelssl%C3%A6gt)_
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brock_(adelssl%C3%A4kt)_
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fionamsinclair.co.uk/genealogy/isles/Sweden.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN SINCLAIR, married to Mary Bruis of Onovitz [Muness], by whom he had a son ANDREW SINCLAIR, who went to Sweden in 1635, and attained the rank of Colonel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [Andrew Sinclair] He was Governor in Thorn, where he rejected the storm of the enemy eight times successively. He was made Swedish nobleman (Number 965) in 1680, and died in 1689, leaving by his wife, Anna Amendsson, a son, his su
2 CONC ccessor - CHARLES ANDREW SINCLAIR, Colonel in a Regiment of Foot; Major-General, who died in 1753. 
