1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Alexander Logan=
2 CONT
2 CONT Who was Lord Alexander Logan's 2nd or other wife or concubine, the mother of Patrick Logan, to whom Janet Marsden is known to have been only his stepmother?
2 CONT * The name of Logan did not, however, any more than that of MacGregor, disappear altogether from use. Among noted personages of the name was James Logan, who, as secretary, accompanied Penn to Pennsylvania in 1699, and rose throug
2 CONC h many legal offices to be governor of the colony in 1736. The Rev. John Logan, author of the tragedy of "Runnymead," disputes with Michael Bruce the authorship of the exquisite "Ode to the Cuckoo," and some of our finest Paraphra
2 CONC ses. And James Richardson Logan, editor of the Penang Gazette, remains noted for his services to the struggling settlement, and for his scientific contributions to the study of the East. Logan of that ilk in Ayrshire, the last of 
2 CONC his house, has left a name for wit and eccentricity, though the volume of drolleries published under the title of The Laird of Logan can only in part be attributed to him.\
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married= 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000010471342633?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000227625479830  '''Jennett Merstone'''] on 2 Jan 1616 in Tranent, Haddingtonshire, Scotland
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ...ALEXANDER, JONET, AND ANNE are named in the Testament Dative of 1607, and in 1616 they are granted a reversal of attainder, on the grounds of their being at the time of their father's forfeiture all minors and had not participa
2 CONC ted in any of his crimes. This restored them tho their former good fame and gave them the right to enjoy any lands they might acquire, otherwise than by succession to their father.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
