1 NAME Magdalene /Scrimgeour/
2 GIVN Magdalene
2 SURN Scrimgeour
2 _MARNM Scrimgeour
2 NICK Magdalene Irvine
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1574
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1630
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == DAME MAGDALENE SCRIMGEOUR ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''A date and place of death has not been identified for Dame Magdalene Scrimgeour. She was alive on 6 January 1664, [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f1%2f594&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=
2 CONC n&tp=n&k=Magdalen+Scrymgeor&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD112/1/594] but she died before 24 March 1683.  [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f1709&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp
2 CONC =n&k=sir+alexander+irvine&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n NRS: GD45/16/1709]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''6 January 1664: Extract tack by dame Magdalen Scrymgeor, relict of Sir Alexander Irwin of Drum, to Francis Irwin, youngest son of granter and said Alexander, of her liferent conjunct fee lands of Auchtetoull and others all in C
2 CONC romarre in parishes of Coull, Logie, Tarland and Aboyne, sheriffdom of Aberdeen, for her lifetime. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD112%2f1%2f594&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Magdalen+
2 CONC Scrymgeor&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Campbell Family, Earls of Breadalbane (Breadalbane Muniments), reference GD112/1/594]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 March 1683: Decree of transference at instance of Alexander Irvine of Drum as heir to his deceased father, Sir Alexander Irvine of Drum, against the heirs and executors of the deceased Dame Magdalen Scrymgeor, relict of the 
2 CONC said Sir Alexander, and the heirs and executors of the deceased Charles and Francis Irvine, sons of the said Sir Alexander, in respect of a summons and action of reduction and improbation at instance of the said Alexander against 
2 CONC the said Dame Magdalen, the said Charles and Francis, her sons, and Anna, Elizabeth, Jean, Isobel and Margaret, her daughters, the summons dated 22 July 1657. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?re
2 CONC ference=GD45%2f16%2f1709&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+alexander+irvine&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Maule Family, Earls of Dalhousie, Titles to Land, reference GD45/16/1709]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 April 1684: Decree of certification following on GD45/16/1709 in respect of a bond by the deceased Sir Alexander Irvine of Drum to the deceased Dame Magdalen Scrymgeour, his wife, dated 20 April 1652. [https://catalogue.nrsc
2 CONC otland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD45%2f16%2f1710&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=sir+alexander+irvine&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Maule Family, Earls of Dalhousie, T
2 CONC itles to Land, reference GD45/16/1710]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Notes ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1617 Married: Magdalen eldest daughter of Sir John Scrimgeour of Dudhope, Constable of Dundee. Page 14, Forbes Leslie.
