4 CONT Warres, are now among the family relics in possession of Mrs. Walter Brooke of Washington, having been brought to this country by her great-great-grandfather, Sir Thomas West ; and, so precious was the porcelain heirloom, that whe
4 CONC n broken, a hundred years ago, it was sent to England to be repaired with bands of silver. After the Revolution, the law of entail being set aside, the estate of West Point was divided among the several children of Mr. John West a
4 CONC nd Elizabeth Seaton, his wife. Their elder son, Thomas, married
