4 CONT immortal Patrick Henry. Colonel John Henry, a native of Aberdeen, Scotland, and nephew of the historian Robertson, came to this country in quest of fortune, enjoying the patronage and friendship of Governor Dinwiddie of Virginia, 
4 CONC by whom he was introduced to Colonel Syme of Hanover,
4 CONT whose wife was Miss Sarah Winston, in whose family he became domesticated, and whose widow he subsequently married, continuing to reside on the family estate of Studleigh, where their son Patrick Henry
4 CONT was born.
