1 TITL 1st Lord of Kinnaird
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>George Kinnaird</strong>, the second son, acquired all the family properties from his brother John in 1660. A staunch royalist, he was knighted by King Charles II in 1661, and made a Privy Councillor. A Sir George Kinnair
2 CONC d of Rossie he sat in Parliament for Perthshire 1661-63...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...On 28 December 1682 he was created <strong>Lord Kinnaird</strong> of Inchture, with remainder to the heirs-male of his body. He was one of those who voted for the execution of Argyll in 1685. He did not live many years after th
2 CONC is, dying on 29 December 1689. He married, 19 November 1650, Margaret, daughter of James Crichton of Ruthven. She died 31 October 1704."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun05pauluoft#page/208/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. V, page 209
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
