1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to Burke's, had ten sons and 5 daughters. [However, where is a listing of them?]
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in 1668, the 2nd Baronet of Birkenbog in Banffshire, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1705 in Fife, Scotland, he married Mary Gordon, who was born in Stralock, Scotland in 1687, daughter of Sir Arthur Gordon.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir James Abercromby of Birkenbog, 2nd Baronet</strong> (c. 1670 – 20 September 1734) was a Scottish baronet and politician...
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ...He was the oldest son of Sir Alexander Abercromby, 1st Baronet and his third wife Elizabeth Baird, daughter of Sir James Baird. Abercromby succeeded his father as baronet in 1684. He entered the Parliament of Scotland in 1693, 
2 CONC sitting as a Member of Parliament (MP) for Banffshire until 1702...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...In 1645, Abercromby married Mary Gordon, daughter of Arthur Gordon. They had fifteen children, ten sons and five daughters. Abercromby was succeeded in the baronetcy by his third and oldest surviving son Robert."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'Sir James Abercromby, 2nd Baronet', <em>Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia</em>, 5 August 2012, 11:46 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Sir_James_Abercromby,_2nd_Baronet&oldid=50588835
2 CONC 5> [accessed 17 September 2012]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
