1 NAME Alexander /Abercromby/ 1st of Tullibody
2 GIVN Alexander
2 SURN Abercromby
2 NSFX 1st of Tullibody
2 _MARNM Abercromby
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1675
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1753
1 OCCU an Advocate
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alexander Abercrombie, 1st of Tullibody, was the second son of Sir Alexander Abercromby (1608-84), 1st baronet of Birkenbog. and his third wife, Elizabeth, dau of Sir James Baird of Auchmeddan.  He settled at Tulli
2 CONC body in Clackmannanshire, which he inherited from cousin George Abercromby of Tullibody & Skeith, succeeding to the honor of Tullibody after the latter's death 29 June 1699. Alexander was MP for Clackmannanshire 1703-07. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He also bought Menstrie Castle (Clackmannanshire) in 1719.  His son, George Abercromby (1705-1800) purchased the Brucefield (Clackmannanshire) estate in about 1758. (For photos and histories of the houses, see https://landedfamili
2 CONC es.blogspot.com/2013/02/abercromby-of-tullibody-and-airthrey.html).
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary Duff, daughter of Alexander Duff of Braco. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in March 1753.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT * George, 2nd of Tullibody bap 8 Jul 1705
2 CONT * Alexander bap 27 May 1707, of Alloa, m. 1732 Rebecca, dau of Alexander Colquhoun
2 CONT * James bap 24 Aug 1708 (1707-75) of Brucefield; educated at Westminster, University of Leiden, Lincolns Inn (called to bar, 1738); attorney general of South Carolina, 1731-44; member of South Carolina Assembly, 1739-45; agent in 
2 CONC London for North Carolina and Virginia, 1745-71; MP for Clackmannanshire 1761-68; deputy auditor-general of plantations 1757-65. Lived on his brother George’s Brucefield estate (Clackmannanshire), 1757-75, and owned substantial pr
2 CONC operty (nearly 7,000 acres) in South Carolina.
2 CONT * John bap 1 May 1722
2 CONT * William bap 28 May 1723
2 CONT * Robert bap 28 Oct 1724
2 CONT * Mary bap 14 Dec 1710. Died young.
2 CONT * Helen bap 14 Jan 1713 married Sir Robert Abercrombie, 3rd of Birkenbog
2 CONT * Anna bap 17 Jan 1719
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Red Book of Scotland (http://redbookofscotland.co.uk/abercromby-of-tullibody), https://landedfamilies.blogspot.com/2013/02/abercromby-of-tullibody-and-airthrey.html
