1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Stewart,_9th_Seigneur_d%27Aubigny
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a descendant of Cardinal Beaton.
2 CONT
2 CONT After her husband was killed at the Battle of Edgehill, she acted as a spy during the Civil War. In 1643, hidden in her ringlets, shea secretly carried a commission from Charles I to plot an uprising in London, but was caught and 
2 CONC imprisoned in the Tower of London for a year, unsuccessfully arguing that her French title made her a subject of the King of France and thus immune from arrest.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1648 she engineered a plot to try and rescue Charles I from captivity, but this failed and she fled to The Hague where she died in 1650
