1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>William Lyon, of Wester Ogil</strong>, born Wester Ogil, 9th Oct. 1675, second son of George L. of Wester Ogil, and Jean, daugh. of Sir William Nisbet of Dean, and nephew of preceding; educated at Forfar Academy and Univ. 
2 CONC of St Andrews; licen. by United Presb. of Dundee and Forfar in 1700; elected by heads of families in July ; ord. 25th Sept. 1700 ; served heir to his father 21st Jan. 1703 (his elder brother John having died) to the lands of Milnt
2 CONC own of Ogil and others in the parish of Tannadice, and on 6th Oct. 1704 to the life-rent rights of Wester Ogil. He supported the Government in 1715, and through his influence prevented his parishioners joining the Earl of Mar. He 
2 CONC joined in a dissent against a judgment of the Presb. of Dundee condemnatory of the voluntary opinions of his brother-in-law, John Glas, min. of Tealing, and carried his dissent to the Commission of Assembly March 1730. He maintain
2 CONC ed all the ecclesiastical buildings during his ministry at his own expense, spending over £1000. He died suddenly, 4th Jan. 1743. He marr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) 16th Nov. 1704, Jean, daugh. of David Melvill of Pitgarvy, and had issue — 
2 CONT * Jean, born 8th June 1708 (marr. as his second wife, Alexander Moncrieff of Culfargie, min. of Abernethy) ; 
2 CONT * Margaret, born 5th Aug. 1709, died young; 
2 CONT * George of Wester Ogil, min. of Longforgan
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) 16th Dec. 1719, Agnes (died 24th April 1778), daugh. of Alexander Glas, min. of Kinclaven, and had issue — 
2 CONT * Christian, born 16th Sept. 1720, died unmarr. 16th Dec. 1783 ; 
2 CONT * William, solicitor, Dundee, and commissary clerk of St Andrews, born 2nd June 1722, died 27th Aug. 1803 
2 CONT * Katherine, born 13th July 1723, died 1743 
2 CONT * Alexander, born 10th July 1725, died 1764 
2 CONT * John, born 15th Feb. 1727, died in infancy 
2 CONT * Margaret, born 22nd Aug. 1729, died in infancy
2 CONT * Elizabeth, born 21st Dec. 1730, died unmarr. 9th Jan. 1801 ; 
2 CONT * Robert, merchant, Dundee, born 16th Aug. 1733, died 14th Sept. 1801 ; 
2 CONT * Thomas, born 14th Aug. 1736, died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/fastiecclesiaesc05scot#page/246/mode/2up Fasti ecclesiae scoticanae: the succession of ministers in the Church of Scotland from the reformation], Vol. V, page 247
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
