1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''From [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Hamilton,_2nd_Earl_of_Haddington Wikipedia - Thomas Hamilton, 2nd Earl of Haddington]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Hamilton, 2nd Earl of Haddington (Thursday, 25 May 1600 – Thursday, 30 August 1640) was a Scottish nobleman.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Life''
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Hamilton, Lord Binning was the eldest son of Thomas Hamilton, 1st Earl of Haddington and his second wife, Margaret Foulis of Colinton. Until his accession to his father's Earldom, he was known by the courtesy title Lord Bin
2 CONC ning. Following education abroad Binning returned to Scotland where he attended Parliament in 1621. Binning attended his father at the funeral of King James in London, and later was a canopy bearer during Charles I's 1633 coronati
2 CONC on in Edinburgh at Holyrood Abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Binning succeeded to his father's titles in 1637, and the following year, at the King's urging, signed the National Covenant. At the start of the Bishops' War, Haddington was commissioned Major General for the Lothians, under Gene
2 CONC ral Leslie. When General Leslie advanced into England in 1640, he left armaments behind at Duns, Haddington retrieved them back to his headquarters at Dunglass Castle, to prevent their capture by the English garrison at Berwick up
2 CONC on Tweed. On Wednesday, 29 August 1640, he beat back an attempt of the garrison of Berwick to capture a magazine of victuals and arms near Coldstream.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Thursday, 30 August 1640, a huge explosion took place in the powder magazine of the castle, destroying it. Haddington, who was standing in the courtyard reading correspondence from Leslie to his kinsfolk and men, was killed. Ot
2 CONC hers killed were Haddington's brother, Robert Hamilton of Wester Binning; his natural brother, Patrick Hamilton; his cousins John Hamilton of Redhouse and Alexander Hamilton of Innerwick; Alexander's son, Haddington's brother-in-l
2 CONC aw, Colonel Sir John Erskine; and the Minister of Bonkyl Kirk, Master John Gaittis.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Marriage and Issue''
2 CONT
2 CONT Haddington married Lady Catherine Erskine (died1635), daughter of John Erskine, Earl of Mar and Lady Mary Stuart, herself a daughter of Esmé Stewart, 1st Duke of Lennox, and by her had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Thomas Hamilton, 3rd Earl of Haddington
2 CONT * John Hamilton, 4th Earl of Haddington
2 CONT * Hon. Robert Hamilton died in infancy
2 CONT * Hon. James Hamilton died in infancy
2 CONT * Lady Margaret Hamilton died in infancy
2 CONT
2 CONT Following his Countess's death in 1635, Haddington married secondly in 1640 to Lady Jean Gordon, daughter of George Gordon, 2nd Marquess of Huntly, and Lady Anne Campbell, herself a daughter of Archibald Campbell, 7th Earl of Argy
2 CONC ll and by her had issue a posthumous daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Lady Margaret Hamilton, married John Keith, 1st Earl of Kintore.
