1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===SIR JOHN HAMILTON OF TRABROUN===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sir John Hamilton of Trabroun is the son of Thomas Hamilton, first Earl of Haddington, and his second wife, Margaret Foulis. He was born on 3 November 1605. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/314/mode/
2 CONC 1up/search/anna+bannatyne The Scots Peerage IV: 314]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===His Testament Dative and Inventory===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Confirmation was granted on 24 February 1639. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Dative and Inventory of Sir John Hammiltoun of Traboun, knight, reference CC8/8/58]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Evidence from the National Records of Scotland===
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1607-1621: James Heriot of Trabroun, as heir of deceased James Heriot of Trabroun, his father, (1607) John Hamiltoun, younger son of Thomas Hamiltoun of Byris, kt., H.M. advocate, (1611) great seal charter of confirmation, 2 Fe
2 CONC bruary 1619, RMS vii/1972 (of charter of 1611) John Hamiltoun of Trabroun and Katherine Peblis, his future spouse, (1621) With a receipt by Fraser for 6 unspecified documents from this bundle, and a note of two others also removed
2 CONC , 25 Oct 1531 and 23 Jan 1486/7. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD157%2f388&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=katherine+peblis&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers 
2 CONC of the Scott Family of Harden, Lords Polwarth, Berwickshire, reference GD157/388]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
