2 CONT '''20 July 1621: (Extract) Marriage Contract between Thomas, earl of Melros, Lord Byres and Bineing, president of the College of Justice and secretary to the King, and John Hammilton of Trabroun, his third lawful son, with consent
2 CONC  of Sir Andrew Hammiltoun of Reidhous, knight, one of the senators of the College of Justice, Sir James Foulles of Coleintoun, Mr. Patrick Hammiltoun of Prestoun, and George Foulles, master coiner to the King, his curators, on the
2 CONC  one part, and Mr. Alexander Peibles of Skirling, advocate, and Agnes McKartney, his spouse, and Katherine Peibles, their only daughter, containing procuratories of resignation of said John Hammiltoun's lands of Trabroun in Berwic
2 CONC kshire and of said Alexander Peible's lands and barony of Skirling and others for new infeftment in favour of the intended spouses (said John and Katherine) under reservation of the liferents specified. Dated 20 July, 1621 and rec
2 CONC orded in the Books of Council and Session, 2 January, 1634. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD89%2f1%2f59&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=trabroun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1620&dt=1640&di=y National
2 CONC  Records of Scotland, Papers of the Carmichael Family of Skirling, reference GD89/1/59]'''
