2 CONT '''3 August 1621: [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/69/mode/1up RMS VIII: 217]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''3 July 1629: Crown Charter of Resignation following on a procuratory of resignation by said Sir John Hammiltone of Trabroun and his spouse, in favour of Thomas, their eldest lawful son, under reversion to said Sir John, of the 
2 CONC lands of Trabroun and the lands and barony of Skirling, 3 July, 1629
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note: This charter was published in full in [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi08scot/page/485/mode/1up RMS VIII: 1437] Previous to the sale to Hamilton of Broomhill, Trabroun appears to have appointed his son to the 
2 CONC succession under reversion but the latter died infeft in the lands and the impediment in the title was not observed until after the sale by Mr. John Hamilton to Mr. James Livingstone (see GD89/1/84, 91, 95)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''24 December 1633: (Extract) Disposition by Sir John Hamiltoun of Trabroun, with consent of Dame Katharine Peiblis, his spouse, and of Thomas, Lord Binning, his nephew and Sir James Hamiltoun of Priestfield, his brother, of (1) 
2 CONC the Meikle Mains of Skirling and the Kirklandhill to Sir James Hamiltoun of Broomehill, in liferent, and John H., younger, of Broomehill, his eldest son, and Margaret H., his spouse, in conjunct fee and (2) the other lands and bar
2 CONC ony of Skirling, with the templelands, to said Sir James in liferent and his said son in fee, 24 and 30 December, 1633 [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD89%2f1%2f66&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n
2 CONC &tp=n&k=skirling&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1620&dt=1670&di=yNational Records of Scotland, Papers of the Carmichael Family of Skirling, reference GD89/1/66]''' 
