2 CONT '''6 February 1649: Extract marriage contract dated 27 November 1639 between Mr Laurence Rollock [Rollo], third son of Sir Andrew Rollok [Rollo] of Duncrub, and Katherine Peblis [Peebles], daughter of Alexander Peblis [Peebles] of
2 CONC  Chappelhill and deceased Elizabeth Gaw [Gall], his spouse, with consent of her said father; whereby the parties agreed to marry and the said Mr Laurence Rollok and with him Sir James Rollok [Rollo], fiar of Duncrub, his brother-g
2 CONC erman, bound themselves to lay out upon land or annualrents the sum of 8,000 merks for behoof of the future spouses, survivor and heirs, with the advice of the said Alexander Peblis and, failing him, with the advice of Lady Kather
2 CONC ine Peblis [Peebles], widow of Sir John Hamyltoune [Hamilton] of Trabroun, and William Bonnare [Bonar] of Keltie [Kelty], and the said Laurence Rollik bound himself to lay out the money received from Alexander Peblis by way of toc
2 CONC her upon lands or annualrent for behoof of himself and his future spouse, survivor and heirs; and on the other part the said Alexander Peblis of Chappellhill bound himself to pay a certain sum [blank] by way of tocher, to the said
2 CONC  Mr Laurence Rollok reserving the annualrent thereof to himself during his lifetime; and the said Katharine Peblis bound herself to resign certain heritages, to which she succeeded on the death of Elizabeth Gaw her mother and her 
2 CONC sister, for new infeftments in favour of her future spouse and herself, and to assign certain sums of money, to which she had succeeded, to the said Mr Laurence to be laid out on lands and annualrents for their behoof, and provisi
2 CONC on was made that if there were children of the marriage the said Katharine should have a right of liferent only to the said lands and sums of money pertaining to her, provided to her by her father, and to which she succeeded by th
2 CONC e death of her mother and sister, together with the annualrent of the sum of 3,000 merks provied by the said Mr Laurence from his own estate; and that, if there were no children, Katharine should have right of liferent to all the 
2 CONC above sums provided by herself and Mr Laurence, and to leave the sum of 3,500 merks to whomsoever she pleased during her lifetime after the death of her future spouse. [Damaged]. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalo
2 CONC gue/details.aspx?reference=GD56%2f68&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=Hamilton+of+Trabroun&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Rollo family of Duncrub, Perthshire, reference GD56/68]'''
2 CONT
