1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Alexander Foulis, <em>Fear of Colinton</em></strong>, co. Edinburgh, only son and heir apparent of Sir James Foulis of Colinton, Advocate [S] 1576, and sometime [1612] M.P. [S] for Edinburgh, by Mary, daughter of Sir John
2 CONC  Lauder of Hatton, was created a Baronet [S] 7 June, sealed 22 July 1634 but not recorded in the Great Seal Register [S], with rem. to heirs male watsoever, and with a grant of , presumably, 16,000 acres in Nova Scotia, of which h
2 CONC e had seizin in August 1634. He married v.p. (settlement 30 March 1619) Elizabeth, widow of Sir John Stewart, of Bute, 1st daughter and coheir of Robert Hepburn of Foord, co. Edinburgh. He was living 7 August 1643, and probably in
2 CONC  1663, but was dead in 1672."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n419/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II, page 401
