2 DATE 1658
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == THOMAS HEPBURN OF HUMBIE ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Misinformation'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''Contrary to what has been claimed elsewhere, Thomas Hepburn of Humbie, here treated, was not a knight. Nor did he die on 17 August 1661. It should also be said that he was probably not born at Humbie in East Lothian
2 CONC . His baptism was registered at Edinburgh and it seems quite likely, probable even, that he was born there. [https://www.ancestry.co.uk/genealogy/records/sir-thomas-hepburn-of-humbie-24-12fwqq6?geo_a=r&o_iid=41013&o_lid=41013&o_sc
2 CONC h=Web+Property Ancestry]'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Birth and Baptism ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Hepburn of Humbie, here treated, is the eldest son of Sir Adam Hepburn of Humbie and his wife Agnes Fowlis. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD1%2f199%2f12&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=
2 CONC n&tp=n&k=agnes+foulis&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1670&di=n NRS: GD1/199/12] He was born before 14/11/1631, the date upon which his baptism was registered at Edinburgh in Midlothian, in the Kingdom of Scotland. He was probably born in
2 CONC  Edinburgh. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Baptisms, 1630-42, reference OPR.685/1/4]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == His Last Will and Testament ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Hepburn of Humbie made his last will and testament on 13 December 1658. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD34%2f611&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hepburn+of+humbie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&d
2 CONC f=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD34/611] Confirmation was granted on 17 August 1661. [National Records of Scotland, Edinburgh Commissary Court, The Testament Testamentar and Inventory of Thomas Hepburne of Humbie, reference CC8/8/70]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Death ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Hepburn of Humbie died in 1658. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD157%2f3022&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hepburn+of+humbie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y NRS: GD157/3022]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT . 
2 CONT == Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Elizabeth Johnstoun, here treated, married Thomas Hepburn of Humbie. The marriage was booked on 9 December 1657, at Humbie in East Lothian, Scotland. [National Records of Scotland, Humbie Marriages, reference OPR.710/1]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT # https://www.geni.com/people/Helen-Scott-Dowager-Countess-of-Tarras/6000000017212000690?from_flash=1&fsession_id=1554576829375&through=6000000073423933156
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''29 July 1637: Instrument of Resignation narrating resignation by Sir John Lawsoun of Humbie, Kt., Bt., with consent of Mr. William Cokburne of Vogrie, in the hands of the King, of said lands of Gilkirstoun, with the mill, and W
2 CONC ansyd, in favour of Mr. Adame Hepburne, clerk of H.M. taxation, and Agnes Foulis, his spouse, in liferent, and to Thomas Hepburne, their eldest son, in fee. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?refe
2 CONC rence=GD1%2f199%2f12&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=agnes+foulis&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=1600&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, East and West Lothian Titles, reference GD1/199/12]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''8 Novemver 1657: Antenuptial contract of marriage between Thomas Hepburne of Humbie and Elizabeth Johnstoun, eldest daughter of Sir Archibald Johnstoun of Wariestoun, kt., clerk of register. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/
2 CONC nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD157%2f3017&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hepburne+of+humbie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott Family of Harden, Lords Polwarth, Berwickshire, refer
2 CONC ence GD157/3017]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 November 1658: Extract certificate of baptism of Helen, daughter of Thomas Hepburn of Humbie and Elizabeth Johnstoun, his wife. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD157%2f3019&st=1&t
2 CONC c=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hepburn+of+humbie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott Family of Harden, Lords Polwarth, Berwickshire, reference GD157/3019]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1659: Helen Hepburne, as heir of deceased Thomas Hepburne of Humbie, her father, 1659. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD157%2f3022&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hepburn+of+humbie&ko=p
2 CONC &r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott Family of Harden, Lords Polwarth, Berwickshire, reference GD157/3022]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''15 June 1663: Summons at the instance of Mr Andrew Hay, brother of Mr John Hay of Haystown [Haystoun], against Helen Hepburne, only daughter and heir of the deceased Thomas Hepburne [Hepburn] of Humbie, for payment of 5,000 mer
2 CONC ks disponed to him by the said deceased Thomas Hepburne by his latter will and testament dated 13 December 1658. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD34%2f611&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=h
2 CONC epburn+of+humbie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the family of Hay of Haystoun, Peeblesshire, reference GD34/611]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     6
2 CONT
2 CONT '''7 February 1678: Bond by George, Lord Melvill [Melville], on behalf of Duke and Duchess of Buccleuch and Monmouth, to Walter, Earl of Tarras, whereby, said Walter having granted a renunciation of marriage contract, dated 9 Febr
2 CONC uary 1659 between himself and deceased Mary, Countess of Buccleuch, said Duke and Duchess are bound to pay him £24,000 Scots, with the provision that if Lady Helen Hepburn, now spouse of said Walter, daughter of deceased Thomas He
2 CONC pburn, Laird of Humbie, succeeded in her action to be declared heir of line and tailzie to her said father, or otherwise recover the estate and lands of Humbie, or gain, either in land or money the sum of 100,000 merks in lieu of 
2 CONC said estate, then said bond was to be null and void. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD26%2f5%2f447&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=tarras&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=1700&di=y National Records of 
2 CONC Scotland, Papers of the Leslie family, Earls of Leven and Melville, reference GD26/5/447]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     7
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 June 1682: Ratification by Helen, countess of Tarras, of decreets 28 February 1663, 2, 13 June 1682. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD157%2f3024&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hepbur
2 CONC n+of+humbie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott Family of Harden, Lords Polwarth, Berwickshire, reference GD157/3024]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     8
2 CONT
2 CONT '''X 1691: Papers in action over estate of Humbie, claimed by Helen Hepburne as only child of Thomas Hepburne of Humbie, and by Adam Hepburne of Trabroun, his brother, as heir male. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecat
2 CONC alogue/details.aspx?reference=GD157%2f3025&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=hepburne+of+humbie&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=y National Records of Scotland, Papers of the Scott Family of Harden, Lords Polwarth, Berwickshire, reference GD157/3
2 CONC 025]'''
