2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Home,_Lord_Renton
2 CONT
2 CONT John Home was the son of Sir Alexander Home of Renton and Margaret Cockburn. Alexander Home was Sheriff of Berwickshire from 1616 to 1621.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Home wrote to his cousin Sir Patrick Home of Polworth that his father had conducted eight witch trials in his jurisdiction.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Renton married (1) (contract dated 15 February 1622) Janet, daughter of Sir George Home of Manderston. They had at least three sons, of whom:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sir Patrick Home of Lumsden, Bt., whose male issue became extinct in the person of his grandson in 1783.
2 CONT # Charles, who, in an action about his share of his father's estate, was designed third lawful son of the late Sir John Home of Renton.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getperson.php?personID=I46302&tree=CC
2 CONT * https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Home,_Lord_Renton
