2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''4 December 1652: Disposition and Declaration of trust by the said Sir James Dundas in favor of Robert Dundas of Harvieston his Brother German, whereby the said lands of Godscroft, Malcolmshiell, and Luckieshiell, with the Desk 
2 CONC or seat in the Church of St. Bothens, are disponed to the said Robert Dundas, in regard that the money paid for the same by the above Robert Home was the proper money of the said Robert Dundas [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/
2 CONC nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD267%2f26%2f25%2f563&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=dundas+of+harvieston&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Title Deeds of the lands and estate of Billie, Berwickshire, r
2 CONC eference GD267/26/25/563]'''
2 CONT
