1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Robert, second Lord</strong>, succeeded his uncle on 25 August 1662, and was served heir to him on 6 November 1662. He married, at Falkland, 19 August 1662, Margaret, eldest daughter of David Wemyss of Fingask, and died a
2 CONC t Cleish 12 February 1671. His widow was committed prisoner to the Tolbooth of Edinburgh, 2 December 1684, for bringing up her son in fanaticism and in disloyalty, and putting him out of the way when the Privy Council was going to
2 CONC  commit his education to others. He had issue : 
2 CONT * Robert, third Lord. 
2 CONT * Margaret, married, as second wife in 1701, to Sir John Ayton of Ayton, Fifeshire, who died in 1703, and had issue : 
2 CONT ** Robert, who assumed the name of Colvill on succeeding to Ochiltree on the death of his uncle, and married Janet, eldest daughter of Sir Peter Wedderburn of Gosford, Bart., and had issue. 
2 CONT ** Andrew, whose descendants succeeded to Craigflower. 
2 CONT * Mary, who married the Rev. Allan Logan of that Ilk, minister of Torryburn 1695, and of Culross 1717, till his death in September 1733. She survived him, and died before 19 November 1739."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun02pauluoft#page/572/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. II, page 573
