1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Not a known son of https://www.geni.com/people/Laurence-Oliphant-2nd-of-Gask/6000000003613958946?through=6000000003613958356 & https://www.geni.com/people/Lilias-Oliphant/6000000003613958940?through=6000000003613958356
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From “John Oliphant and Janet Gilchrist: From Leith to Perth Amboy.” ''Oliphant Clan and Family Association of North America'' < [https://www.oliphantofnorthamerica.org/johnandjanet link] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Not much is known about John and Janet. It was once claimed the possibility of [https://www.geni.com/people/Duncan-Oliphant/6000000001384006680 Duncan Oliphant]  being the son of [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Oliphant/6000000
2 CONC 003613958356?through=6000000003613958364 John]  and [https://www.geni.com/people/Janet-Oliphant/6000000003613958364?through=6000000001384006680 Janet], due to their proximity, but now this is no longer believed. First, because bot
2 CONC h locations had a large Scottish populations due to the emigration of Covenanters, and secondly merely because amateur historians like to find answers, even if the facts sometimes don’t work.  … <BR>
2 CONT
2 CONT >On August 19th, 1685 John and Janet signed their indenture to gain passage to the New World. The couple sailed on the Henry and Francis, and is assumed they set off out of Leith on September 5th, 1685. John Hancock (not the famou
2 CONC s one) of Edinburgh held their indenture, as well as the indenture of three men convicted and sentenced to the Colonies. It’s to be noted that none of the people who signed indenture to Hancock indicated any trade. This is unusual
2 CONC , considering the cost that went into transport and living, so it can be assumed that the people themselves – not the duties they could do – were more important to their debtor. Since John and Janet signed their indenture less tha
2 CONC n a month before sailing, it could be reasoned that it was to follow and support someone important to them. Perth Amboy, the destined city, had only been settled 3 years earlier, so the decision to move to an unknown and barely ci
2 CONC vilized land was a major decision for two illiterate 40 somethings from the Scottish countryside. As far as we can tell, they had barely traveled 20 miles in their entire lives, but had decided to move 4,793 miles in less than a m
2 CONC onth’s time. <BR>
2 CONT >From then on, there is no more mention of John and Janet. What we can do is make educated guesses on their American experience. <BR>
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Oliphant and Janet Gilchrist (Abt 1641 - )  married 15 Feb 1662/63 Place: Kilconquhar, Fife, Scotland 3
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children born in Scotland were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Margaret Oliphant (Feb 1671/72 - Aft 1723).  Married Samuel Layton, 1691, Middleton, NJ.
2 CONT # Eupham Oliphant (1672 - 1672) (died young) 
2 CONT # Janet Oliphant (Abt 1674 - Aft Apr 1734).  Married William Davison around 1695. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT On 19 Aug 1685 in Edinburgh, John Oliphant of Pencaitland signed an indenture of service for himself, his wife Janet Gilchrist, daughters Margret and Janet Oliphant, to John Hancock of Edinburgh as servants in East New Jersey for 
2 CONC four years, the daughters until they are 21 - in return for 25 acres. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They departed Scotland aboard the “Henry and Francis” on 5 Sep 1685 in Leith, Midlothian, arriving on  7 Dec 1685 in Perth Amboy, New Jersey.  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT *  https://www.geni.com/people/William-Oliphant/6000000003613958952?through=6000000003613958356 (Abt 1664 - )  Transported prisoner. (Covenanter).  Living in Monmouth NJ on 14 Jul 1690. From https://www.oliphantofnorthamerica.org/
2 CONC johnandjanet: “Janet and her sister Margaret are also seen in a set of wills concerning William Oliphant. At one time William was thought to be John and Janet’s son, but he is a little too young for this to be possible. They did a
2 CONC ll sail together on the Henry and Francis so it is possible they were some other relation.”
2 CONT *Removed death data of November 02, 1707 (64)  Edinburgh, SCT Place of Burial:	Greyfriars Kirkyard, Edinburgh, Edinburgh, Scotland, United Kingdom
2 CONT * Removed birth data of July 30, 1643, Saint Monance, Fife, Scotland 
2 CONT ----
