1 NOTE {geni:about_me} lie. James Mackay of Kirtomy, son of John Mackay I. of Strathy, had sasine on a contract of wadset, 6th July, 1670, of the four pennylands of Kirtomy and the two pennylands of Swordlie. He m. Mary, dau. of the Hon.
2 CONC  Sir James Fraser of Brae, son of Simon, Lord Lovat, and had known issue three children : —
2 CONT * i. John, of whom follows.
2 CONT * ii. James of Borgiemore, had a wadset of Borgiemore of which hetook sasine, 15th September', 1705. He m. Elizabeth, dau. of Rev. D. Munro, Beay, and had issue :—Margaret, heiress of Borgie, who m. her cousin, Ensign James Mackay
2 CONC , younger of Kirtomy, as will appear.
2 CONT * iii. Madeline, m. John Fearn, Balchladich.
2 CONT
2 CONT pg. 318
2 CONT
2 CONT THE BOOK OF MACKAY BY ANGUS MACKAY, M.A. (St. Andrews University) Minister at Westerdale, Caithness EDINBURGH : NORMAN MACLEOD,  -25 GEORGE IV. BRIDGE CANADA : EDWARD MACKAY, ST. PETER'S MANSE, MADOC, ONT. M DCCCC VI
2 CONT
2 CONT =================
2 CONT
2 CONT  THE STRATIIY BRANCH OF MACKAYS.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Mackay of Kwtomy, third son of John of Dirlet and Strathy, had sasine in the lands of Kirtomy' and Swordly, dated 30th June 1670; he married Jane, third daughter of the Hon. Sir James Fraser of Brea, third son of Simon Lord 
2 CONC Lovat : issue, two sons, 
2 CONT * John of Kirtomy, and  
2 CONT * James of Borgy ; and a daughter,  
2 CONT * Magdaline, married to John Fearn of Balachladicb. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pg  573  .HISTORY THE HOUSE AND CLAN MACKAY,BY ROBERT MACKAY, 1829
