2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ha. John Mackay of Skerray, son of Hugh Mackay I. of Strathy, was captured at Balveny in 1649, appointed a commissioner of supply for the shire of Sutherland in 1685 and again in 1690 (Records of Pari.). He obtaine
2 CONC d in wadset the town and lands of Skerray-Horisdale, port and strath thereof, 28th November, 1659, and m. Margaret, dau. of Hector Munro of Eriboll. He was alive in 1709, and had four known children :—
2 CONT * i. John, d. without issue before 1679.
2 CONT * ii. Hector, of whom follows.
2 CONT * iii. Donald, a notary public in Skerray, Strathan-Tongue...
2 CONT * iv. Hugh of Cairnloch, of whom afterwards as Illb.
2 CONT
2 CONT pg. 314-315
2 CONT
2 CONT THE BOOK OF MACKAY BY ANGUS MACKAY, M.A. (St. Andrews University) Minister at Westerdale, Caithness EDINBURGH : NORMAN MACLEOD,  -25 GEORGE IV. BRIDGE CANADA : EDWARD MACKAY, ST. PETER'S MANSE, MADOC, ONT. M DCCCC VI
2 CONT
2 CONT ==========================
2 CONT
2 CONT John Mackay of Skerray, the second son, had sasine in the town and lands of Skerray and others, dated 18th May 1675."
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret, daughter of Hector Munro of Eriboll : issue four sons and three daughters : His sons were, 
2 CONT * 1st, Hector, who succeeded him in Skerray ; 
2 CONT * 2nd, Donald, who studied the law, and was a writer in 1686, and who married Marion, daughter of Donald Munro of Arnaboll : issue Hugh and John ; 
2 CONT * 3d Hugh of Cairnloch  who was twice married: lst, to Christian,
2 CONT * third daughter of Robert Mackay of Achness, (as mentioned in the clan-Abrach branch) : and, 2nd, to his cousin-german, Margaret, youngest danghter of Patrick Sinclair of Ulbster.4th son of John of Skerray, married and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pg 571-572  .HISTORY THE HOUSE AND CLAN MACKAY,BY ROBERT MACKAY, 1829
