2 CONT
2 CONT '''20 February 1640: Extract Registered Contract of Marriage between Patrick Sinclair of Ulbster and Elizabeth McKy [McKay], eldest lawful daughter of John McKy of Dilret. Dated 20th February 1640 and Registered in the Sheriff Cou
2 CONC rt Books of Caithness 25th February 1647. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD84%2f2%2f130&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=patrick+sinclair&ko=p&r=&ro=s&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scot
2 CONC land, Papers of the Mackay Family, Lords Reay, reference GD84/2/130]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary for John Mackaey of Dilred ==
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN MACKAEY of Dilred or Dirlet and Strathy, second son of Hugh Mackay of Farr by his wife Lady Jane Gordon, eldest daughter of Alexander Earl of Sutherland, was the first of this branch. …. In 1619, he married Agnes, daughter of
2 CONC  Sir James Sinclair of Murkle, county of Caithness, by his wife Lady Elizabeth, third daughter of Robert Stuart, Earl of Orkney issue three sons, and two daughters,
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. '''Elizabeth''', who married Patrick Sinclair of Ulbster, son of John Sinclair of Brims, as appears by their marriage contract, dated 20th February 1640 ; and 
2 CONT *2. Jane who married the second William Mackay of Bighouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT
