1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Agnes-Sinclair/6000000020800125591
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Mackay,_1st_Lord_Reay#Family
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Donald Mackay, 1st Lord Reay married thirdly, a daughter of Francis Sinclair of Stirkoke, Caithness and had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # William Mackay, who married Ann, daughter of Colonel Hugh Mackay of Scoury.
2 CONT # Charles Mackay, progenitor of the Mackay of Sandwood branch of the clan.
2 CONT # Rupert Mackay, twin brother of Charles and who died unmarried.
2 CONT # Margaret Mackay, who died at Thurso, unmarried in 1720.
2 CONT # Christian Mackay, who married Alexander Gunn of Killeranan, chieftain of the MacHamish Gunns of Clan Gunn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Donald Mackay, 1st Lord Reay also married Rachel Winterfield or Harrison, sometime before 1631, but this marriage was annulled.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT " In February 1649," says Gordon, lC Donald Mackay, Lord Reay, having retired to Denmark, died in that kingdom... 5th, Marjory, daughter of Francis Sinclair of Stircoke :" issue, three sons, William of Kinloch, Charles of Sandwood
2 CONC , and his twin brother Rupert who died without issue; and two daughters, Margaret, who died at Thnrso, May 1720, and Christian  pg. 328-329
