0 @N6000000000437223301@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Lord knighted in 1641 by Charles I who was visiting Scotland;
1 CONT
1 CONT 1643 represented county of Edinburgh in Estates of parliament, appointed speaker to the barons;
1 CONT
1 CONT 1646 became lord advocate, proclaiming Charles II king on Feb. 5, 1649
1 CONT
1 CONT Mar. 10, 1649 appointed lord-clerk-register
1 CONT
1 CONT after Battle of Dunbar, in 1650, lived in retirement;
1 CONT
1 CONT accepted office under Cromwell and in July 1657, reappointed lord-clerk-register
1 CONT
1 CONT escaped to France whenCromwell resigned; outlawed on Oct. 10, 1660; condemned to death on May 15,1661; brought back to be prisoner in Tower in England, then in Edinburgh
1 CONT
1 CONT hanged at the Cross without trial, July 22, 1663
