0 @N6000000004547882861@ NOTE The English origins of Sampson Mason and Mary Butterworth Mason of Swansea, Mass, by Anne O. Mueller, Camden, Maine in 1984
1 CONT
1 CONT An attempt to identify this Mary Butterworth of Weymouth, Mass. by connecting her with an associated context lead to Charles Henry Pope's statement in "Pioneers of Massachusetts" in which he alleges that a Henry, John, Samuel and 
1 CONC Mary Butterworth were residing in Weymouth by 1635.
1 CONT
1 CONT In N, E. H. & G. Register XLI, pg 191 it was noted that Mary Butterworth, sister of Henry, John, Samuel was married to a Thomas Clifton in Jan-Feb 1641 in Weymouth. Thomas Clifton was made a freeman in Massachusetts Bay Colony 2 J
1 CONC une 1641. No other information about this Clifton family is found either in Weymouth or in Rehoboth. Savage informs that the family moved to Rhode Island.
1 CONT
1 CONT Samuel Butterworth of Rehoboth, John Butterworth of Weymouth and Mary (Butterworth) Clifton of Rhode Island appear to be the brothers and sister who had lived together in Weymouth, Mass. till 1641-42. Samuel's will in 1684 does no
1 CONC t mention John nor Mary (Butterworth) Clifton so presumably they were both deceased by this time.
